{"format":"bbdb","version":1,"name":"Real World 2026","exportedAt":"2026-09-25T11:03:28.555Z","files":{"wrestlers.json":[{"id":1,"name":"Aron Stevens","realName":"Aron Stevens","picture":"Damien Sandow.jpg","ability":70,"currentAbility":68,"potentialAbility":68,"charisma":58,"micSkills":67,"popularity":18,"condition":81,"hardcoreAbility":78,"injuryProne":98,"type":"manager","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":110,"height":190,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1982-04-03T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2001-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"To see Damien Sandow in action was like watching a kaleidoscope in human form: He stuck and moved, avoiding stagnation and keeping opponents guessing as to how — or whom — he would attack.\r\n\r\nAs a snooty brute in a blue robe, he connived his way to a Money in the Bank contract and nearly took the World Heavyweight Championship from John Cena. Next, as master mimic Damien Mizdow, he stormed from under The Miz’s shadow to steal the spotlight (and earn the WWE Tag Team Titles for the pair). And, as “Macho Mandow,” he briefly resurrected the spirit of one of the most beloved WWE Hall of Famers in history.\r\n\r\nWas it madness? Perhaps. However, Sandow’s willingness to take the ball and run with it endeared him to the WWE Universe, who cheered his dogged determination.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":79,"teams":[1221,1295,1466,2002,2744,2927,2928,3078],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":67,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":69,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":79,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":79,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":79,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":77,"awareness":62,"judgement":77},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1","wrestlerId":1,"promotionId":79,"startDate":"2019-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":2,"name":"Santino Marella","realName":"Santino Marella","picture":"Santino Marella_alt.jpg","ability":62,"currentAbility":61,"potentialAbility":61,"charisma":61,"micSkills":76,"popularity":30,"condition":70,"hardcoreAbility":73,"injuryProne":100,"type":"manager","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":106,"height":175,"base":"Canada","birthplace":"Canada","dateOfBirth":"1974-03-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2003-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Anthony Carelli, best known by his WWE ring name Santino Marella, is an Italian-Canadian professional wrestler. Carelli started his career on the Ontario independent circuit as Johnny GeoBasco, debuting with a disqualification win over Xhibit (now Rico Montana) in the opening match of a Ring Wars show in Orangeville, Ontario, on August 17, 2003. In the second half of 2004, Carelli wrestled four matches for BattlARTS in Japan, as Joe Basko. In 2005, Carelli (as Johnny Geo Basco) began training at Ohio Valley Wrestling (OVW), a developmental territory for World Wrestling Entertainment (WWE). In July, during a storyline where he was supposed to act afraid of The Boogeyman, but instead laughed, Carelli was shouted at and slapped by Jim Cornette, OVW's head booker and co-owner.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":28,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":73,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":26,"matchLayout":74,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":67,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":77,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":74,"mediaHandling":77,"brandBuilding":53,"socialMediaSavvy":82,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":67,"consistency":75,"awareness":68,"judgement":81},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-2","wrestlerId":2,"promotionId":28,"startDate":"2023-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":3,"name":"AJ Mendez","realName":"AJ Mendez","picture":"AJ Lee.jpg","ability":45,"currentAbility":50,"potentialAbility":50,"charisma":50,"micSkills":55,"popularity":53,"condition":77,"hardcoreAbility":34,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"F","weight":52,"height":154,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1987-03-19T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2007-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"April Jeanette Mendez is an American professional wrestler. Shortly after leaving university Mendez researched wrestling schools and enrolled in one a mile away from her house. To pay the tuition she began working full-time and became an official student in March 2007, debuting six months later as \"Miss April\" to work the New Jersey independent wrestling circuit. On October 10, 2008, Miss April made her debut for Women Superstars Uncensored (WSU). Mendez signed a contract with World Wrestling Entertainment on May 5, 2009, and was assigned to Florida Championship Wrestling, WWE's developmental territory. AJ made her main roster debut on the May 27, 2011, episode of SmackDown when she and Kaitlyn (known as The Chickbusters) lost to the team of Alicia Fox and Tamina.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[1405],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":60,"storytelling":62,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":32,"matchLayout":62,"psychology":60,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":65,"technicalCoaching":38,"characterCoaching":78,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":68,"mediaHandling":78,"brandBuilding":78,"socialMediaSavvy":68,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":65,"consistency":71,"awareness":60,"judgement":76},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-3","wrestlerId":3,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2025-09-05T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":5,"name":"Arn Anderson","realName":"Arn Anderson","picture":"Arn Anderson.jpg","ability":56,"currentAbility":64,"potentialAbility":64,"charisma":62,"micSkills":68,"popularity":29,"condition":47,"hardcoreAbility":56,"injuryProne":78,"type":"manager","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":116,"height":180,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1958-09-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1982-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Arn Anderson is a retired American wrestler who works as a manager and a road agent. He is best known for his work with WWE, WCW and AEW. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business. He was one half of the Tag Team Of The Year in 1991. He is part of the WWE Hall Of Fame.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[2697,2698,3270],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":91,"storytelling":94,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":18,"matchLayout":95,"psychology":91,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":28,"technicalCoaching":20,"characterCoaching":73,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":82,"mediaHandling":73,"brandBuilding":33,"socialMediaSavvy":70,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":28,"consistency":75,"awareness":91,"judgement":95}},{"id":6,"name":"B.G. James","realName":"B.G. James","picture":"BG James.jpg","ability":23,"currentAbility":29,"potentialAbility":29,"charisma":40,"micSkills":30,"popularity":35,"condition":52,"hardcoreAbility":49,"injuryProne":100,"type":"commentator","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":109,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1969-05-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1986-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Brian Girard \"B.G.\" James is an American professional wrestler and former United States Marine. James is best known for his appearances with the World Wrestling Federation (WWF) as The Roadie from 1994 to 1995 and as \"The Road Dogg\" Jesse James or simply Road Dogg from 1996 to 2001. He is also known for his appearances with Total Nonstop Action Wrestling as B.G. James from 2002 to 2009, and has also made appearances for several other promotions such as Smoky Mountain Wrestling, World Championship Wrestling, the United States Wrestling Association, the Catch Wrestling Association, and World Wrestling All-Stars. James has held numerous championships over the course of his career, including the WWF Intercontinental Championship once, the WWF Tag Team Championship five times with Billy Gunn as the New Age Outlaws, the WWF Hardcore Championship once, and the NWA World Tag Team Championship twice with Konnan and Ron Killings under the Freebird Rule as the 3Live Kru.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[909,910,1246,1560,2777,2799],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":71,"storytelling":74,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":75,"psychology":71,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":42,"technicalCoaching":29,"characterCoaching":77,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":77,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":70,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":42,"consistency":63,"awareness":71,"judgement":83}},{"id":8,"name":"Billy Kidman","realName":"Billy Kidman","picture":"Billy Kidman.jpg","ability":85,"currentAbility":86,"potentialAbility":86,"charisma":73,"micSkills":80,"popularity":8,"condition":74,"hardcoreAbility":100,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":88,"height":175,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1974-05-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1994-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Peter Alan Gruner, Jr. is an American professional wrestler, trainer, and wrestling producer, better known by his ring name Billy Kidman. Kidman is best known for his work with World Championship Wrestling (WCW) and WWE throughout the late 1990s, early to late 2000s, and the early 2010s. He trained the likes of Wade Barrett in Florida Championship Wrestling. He joined World Championship Wrestling (WCW) and ultimately gained fame as a key member of several strong wrestling factions. In addition to being a member of Raven's Flock, he also was a member of the Filthy Animals and later The New Blood. As a member of these factions, Gruner participated in memorable rivalries with top WCW names, including Hulk Hogan, Jeff Jarrett, and Rey Mysterio. Kidman wrestled for WCW for many years and won tag team gold with partner and real life friend Mysterio. After leaving the group, he won the WCW Cruiserweight Championship three times.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[1422,2750,2751],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":72,"storytelling":75,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":76,"psychology":72,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":42,"technicalCoaching":34,"characterCoaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":40,"brandBuilding":64,"socialMediaSavvy":27,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":42,"consistency":58,"awareness":72,"judgement":83},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-8","wrestlerId":8,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2010-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":9,"name":"Booker T","realName":"Booker T","picture":"Booker T.jpg","ability":63,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":53,"charisma":66,"micSkills":53,"popularity":41,"condition":62,"hardcoreAbility":62,"injuryProne":100,"type":"commentator","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":116,"height":187,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1965-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1989-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Can you dig it? Booker T is an 11-time WCW Tag Team Champion, a six-time World Champion, winner of the 2006 King of the Ring Tournament and the man responsible for popularizing the word, “Sucka!” in sports-entertainment. He also bears the distinction of holding the WCW World Heavyweight Championship when the promotion folded in 2001.\r\n\r\nFrom the moment he stepped into the WWE ring, Booker T Spinaroonied his way into Superstardom, tangling with a who’s who of squared circle greats, including “Stone Cold” Steve Austin, The Undertaker, John Cena, Triple H, Randy Orton, Batista, Rey Mysterio, Ric Flair, Christian, Mark Henry and many others.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":65,"teams":[2714,3285],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":78,"storytelling":80,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":81,"psychology":78,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":45,"technicalCoaching":35,"characterCoaching":81,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":81,"brandBuilding":75,"socialMediaSavvy":76,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":45,"consistency":62,"awareness":78,"judgement":87},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-9","wrestlerId":9,"promotionId":65,"startDate":"2022-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":11,"name":"Bret Hart","realName":"Bret Hart","picture":"Bret Hart.jpg","ability":100,"currentAbility":100,"potentialAbility":100,"charisma":100,"micSkills":100,"popularity":58,"condition":47,"hardcoreAbility":85,"injuryProne":42,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":107,"height":180,"base":"Canada","birthplace":"Canada","dateOfBirth":"1957-07-02T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1978-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Bret Hart is a Canadian writer, actor, and retired professional wrestler. A member of the Hart wrestling family, Hart has an amateur wrestling background, wrestling at Ernest Manning High School and Mount Royal College. Along with his \"Hitman\" nickname, Hart was known by the monikers \"The Excellence of Execution\", \"The Best There Is, The Best There Was, and The Best There Ever Will Be\" and \"The Pink and Black Attack\". Hart joined his father Stu Hart's promotion Stampede Wrestling in 1976, made his in-ring debut in 1978. He gained popularity and championship success throughout the 1980s and 1990s in the World Wrestling Federation (WWF, now WWE), where he helmed The Hart Foundation faction. He left for World Championship Wrestling (WCW) following the controversial \"Montreal Screwjob\" in November 1997, where he remained until October 2000 when he retired following a concussion, achieving much success despite his creative handling being widely criticized.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1093],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":100,"storytelling":100,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":100,"psychology":100,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":29,"technicalCoaching":52,"characterCoaching":74,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":74,"brandBuilding":63,"socialMediaSavvy":63,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":29,"consistency":42,"awareness":100,"judgement":100}},{"id":12,"name":"Brian Myers","realName":"Brian Myers","picture":"Curt Hawkins.jpg","ability":66,"currentAbility":62,"potentialAbility":62,"charisma":62,"micSkills":73,"popularity":20,"condition":84,"hardcoreAbility":82,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":101,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1985-04-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"There have been some legendary streaks in sports-entertainment history, but no Superstar can touch the streak held by Curt Hawkins — 269 consecutive losses without a single win. \r\n\r\nOf course, there's much more to Hawkins than a couple hundred consecutive L's. One of the rare Superstars who can claim to be a veteran without a single gray hair, Hawkins has been competing in WWE since 2007 when he backed up Edge alongside Zack Ryder as the lookalike Edgeheads. The pair not only claimed the WWE Tag Team Titles during this time, but mixed it up with The Undertaker in the main event of WrestleMania XXIV when their mentor took on The Deadman.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":28,"teams":[15,961,1419,2660,3409,3494,3811,4001],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":70,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":10,"matchLayout":71,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":54,"characterCoaching":65,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":90,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":63,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":86,"awareness":68,"judgement":81},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-12","wrestlerId":12,"promotionId":28,"startDate":"2020-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":13,"name":"Brock Lesnar","realName":"Brock Lesnar","picture":"Brock Lesnar.jpg","ability":65,"currentAbility":71,"potentialAbility":71,"charisma":81,"micSkills":66,"popularity":80,"condition":71,"hardcoreAbility":83,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"striker","gender":"M","weight":130,"height":187,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1977-07-12T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-10-11T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"excellent","prestige":"high","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Glory to The Conqueror, The Beast Incarnate, The Anomaly or whatever godlike title you choose to bestow upon Brock Lesnar. Surely, this creature fits each and every one of them.\r\n\r\nPossessing the type of staggering strength and frightening intensity seen only among Superman villains, this 6-foot-3, 266-pound freak of nature from Minneapolis, Minn., has forced his way to the top of every major combat sport. He won the NCAA Division I collegiate wrestling championship as a senior at the University of Minnesota, the WWE Championship within six months of his debut and the UFC Heavyweight Title in his fourth professional MMA fight. He also became The One in 21-1. Plain and simple, the man was built to destroy.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1225],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":75,"storytelling":77,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":55,"matchLayout":78,"psychology":75,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":60,"technicalCoaching":43,"characterCoaching":84,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":45,"mediaHandling":84,"brandBuilding":96,"socialMediaSavvy":76,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":60,"consistency":62,"awareness":75,"judgement":85}},{"id":14,"name":"Bryan Danielson","realName":"Bryan Danielson","picture":"Daniel Bryan.jpg","ability":26,"currentAbility":35,"potentialAbility":35,"charisma":27,"micSkills":25,"popularity":64,"condition":64,"hardcoreAbility":47,"injuryProne":95,"type":"commentator","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":89,"height":170,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1981-05-22T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Bryan Danielson is a retired American wrestler who works as a colour commentator and a road agent. He is best known for his work with WWE, AEW, CMLL, NJPW, NOAH, PWG and ROH. He is married to Brie Garcia. He is part of the ROH Hall Of Fame.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[259,1359,1892,2752,3459],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":91,"storytelling":92,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":92,"psychology":91,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":92,"technicalCoaching":92,"characterCoaching":85,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":85,"brandBuilding":64,"socialMediaSavvy":78,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":92,"consistency":91,"awareness":91,"judgement":95},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-14","wrestlerId":14,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2021-09-05T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":15,"name":"Kaitlyn","realName":"Kaitlyn","picture":"Kaitlyn.jpg","ability":38,"currentAbility":45,"potentialAbility":45,"charisma":32,"micSkills":37,"popularity":10,"condition":98,"hardcoreAbility":50,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"F","weight":58,"height":162,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1986-10-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Celeste Beryl Bonin is an American body builder, model, and professional wrestler better known by her ring name, Kaitlyn. In July 2010, Bonin signed a developmental contract with World Wrestling Entertainment, and was assigned to Florida Championship Wrestling (FCW), WWE's developmental territory. In September 2010, she competed in the all-female third season of NXT where she made her mark by feuding with her Pro Vickie Guerrero, and went on to win the competition in November 2010, thus becoming the only female in history to have won NXT. Prior to her debut to the main roster in December 2010, she formed a tag team with AJ known as The Chickbusters in May 2011. After the split of the team in May 2012, she returned to singles competition, and started to become known as \"The Hybrid Diva of the WWE\" (combination of beauty and power).","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1405],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":42,"storytelling":47,"productFit":30,"riskTaking":40,"matchLayout":48,"psychology":42,"workerManagement":30,"trainingIntensity":53,"technicalCoaching":32,"characterCoaching":57,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":60,"mediaHandling":57,"brandBuilding":64,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":6,"reactionSpeed":53,"consistency":56,"awareness":42,"judgement":37}},{"id":16,"name":"Chad Patton","realName":"Chad Patton","picture":"Chad Patton.jpg","ability":92,"currentAbility":84,"potentialAbility":84,"charisma":88,"micSkills":80,"popularity":5,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":88,"injuryProne":98,"type":"referee","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":77,"height":175,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1976-05-05T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1994-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Chad Patton was first introduced to the WWE family by friend, Jack Doan. On his days off and on the weekend, Patton would help set up the ring for WWE events in the Midwest. Officials recognized his hard work and put him in charge of putting up the stage. Eventually, it became a full-time job for Patton. At one point, he was asked to try his hand at ring announcing, which Patton says he was terrible at. Patton was thrilled when a referee position became available and tried out. He's been a WWE referee ever since.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":0,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":0,"brandBuilding":16,"socialMediaSavvy":0,"ruleKnowledge":84,"positioning":67,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-16","wrestlerId":16,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2005-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":17,"name":"Charles Robinson","realName":"Charles Robinson","picture":"Charles Robinson.jpg","ability":92,"currentAbility":94,"potentialAbility":94,"charisma":100,"micSkills":92,"popularity":11,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":96,"injuryProne":96,"type":"referee","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":68,"height":167,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1964-07-02T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1993-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Charles Shane Robinson is an American professional wrestling referee. While growing up, Robinson idolized NWA superstar Ric Flair. He also studied NWA referee Tommy Young in order to hone his mannerisms as a referee. His professional wrestling career began when he joined the Pro Wrestling Federation (PWF) as a photographer in 1993, supplementing his income by working as a salesman. After being used as a special guest referee, he later became a full-time referee for the PWF. Robinson repeatedly petitioned the World Championship Wrestling (WCW) professional wrestling promotion for a job. In 1997, after working with Dan Hedman as a professional sales representative, he was given a tryout match, referreeing a dark match between Chris Taylor and a jobber. Following the match, Robinson was signed to a contract by WCW. In 1999, Robinson became the heel referee of the Four Horsemen, aligning himself with his hero, Ric Flair.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":35,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":35,"brandBuilding":18,"socialMediaSavvy":18,"ruleKnowledge":94,"positioning":75,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":80,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-17","wrestlerId":17,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2004-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":18,"name":"Chris Jericho","realName":"Chris Jericho","picture":"Chris Jericho_alt.jpg","ability":73,"currentAbility":70,"potentialAbility":70,"charisma":79,"micSkills":63,"popularity":64,"condition":64,"hardcoreAbility":80,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":103,"height":177,"base":"Canada","birthplace":"Canada","dateOfBirth":"1970-11-09T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1990-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Chris Jericho is a Canadian wrestler who works in the USA, Canada, Mexico, the British Isles, Japan and Europe. He is a 5'11\", 227lb worker who is classed as using a Regular style. He uses the Code Breaker, the Judas Effect and the Walls of Jericho as his finishers. He is best known for his work with WWE, AEW, NJPW, WCW, CMLL and ECW. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business. He has been voted Male Wrestler Of The Year three times. He has been voted Male Veteran Wrestler Of The Year three times. Outside of wrestling he is a relatively well known musician.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[584,1114,2663,2701,3822,3928],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":87,"storytelling":89,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":15,"matchLayout":89,"psychology":87,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":63,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":88,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":85,"mediaHandling":88,"brandBuilding":76,"socialMediaSavvy":85,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":63,"consistency":58,"awareness":87,"judgement":92},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-18","wrestlerId":18,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2019-01-08T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":19,"name":"Claudio Castagnoli","realName":"Claudio Castagnoli","picture":"Cesaro.jpg","ability":88,"currentAbility":79,"potentialAbility":79,"charisma":73,"micSkills":77,"popularity":48,"condition":78,"hardcoreAbility":95,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":110,"height":193,"base":"Europe","birthplace":"Switzerland","dateOfBirth":"1980-12-27T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"mid","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"While his greatness has shined through in every one of his accomplishments, from his reign as United States Champion to being one-half of the powerhouse “Real Americans” alongside Jack Swagger to winning the first-ever Andre the Giant Memorial Battle Royal at WrestleMania 30 to using his inhuman stamina to take Superstars like John Cena to the limit to forging a championship tandem with Tyson Kidd, his greatest glory to date has come from his alliance with Sheamus.\r\n\r\nThe powerhouse combination ripped through the tag team ranks to capture multiple Tag Team Championships and has shown every team exactly why “[they] don’t set the bar, [they] are The Bar!” The Swiss Cyborg has since formed a powerful alliance with Shinsuke Nakamura and Sami Zayn, and he teamed up with WWE's Rockstar at The Horror Show at WWE Extreme Rules to win the SmackDown Tag Team Titles in a wild Tables Match.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[419,993,1144,1316,1493,2103],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":75,"storytelling":79,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":12,"matchLayout":80,"psychology":75,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":85,"technicalCoaching":76,"characterCoaching":59,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":88,"mediaHandling":59,"brandBuilding":73,"socialMediaSavvy":52,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":85,"consistency":85,"awareness":75,"judgement":85},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-19","wrestlerId":19,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2022-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":20,"name":"CM Punk","realName":"CM Punk","picture":"CM Punk.jpg","ability":85,"currentAbility":76,"potentialAbility":76,"charisma":89,"micSkills":84,"popularity":78,"condition":64,"hardcoreAbility":74,"injuryProne":68,"type":"wrestler","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":99,"height":180,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1978-10-26T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"great","prestige":"high","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"CM Punk is an American wrestler who works exclusively in America. He is a Middleweight who is classed as using a Technician Striker style. He is best known for his work with WWE, AEW, TNA, PWG, ROH, MLW, ZERO1, GCW and IWA-MS. He is married to AJ Lee. He is part of the ROH Hall Of Fame.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[1311],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":88,"storytelling":89,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":89,"psychology":88,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":79,"technicalCoaching":71,"characterCoaching":96,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":96,"brandBuilding":86,"socialMediaSavvy":92,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":79,"consistency":76,"awareness":88,"judgement":93},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-20","wrestlerId":20,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2023-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":21,"name":"Cody Rhodes","realName":"Cody Rhodes","picture":"Cody Rhodes.jpg","ability":71,"currentAbility":70,"potentialAbility":70,"charisma":70,"micSkills":57,"popularity":79,"condition":82,"hardcoreAbility":86,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":100,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1985-06-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2006-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"great","prestige":"high","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Cody Rhodes is an American wrestler who works in America, Canada, Mexico, the British Isles and Japan. He is a Middleweight who is classed as using a Regular style. He is best known for his work with WWE, NJPW, AEW, AAA, TNA, PWG, ROH, wXw, NWA, RevPro, HOH, DEFY, The Crash, EVOLVE, AAW, OTT, Smash, C4, A1, Defiant and SWE. He is married to Brandi Rhodes. He was voted Independent Wrestler Of The Year in 2018.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[1019,1037,1295,1903,2707,2708,2709,3420],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":84,"storytelling":83,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":14,"matchLayout":83,"psychology":84,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":84,"technicalCoaching":55,"characterCoaching":83,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":86,"mediaHandling":83,"brandBuilding":90,"socialMediaSavvy":89,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":84,"consistency":78,"awareness":84,"judgement":90},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-21","wrestlerId":21,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2022-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":22,"name":"The Great Khali","realName":"The Great Khali","picture":"The Great Khali.jpg","ability":26,"currentAbility":34,"potentialAbility":34,"charisma":28,"micSkills":27,"popularity":46,"condition":44,"hardcoreAbility":37,"injuryProne":72,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":190,"height":213,"base":"Other","birthplace":"India","dateOfBirth":"1972-08-27T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Everyone looked up to The Great Khali – whether you wanted to or not.\r\n\r\nThat’s because the 7-foot-1, 347-pound skyscraper of a man towered over all of the WWE Universe. Khali stood out from every crowd not only for his overwhelming size, but also for being the first to blaze a trail to WWE from his native India.\r\n\r\nKhali’s battle-ready mentality and intimidating presence combined to make him a unique threat to every member of the WWE roster. He successfully stood tall against celebrated WWE Superstars, including The Undertaker, Kane, Big Show, John Cena and Shawn Michaels. And he was the last man standing in a 20-Man Battle Royal on SmackDown in 2007 that allowed Khali to realize his dream of becoming World Heavyweight Champion.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":54,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":28,"matchLayout":51,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":34,"technicalCoaching":4,"characterCoaching":50,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":72,"mediaHandling":50,"brandBuilding":76,"socialMediaSavvy":55,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":34,"consistency":54,"awareness":62,"judgement":77}},{"id":23,"name":"David Otunga","realName":"David Otunga","picture":"David Otunga.jpg","ability":61,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":53,"charisma":44,"micSkills":53,"popularity":16,"condition":92,"hardcoreAbility":33,"injuryProne":100,"type":"manager","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":104,"height":180,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1980-04-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2009-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"David Daniel Otunga, Sr. is an American professional wrestler, lawyer, and actor. In November 2008, Otunga signed a developmental contract with World Wrestling Entertainment and was assigned to its development territory, Florida Championship Wrestling. He made his debut on May 29, 2009, under the ring name Dawson Alexander. On February 16, 2010, after numerous dark matches on both Raw and Smackdown, it was announced that Otunga would wrestle on the first season of WWE NXT under his real name, with R-Truth as his storyline mentor.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[2754],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":40,"storytelling":49,"productFit":63,"riskTaking":36,"matchLayout":52,"psychology":40,"workerManagement":63,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":27,"characterCoaching":53,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":64,"mediaHandling":53,"brandBuilding":69,"socialMediaSavvy":58,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":13,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":56,"awareness":40,"judgement":49}},{"id":24,"name":"Dean Malenko","realName":"Dean Malenko","picture":"Dean Malenko.jpg","ability":98,"currentAbility":94,"potentialAbility":94,"charisma":100,"micSkills":100,"popularity":27,"condition":42,"hardcoreAbility":100,"injuryProne":60,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":96,"height":175,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1960-08-04T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1979-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Dean Simon better known by his ring name Dean Malenko, is a retired professional wrestler.  He is best known for his time with Extreme Championship Wrestling (ECW), New Japan Pro Wrestling (NJPW) and World Championship Wrestling (WCW). In WWF, he was a 2-time Light Heavyweight Champion. In WCW, he was a 1-time United States Champion, a 4-time Cruiserweight Champion and a 1-time World Tag Team Champion with Chris Benoit. In ECW, he was a 2-time Television Champion and a 1-time Tag Team Champion with Chris Benoit.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":87,"storytelling":90,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":11,"matchLayout":91,"psychology":87,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":29,"technicalCoaching":49,"characterCoaching":64,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":89,"mediaHandling":64,"brandBuilding":49,"socialMediaSavvy":49,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":29,"consistency":46,"awareness":87,"judgement":92},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-24","wrestlerId":24,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2019-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":25,"name":"Alberto El Patrón","realName":"Alberto El Patrón","picture":"Alberto Del Rio.jpg","ability":68,"currentAbility":68,"potentialAbility":68,"charisma":73,"micSkills":83,"popularity":51,"condition":70,"hardcoreAbility":67,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":108,"height":193,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1977-05-25T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Alberto El Patrón is a Mexican luchador who works in the USA, Canada, Mexico, Japan and Europe. He is a 6'5\", 239lb worker who is classed as using a Technician style. He uses the Cross Armbreaker as his finisher. He is best known for his work with WWE, CMLL, AAA, ROH, GLEAT and Lucha Ungrnd. Outside of wrestling he is a former MMA fighter.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":119,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":75,"storytelling":78,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":14,"matchLayout":79,"psychology":75,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":69,"technicalCoaching":65,"characterCoaching":78,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":86,"mediaHandling":78,"brandBuilding":79,"socialMediaSavvy":64,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":69,"consistency":70,"awareness":75,"judgement":85},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-25","wrestlerId":25,"promotionId":119,"startDate":"2026-01-16T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2028-01-16T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2028-01-16T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":26,"name":"Drew Galloway","realName":"Drew Galloway","picture":"Drew Galloway.jpg","ability":64,"currentAbility":73,"potentialAbility":73,"charisma":71,"micSkills":66,"popularity":67,"condition":81,"hardcoreAbility":68,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"striker","gender":"M","weight":121,"height":193,"base":"UK","birthplace":"Scotland","dateOfBirth":"1985-06-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2001-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"great","prestige":"mid","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"While many fellow 15-year-olds were worried about sitting at the “popular table” at lunchtime, Drew McIntyre was already training to become a WWE Superstar. He didn’t have to wait terribly long to achieve his dream, either, as the endlessly athletic Scotsman skyrocketed from the U.K. independent scene to WWE before he was old enough to rent a car.\r\n\r\nMcIntyre secured himself a long-awaited World Championship opportunity when he won the 30-Man Royal Rumble Match in January 2020. The Scotsman took his career to the next level with a win over Brock Lesnar at WrestleMania 36 to capture his first WWE Title, finally earning the World Championship that Mr. McMahon had predicted.\r\n\r\nAfter several impressive WWE Title defenses against the likes of Seth Rollins, Bobby Lashley and Randy Orton, McIntyre was recognized as the face of Monday Night Raw when the red brand made him the first overall selection of the 2020 WWE Draft.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[913,915,1019,1044,1745,3664],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":76,"storytelling":78,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":78,"psychology":76,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":84,"technicalCoaching":57,"characterCoaching":76,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":76,"brandBuilding":84,"socialMediaSavvy":79,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":84,"consistency":83,"awareness":76,"judgement":86},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-26","wrestlerId":26,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2018-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":27,"name":"The Rock","realName":"The Rock","picture":"The Rock.jpg","ability":64,"currentAbility":68,"potentialAbility":68,"charisma":68,"micSkills":67,"popularity":90,"condition":65,"hardcoreAbility":76,"injuryProne":93,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":120,"height":190,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1972-05-02T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1996-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"excellent","prestige":"high","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"He has been dubbed The Great One, The People’s Champion and The Most Electrifying Man in All of Entertainment. Mere words fail to capture the essence of the most charismatic Superstar of all time, though the catchphrase “boots to asses” comes awfully close.\r\n\r\nThe first third-generation Superstar in WWE history, the man born Dwayne Johnson was destined for sports-entertainment immortality since birth, but his rise to the status of a pop culture icon was harder to predict. In the time since he made his debut as a grinning good guy at the 1996 Survivor Series, The Brahma Bull has won eight WWE Championships, headlined WrestleMania, hosted “Saturday Night Live,” written a New York Times bestselling autobiography, top-billed the popular HBO series “Ballers” and starred in films like “Fast Five” and “The Game Plan,” which have grossed literally billions of dollars. The amazing thing is, he’s just getting started.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[1498],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":86,"storytelling":84,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":28,"matchLayout":83,"psychology":86,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":56,"technicalCoaching":38,"characterCoaching":100,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":72,"mediaHandling":100,"brandBuilding":100,"socialMediaSavvy":100,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":56,"consistency":61,"awareness":86,"judgement":92},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-27","wrestlerId":27,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":28,"name":"Eddie Colón","realName":"Eddie Colón","picture":"Primo.jpg","ability":54,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":55,"charisma":69,"micSkills":62,"popularity":15,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":44,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":95,"height":175,"base":"USA","birthplace":"Puerto Rico","dateOfBirth":"1982-12-21T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Edwin \"Eddie\" Carlos Colón is a Puerto Rican professional wrestler. He is the son of Carlos Colón, Sr. and the younger brother of wrestlers Stacy and Carly Colón, (better known as Carlito in his WWE stint). He began wrestling in the World Wrestling Council, where he won the WWC Universal Heavyweight Championship five times, as well as numerous secondary and tertiary titles. In 2007, Colón signed a developmental contract with WWE, being assigned to Florida Championship Wrestling. In this promotion he was teamed with Eric Pérez, forming a tag team known as The Puerto Rican Nightmares. On February 23, 2008, they became the first wrestlers to hold the FCW Florida Tag Team Championship. Upon being promoted to the main brand, he was teamed with his brother. Subsequently, The Colóns became the first team to hold the WWE Tag Team Championship and World Tag Team Championship at the same time, making them the first Unified WWE Tag Team Champions.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":79,"teams":[983,1410,3163],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":54,"storytelling":62,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":29,"matchLayout":64,"psychology":54,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":69,"technicalCoaching":50,"characterCoaching":49,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":71,"mediaHandling":49,"brandBuilding":47,"socialMediaSavvy":46,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":69,"consistency":78,"awareness":54,"judgement":72},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-28","wrestlerId":28,"promotionId":79,"startDate":"2024-10-05T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-10-05T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-10-05T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":29,"name":"Big E","realName":"Big E","picture":"Big E.jpg","ability":72,"currentAbility":79,"potentialAbility":79,"charisma":89,"micSkills":76,"popularity":56,"condition":80,"hardcoreAbility":90,"injuryProne":100,"type":"manager","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":129,"height":177,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1986-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2009-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"The New Day love to have a good time. Good times come easy when you have a powerhouse like Big E on your team who is willing to wear a unicorn horn on his head.\r\n\r\nThe word “Big” almost feels like an understatement when talking about Big E, but how else do you describe a 290-pound tank of a man who can deadlift a Fiat? “Superhuman” comes to mind, as does “Herculean.” “Big,” though, leaves no question about the type of punishment he dishes out inside the ring.\r\n\r\nLong before he was chanting “New Day Rocks,” Big E was destined to command the spotlight. He was always the strongest kid in class — an advantage he used to win state championships in high school wrestling and punish quarterbacks on the defensive line for the University of Iowa.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[1247,1248],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":63,"storytelling":65,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":37,"matchLayout":66,"psychology":63,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":38,"characterCoaching":85,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":63,"mediaHandling":85,"brandBuilding":83,"socialMediaSavvy":72,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":81,"awareness":63,"judgement":78},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-29","wrestlerId":29,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2013-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":30,"name":"Fred Rosser","realName":"Fred Rosser","picture":"Darren Young.jpg","ability":61,"currentAbility":60,"potentialAbility":60,"charisma":64,"micSkills":75,"popularity":17,"condition":80,"hardcoreAbility":61,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":108,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1983-11-02T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Fred Rosser is an American wrestler who works in America, Canada and Japan. He is a Middleweight who is classed as using a Entertainer style. He is best known for his work with WWE, NJoA and NWA. He is the protege of Mark Henry.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1282,4036,4037],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":59,"storytelling":62,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":18,"matchLayout":63,"psychology":59,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":71,"technicalCoaching":51,"characterCoaching":58,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":82,"mediaHandling":58,"brandBuilding":55,"socialMediaSavvy":49,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":71,"consistency":69,"awareness":59,"judgement":75}},{"id":32,"name":"Matt Bloom","realName":"Matt Bloom","picture":"Jason Albert.jpg","ability":94,"currentAbility":84,"potentialAbility":84,"charisma":89,"micSkills":90,"popularity":25,"condition":65,"hardcoreAbility":66,"injuryProne":74,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":150,"height":198,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1972-11-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1997-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Matthew Jason \"Matt\" Bloom is an American professional wrestler. Bloom first rose to prominence under the ring names Albert and A-Train during his first tenure with WWE when it was named the World Wrestling Federation, during which he also became a one time Intercontinental Champion. After leaving WWE, In March 2005, Bloom began wrestling for the Japanese All Japan Pro Wrestling promotion, adopting the ring name Giant Bernard, a reference to former wrestler Brute Bernard. He went on to join the Voodoo Murders stable alongside fellow WWE alumni Chuck Palumbo and Johnny Stamboli. He became a three time World Tag Team Champion by winning New Japan Pro Wrestling's IWGP Tag Team Championship twice (once with Travis Tomko and once with Karl Anderson as Bad Intentions) and Pro Wrestling Noah's GHC Tag Team Championship once with Anderson.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":65,"teams":[942,943,2814],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":71,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":5,"matchLayout":72,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":47,"technicalCoaching":35,"characterCoaching":61,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":95,"mediaHandling":61,"brandBuilding":53,"socialMediaSavvy":44,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":47,"consistency":70,"awareness":68,"judgement":81},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-32","wrestlerId":32,"promotionId":65,"startDate":"2014-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":33,"name":"Kane","realName":"Kane","picture":"Kane_suit.jpg","ability":71,"currentAbility":74,"potentialAbility":74,"charisma":78,"micSkills":74,"popularity":52,"condition":61,"hardcoreAbility":94,"injuryProne":100,"type":"manager","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":147,"height":210,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1967-04-26T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1992-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"At 7 feet tall and weighing in at more than 300 pounds, Kane is a monstrous abomination that seems to have been extracted directly from your childhood nightmares.\r\n\r\nConsumed by an infernal desire to set ablaze the lives of his fellow Superstars, Kane leaves a scorched path of destruction behind his fiery footsteps. Some of The Big Red Monster’s more demented acts have included setting a WWE Hall of Famer on fire, hitting a WWE executive with a Tombstone, kidnapping too many Superstars to mention and forcing Lita to marry him. No one is safe from his twisted desires and demonic impulses. Least of all, it would seem, Kane himself.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1129,1130,1131,1359,1400,3355],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":78,"storytelling":79,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":17,"matchLayout":79,"psychology":78,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":54,"technicalCoaching":29,"characterCoaching":73,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":83,"mediaHandling":73,"brandBuilding":65,"socialMediaSavvy":67,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":54,"consistency":64,"awareness":78,"judgement":87}},{"id":34,"name":"Heath","realName":"Heath","picture":"Heath Slater.jpg","ability":65,"currentAbility":59,"potentialAbility":59,"charisma":72,"micSkills":55,"popularity":27,"condition":87,"hardcoreAbility":60,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":98,"height":185,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1983-07-15T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Fueled by a mouth that never stops running and arrogance as scorching as the shock of red hair on his head, Heath Slater certainly lives up to his self-imposed moniker, “The One-Man Band.”\r\n\r\nHailing from West Virginia, Slater first exploded onto the WWE scene as a Rookie on WWE NXT’s inaugural season. Right out of the gate, Slater made an impact, becoming the first-ever NXT Rookie to defeat a WWE Pro in a singles match. From there, he joined The Nexus in its hostile takeover of WWE and, like all good rockers before him, refused to stay painted into a single corner.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[913,914,1321,1322,1932,2419,2420],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":59,"storytelling":63,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":15,"matchLayout":65,"psychology":59,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":68,"technicalCoaching":50,"characterCoaching":78,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":85,"mediaHandling":78,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":72,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":68,"consistency":72,"awareness":59,"judgement":75}},{"id":36,"name":"Jake Hager","realName":"Jake Hager","picture":"Jack Swagger.jpg","ability":58,"currentAbility":67,"potentialAbility":67,"charisma":56,"micSkills":52,"popularity":32,"condition":72,"hardcoreAbility":75,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":125,"height":198,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1982-03-24T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2006-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Jacob \"Jake\" Hager, Jr. is an American professional wrestler. Hager attended the University of Oklahoma as a two sport athlete, participating in both football and wrestling. He switched to wrestling full-time in his sophomore year, and in 2006, set the record for most pins in a season with 30 as an All-American. Following a try-out, Hager signed a WWE contract in mid-2006. He made his debut for the WWE developmental territory Deep South Wrestling in September, and was moved to the Ohio Valley Wrestling territory in January 2007. A few months later, Hager debuted for Florida Championship Wrestling, where he was the final FCW Southern Heavyweight Champion and the inaugural FCW Florida Heavyweight Champion. In late 2008, he debuted for the ECW brand under the name Jack Swagger, and in January 2009, he won his first world championship, the ECW Championship after defeating Matt Hardy.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1493,1583],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":63,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":29,"matchLayout":65,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":75,"technicalCoaching":69,"characterCoaching":62,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":71,"mediaHandling":62,"brandBuilding":67,"socialMediaSavvy":53,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":75,"consistency":77,"awareness":56,"judgement":74}},{"id":37,"name":"Christian Cage","realName":"Christian Cage","picture":"Christian.jpg","ability":80,"currentAbility":74,"potentialAbility":74,"charisma":71,"micSkills":63,"popularity":51,"condition":67,"hardcoreAbility":80,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":95,"height":182,"base":"Canada","birthplace":"Canada","dateOfBirth":"1973-11-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1995-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Christian Cage, who graduated from Funking Conservatory on 01 January 1998, is a Canadian wrestler who works in the USA, Canada and the British Isles. He is a 6'1\", 209lb worker who is classed as using a Entertainer style. He uses the Killswitch and the Spear as his finishers. He is best known for his work with WWE, AEW and TNA. He was one half of the Male Tag Team Of The Year in 2000. He was voted Male Veteran Wrestler Of The Year in 2023.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[38,1039,2663,4268],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":84,"storytelling":85,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":11,"matchLayout":85,"psychology":84,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":75,"technicalCoaching":68,"characterCoaching":84,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":89,"mediaHandling":84,"brandBuilding":71,"socialMediaSavvy":84,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":75,"consistency":83,"awareness":84,"judgement":90},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-37","wrestlerId":37,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2021-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":38,"name":"JTG","realName":"JTG","picture":"JTG.jpg","ability":46,"currentAbility":50,"potentialAbility":50,"charisma":64,"micSkills":40,"popularity":14,"condition":85,"hardcoreAbility":54,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":106,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1984-12-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"The street-savvy robbin’ hood wasn’t just about flossed-out grills, swiping wallets and hot steppin’. JTG’s heart was in competing and stealing the spotlight. From his early days as one-half of the controversial tag team Cryme Tyme to a notable run as a singles star on SmackDown, JTG proved himself a tough Brooklyn brawler both in and out of the ring.\r\n\r\nThe wildly popular Cryme Tyme effectively combined JTG’s speed with Shad’s brute strength for a winning combination in WWE’s tag team division. Together, JTG and Shad were embraced by the WWE Universe, who learned its share of hip lingo on the pair’s WWE.com series “Word Up!” When Cryme Tyme’s seemingly unbreakable bond shattered in 2010, JTG was forced to go his own way, navigating the singles ranks on SmackDown.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1009,3289,3371],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":44,"storytelling":52,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":33,"matchLayout":55,"psychology":44,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":68,"technicalCoaching":33,"characterCoaching":63,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":67,"mediaHandling":63,"brandBuilding":52,"socialMediaSavvy":59,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":68,"consistency":54,"awareness":44,"judgement":66}},{"id":39,"name":"Jerry Lawler","realName":"Jerry Lawler","picture":"Jerry Lawler.jpg","ability":42,"currentAbility":51,"potentialAbility":51,"charisma":39,"micSkills":50,"popularity":40,"condition":42,"hardcoreAbility":53,"injuryProne":93,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":110,"height":180,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1949-11-29T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1970-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"It’s good to be the king. Just ask Jerry Lawler.\r\n\r\nReigning over sports-entertainment since the 1970s, Jerry “The King” Lawler has thrilled in the ring as the pride of Memphis, Tenn. and entertained from the announce table as Raw’s most irrepressible broadcaster. Effective as both a hero and villain, The King enraged WWE fans when he offended Bret Hart’s parents during a personal rivalry with The Hit Man, and then inspired them when he stepped in the ring to challenge The Miz for the WWE Title at 61 years of age. This aptitude for every aspect of sports-entertainment has earned Lawler countless titles, legions of fans and entry into the WWE Hall of Fame.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3187],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":72,"storytelling":80,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":83,"psychology":72,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":31,"technicalCoaching":22,"characterCoaching":75,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":75,"brandBuilding":53,"socialMediaSavvy":70,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":31,"consistency":47,"awareness":72,"judgement":83}},{"id":40,"name":"Ricardo Rodríguez","realName":"Ricardo Rodríguez","picture":"Ricardo Rodriguez_alt.jpg","ability":47,"currentAbility":54,"potentialAbility":54,"charisma":65,"micSkills":40,"popularity":13,"condition":87,"hardcoreAbility":38,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":87,"height":170,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1986-02-17T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2006-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Jesús Rodríguez is a Mexican American professional wrestler and ring announcer. Before wrestling for independent California promotions, Rodriguez wrestled with other upcoming wrestlers in backyards for BBW Beyond Backyard Wrestling. Rodriguez formerly wrestled for various promotions as the masked wrestler Chimaera, and his professional wrestling debut came at UEW's 1st Annual West Coast Cruiser Cup Tournament on August 11, 2006. In Chikara, he participated in the Young Lions Cup VII and was eliminated by KC Day. At Dragon Gate USA, Chimaera competed in a Dragon Gate Fray match which was won by Brad Allen on March 26, 2010. For Deutsche Wrestling Allianz Chimaera had two championship opportunities one for the DWA Cruiserweight Championship and one for DWA Tag Team Championship. He also participated in Vendetta Pro Triforce Championship tournament and won the vacant Vendetta Pro Triforce Championship which he vacated when he signed for WWE.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":68,"teams":[3190],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":61,"storytelling":63,"productFit":86,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":64,"psychology":61,"workerManagement":86,"trainingIntensity":62,"technicalCoaching":48,"characterCoaching":70,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":70,"brandBuilding":32,"socialMediaSavvy":72,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":17,"reactionSpeed":62,"consistency":60,"awareness":61,"judgement":71},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-40","wrestlerId":40,"promotionId":68,"startDate":"2023-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":41,"name":"Jim Ross","realName":"Jim Ross","picture":"Jim Ross.jpg","ability":65,"currentAbility":61,"potentialAbility":61,"charisma":64,"micSkills":48,"popularity":48,"condition":44,"hardcoreAbility":65,"injuryProne":74,"type":"commentator","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":110,"height":180,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1952-01-03T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1974-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Jim Ross is an American man who works primarily as an announcer. He is best known for his work with WWE, WCW, NJPW and AEW. He has been voted Announcer Of The Year twelve times. He is in the Hall Of Fame for WWE and NWA.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":80,"storytelling":56,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":48,"psychology":80,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":5,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":78,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":78,"brandBuilding":26,"socialMediaSavvy":66,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":0,"reactionSpeed":5,"consistency":0,"awareness":80,"judgement":48},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-41","wrestlerId":41,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2019-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":42,"name":"Roman Reigns","realName":"Roman Reigns","picture":"Roman Reigns.jpg","ability":79,"currentAbility":70,"potentialAbility":70,"charisma":64,"micSkills":68,"popularity":80,"condition":78,"hardcoreAbility":56,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":120,"height":187,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1985-05-25T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-08-19T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"excellent","prestige":"high","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Roman Reigns is an American wrestler who works exclusively in the USA. He is a 6'3\", 265lb worker who is classed as using a Powerhouse style. He uses the Spear as his finisher. He is best known for his work with WWE and NXT. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business. He was one half of the Male Tag Team Of The Year in 2013.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[1503],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":82,"storytelling":82,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":17,"matchLayout":82,"psychology":82,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":85,"technicalCoaching":46,"characterCoaching":88,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":83,"mediaHandling":88,"brandBuilding":94,"socialMediaSavvy":84,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":85,"consistency":89,"awareness":82,"judgement":89},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-42","wrestlerId":42,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2012-11-18T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1300000,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1300000},{"id":43,"name":"Curtis Axel","realName":"Curtis Axel","picture":"Curtis Axel.jpg","ability":80,"currentAbility":84,"potentialAbility":84,"charisma":87,"micSkills":99,"popularity":22,"condition":85,"hardcoreAbility":86,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":103,"height":187,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1979-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2007-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Joseph Curtis \"Joe\" Hennig is a 3rd generation American professional wrestler. He is the grandson of Larry \"The Axe\" Hennig and the son of \"Mr. Perfect\" Curt Hennig. Hennig made his professional debut on July 13, 2007 in Waterloo, Iowa for World League Wrestling (WLW), teaming with Ted DiBiase, Jr. On March 31, 2007, Hennig along with his mother, siblings, and his grandfather represented his father \"Mr. Perfect\" Curt Hennig at the 2007 WWE Hall of Fame ceremony by accepting the award on his behalf. Hennig signed a developmental contract with World Wrestling Entertainment and was assigned to its developmental territory Florida Championship Wrestling (FCW). On September 11, 2008, Hennig and Sebastian Slater defeated Nic Nemeth and Gavin Spears to win the FCW Florida Tag Team Championship.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1221,1305,1612,2754],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":73,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":14,"matchLayout":75,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":71,"technicalCoaching":58,"characterCoaching":55,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":86,"mediaHandling":55,"brandBuilding":51,"socialMediaSavvy":48,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":71,"consistency":85,"awareness":68,"judgement":81}},{"id":45,"name":"John Cena","realName":"John Cena","picture":"John Cena.jpg","ability":60,"currentAbility":69,"potentialAbility":69,"charisma":56,"micSkills":79,"popularity":82,"condition":63,"hardcoreAbility":54,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":114,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1977-04-23T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"excellent","prestige":"high","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"He’s a 16-time World Champion, New York Times best-selling author and record-setting Make-A-Wish granter. He’s released a hit album, starred in blockbuster movies and carried the torch for WWE since he first set foot in a WWE ring nearly two decades ago. If you really can’t see John Cena at this point, chances are you simply aren’t looking.\r\n\r\nWas there any doubt Cena would become the living legend he is today? You practically knew you were glimpsing the future “Face That Runs the Place” when a muscular Massachusetts kid threw down with Kurt Angle for a chance to become a true WWE Superstar. Sure enough, a little ruthless aggression went a long way. After gaining the respect of his peers by stepping to The Olympic Hero, Cena went supernova as the fire-spitting Doctor of Thuganomics, eventually reaching the peak by upending JBL for his first WWE Championship at WrestleMania 21.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":85,"storytelling":83,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":18,"matchLayout":82,"psychology":85,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":66,"technicalCoaching":52,"characterCoaching":92,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":82,"mediaHandling":92,"brandBuilding":95,"socialMediaSavvy":85,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":66,"consistency":70,"awareness":85,"judgement":91},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-45","wrestlerId":45,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2002-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":46,"name":"John Cone","realName":"John Cone","picture":"John Cone.jpg","ability":83,"currentAbility":80,"potentialAbility":80,"charisma":72,"micSkills":69,"popularity":9,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":63,"injuryProne":98,"type":"referee","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":79,"height":172,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1974-11-16T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1995-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Cone started refereeing independent wrestling matches in August 1995. He worked for Harley Race World League Wrestling from 1999 to 2006 and got his big break when a WWE official attended a match he refereed. Cone tried out for WWE and was quickly signed. He was sent to WWE developmental territory Ohio Valley Wrestling and later Deep South Wrestling. John was one of the first referees to work for all three WWE brands ECW, SmackDown, and Raw. Since signing with WWE, John has refereed in 15 countries and on 5 continents. John has said he is most proud of his performance in the boxing match between Matt Hardy and Evander Holyfield, which took place in August, 2007 in front of a sold out crowd at Madison Square Garden.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":20,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":20,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":6,"ruleKnowledge":80,"positioning":64,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":65,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-46","wrestlerId":46,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2005-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":47,"name":"John Layfield","realName":"John Layfield","picture":"JBL.jpg","ability":66,"currentAbility":70,"potentialAbility":70,"charisma":58,"micSkills":68,"popularity":41,"condition":58,"hardcoreAbility":80,"injuryProne":100,"type":"manager","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":132,"height":195,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1966-11-29T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1992-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"mid","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Never challenge John Bradshaw Layfield to a street fight — especially on Wall Street. The former WWE Champion may have been vicious in the ring, but the self-made millionaire is downright heartless when it comes to making a buck. Gifted with the business sense of a banking executive, the big man from Sweetwater, Texas could’ve easily made his fortune by sitting behind a desk, but there was nothing JBL loved more than a fight. A pro football player before stepping in the ring, Bradshaw first made an impression in WWE as a member of The New Blackjacks alongside Barry Windham in 1997. The WWE Universe took notice of the aggressive Texan, but it wasn’t until JBL linked up with the imposing Ron Simmons that he made a lasting impact. JBL retired to a tropical island with millions in his bank account in 2009, but he returned to WWE in 2012 as a color commentator on SmackDown and the host of WWE.com’s “JBL & Cole Show.”","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":5,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":75,"storytelling":80,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":35,"matchLayout":82,"psychology":75,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":67,"technicalCoaching":12,"characterCoaching":71,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":65,"mediaHandling":71,"brandBuilding":66,"socialMediaSavvy":63,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":67,"consistency":66,"awareness":75,"judgement":85},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-47","wrestlerId":47,"promotionId":5,"startDate":"2024-07-17T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":48,"name":"Dirty Dango","realName":"Dirty Dango","picture":"Fandango.jpg","ability":65,"currentAbility":59,"potentialAbility":59,"charisma":51,"micSkills":74,"popularity":22,"condition":71,"hardcoreAbility":42,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":109,"height":187,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1983-07-22T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"First introduced in a series of vignettes that showed him moving seductively in a nightclub with a gorgeous woman, Fandango shocked the sports-entertainment world when he defeated Chris Jericho in his in-ring debut at WrestleMania 29. That win still ranks as one of the greatest upsets in sports-entertainment history and shot the dancing devil into the viral stratosphere with a trend known as “Fandangoing.”\r\n\r\nAfter hanging up his dancing shoes, the 6-foot-4, 244-pounder teamed up with Tyler Breeze to form Breezango. With more style than a stack of GQ magazines, the duo captured the hearts of the WWE Universe when they dubbed themselves “The Fashion Police” and sought to rid the blue brand of any fashion faux pas, and they achieved their greatest victory to date when they finally captured tandem gold by defeating Imperium for the NXT Tag Team Titles.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":28,"teams":[960,2548,2664,3371,3784],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":64,"storytelling":68,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":19,"matchLayout":69,"psychology":64,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":65,"technicalCoaching":46,"characterCoaching":75,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":81,"mediaHandling":75,"brandBuilding":64,"socialMediaSavvy":64,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":65,"consistency":68,"awareness":64,"judgement":78},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-48","wrestlerId":48,"promotionId":28,"startDate":"2022-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":49,"name":"Jon Moxley","realName":"Jon Moxley","picture":"Jon Moxley.jpg","ability":66,"currentAbility":68,"potentialAbility":68,"charisma":65,"micSkills":68,"popularity":63,"condition":76,"hardcoreAbility":65,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"striker","gender":"M","weight":102,"height":185,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1985-12-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Jonathan Good is an American professional wrestler. Good got his start in Heartland Wrestling Association (HWA) in 2004 using the ring name Jon Moxley. He started training under the tutelage of Cody Hawk and Les Thatcher. In June 2004, Moxley made his debut. On June 6, 2009, Moxley was a participant in Combat Zone Wrestling (CZW)'s Tournament of Death VIII. In the first round, Moxley defeated Brain Damage in a Dining Death match, but lost to Nick \"F'N\" Gage in a triple threat fans bring the weapons match, also including Scotty Vortekz, in the semi-finals. Moxley started working for Dragon Gate USA (DGUSA) in 2009 and made appearances with the company until 2011. On April 4, 2011, it was confirmed that Good had signed a developmental deal with World Wrestling Entertainment, and Dragon Gate USA granted his release from the promotion. On May 27 he joined WWE's developmental territory, Florida Championship Wrestling, under the name Dean Ambrose.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[1348,2440,3459],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":75,"storytelling":76,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":24,"matchLayout":76,"psychology":75,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":82,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":85,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":76,"mediaHandling":85,"brandBuilding":78,"socialMediaSavvy":73,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":82,"consistency":78,"awareness":75,"judgement":85},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-49","wrestlerId":49,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2019-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":50,"name":"Jimmy Uso","realName":"Jimmy Uso","picture":"jimmy uso.jpg","ability":58,"currentAbility":61,"potentialAbility":61,"charisma":52,"micSkills":72,"popularity":58,"condition":92,"hardcoreAbility":67,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":114,"height":187,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1985-08-22T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2009-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"The Usos don’t care if you like them. They might actually prefer it if you didn’t.\r\n\r\nThe twin sons of WWE Hall of Famer Rikishi, Jey and his brother Jimmy bubbled under the radar for years as a workhorse tag team in WWE before finally hitting the big time while embracing their Samoan heritage. The brothers would repeatedly take to the skies in bright colors, flying tassels and dazzling war paint, winning the WWE Tag Team Championship and Slammy for Tag Team of the Year twice.\r\n\r\nAs four-time SmackDown Tag Team Champions, these Usos are perhaps the most ruthless tag team walking WWE today. They’ll bring the crowd to its feet with their skills virtually every time they enter the ring (their battles with The New Day in 2017 were all instant classics). Back on SmackDown, all Jey & Jimmy need is each other: The only two who have been down since Day One.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[266,1521],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":70,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":24,"matchLayout":71,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":75,"technicalCoaching":43,"characterCoaching":70,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":76,"mediaHandling":70,"brandBuilding":68,"socialMediaSavvy":70,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":75,"consistency":80,"awareness":68,"judgement":81},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-50","wrestlerId":50,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2014-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":51,"name":"Josh Mathews","realName":"Josh Mathews","picture":"Josh Matthews.jpg","ability":38,"currentAbility":46,"potentialAbility":46,"charisma":49,"micSkills":54,"popularity":13,"condition":94,"hardcoreAbility":47,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":65,"height":172,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1980-11-25T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2001-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Josh Matthew Lomberger is an American presenter, announcer, and former pro wrestler, better known by his ring name Josh Mathews. Lomberger was a runner-up to Maven and Nidia in the first WWE Tough Enough in 2001. After Tough Enough, Lomberger gained some in-ring experience on the independent circuit and in Xcitement Wrestling Federation, which was run by WWE Hall of Famer Jimmy Hart. Lomberger was eventually hired by World Wrestling Entertainment, and began using the name \"Josh Matthews\". In December 2002, he began appearing as the backstage interviewer for the SmackDown! brand and as an announcer on WWE Velocity. Mathews became the play by play commentator of Saturday Morning Slam upon the show's debut on August 18, 2012 on The CW. Two months later he joined former adversary JBL to become the new Smackdown commentary team.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":60,"productFit":30,"riskTaking":33,"matchLayout":60,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":30,"trainingIntensity":66,"technicalCoaching":24,"characterCoaching":55,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":67,"mediaHandling":55,"brandBuilding":30,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":6,"reactionSpeed":66,"consistency":66,"awareness":62,"judgement":49},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-51","wrestlerId":51,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2025-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2027-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2027-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":52,"name":"Jey Uso","realName":"Jey Uso","picture":"Jey Uso.jpg","ability":72,"currentAbility":64,"potentialAbility":64,"charisma":75,"micSkills":74,"popularity":64,"condition":91,"hardcoreAbility":73,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":109,"height":185,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1985-08-22T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2009-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"The Usos don’t care if you like them. They might actually prefer it if you didn’t.\r\n\r\nThe twin sons of WWE Hall of Famer Rikishi, Jey and his brother Jimmy bubbled under the radar for years as a workhorse tag team in WWE before finally hitting the big time while embracing their Samoan heritage. The brothers would repeatedly take to the skies in bright colors, flying tassels and dazzling war paint, winning the WWE Tag Team Championship and Slammy for Tag Team of the Year twice.\r\n\r\nAs four-time SmackDown Tag Team Champions, these Usos are perhaps the most ruthless tag team walking WWE today. They’ll bring the crowd to its feet with their skills virtually every time they enter the ring (their battles with The New Day in 2017 were all instant classics). Back on SmackDown, all Jey & Jimmy need is each other: The only two who have been down since Day One.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[266,1521],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":72,"storytelling":74,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":74,"psychology":72,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":75,"technicalCoaching":45,"characterCoaching":84,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":84,"brandBuilding":77,"socialMediaSavvy":81,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":75,"consistency":70,"awareness":72,"judgement":83},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-52","wrestlerId":52,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2014-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":54,"name":"Kevin Nash","realName":"Kevin Nash","picture":"Kevin Nash.jpg","ability":42,"currentAbility":51,"potentialAbility":51,"charisma":57,"micSkills":57,"popularity":53,"condition":48,"hardcoreAbility":53,"injuryProne":47,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":149,"height":205,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1959-07-09T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1990-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"As Kevin Nash lifted one of his mighty legs over the ropes, you immediately knew what was to follow. And no, we're not talking about that other leg. It was time for trouble. Whether he's known as Diesel, one of \"The Outsiders\" or simply Big Kev, this imposing Superstar has never been afraid to make waves at every stop. He's got the list of enemies to prove it.\r\n\r\nDebuting as a sunglassed ringside enforcer in WWE, Nash quickly made an impact by taking on the role of Shawn Michaels' personal – and cold-blooded – bodyguard. Within his first year, Diesel eliminated seven men in the 1994 Royal Rumble Match and later won the Intercontinental Championship. Shortly thereafter, Diesel and Michaels captured the World Tag Team Titles together, making \"Big Daddy Cool\" a double champion in WWE.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1486,1549,3152,3218,3219,3220],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":78,"storytelling":75,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":37,"matchLayout":74,"psychology":78,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":42,"technicalCoaching":16,"characterCoaching":85,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":63,"mediaHandling":85,"brandBuilding":67,"socialMediaSavvy":84,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":42,"consistency":40,"awareness":78,"judgement":87}},{"id":55,"name":"Kofi Kingston","realName":"Kofi Kingston","picture":"Kofi Kingston.jpg","ability":58,"currentAbility":67,"potentialAbility":67,"charisma":60,"micSkills":71,"popularity":48,"condition":82,"hardcoreAbility":64,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":97,"height":182,"base":"Other","birthplace":"Ghana","dateOfBirth":"1981-08-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2006-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"The New Day’s Kofi Kingston is powered by positivity, and he’s used it to catapult himself to new heights, including the WWE Championship.\r\n\r\nSince bursting on the WWE scene in 2007, Kingston has established himself as one of WWE’s premier high-flyers. That, paired with his upbeat attitude, made him a perennial favorite of the WWE Universe as he racked up Intercontinental, United States and Tag Team Championships. Kingston also cemented his place in WWE history with a series of daredevil moments where he saved himself from elimination in several Royal Rumble Matches.\r\n\r\nWhen he joined forces with Big E and Xavier Woods to form The New Day, though, no one could have guessed that the trio of unicorn horn-wearing, Booty-O-chomping Superstars would achieve the feats that they have in WWE. In fact, the WWE Universe despised them at first, but soon grew to love them.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[920,1003,1148,1247,1249,3660,4402],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":73,"storytelling":75,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":30,"matchLayout":75,"psychology":73,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":78,"technicalCoaching":61,"characterCoaching":77,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":70,"mediaHandling":77,"brandBuilding":72,"socialMediaSavvy":69,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":78,"consistency":71,"awareness":73,"judgement":84}},{"id":57,"name":"Mark Henry","realName":"Mark Henry","picture":"Mark Henry.jpg","ability":26,"currentAbility":28,"potentialAbility":28,"charisma":35,"micSkills":26,"popularity":39,"condition":57,"hardcoreAbility":31,"injuryProne":95,"type":"commentator","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":163,"height":190,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1971-06-12T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1996-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Imagine every bone in your body being crushed into sawdust while you struggle to take a breath. Either you’re about to become python food, or you’re on the business end of Mark Henry’s World’s Strongest Slam.\r\n\r\nHenry burst onto the scene at the 1992 Summer Olympics in Barcelona, where he competed in weightlifting in the super-heavyweight division. Three years later at the Pan American Games, Henry captured a gold, silver and bronze medal. Henry’s intimidating size and weightlifting prowess earned the attention of WWE, which signed him in 1996. He stands as the first developmental talent for WWE and was under contract for more than two decades. From there, the new Superstar joined the infamous Nation of Domination, where he established himself as a ruthless and powerful big man — traits he channeled to earn first prize in the 2002 \"World's Strongest Man\" competition at the Arnold Schwarzenegger Classic.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1471],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":69,"storytelling":77,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":30,"matchLayout":79,"psychology":69,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":47,"technicalCoaching":25,"characterCoaching":78,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":70,"mediaHandling":78,"brandBuilding":69,"socialMediaSavvy":75,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":47,"consistency":58,"awareness":69,"judgement":81}},{"id":58,"name":"Matt Striker","realName":"Matt Striker","picture":"Matt Striker.jpg","ability":38,"currentAbility":43,"potentialAbility":43,"charisma":43,"micSkills":58,"popularity":15,"condition":88,"hardcoreAbility":58,"injuryProne":100,"type":"commentator","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":102,"height":175,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1974-06-26T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2001-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Matt Striker is a retired American wrestler who works as an announcer and a road agent. He was one half of Young Bluds alongside Rob Eckos. He is best known for his work with WWE, IMPACT, NOAH, wXw, MLW, GCW, HOH, ZERO1, Lucha Ungrnd, CWFH, ICW NHB and Defiant. He was voted Announcer Of The Year in 2008.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[2818],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":61,"storytelling":65,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":24,"matchLayout":66,"psychology":61,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":55,"characterCoaching":73,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":76,"mediaHandling":73,"brandBuilding":49,"socialMediaSavvy":69,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":74,"awareness":61,"judgement":77}},{"id":59,"name":"Matt Sydal","realName":"Matt Sydal","picture":"Matt Sydal.jpg","ability":55,"currentAbility":57,"potentialAbility":57,"charisma":65,"micSkills":45,"popularity":28,"condition":78,"hardcoreAbility":39,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":75,"height":172,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1983-03-19T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"If you are his opponent, don't let his boyish smile and peace signs catch you off guard because, the next thing you know, Evan Bourne will be executing a Shooting Star Press off a ladder down onto your ribs!\r\n\r\n\"Air Bourne,\" as he called the move, was perhaps the most breathtaking aerial assault in WWE, but it was far from the only trick in the high-flyer's arsenal. Bourne proved time and time again that he was willing to throw caution to the wind, especially when opponents least expected it. When you look like a happy-go-lucky sprout in a land of snarling giants, extreme measures need to be taken.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[920,1219,1340,2452,2649,2702,2732,3516],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":60,"storytelling":66,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":45,"matchLayout":68,"psychology":60,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":75,"technicalCoaching":58,"characterCoaching":58,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":55,"mediaHandling":58,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":48,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":75,"consistency":64,"awareness":60,"judgement":76},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-59","wrestlerId":59,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2020-09-05T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":60,"name":"Matt Cardona","realName":"Matt Cardona","picture":"Zack Ryder.jpg","ability":55,"currentAbility":62,"potentialAbility":62,"charisma":66,"micSkills":48,"popularity":35,"condition":79,"hardcoreAbility":56,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":102,"height":185,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1985-05-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Matt Cardona is an American wrestler who works in the USA, Canada, the British Isles and Japan. He is a 6'2\", 224lb worker who is classed as using a Entertainer style. He uses the Rough Ryder as his finisher. He is best known for his work with WWE, AEW, TNA, DDT, NWA, GCW, MLP, JCW and AIW. He is married to Chelsea Green. He was voted Male Independent Wrestler Of The Year in 2023.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[15,1419,1449,1450,3409,3494,3731],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":63,"storytelling":67,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":31,"matchLayout":68,"psychology":63,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":54,"characterCoaching":82,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":69,"mediaHandling":82,"brandBuilding":77,"socialMediaSavvy":65,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":62,"awareness":63,"judgement":78},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-60","wrestlerId":60,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2026-01-02T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2028-01-02T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2028-01-02T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":61,"name":"Michael Cole","realName":"Michael Cole","picture":"Michael Cole.jpg","ability":52,"currentAbility":43,"potentialAbility":43,"charisma":45,"micSkills":55,"popularity":41,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":43,"injuryProne":100,"type":"commentator","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":80,"height":172,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1968-12-08T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1997-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Michael Sean Coulthard, better known by his stage name, Michael Cole, is an American professional wrestling commentator, wrestling show host, seldom wrestler, and former news journalist. Coulthard began his career in the media as a journalist, working for CBS Radio. His first high-profile assignment was to cover the failed 1988 US presidential campaign of Democratic Party nominee Michael Dukakis. Cole came to the World Wrestling Federation in mid-1997 after being recommended to company officials by Todd Pettengill and started using the stage name \"Michael Cole.\" He provided voice-overs for promotional videos and later became the host of LiveWire show alongside Jim Cornette. He signed for WWE where he served as commentator for SmackDown starting in 1999, before being shifted to the company's flagship program, Raw, where his has been since 2008 to the present.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":1,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":1,"trainingIntensity":20,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":71,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":71,"brandBuilding":41,"socialMediaSavvy":73,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":0,"reactionSpeed":20,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-61","wrestlerId":61,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2003-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":62,"name":"Mick Foley","realName":"Mick Foley","picture":"Mick Foley.jpg","ability":80,"currentAbility":73,"potentialAbility":73,"charisma":65,"micSkills":59,"popularity":52,"condition":38,"hardcoreAbility":85,"injuryProne":87,"type":"manager","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":130,"height":190,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1965-06-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1983-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Inspired to become a Superstar after watching Jimmy Snuka leap from the top of a steel cage in Madison Square Garden, Mick Foley adopted Superfly’s fearlessness when he entered the ring himself. As Cactus Jack, he earned a fan following not for winning matches, but for surviving them. In a bout against the punishing Big Van Vader in Germany, Foley’s ear was torn off. In Japan, he suffered third-degree burns in an exploding ring. Still, no matter what he suffered through, Foley kept fighting back.\r\n\r\nWhen he came to WWE in 1996, he turned into Mankind, a deranged miscreant who lurked in boiler rooms and shoved his fingers down opponents’ throats. Under the leather mask of this maniac, Foley lived through sports-entertainment’s most shocking moment when he was thrown off the top of the Hell in a Cell by The Undertaker. The unforgettable image of Foley’s body artlessly plummeting to the ground below defined not only his career, but WWE’s “Attitude Era” as a whole.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[1498,3245,3246],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":92,"storytelling":89,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":36,"matchLayout":88,"psychology":92,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":45,"technicalCoaching":15,"characterCoaching":88,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":64,"mediaHandling":88,"brandBuilding":47,"socialMediaSavvy":83,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":45,"consistency":52,"awareness":92,"judgement":95},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-62","wrestlerId":62,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2028-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2028-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":63,"name":"Mike Rotunda","realName":"Mike Rotunda","picture":"Mike Rotunda.jpg","ability":81,"currentAbility":84,"potentialAbility":84,"charisma":98,"micSkills":84,"popularity":10,"condition":79,"hardcoreAbility":71,"injuryProne":80,"type":"writer","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":116,"height":190,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1958-03-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1981-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Lawrence Michael \"Mike\" Rotunda is a former American professional wrestler, perhaps best known under the names Irwin R. Schyster or Michael Wallstreet. Rotunda was a varsity wrestler for the Syracuse Orangemen in New York. While he was never an All American, he did win the EIWA Championships in 1981 as a Heavyweight. Rotunda and Windham joined the World Wrestling Federation as the U.S. Express in 1984. They won the WWF World Tag Team Championship twice. Rotunda left the WWF in early 1987 and returned to Florida, where he won the NWA Florida Heavyweight Championship in March. In the WWF, Rotunda became Irwin R. Schyster (or I.R.S.). Schyster had a heel \"tax-man\" gimmick (he was portrayed as a former IRS tax collector from Washington, D.C.), and harassed the faces and fans, scolding them to pay their taxes.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1228],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":67,"storytelling":77,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":29,"matchLayout":80,"psychology":67,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":19,"technicalCoaching":18,"characterCoaching":63,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":71,"mediaHandling":63,"brandBuilding":31,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":19,"consistency":29,"awareness":67,"judgement":80}},{"id":65,"name":"Místico","realName":"Místico","picture":"Caristico.jpg","ability":66,"currentAbility":65,"potentialAbility":65,"charisma":62,"micSkills":54,"popularity":42,"condition":80,"hardcoreAbility":46,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":86,"height":167,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1982-12-22T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"He is without a doubt one of the greatest figures in the history of wrestling. Protagonist of one of the greatest phenomena in the history of this sport and the engine of the new boom in this sport.\r\n\r\nYou can't talk about modern wrestling without mentioning this man. He began with the name Dr. Karonte Jr. in 1998 taking the name his father had wrestled with. Later, under the name Astro Boy, he joined the ranks of the World Wrestling Council where he began to show his great talent. As of 2004, he takes on the character Místico where he immediately captures the attention of the fans. \r\n\r\nIn 2004 he participated in the La Gran Alternativa Tournament which is a fair where a high-ranking fighter sponsors a rookie to give him a boost, there he was supported by El Hijo del Santo causing a real stir and winning said tournament. From that moment on, he captured the attention of the media and fans who began to fill the arenas where he performed, thus starting a new era in wrestling.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[982,1176,2775,2918],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":76,"storytelling":79,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":30,"matchLayout":80,"psychology":76,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":82,"technicalCoaching":73,"characterCoaching":79,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":70,"mediaHandling":79,"brandBuilding":88,"socialMediaSavvy":52,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":82,"consistency":63,"awareness":76,"judgement":86},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-65","wrestlerId":65,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2015-12-18T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":66,"name":"Yoshitatsu","realName":"Yoshitatsu","picture":"Yoshi Tatsu.jpg","ability":58,"currentAbility":56,"potentialAbility":56,"charisma":41,"micSkills":43,"popularity":10,"condition":69,"hardcoreAbility":39,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"submission","gender":"M","weight":102,"height":185,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1977-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Naofumi Yamamoto is a Japanese professional wrestler and former boxer. Yamamoto is a graduate from Kokushikan University with a degree in political science. He trained for his professional wrestling career in the New Japan Pro Wrestling Dojo before making his professional wrestling debut on October 12, 2002. Yamamoto lost to Wataru Inoue in his debut match in the first match of a show in the Korakuen Hall. In late 2007 Yamamoto was signed by World Wrestling Entertainment (WWE) to a full-time contract, which meant that he had to relocate to the United States. He immediately was assigned to WWE's developmental territory Florida Championship Wrestling (FCW), to undergo assessment and training in the \"WWE Style\" of wrestling. Initially he wrestled as Mr. Yamamoto, then simply as Yamamoto.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":45,"teams":[1103,1239,1253,1696,2144,2306],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":54,"storytelling":59,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":60,"psychology":54,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":65,"technicalCoaching":53,"characterCoaching":55,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":55,"brandBuilding":55,"socialMediaSavvy":37,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":65,"consistency":45,"awareness":54,"judgement":72},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-66","wrestlerId":66,"promotionId":45,"startDate":"2024-10-14T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-10-14T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-10-14T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":67,"name":"Natalya","realName":"Natalya","picture":"Natalya.jpg","ability":76,"currentAbility":68,"potentialAbility":68,"charisma":79,"micSkills":59,"popularity":40,"condition":76,"hardcoreAbility":66,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"F","weight":61,"height":162,"base":"Canada","birthplace":"Canada","dateOfBirth":"1982-05-27T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"mid","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Natalya is a Canadian wrestler who works in the USA, Canada, the British Isles, Japan, Europe and Oceania. She is a 5'5\", 134lb worker who is classed as using a Technician style. She uses the German Suplex and the Sharpshooter as her finishers. She is best known for her work with WWE, AAA and GCW. She is married to TJ Wilson.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":65,"teams":[2443,2770],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":80,"storytelling":82,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":13,"matchLayout":82,"psychology":80,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":76,"technicalCoaching":70,"characterCoaching":48,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":87,"mediaHandling":48,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":45,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":76,"consistency":65,"awareness":80,"judgement":88},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-67","wrestlerId":67,"promotionId":65,"startDate":"2011-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"inDevelopment":true},{"id":68,"name":"Nic Nemeth","realName":"Nic Nemeth","picture":"Dolph Ziggler.jpg","ability":82,"currentAbility":72,"potentialAbility":72,"charisma":72,"micSkills":59,"popularity":47,"condition":77,"hardcoreAbility":81,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":99,"height":180,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1980-07-27T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-11-03T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"mid","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Nic Nemeth is an American wrestler who works in America, Canada and Japan. He is a Middleweight who is classed as using a Regular style. He is best known for his work with WWE, NJPW and TNA. He is currently the IWGP Global Heavyweight champion.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":28,"teams":[271,1583,1745,1965,3986,3987],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":76,"storytelling":78,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":79,"psychology":76,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":88,"technicalCoaching":66,"characterCoaching":75,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":75,"brandBuilding":75,"socialMediaSavvy":68,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":88,"consistency":76,"awareness":76,"judgement":86},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-68","wrestlerId":68,"promotionId":28,"startDate":"2024-01-13T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":69,"name":"Orlando Colón","realName":"Orlando Colón","picture":"Epico.jpg","ability":60,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"charisma":46,"micSkills":70,"popularity":16,"condition":87,"hardcoreAbility":41,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":104,"height":180,"base":"USA","birthplace":"Puerto Rico","dateOfBirth":"1982-03-24T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2005-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Orlando Colón is a Puerto Rican professional wrestler. He is the son of José Colón, nephew of Carlos Colón, Sr. and the cousin of professional wrestlers Carly (Carlito), Eddie (Primo), & Stacy Colón. Colón began wrestling in the independent circuit of the United States, performing in Hybrid Pro Wrestling, a promotion based in Schoolcraft, Michigan. He was given a villainous persona, which noted his lineage as a member of the Colón family, as well as a gimmick of \"winning by any means necessary\", emphasizing his heel character. Colón debuted as the mystery opponent in a stipulation match that promoted the debut of “another member of the Colón family”. Shortly afterwards, he made his return to the company under a masked gimmick named “Fireblaze”. On the November 4 episode of SmackDown, Colón made his debut in WWE as a heel, under the Epico name but without the mask.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":79,"teams":[1410,1587,3163],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":57,"storytelling":63,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":30,"matchLayout":65,"psychology":57,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":65,"technicalCoaching":55,"characterCoaching":50,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":70,"mediaHandling":50,"brandBuilding":47,"socialMediaSavvy":48,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":65,"consistency":62,"awareness":57,"judgement":74},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-69","wrestlerId":69,"promotionId":79,"startDate":"2024-10-05T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-10-05T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-10-05T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":70,"name":"Paul Heyman","realName":"Paul Heyman","picture":"Paul Heyman.jpg","ability":70,"currentAbility":64,"potentialAbility":64,"charisma":74,"micSkills":68,"popularity":63,"condition":65,"hardcoreAbility":76,"injuryProne":27,"type":"manager","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":106,"height":177,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1965-09-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1987-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Paul Heyman is an American entertainment producer, most well-known for his former roles in professional wrestling as promoter, manager, and commentator. He is also an occasional actor in film. Heyman was the creative force behind the revolutionary promotion Extreme Championship Wrestling in the 1990s. He has also worked in Ted Turner's World Championship Wrestling, the American Wrestling Association and World Wrestling Entertainment, including WWE's ECW brand where he was recognized as the ECW Representative in front of the camera, and was the general manager and brand manager behind the scenes. Heyman began as a photographer and writer for third-party wrestling publications such as Pro Wrestling Illustrated. Heyman made his managerial debut on January 2, 1987, initially appearing on the Northeast independent circuit before moving to a more high-profile stint with Florida Championship Wrestling in February 1987. There, he became Paul E. Dangerously.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":85,"storytelling":59,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":51,"psychology":85,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":6,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":89,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":89,"brandBuilding":41,"socialMediaSavvy":93,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":6,"consistency":0,"awareness":85,"judgement":91},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-70","wrestlerId":70,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2017-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":71,"name":"Paul Levesque","realName":"Paul Levesque","picture":"Triple H.jpg","ability":65,"currentAbility":74,"potentialAbility":74,"charisma":63,"micSkills":68,"popularity":70,"condition":56,"hardcoreAbility":80,"injuryProne":78,"type":"manager","style":"striker","gender":"M","weight":116,"height":190,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1969-07-27T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1992-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"great","prestige":"high","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"He’s The King of Kings, a nickname with no hint of exaggeration considering that Triple H is essentially WWE royalty.\r\n\r\nFrom his days as a Greenwich, Conn. snob, to his era-defining run as a co-founder of D-Generation X, to the unrelenting drive that made him an absolute squared circle institution, to shepherding future main-eventers Randy Orton and Batista toward WWE greatness in Evolution, Triple H hasn’t just existed on the cutting edge —  he’s been the one sharpening the blade.\r\n\r\nA 14-time World Champion, The Game has clashed with a litany of ring legends to seize the throne as The King of Kings. The Rock, “Stone Cold” Steve Austin, Ric Flair, Shawn Michaels, The Undertaker, John Cena and even WWE Chairman Vince McMahon — each mowed down by the sledgehammer-wielding fist of The Cerebral Assassin.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[1021,1550],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":85,"storytelling":86,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":14,"matchLayout":87,"psychology":85,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":45,"technicalCoaching":55,"characterCoaching":78,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":86,"mediaHandling":78,"brandBuilding":80,"socialMediaSavvy":74,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":45,"consistency":75,"awareness":85,"judgement":91},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-71","wrestlerId":71,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"1995-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":72,"name":"PJ Black","realName":"PJ Black","picture":"PJ Black.jpg","ability":63,"currentAbility":63,"potentialAbility":63,"charisma":59,"micSkills":76,"popularity":14,"condition":74,"hardcoreAbility":59,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":97,"height":182,"base":"Other","birthplace":"South Africa","dateOfBirth":"1981-03-03T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1997-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Since making his in-ring debut at 16 in 1997, PJ Black has earned a reputation for being one of the top high-flyers and risk-takers in the sport. After starting his career in his native South Africa and Europe, Black came to the United States in 2008 and signed with WWE, where he went on to become a three-time tag team champion and defeat some of the biggest stars in the industry.\r\n\r\nBlack, who made his ROH debut at Survival of the Fittest in November 2018 and signed with the company a few months later, has competed in 61 countries and 48 states. When he’s not flying around the ring, the “Darewolf” is a thrill-seeker who enjoys adrenaline-pumping activities such as jumping out of airplanes, surfing and doing dirt bike stunts.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1063,1321,2082],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":60,"storytelling":67,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":69,"psychology":60,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":80,"technicalCoaching":61,"characterCoaching":64,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":64,"brandBuilding":60,"socialMediaSavvy":53,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":80,"consistency":59,"awareness":60,"judgement":76}},{"id":73,"name":"Paul Wight","realName":"Paul Wight","picture":"Big Show.jpg","ability":39,"currentAbility":29,"potentialAbility":29,"charisma":33,"micSkills":16,"popularity":53,"condition":57,"hardcoreAbility":41,"injuryProne":98,"type":"commentator","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":180,"height":210,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1972-02-08T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1994-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"From the moment he stomped into WWE in 1999, he ripped through the competition to amass a giant collection of titles, including the WWE Championship.\r\n\r\nWith accolades that stretch as far as his gigantic reach, Big Show is one of the most decorated and feared Superstars to ever step foot inside the squared circle. He is the first Superstar to capture the WWE, WCW and ECW Championships and won the Andre the Giant Memorial Battle Royal at WrestleMania 31.\r\n\r\nStill knocking heads more than two decades after his in-ring debut, Big Show remains a monstrous threat. Best of luck to anyone who crosses his path.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[1129,1319,1320,1520,2701],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":74,"storytelling":76,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":17,"matchLayout":77,"psychology":74,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":55,"technicalCoaching":19,"characterCoaching":79,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":83,"mediaHandling":79,"brandBuilding":76,"socialMediaSavvy":72,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":55,"consistency":64,"awareness":74,"judgement":84},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-73","wrestlerId":73,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2021-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":74,"name":"Randy Orton","realName":"Randy Orton","picture":"Randy Orton.jpg","ability":66,"currentAbility":76,"potentialAbility":76,"charisma":80,"micSkills":74,"popularity":73,"condition":68,"hardcoreAbility":63,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":113,"height":193,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1980-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"great","prestige":"high","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Randy Orton was born a WWE Superstar.\r\n\r\nEarly after he arrived in WWE, Triple H and Ric Flair mentored him, welcoming him into their elite faction, Evolution. Under their tutelage, the 24-year-old Orton became the youngest World Heavyweight Champion, and he only kept going from there. Not only did Orton cement himself as a “Legend Killer” by dispatching WWE’s most decorated in-ring veterans, he became the centerpiece of two more factions, Legacy and The Authority, all en route to unifying the WWE and World Heavyweight Titles to become the first WWE World Heavyweight Champion in history.\r\n\r\nWhich isn’t to say the two-time Royal Rumble Match winner is content with being known as a team player. You don’t get a name like The Apex Predator for being friendly, and Orton certainly does not play well with others. Friend and foe alike have felt the sting of his RKO or the boom of his dreaded punt, and well into his second decade as a WWE Superstar, there’s no telling what comes next.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[1287,2479],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":86,"storytelling":87,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":11,"matchLayout":88,"psychology":86,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":84,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":82,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":89,"mediaHandling":82,"brandBuilding":88,"socialMediaSavvy":79,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":84,"consistency":62,"awareness":86,"judgement":92},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-74","wrestlerId":74,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2002-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":75,"name":"Rey Mysterio","realName":"Rey Mysterio","picture":"Rey Mysterio.jpg","ability":62,"currentAbility":69,"potentialAbility":69,"charisma":77,"micSkills":67,"popularity":65,"condition":70,"hardcoreAbility":75,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":74,"height":160,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1974-12-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1989-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"great","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"He stands only 5-foot-6 and barely weighs 175 pounds, but a lack of size didn’t stop the incomparable Rey Mysterio from achieving giant dreams like capturing the WWE Championship or outlasting 29 other Superstars to win the Royal Rumble as the No. 2 entrant. Whether he was standing up to a dangerous giant like Kane or flying down from the top of a steel cage, The Ultimate Underdog is known for refusing to be intimidated inside ring.\r\n\r\nAfter taking a sabbatical from WWE, Mysterio made his jaw-dropping return as a surprise entrant in the 2018 Royal Rumble! Mysterio hasn't missed a beat since returning, as his edge-of-your seat matches against Andrade are already the stuff of legend. Now on Raw after the 2019 Superstar Shake-up, Mysterio has enjoyed a United States Title reign and had several thrilling matches against Andrade, Samoa Joe and even Brock Lesnar.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[1303,1422,1423,2341,2750,2775],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":83,"storytelling":84,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":18,"matchLayout":84,"psychology":83,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":66,"characterCoaching":82,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":82,"mediaHandling":82,"brandBuilding":83,"socialMediaSavvy":73,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":80,"awareness":83,"judgement":90},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-75","wrestlerId":75,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2020-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":76,"name":"Ron Killings","realName":"Ron Killings","picture":"Ron Killings.jpg","ability":55,"currentAbility":64,"potentialAbility":64,"charisma":53,"micSkills":64,"popularity":49,"condition":80,"hardcoreAbility":78,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":104,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1972-01-19T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1997-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"He was rowdy for a hot minute as K-Kwik during the Attitude Era. Then, after a WWE sabbatical, he came back stronger than ever as R-Truth. Then, when it seemed like he had his moment in the spotlight, Truth turned into a full-on maniac, ranting and raving against his invisible tormentor Little Jimmy and coming a hair away from a WWE World Heavyweight Championship. Then, Little Jimmy went away … only Truth came back again, winning a Tag Team Title with Kofi Kingston and heisting the Intercontinental Championship to set up a Ladder Match scramble at WrestleMania 31. Then, he danced his way to victory with Carmella in Mixed Match Challenge Season 2. Then, he captured his second United States Title. Then, he became one of the most entertaining and endearing 24/7 Champions in the title's young history. Then …  \r\n\r\nOK, you get the idea. Point is, you can never count R-Truth out. He’ll always come back, you’ll never expect it and you’ll certainly be glad that he did. Now that’s what’s up.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[909,911,1081,1148,1380,2777],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":76,"storytelling":76,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":14,"matchLayout":76,"psychology":76,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":67,"technicalCoaching":50,"characterCoaching":87,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":86,"mediaHandling":87,"brandBuilding":68,"socialMediaSavvy":84,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":67,"consistency":74,"awareness":76,"judgement":86},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-76","wrestlerId":76,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2025-06-07T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":77,"name":"Ryback","realName":"Ryback","picture":"Ryback.jpg","ability":52,"currentAbility":49,"potentialAbility":49,"charisma":35,"micSkills":48,"popularity":33,"condition":69,"hardcoreAbility":53,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":132,"height":187,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1981-07-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Crushing his opponents with palpable intensity, the 6-foot-3, 291-pound monster known as Ryback had the strength and focus of an android that was designed to annihilate.\r\n\r\nRyback approached every challenge with brute force and a no-nonsense demeanor that exuded supreme confidence in his abilities. Operating under the mantra of “start full, finish empty,” he didn’t just possess the skills to destroy a rival at any time. He carried himself as if that result was never in doubt and prepared himself immediately for an encore, hence his famous war cry of “Feed Me More.”\r\n\r\nThe behemoth proved his intimidating presence can make any competitor back down, from formidable toughmen like Mark Henry to living legends like John Cena. In 2015, after battling his way through WWE for three years, The Big Guy defeated five other competitors in an Elimination Chamber Match to earn his first title, the Intercontinental Championship.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1305],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":45,"storytelling":51,"productFit":78,"riskTaking":49,"matchLayout":53,"psychology":45,"workerManagement":78,"trainingIntensity":58,"technicalCoaching":20,"characterCoaching":70,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":51,"mediaHandling":70,"brandBuilding":80,"socialMediaSavvy":58,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":16,"reactionSpeed":58,"consistency":69,"awareness":45,"judgement":58}},{"id":79,"name":"Scott Armstrong","realName":"Scott Armstrong","picture":"Scott Armstrong.jpg","ability":73,"currentAbility":76,"potentialAbility":76,"charisma":78,"micSkills":69,"popularity":4,"condition":81,"hardcoreAbility":87,"injuryProne":100,"type":"referee","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":96,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1959-05-04T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1983-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Scott Armstrong is a retired American wrestler who works as a referee and a road agent. He was one half of Southern Boys alongside Tracy Smothers. He is best known for his work with WWE, WCW and IMPACT. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[2825],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":63,"storytelling":72,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":75,"psychology":63,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":71,"technicalCoaching":39,"characterCoaching":59,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":59,"brandBuilding":25,"socialMediaSavvy":53,"ruleKnowledge":76,"positioning":81,"reactionSpeed":71,"consistency":52,"awareness":63,"judgement":78}},{"id":81,"name":"Sgt. Slaughter","realName":"Sgt. Slaughter","picture":"Sgt Slaughter.jpg","ability":91,"currentAbility":87,"potentialAbility":87,"charisma":77,"micSkills":100,"popularity":18,"condition":73,"hardcoreAbility":100,"injuryProne":53,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":138,"height":195,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1948-08-27T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1972-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Robert Remus is a retired professional wrestler better known by the ring name Sgt. Slaughter. From the late 1970s to the early 1990s, Slaughter had success in the National Wrestling Alliance, American Wrestling Association, and World Wrestling Federation. In the 1980s, an alternate version of the Sgt. Slaughter character was incorporated into the G.I. Joe: A Real American Hero toy line as well as its animated series and comic books. Sgt. Slaughter held numerous regional titles early in his career and experienced his first major success in the National Wrestling Alliance (NWA) capturing the NWA World Tag Team Championship with Don Kernodle. During the late 1970s, Remus worked the American Wrestling Association (AWA) territory under a mask as Super Destroyer Mark II with managers Lord Alfred Hayes and Bobby Heenan. He is a 1 time WWF Champion.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3192],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":74,"storytelling":78,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":42,"matchLayout":79,"psychology":74,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":23,"technicalCoaching":23,"characterCoaching":70,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":58,"mediaHandling":70,"brandBuilding":65,"socialMediaSavvy":64,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":23,"consistency":14,"awareness":74,"judgement":84}},{"id":82,"name":"Shawn Michaels","realName":"Shawn Michaels","picture":"Shawn Michaels.jpg","ability":94,"currentAbility":95,"potentialAbility":95,"charisma":100,"micSkills":81,"popularity":64,"condition":62,"hardcoreAbility":100,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":102,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1965-07-22T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1984-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"A cocky, confident heartbreaker from San Antonio, Texas, HBK started off his career as one half of The Rockers and ended it in a classic match with The Undertaker at WrestleMania XXVI. Along the way, he won every major WWE title, two Royal Rumbles, entry into the WWE Hall of Fame and a reputation as The Icon, The Showstopper, The Main Event.\r\n\r\nHis days in the ring weren’t always glorious, though. After charming crowds as a Rocker in the ’90s, HBK infamously severed his partnership with Marty Jannetty by smashing his friend’s head through a window. And the notorious “Montreal Screwjob” of the 1997 Survivor Series involving his greatest rival, Bret “Hit Man” Hart, could have killed a lesser Superstar’s career. Instead, it only added to the allure of one of sports-entertainment’s most captivatingly flawed figures.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":65,"teams":[1021,1499,1549],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":90,"storytelling":93,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":15,"matchLayout":94,"psychology":90,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":65,"technicalCoaching":68,"characterCoaching":83,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":85,"mediaHandling":83,"brandBuilding":73,"socialMediaSavvy":81,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":65,"consistency":63,"awareness":90,"judgement":94},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-82","wrestlerId":82,"promotionId":65,"startDate":"2018-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":83,"name":"Sheamus","realName":"Sheamus","picture":"Sheamus.jpg","ability":70,"currentAbility":74,"potentialAbility":74,"charisma":64,"micSkills":61,"popularity":59,"condition":73,"hardcoreAbility":88,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"striker","gender":"M","weight":121,"height":190,"base":"UK","birthplace":"Ireland","dateOfBirth":"1978-01-28T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"With a red-hot temper that matches his fiery head of hair, Sheamus never backs down from a fight and has never been in one he didn’t think he could win. Hailing from Dublin, the ginger-headed juggernaut brings to the ring a ferocious offensive style that harkens to his noble and heroic Celtic ancestors. Whether by upbringing or by birthright, this modern-day Irish warrior was fated for combat.\r\n\r\nAnd what's a warrior without spoils from his many conquests? Sheamus can lay claim to being a four-time WWE World Heavyweight Champion, the 2010 King of the Ring, a two-time United States Champion, the winner of the 2012 Royal Rumble Match — an honor which paved the way for him to defeat Daniel Bryan in 18 seconds at WrestleMania to win the World Heavyweight Title — and the winner of the 2015 Money in the Bank contract.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1239,1316,3664],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":77,"storytelling":79,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":37,"matchLayout":79,"psychology":77,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":80,"technicalCoaching":54,"characterCoaching":73,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":63,"mediaHandling":73,"brandBuilding":75,"socialMediaSavvy":70,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":80,"consistency":85,"awareness":77,"judgement":86}},{"id":84,"name":"Stephanie McMahon","realName":"Stephanie McMahon","picture":"Stephanie McMahon.jpg","ability":14,"currentAbility":23,"potentialAbility":23,"charisma":14,"micSkills":13,"popularity":53,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":42,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"F","weight":65,"height":170,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1976-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Think sports-entertainment is a man’s world? Stephanie McMahon will make sure you think again.\r\n\r\nMr. McMahon’s only daughter, Stephanie has been bossing WWE’s most powerful men around since she was old enough to form coherent sentences. As one of the principal owners of WWE and the company's Chief Brand Officer, however, she does a lot more than just talk. She’s proven herself to be a force with which to be reckoned both in and out of the ring. After all, how many of CableFax’s \"Most Powerful Women in Cable” are also former Women’s Champions?\r\n\r\nBorn into the sports-entertainment industry, Stephanie first got in on the family business by modeling Rockers T-shirts in the WWE Shop catalog when she was still in middle school. By the time WWE’s “Attitude Era” had taken pop culture by storm, the youngest McMahon was caught up in a rivalry between her father’s Corporation and The Undertaker’s wicked Ministry of Darkness.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":32,"storytelling":33,"productFit":13,"riskTaking":48,"matchLayout":33,"psychology":32,"workerManagement":13,"trainingIntensity":35,"technicalCoaching":11,"characterCoaching":75,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":52,"mediaHandling":75,"brandBuilding":70,"socialMediaSavvy":70,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":3,"reactionSpeed":35,"consistency":49,"awareness":32,"judgement":24},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-84","wrestlerId":84,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2024-04-07T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-04-07T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-04-07T00:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":85,"name":"Steve Austin","realName":"Steve Austin","picture":"Steve Austin.jpg","ability":82,"currentAbility":79,"potentialAbility":79,"charisma":91,"micSkills":86,"popularity":73,"condition":48,"hardcoreAbility":61,"injuryProne":69,"type":"manager","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":114,"height":185,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1964-12-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1989-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"great","prestige":"high","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Proudly raising his middle fingers in the faces of everyone who dared oppose him, \"Stone Cold\" Steve Austin was the blue-collar warrior for the common man. Clad in jeans and black leather often soaked in beer foam, Austin was defiant, brash and dared anyone to try and tell him what to do. When the signature sound of shattering glass erupted throughout the arena, everyone there knew that it was time to raise hell. And if you happened to be on the receiving end, well, you have our sympathies.\r\n\r\nTrained by \"Gentleman\" Chris Adams, Steve Austin broke into the wrestling business in Texas in 1990, as part of the USWA. After a year, he moved on to WCW, where he won the WCW Television Championship under the name \"Stunning\" Steve Austin. An elbow injury led to his firing from WCW, but Austin found a lifeboat in ECW, and, with the freedom afforded him by Paul Heyman, began crafting a voice that would lead to superstardom in WWE.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1550],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":91,"storytelling":91,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":30,"matchLayout":91,"psychology":91,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":46,"technicalCoaching":38,"characterCoaching":89,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":70,"mediaHandling":89,"brandBuilding":76,"socialMediaSavvy":84,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":46,"consistency":53,"awareness":91,"judgement":95}},{"id":86,"name":"Steve Lombardi","realName":"Steve Lombardi","picture":"Steve Lombardi.jpg","ability":71,"currentAbility":81,"potentialAbility":81,"charisma":95,"micSkills":67,"popularity":13,"condition":53,"hardcoreAbility":92,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":109,"height":180,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1961-04-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1983-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Steve Lombardi is an Italian American professional wrestler and road agent. He is probably most known for his Brooklyn Brawler character - and losing streak! Lombardi began his WWF career in late 1983, competing under his real name, primarily as an enhancement talent, until early 1989, when he was repackaged as The Brooklyn Brawler. The Brawler character was that of a street fighter, wearing battered jeans and a torn New York Yankees t-shirts. Lombardi was used in a number of gimmicks, often under a mask. In late 1993 early 1996, he briefly replaced Matt Borne as Doink the Clown until Ray Apollo was hired. He also regularly portrayed Kim Chee (Kamala's handler) during his 1986-87 and 1992 stints with the WWF and briefly in 1993 as a singles wrestler after Kamala left him for the newly ordained Reverend Slick. He still regularly used the Brooklyn Brawler gimmick during this period.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":73,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":19,"matchLayout":77,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":27,"technicalCoaching":24,"characterCoaching":57,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":81,"mediaHandling":57,"brandBuilding":18,"socialMediaSavvy":42,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":27,"consistency":48,"awareness":62,"judgement":77}},{"id":87,"name":"Stu Bennett","realName":"Stu Bennett","picture":"Wade Barrett.jpg","ability":42,"currentAbility":35,"potentialAbility":35,"charisma":34,"micSkills":33,"popularity":35,"condition":76,"hardcoreAbility":26,"injuryProne":100,"type":"commentator","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":112,"height":198,"base":"UK","birthplace":"England","dateOfBirth":"1980-08-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Trained in bare-knuckle brawling on the mean streets of Preston, England, Wade Barrett brought strength, arrogance and cunning to the ring in equal measure. He was imbued with confidence and eloquence, character traits that propelled the cocky young Brit to the top ranks in WWE.\r\n\r\nAfter coming to WWE prominence as the winner of WWE NXT season one, Barrett proved he was not content merely to share the spotlight with his fellow Superstars. He wanted total control, and he’s willing to do whatever it takes to get it. Whether as the firebrand leader of not one, but two insurgent squads, or a lone fighter intent on delivering “Bad News” in the most painful form imaginable, Barrett proved himself to be one of the tougher specimens to ever set foot in a ring.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[1044],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":63,"storytelling":71,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":73,"psychology":63,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":81,"technicalCoaching":49,"characterCoaching":77,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":77,"brandBuilding":72,"socialMediaSavvy":61,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":81,"consistency":83,"awareness":63,"judgement":78},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-87","wrestlerId":87,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2022-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":89,"name":"Tanga Loa","realName":"Tanga Loa","picture":"Tanga Loa.jpg","ability":57,"currentAbility":50,"potentialAbility":50,"charisma":55,"micSkills":37,"popularity":38,"condition":69,"hardcoreAbility":58,"injuryProne":87,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":100,"height":185,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1983-05-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Tanga Loa is an American wrestler who works in America, Canada and Japan. He is a Middleweight who is classed as using a Powerhouse style. He is one half of Guerrillas of Destiny alongside Tama Tonga. He is best known for his work with WWE, NJPW, CMLL, IMPACT, NXT and NJoA.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1086,1497,1586,3027,3674,3974],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":52,"storytelling":54,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":55,"psychology":52,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":63,"technicalCoaching":35,"characterCoaching":54,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":54,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":44,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":63,"consistency":62,"awareness":52,"judgement":71}},{"id":90,"name":"Titus O'Neil","realName":"Titus O'Neil","picture":"Titus O'Neil.jpg","ability":36,"currentAbility":44,"potentialAbility":44,"charisma":59,"micSkills":44,"popularity":27,"condition":73,"hardcoreAbility":27,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":122,"height":195,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1977-04-29T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2009-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"One of the most imposing NXT Rookies on the show’s second season, “The Real Deal” saw his hard work paid off in early 2012, when then-General Manager John Laurinaitis formally placed O’Neil and his main man Darren Young on the SmackDown roster. Taking on the name of The Prime Time Players, Young and O’Neil set out to prove to the WWE Universe that they were worth the “millions of dollars” they said they were, capturing the Tag Team Championships in 2015 after resolving a conflict that had initially driven them apart.\r\n\r\nNot that the mind behind Titus Worldwide is simply a tag-team stalwart. The gridiron grappler has left his fair share of Superstars lying limp on the mat in singles competition as well, bringing the same intensity and passion to his charity commitments outside the ring. He even became the first-ever 24/7 Champion when the title was introduced in May 2019. A hell of a competitor and a hell of a humanitarian, it’s only a matter of time before the name on everyone’s lips i","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[1282,1719,1932],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":42,"storytelling":47,"productFit":50,"riskTaking":39,"matchLayout":49,"psychology":42,"workerManagement":50,"trainingIntensity":59,"technicalCoaching":22,"characterCoaching":72,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":61,"mediaHandling":72,"brandBuilding":63,"socialMediaSavvy":47,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":10,"reactionSpeed":59,"consistency":51,"awareness":42,"judgement":45},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-90","wrestlerId":90,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2014-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":91,"name":"The Miz","realName":"The Miz","picture":"The Miz.jpg","ability":58,"currentAbility":62,"potentialAbility":62,"charisma":54,"micSkills":55,"popularity":51,"condition":88,"hardcoreAbility":70,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":105,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1980-10-08T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2003-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"First introduced to TV audiences as one of the seven strangers on “The Real World: Back to New York,” The Miz parlayed his reality TV fame into a legitimate WWE career.\r\n\r\nMiz’s first taste of WWE cred came alongside John Morrison, as the duo won the WWE Tag Team Championship and the attention of WWE Universe on their WWE.com web series, “The Dirt Sheet.” The team was split up thanks to the 2009 WWE Draft, and many expected Miz to fade into obscurity. He proved everyone wrong, though, by winning the United States Championship, the Unified Tag Team Championship and several high-profile matches.\r\n\r\nThen in July 2010, Miz’s career hit a turning point. By winning the Raw Money in the Bank Ladder Match, the Ohio native guaranteed himself a chance to capture his ultimate goal — the WWE Championship.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[1319,1380,1466,1468,4267],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":75,"storytelling":75,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":8,"matchLayout":75,"psychology":75,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":78,"technicalCoaching":48,"characterCoaching":86,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":92,"mediaHandling":86,"brandBuilding":72,"socialMediaSavvy":80,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":78,"consistency":88,"awareness":75,"judgement":85},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-91","wrestlerId":91,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2005-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":92,"name":"The Undertaker","realName":"The Undertaker","picture":"Undertaker.jpg","ability":99,"currentAbility":99,"potentialAbility":99,"charisma":99,"micSkills":100,"popularity":74,"condition":36,"hardcoreAbility":100,"injuryProne":68,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":140,"height":205,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1965-03-24T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1984-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"great","prestige":"high","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"For three decades, The Undertaker loomed over the WWE landscape like a menacing shadow, spelling out doom for those who dared cross him. Imbued with seemingly mystical abilities and preternatural in-ring skill, The Deadman was a WWE great in a class by himself, and no list of legends would be complete without him.\r\n\r\nA multi-time WWE and World Heavyweight Champion, a six-time tag team titleholder and a Royal Rumble Match winner in 2007, Undertaker’s accomplishments in WWE have cemented his place among the greatest in the game. A true in-ring pioneer, he was part of many WWE firsts, including the first-ever Casket Match at Survivor Series 1992, the first-ever Buried Alive match in 1996 and the inaugural Hell in a Cell Match in October 1997.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[1400,1520],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":97,"storytelling":94,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":19,"matchLayout":93,"psychology":97,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":45,"technicalCoaching":37,"characterCoaching":81,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":81,"mediaHandling":81,"brandBuilding":75,"socialMediaSavvy":75,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":45,"consistency":45,"awareness":97,"judgement":98},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-92","wrestlerId":92,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"1990-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":93,"name":"Theodore Long","realName":"Theodore Long","picture":"Teddy Long.jpg","ability":53,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":55,"charisma":51,"micSkills":43,"popularity":28,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":64,"injuryProne":83,"type":"manager","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":73,"height":175,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1947-09-15T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1985-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Theodore R. \"Teddy\" Long is a former American professional wrestling referee and manager. Long started out as an errand boy for wrestlers Tommy Rich and Abdullah the Butcher. He eventually became a member of the ringcrew and was promoted to referee in the NWA's Jim Crockett Promotions in 1985 as Teddy Long. Shortly thereafter, Long began to turn into a villainous character when he started to bend the rules for heel wrestlers. On April 2, 1989 at Clash of the Champions VI in New Orleans, Long blatantly made a fast count allowing Mike Rotunda and \"Dr. Death\" Steve Williams to defeat the Road Warriors for the NWA World Tag Team Championship. After this match, the National Wrestling Alliance relieved Long of his refereeing duties. Long debuted in the WWF as a referee on the 21st December 1998 episode of Raw is War and stayed with that role until September 2002, when he was taken off the road.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":60,"storytelling":42,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":36,"psychology":60,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":30,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":78,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":78,"brandBuilding":43,"socialMediaSavvy":70,"ruleKnowledge":67,"positioning":54,"reactionSpeed":30,"consistency":0,"awareness":60,"judgement":36}},{"id":94,"name":"Jinder Mahal","realName":"Jinder Mahal","picture":"Jinder Mahal.jpg","ability":57,"currentAbility":54,"potentialAbility":54,"charisma":59,"micSkills":53,"popularity":38,"condition":83,"hardcoreAbility":39,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":108,"height":193,"base":"Canada","birthplace":"Canada","dateOfBirth":"1986-07-19T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Jinder Mahal is a Canadian wrestler who works in the USA, Canada, Mexico, the British Isles, Europe, Oceania and India. He is a 6'5\", 238lb worker who is classed as using a Entertainer style. He uses the Karachi Valley Driver and the Sands of Time as his finishers. He is best known for his work with WWE, NXT, AAA, BLP and WXM.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[914,915,2758,3068],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":58,"storytelling":59,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":28,"matchLayout":60,"psychology":58,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":68,"technicalCoaching":38,"characterCoaching":62,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":72,"mediaHandling":62,"brandBuilding":70,"socialMediaSavvy":58,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":68,"consistency":80,"awareness":58,"judgement":75}},{"id":95,"name":"TJ Wilson","realName":"TJ Wilson","picture":"Tyson Kidd.jpg","ability":91,"currentAbility":93,"potentialAbility":93,"charisma":85,"micSkills":100,"popularity":19,"condition":50,"hardcoreAbility":100,"injuryProne":98,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":93,"height":175,"base":"Canada","birthplace":"Canada","dateOfBirth":"1980-07-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1995-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Theodore James (TJ) Wilson, sometimes spelled T.J. Wilson, is a Canadian professional wrestler. The final graduate of the Hart Dungeon, Wilson wrestled internationally in several promotions such as Stampede Wrestling in 1995 to 2007. As the Stampede Kid he completed several tours of Japan, competing at New Japan Pro Wrestling. Wilson signed with World Wrestling Entertainment in November 2006 at the age of 26, after receiving impressive reviews from former WWE trainer Bill DeMott. He moved to WWE developmental territory Deep South Wrestling (DSW) in February 2007 with fellow signee and girlfriend Nattie Neidhart. Wilson made his WWE television debut on the February 10, 2009, episode of ECW on Sci Fi managed by real-life girlfriend Natalya, under the name Tyson Kidd.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[993,1063,1437,1509,3190],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":85,"storytelling":87,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":15,"matchLayout":87,"psychology":85,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":76,"characterCoaching":55,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":85,"mediaHandling":55,"brandBuilding":46,"socialMediaSavvy":39,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":76,"awareness":85,"judgement":91},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-95","wrestlerId":95,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2011-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":96,"name":"Trish Stratus","realName":"Trish Stratus","picture":"Trish Stratus.jpg","ability":58,"currentAbility":62,"potentialAbility":62,"charisma":47,"micSkills":71,"popularity":60,"condition":74,"hardcoreAbility":53,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"F","weight":57,"height":162,"base":"Canada","birthplace":"Canada","dateOfBirth":"1975-12-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Patricia Anne Stratigias, better known as Trish Stratus, is a former fitness model, former professional wrestler and television personality from Canada. After beginning her career as a fitness model, Stratus began working for World Wrestling Entertainment. Early in her career, she was involved in sexually themed storylines. As Stratus spent more time in the ring, her wrestling skills and popularity strengthened. Because of this, she was a one-time WWE Hardcore Champion, three-time \"WWE Babe of the Year\" and was proclaimed \"Diva of the Decade\". After nearly seven years in the business, Stratus retired from wrestling on September 17, 2006 after winning her seventh WWE Women's Championship, the most in WWE history.\r\n\r\nAside from professional wrestling, Stratus modeled for and appeared on numerous magazine covers and has been involved in charity work. She has also been the host of several award and television shows, including Stratusphere in 2008.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1546],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":75,"storytelling":76,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":77,"psychology":75,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":63,"technicalCoaching":53,"characterCoaching":79,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":79,"brandBuilding":83,"socialMediaSavvy":66,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":63,"consistency":63,"awareness":75,"judgement":85}},{"id":97,"name":"Seth Rollins","realName":"Seth Rollins","picture":"Seth Rollins.jpg","ability":84,"currentAbility":76,"potentialAbility":76,"charisma":83,"micSkills":64,"popularity":71,"condition":75,"hardcoreAbility":62,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":98,"height":185,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1986-05-28T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2005-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"great","prestige":"high","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"This is Seth Freaking Rollins. He’s really freaking good.\r\n\r\nDid you know that he beat Brock Lesnar for the Universal Title twice? Or that he’s the only man to cash in a Money in the Bank contract in the main event of WrestleMania? Or that he’s the only human being to ever hold the WWE Championship and United States Championship simultaneously?\r\n\r\nIf you didn't, it won’t be long until this hybrid athlete’s skills turn you into a believer. A veteran of the independent scene who sometimes seems more ninja than wrestler, Rollins set up shop as one of WWE’s on-the-spot history-makers from the second he walked in the door. From his reign as the first-ever NXT Champion to his vaunted time as The Architect of The Shield, Rollins’ first two years in WWE were a master class of evolution. Coincidentally enough, that’s the name of one of the factions he and his fellow Hounds of Justice managed to upend in their near-spotless two-year run throughout WWE’s ranks.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[32,1372,1503,2073,3450],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":84,"storytelling":85,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":85,"psychology":84,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":93,"technicalCoaching":75,"characterCoaching":78,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":78,"brandBuilding":78,"socialMediaSavvy":73,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":93,"consistency":84,"awareness":84,"judgement":90},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-97","wrestlerId":97,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2014-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":99,"name":"Alicia Fox","realName":"Alicia Fox","picture":"Alicia Fox.jpg","ability":63,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":53,"charisma":46,"micSkills":59,"popularity":8,"condition":81,"hardcoreAbility":48,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"F","weight":59,"height":172,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1986-06-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2006-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Victoria Crawford is an American model and professional wrestler best known by her ring name Alicia Fox. Crawford began her professional wrestling career in July 2006, where she signed a developmental contract with World Wrestling Entertainment, and was assigned to Ohio Valley Wrestling (OVW), WWE's developmental territory, where she won the OVW Women's Championship in October 2006. Crawford was later transferred to Florida Championship Wrestling (FCW) in September 2007. She soon debuted on the main roster in June 2008 with a wedding planner gimmick. As of 2013, she is the longest tenured diva currently in the WWE. In 2013, she joined forces with the charity Nothing But Nets to help fight against malaria.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":44,"storytelling":52,"productFit":50,"riskTaking":48,"matchLayout":55,"psychology":44,"workerManagement":50,"trainingIntensity":68,"technicalCoaching":48,"characterCoaching":72,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":52,"mediaHandling":72,"brandBuilding":52,"socialMediaSavvy":68,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":10,"reactionSpeed":68,"consistency":60,"awareness":44,"judgement":46}},{"id":100,"name":"Vince McMahon","realName":"Vince McMahon","picture":"Vince McMahon.jpg","ability":95,"currentAbility":95,"potentialAbility":95,"charisma":99,"micSkills":92,"popularity":71,"condition":38,"hardcoreAbility":100,"injuryProne":68,"type":"writer","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":110,"height":185,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1945-08-24T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1971-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"great","prestige":"high","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Vince McMahon is an American man who tends to stay behind the scenes in the wrestling world. He is best known for his work with WWE. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":90,"storytelling":78,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":42,"matchLayout":74,"psychology":90,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":18,"technicalCoaching":11,"characterCoaching":87,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":58,"mediaHandling":87,"brandBuilding":62,"socialMediaSavvy":82,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":18,"consistency":33,"awareness":90,"judgement":94}},{"id":102,"name":"Billy Gunn","realName":"Billy Gunn","picture":"Billy Gunn.jpg","ability":58,"currentAbility":62,"potentialAbility":62,"charisma":56,"micSkills":58,"popularity":37,"condition":66,"hardcoreAbility":68,"injuryProne":84,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":121,"height":190,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1963-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1993-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Billy Gunn can do it all.\r\n\r\nThe 6-foot-3, 260-pound phenomenon from Orlando, Fla. is a freakish athlete who can bust out a dropkick with textbook precision and hoist an opponent over his head with animal-like strength. He's charismatic, too. A cocky, in-your-face outlaw, Billy rocked with The Honky Tonk Man, threw a lasso as a Smoking Gunn and broke it down with D-Generation X en route to a whopping 11 Tag Team Title reigns and the 1999 King of the Ring crown.\r\n\r\nGunn’s career reached its peak when he returned to the tag division alongside Road Dogg. A fellow frustrated Superstar, the one-time Roadie convinced Rockabilly to abandon his outdated persona and embrace his inner outlaw. By themselves, the competitors were relative nobodies in WWE. Together, they became brash members of DX, five-time World Tag Team Champions and the most popular duo of WWE’s Attitude Era.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[1024,1103,1246,1320,1560,2072,3099],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":73,"storytelling":76,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":15,"matchLayout":77,"psychology":73,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":55,"technicalCoaching":42,"characterCoaching":58,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":85,"mediaHandling":58,"brandBuilding":67,"socialMediaSavvy":53,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":55,"consistency":54,"awareness":73,"judgement":84},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-102","wrestlerId":102,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2019-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":103,"name":"Sean Waltman","realName":"Sean Waltman","picture":"Sean Waltman_alt3.jpg","ability":66,"currentAbility":61,"potentialAbility":61,"charisma":51,"micSkills":63,"popularity":34,"condition":73,"hardcoreAbility":46,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":96,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1972-07-13T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1992-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Sean Michael Waltman is an American professional wrestler. Waltman is best known for his appearances with the World Wrestling Federation under the ring names 1-2-3 Kid and X-Pac, World Championship Wrestling under the ring name Syxx and Total Nonstop Action Wrestling under the ring name Syxx-Pac. Waltman has wrestled on the independent circuit under both his real name and the ring name 6-Pac. He was also contracted to MTV's Wrestling Society X. Waltman was also part of the backstage group of wrestlers known as The Kliq. He is also known for his tumultuous relationship with fellow wrestler Chyna, with whom he made a sex tape. Waltman is the only wrestler in history to have held TNA X Division Championship, WCW Cruiserweight Championship & WWF Light Heavyweight Championship. He is considered one of the pioneers of high-risk, high-flying professional wrestling.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1024,1131,2799],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":59,"storytelling":70,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":73,"psychology":59,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":65,"technicalCoaching":54,"characterCoaching":67,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":67,"brandBuilding":60,"socialMediaSavvy":58,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":65,"consistency":62,"awareness":59,"judgement":75}},{"id":104,"name":"Abyss","realName":"Abyss","picture":"Abyss.jpg","ability":94,"currentAbility":90,"potentialAbility":90,"charisma":98,"micSkills":94,"popularity":28,"condition":51,"hardcoreAbility":72,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"striker","gender":"M","weight":159,"height":200,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1973-10-04T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1995-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Christopher J. \"Chris\" Parks, better known by his ring name \"The Monster\" Abyss, is an American professional wrestler. Chris Parks was trained by Roger Ruffin of the Northern Wrestling Federation (NWF). He won his debut match by disqualification. For the first few years of his career, Parks worked in the NWF as the Original Terminator, Chris Justice, and then Prince Justice. As Abyss in TNA, Parks became a former NWA World Heavyweight Champion, being the first of only two men to hold the title while competing under a mask. Abyss is the heaviest wrestler to hold the X Division Championship. He also captured the Television Championship once and the NWA World Tag Team Championship once with A.J. Styles. With having won all the required championships, Abyss was the fourth man to complete the Triple Crown Championship and the second to complete the Grand Slam Championship. Parks also currently makes appearances in TNA as Abyss' storyline brother Joseph Park.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":80,"storytelling":80,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":28,"matchLayout":80,"psychology":80,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":59,"technicalCoaching":35,"characterCoaching":70,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":72,"mediaHandling":70,"brandBuilding":61,"socialMediaSavvy":63,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":59,"consistency":65,"awareness":80,"judgement":88},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-104","wrestlerId":104,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2019-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":105,"name":"AJ Styles","realName":"AJ Styles","picture":"AJ Styles.jpg","ability":100,"currentAbility":93,"potentialAbility":93,"charisma":99,"micSkills":100,"popularity":63,"condition":75,"hardcoreAbility":94,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":99,"height":177,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1977-06-02T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-02-15T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"AJ Styles is a retired American wrestler who works primarily as a road agent. He is best known for his work with WWE, NJPW, WCW, TNA, NXT and ROH. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business. He has been voted Male Wrestler Of The Year two times.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[1056,1151,1339,1340,2391],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":86,"storytelling":87,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":14,"matchLayout":88,"psychology":86,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":85,"technicalCoaching":79,"characterCoaching":73,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":86,"mediaHandling":73,"brandBuilding":73,"socialMediaSavvy":66,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":85,"consistency":79,"awareness":86,"judgement":92},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-105","wrestlerId":105,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2016-01-24T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":106,"name":"Al Snow","realName":"Al Snow","picture":"Al Snow.jpg","ability":60,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"charisma":44,"micSkills":53,"popularity":9,"condition":55,"hardcoreAbility":68,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":107,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1963-07-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1982-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Allen Ray Sarven is a retired professional wrestler and actor better known by his ring name of Al Snow. He is best known for his work in Extreme Championship Wrestling and World Wrestling Entertainment. After a tour of Japan, Sarven wrestled a match in Michigan against Sabu, an Extreme Championship Wrestling (ECW) regular, who suggested he try ECW. From 1995-1997, Snow was also running a wrestling gym called \"Body Slammers\" in Lima, Ohio hiring D'Lo Brown as an assistant trainer. Sarven began working for the World Wrestling Federation (WWF) when he signed a contract in August 1995. Sarven wrestled under numerous gimmicks in the WWF. Sarven found success back in ECW, billed once again as Al Snow in 1997. Sarven was then recalled to the WWF in 1998 where he continued his gimmick of talking to \"Head,\" creating some of the more memorable humorous skits of \"The Attitude Era\" including fighting himself in a hardcore match. In March 2010 Sarven received a tryout as an agent for TNA Wrestling.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1478,3355],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":74,"storytelling":77,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":24,"matchLayout":78,"psychology":74,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":44,"technicalCoaching":38,"characterCoaching":70,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":76,"mediaHandling":70,"brandBuilding":48,"socialMediaSavvy":65,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":44,"consistency":37,"awareness":74,"judgement":84}},{"id":107,"name":"Alex Silva","realName":"Alex Silva","picture":"alex silva.jpg","ability":53,"currentAbility":45,"potentialAbility":45,"charisma":32,"micSkills":52,"popularity":6,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":62,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"striker","gender":"M","weight":91,"height":180,"base":"Canada","birthplace":"Canada","dateOfBirth":"1990-01-23T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Alexandre Freitas is a is a Canadian/Portuguese professional wrestler. After being trained by his father, Freitas debuted in 2004 for Paul LeDuc's FLQ promotion. Initially, Freitas adopted the ring name Sean Simmons, but soon began wrestling under the name Alex Silva. Silva made his Ohio Valley Wrestling (OVW) debut on November 17, 2010. On December 11, Silva won the OVW Television Championship by defeating Mohamad Ali Vaez. His victory made him the youngest Television Champion in the promotion's history. On the April 26, 2012, episode of Impact Wrestling, Silva made his televised TNA debut in a losing effort to Robbie E as part of the TNA Gut Check. On the following week's episode, Al Snow, Bruce Prichard and Ric Flair voted to give Silva a TNA contract after he cut a promo and he became part of the official roster.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[587,2821],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":38,"storytelling":45,"productFit":60,"riskTaking":44,"matchLayout":47,"psychology":38,"workerManagement":60,"trainingIntensity":84,"technicalCoaching":44,"characterCoaching":36,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":56,"mediaHandling":36,"brandBuilding":51,"socialMediaSavvy":36,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":12,"reactionSpeed":84,"consistency":49,"awareness":38,"judgement":47}},{"id":108,"name":"Madison Rayne","realName":"Madison Rayne","picture":"Madison Rayne.jpg","ability":69,"currentAbility":78,"potentialAbility":78,"charisma":83,"micSkills":88,"popularity":20,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":90,"injuryProne":100