,"prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Jessica Kresa is an American professional wrestler better known as ODB (short for One Dirty Bitch). Kresa's athletic background is in ice hockey, which her father encouraged her to pursue. She began watching professional wrestling as a child. She enjoyed watching wrestlers such as The Killer Bees. Kresa got her start when she tried out for the first season of the World Wrestling Federation's reality show, WWF Tough Enough. She made the top 25, but missed the final cut for the show. On June 5, 2006, Kresa debuted in Ohio Valley Wrestling as a villain under the ring name ODB. Kresa was contacted by Total Nonstop Action Wrestling to appear at their annual pay-per-view Bound for Glory. She made her in-ring re-debut at Bound for Glory, participating in a 10 Knockout Gauntlet to crown the first-ever Knockout Champion.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":55,"storytelling":59,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":17,"matchLayout":60,"psychology":55,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":69,"technicalCoaching":46,"characterCoaching":78,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":83,"mediaHandling":78,"brandBuilding":42,"socialMediaSavvy":63,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":69,"consistency":67,"awareness":55,"judgement":73}},{"id":152,"name":"Gunner","realName":"Gunner","picture":"Gunner.jpg","ability":53,"currentAbility":48,"potentialAbility":48,"charisma":45,"micSkills":56,"popularity":14,"condition":71,"hardcoreAbility":58,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":111,"height":185,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1982-06-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2001-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Chad Lail is an American professional wrestler better known by the ring name Gunner. In TNA, Lail was a member of the Immortal stable and a former one-time TNA Television Champion. In addition to wrestling for TNA, Lail also performs for various promotions on the independent circuit under the ring name Phill Shatter. After serving in the Iraq War, Phill Shatter signed with NWA Anarchy along with fellow Iraq War veteran Truitt Fields. Shatter appeared at Ring of Honor's The Big Bang! pay-per-view on April 3, 2010. At the June 23, 2010, tapings of TNA's Impact! television show, Shatter made his TNA debut, along with Mikael Judas, as TNA's on-air security. On the July 29, 2010 edition of TNA Impact! taping, Shatter, now using the name Gunner and Mikael Judas, using the name Murphy, came out after an altercation involving Jeff Hardy and Mr. Anderson with Matt Morgan, and attacked Hardy and Anderson.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1334,2337,2755],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":46,"storytelling":49,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":33,"matchLayout":50,"psychology":46,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":56,"technicalCoaching":33,"characterCoaching":45,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":67,"mediaHandling":45,"brandBuilding":69,"socialMediaSavvy":36,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":56,"consistency":61,"awareness":46,"judgement":68}},{"id":153,"name":"Robbie E","realName":"Robbie E","picture":"Rob Eckos.jpg","ability":26,"currentAbility":29,"potentialAbility":29,"charisma":32,"micSkills":29,"popularity":19,"condition":85,"hardcoreAbility":28,"injuryProne":100,"type":"commentator","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":91,"height":177,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1983-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Rob Eckos is an American wrestler who works in America and Canada. He is a Lightweight who is classed as using a Entertainer style. He is best known for his work with NXT, IMPACT, NOAH and GCW. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":65,"teams":[1399,2818],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":66,"storytelling":68,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":19,"matchLayout":68,"psychology":66,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":63,"technicalCoaching":51,"characterCoaching":70,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":81,"mediaHandling":70,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":63,"consistency":71,"awareness":66,"judgement":80},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-153","wrestlerId":153,"promotionId":65,"startDate":"2019-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"inDevelopment":true},{"id":155,"name":"Rob Van Dam","realName":"Rob Van Dam","picture":"Rob Van Dam.jpg","ability":73,"currentAbility":65,"potentialAbility":65,"charisma":73,"micSkills":61,"popularity":38,"condition":65,"hardcoreAbility":71,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":107,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1970-12-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1989-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Who has two thumbs, scored a historic WWE Championship win in New York City and is perhaps the most popular ECW icon of all time? Say it with him now: “Rob! Van! Dam!”\r\n\r\nWhen the chilled out martial artist from Battle Creek, Mich. broke into ECW in 1996, he made an impact like few grapplers ever have. Trained alongside future partner and rival Sabu by Sabu’s uncle, The Original Sheik, RVD had the sound fundamentals needed to thrive in the Land of Extreme. Van Dam’s laidback demeanor directly contradicted his agility in the squared circle, which made him an instant favorite among the Philadelphia faithful. He quickly scored victories over Axl Rotten, Mikey Whipwreck and Sabu, but it was his partnership with the latter that launched The Whole Dam Show to a new level.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1130,1303,1304,3281,3282,3283],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":68,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":40,"matchLayout":70,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":58,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":78,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":60,"mediaHandling":78,"brandBuilding":61,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":58,"consistency":68,"awareness":62,"judgement":77}},{"id":156,"name":"Bobby Roode","realName":"Bobby Roode","picture":"Bobby Roode.jpg","ability":96,"currentAbility":89,"potentialAbility":89,"charisma":85,"micSkills":82,"popularity":37,"condition":71,"hardcoreAbility":87,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":107,"height":182,"base":"Canada","birthplace":"Canada","dateOfBirth":"1976-05-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Wherever Robert Roode goes, he makes sure everyone knows of his “glorious” ambitions.\r\n\r\nAlready a world-renowned Superstar by the time he joined NXT in July 2016, Roode promised from the beginning to bring the brand to new heights. He backed up his talk when he defeated Shinsuke Nakamura at TakeOver: San Antonio to win the NXT Championship, beginning an eight-month reign.\r\n\r\nHaving reached the peak of NXT, Roode turned his sights on WWE's main roster. Roode signed with SmackDown LIVE in the hopes of making Team Blue a little more glorious and immediately started a rivalry with Dolph Ziggler before capturing the vacant United States Championship in a tournament. Then, in the 2018 Superstar Shake-up, Roode came to Raw and won the Raw Tag Team Titles alongside Chad Gable.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[945,1026,1357,1845,1965],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":77,"storytelling":79,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":11,"matchLayout":80,"psychology":77,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":76,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":73,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":89,"mediaHandling":73,"brandBuilding":75,"socialMediaSavvy":72,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":76,"consistency":80,"awareness":77,"judgement":86},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-156","wrestlerId":156,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2016-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":157,"name":"Samoa Joe","realName":"Samoa Joe","picture":"Samoa Joe.jpg","ability":65,"currentAbility":75,"potentialAbility":75,"charisma":60,"micSkills":90,"popularity":50,"condition":65,"hardcoreAbility":84,"injuryProne":96,"type":"wrestler","style":"submission","gender":"M","weight":127,"height":180,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1979-03-17T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"A world-traveled veteran of the mat game, the 282-pound Samoa Joe has used a blistering, MMA-inspired offense to rack up championships in top promotions across the globe. Before he ever set foot in WWE, Samoa Joe had already thrown down with the likes of John Cena, Daniel Bryan, Seth Rollins and Cesaro throughout his storied career.\r\n\r\nStill, despite his pedigree, the thought of Samoa Joe entering a WWE ring seemed to be relegated to the imaginations of fantasy matchmakers worldwide. Yet, after barreling through WWE NXT and twice capturing the NXT Title, Joe officially signed to Monday Night Raw in 2017 and has since unleashed his vicious squared circle philosophy on Raw and SmackDown LIVE against opponents like AJ Styles, Roman Reigns, and even Brock Lesnar.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[107,113,1015,2822,3644],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":80,"storytelling":81,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":24,"matchLayout":81,"psychology":80,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":64,"characterCoaching":80,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":76,"mediaHandling":80,"brandBuilding":72,"socialMediaSavvy":78,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":65,"awareness":80,"judgement":88},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-157","wrestlerId":157,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2022-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":158,"name":"Shawn Hernandez","realName":"Shawn Hernandez","picture":"Shawn Hernandez_alt.jpg","ability":47,"currentAbility":56,"potentialAbility":56,"charisma":41,"micSkills":60,"popularity":12,"condition":74,"hardcoreAbility":52,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"striker","gender":"M","weight":129,"height":185,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1973-02-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1996-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Shawn Hernandez is an American wrestler who works exclusively in North America. He is a Heavyweight who is classed as using a Brawler style. He is best known for his work with AAA, IMPACT, NWA, AJPW, ROH, MLW, IWRG, ZERO1, Lucha Ungrnd and IWA-MS. He was one half of the Tag Team Of The Year in 2006.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[997,1152,1233],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":54,"storytelling":59,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":41,"matchLayout":61,"psychology":54,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":64,"technicalCoaching":36,"characterCoaching":60,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":59,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":64,"socialMediaSavvy":48,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":64,"consistency":79,"awareness":54,"judgement":72}},{"id":159,"name":"DJ Z","realName":"DJ Z","picture":"Zema Ion.jpg","ability":62,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"charisma":64,"micSkills":61,"popularity":26,"condition":77,"hardcoreAbility":50,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":77,"height":167,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1986-10-05T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Joaquin Wilde used to literally light up the room when he made his entrance, at least until he turned to the dark side and Legado del Fantasma.\r\n\r\nAlthough Wilde’s talent is undeniable, that doesn’t mean his path to NXT was always a sure bet. While wrestling in Mexico in 2017, two years before inking a contract with NXT, Wilde suffered a ruptured colon and internal bleeding during a match. The injury threatened to not only end his career just as it was reaching full bloom, but his life. Miraculously, he pulled through, and being the fighter that he is, Wilde returned from the setback stronger than before.\r\n\r\nWilde’s resilience isn’t surprising, considering his upbringing. Raised by a single mother who emigrated from the Philippines, Wilde witnessed firsthand what it means to make sacrifices and overcome hardship.\r\n\r\n","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[1755,2161],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":55,"storytelling":62,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":64,"psychology":55,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":60,"characterCoaching":60,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":47,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":68,"awareness":55,"judgement":73},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-159","wrestlerId":159,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2019-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":160,"name":"SoCal Val","realName":"SoCal Val","picture":"So Cal Val.jpg","ability":36,"currentAbility":30,"potentialAbility":30,"charisma":28,"micSkills":29,"popularity":6,"condition":93,"hardcoreAbility":25,"injuryProne":96,"type":"commentator","style":"all rounder","gender":"F","weight":52,"height":167,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1986-03-27T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"SoCal Val is an American woman who works as a colour commentator, a manager and an on-screen personality. She is best known for her work with IMPACT and SHINE.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":44,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":23,"storytelling":28,"productFit":30,"riskTaking":54,"matchLayout":29,"psychology":23,"workerManagement":30,"trainingIntensity":44,"technicalCoaching":16,"characterCoaching":61,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":46,"mediaHandling":61,"brandBuilding":48,"socialMediaSavvy":55,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":6,"reactionSpeed":44,"consistency":33,"awareness":23,"judgement":26},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-160","wrestlerId":160,"promotionId":44,"startDate":"2022-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":161,"name":"Sonjay Dutt","realName":"Sonjay Dutt","picture":"Sonjay Dutt.jpg","ability":90,"currentAbility":84,"potentialAbility":84,"charisma":82,"micSkills":87,"popularity":18,"condition":80,"hardcoreAbility":70,"injuryProne":98,"type":"writer","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":88,"height":170,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1982-04-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Sonjay Dutt, a 2000 graduate of the The Monster Factory, is an American wrestler who works in America, Canada and India. He is a Small worker who is classed as using a High Flyer style. He is best known for his work with WWE, CMLL, AEW, IMPACT, ROH, MLW, ZERO1, AIW, IWA-MS, CHIKARA and CZW. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[1172,2746,2747],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":67,"storytelling":71,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":36,"matchLayout":73,"psychology":67,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":50,"characterCoaching":68,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":64,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":44,"socialMediaSavvy":59,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":56,"awareness":67,"judgement":80},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-161","wrestlerId":161,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2021-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":162,"name":"Sting","realName":"Sting","picture":"Sting.jpg","ability":55,"currentAbility":62,"potentialAbility":62,"charisma":62,"micSkills":50,"popularity":61,"condition":55,"hardcoreAbility":51,"injuryProne":81,"type":"wrestler","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":114,"height":187,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1959-03-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1985-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Often dubbed “The Franchise of WCW,” the man called Sting is one of the most recognizable and unique faces in sports-entertainment history. It was that distinction that made him the backbone of the Atlanta-based organization throughout the late 1980s until the end of WCW in 2001. It would be Triple H's protege, Seth Rollins, who would next face off against the face-painted legend at Night of Champions. The two would battle for the WWE World Heavyweight Championship with Rollins squeaking by with a roll-up on The Stinger. Though The Stinger often likes to say \"the only thing sure about Sting is that nothing is for sure,\" there is one thing nobody can deny - that Sting has had a Hall of Fame-worthy career. That will be confirmed on the eve of WrestleMania 32, when he joins the WWE Hall of Fame as a member of the Class of 2016.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1332,2595],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":88,"storytelling":89,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":16,"matchLayout":89,"psychology":88,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":57,"technicalCoaching":30,"characterCoaching":85,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":84,"mediaHandling":85,"brandBuilding":78,"socialMediaSavvy":76,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":57,"consistency":67,"awareness":88,"judgement":93}},{"id":163,"name":"Taeler Hendrix","realName":"Taeler Hendrix","picture":"Taeler Hendrix.jpg","ability":38,"currentAbility":42,"potentialAbility":42,"charisma":50,"micSkills":28,"popularity":2,"condition":81,"hardcoreAbility":36,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"F","weight":57,"height":167,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1989-06-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Taeler Conrad-Mellen is an American professional wrestler and valet. Starting her career in 2008, she spent her first years working on the independent circuit for promotions including New England Championship Wrestling (NECW), Top Rope Promotions (TRP) and World Women's Wrestling (WWW), before being signed to a contract by Ohio Valley Wrestling (OVW), a Total Nonstop Action Wrestling (TNA) developmental territory, in 2011. In November 2011, Hendrix won the OVW Women's Championship, holding the championship for 203 days. Hendrix cites Tara, Sensational Sherri, Velvet McIntyre and her favorite male wrestlers are Curt Hennig and Chris Jericho.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3388],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":49,"storytelling":51,"productFit":57,"riskTaking":37,"matchLayout":51,"psychology":49,"workerManagement":57,"trainingIntensity":55,"technicalCoaching":34,"characterCoaching":69,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":63,"mediaHandling":69,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":11,"reactionSpeed":55,"consistency":51,"awareness":49,"judgement":52}},{"id":164,"name":"Velvet Sky","realName":"Velvet Sky","picture":"Velvet Sky.jpg","ability":19,"currentAbility":25,"potentialAbility":25,"charisma":26,"micSkills":39,"popularity":16,"condition":67,"hardcoreAbility":20,"injuryProne":100,"type":"commentator","style":"all rounder","gender":"F","weight":57,"height":162,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1981-06-02T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2003-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Velvet Sky is a retired American wrestler who works as a colour commentator and a manager. She was one half of Team T&A alongside April Hunter. She is best known for her work with AAA, IMPACT, ROH and NWA.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1383,1384,3335],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":58,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":30,"matchLayout":59,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":63,"technicalCoaching":48,"characterCoaching":77,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":70,"mediaHandling":77,"brandBuilding":63,"socialMediaSavvy":65,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":63,"consistency":65,"awareness":56,"judgement":74}},{"id":165,"name":"Taz","realName":"Taz","picture":"Taz.jpg","ability":72,"currentAbility":63,"potentialAbility":63,"charisma":66,"micSkills":77,"popularity":25,"condition":57,"hardcoreAbility":43,"injuryProne":68,"type":"commentator","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":109,"height":172,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1967-10-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1987-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Taz is a retired American wrestler who works as a colour commentator, a manager and an on-screen personality. He is best known for his work with WWE, NJPW, AEW, IMPACT and ECW. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business. He was voted Manager Of The Year in 2020.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":81,"storytelling":86,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":32,"matchLayout":87,"psychology":81,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":42,"technicalCoaching":44,"characterCoaching":69,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":68,"mediaHandling":69,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":61,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":42,"consistency":55,"awareness":81,"judgement":89},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-165","wrestlerId":165,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2020-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":166,"name":"Wes Brisco","realName":"Wes Brisco","picture":"Wes Brisco.jpg","ability":35,"currentAbility":45,"potentialAbility":45,"charisma":38,"micSkills":32,"popularity":2,"condition":94,"hardcoreAbility":54,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":102,"height":175,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1983-02-21T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2009-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Wes Brisco is an American professional wrestler. He is a member of the Brisco wrestling family; the son of former Championship Wrestling from Florida mainstay Gerald Brisco and the nephew of former NWA World Heavyweight Champion Jack Brisco. Brisco signed a developmental contract with World Wrestling Entertainment in 2009 and was sent to Florida Championship Wrestling for further training. After being released from WWE, Brisco started wrestling in the independent circuit, primarily in Florida. Brisco debuted on independent circuit at Florida Underground Wrestling, on October 14 2011. Brisco made his Total Nonstop Action Wrestling debut on the October 11, 2012, episode Impact Wrestling, in a backstage segment with Kurt Angle. On the January 31 episode of Impact Wrestling, Brisco and Bischoff revealed themselves as members of Aces & Eights and attacked Kurt Angle, turning heel in the process.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":35,"storytelling":40,"productFit":65,"riskTaking":26,"matchLayout":42,"psychology":35,"workerManagement":65,"trainingIntensity":65,"technicalCoaching":36,"characterCoaching":26,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":74,"mediaHandling":26,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":21,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":13,"reactionSpeed":65,"consistency":63,"awareness":35,"judgement":47}},{"id":167,"name":"William Regal","realName":"William Regal","picture":"William Regal.jpg","ability":92,"currentAbility":97,"potentialAbility":97,"charisma":100,"micSkills":83,"popularity":43,"condition":50,"hardcoreAbility":98,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":110,"height":187,"base":"UK","birthplace":"England","dateOfBirth":"1968-05-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1983-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"As a teenager, Regal traveled the roads of his native United Kingdom, wrestling fellow grapplers, as well as complete strangers out of the crowd, as part of a touring carnival act. Here, he fostered a reputation as a lethal opponent whose crushing submissions and stiff strikes could render even the heartiest adversaries totally helpless. Regal diversified his abilities by traveling the world, mastering different styles and winning championships in Europe, the Middle East and Japan.\r\n\r\nAfter finding further success in WCW, Regal carved a tremendous legacy in WWE, winning numerous championships and accolades worthy of such a competitor, including the mantle of Raw General Manager in 2007. Arguably his crowning achievement, however, was when he became truly regal, winning the prestigious 2008 King of the Ring Tournament.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":65,"teams":[169,2832,2833],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":93,"storytelling":93,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":8,"matchLayout":93,"psychology":93,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":76,"characterCoaching":80,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":92,"mediaHandling":80,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":86,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":68,"awareness":93,"judgement":96},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-167","wrestlerId":167,"promotionId":65,"startDate":"2023-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"inDevelopment":true},{"id":171,"name":"Taryn Terrell","realName":"Taryn Terrell","picture":"Taryn Terrell.jpg","ability":62,"currentAbility":52,"potentialAbility":52,"charisma":51,"micSkills":39,"popularity":8,"condition":82,"hardcoreAbility":50,"injuryProne":100,"type":"manager","style":"all rounder","gender":"F","weight":57,"height":165,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1985-12-28T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Taryn Terrell is a retired American wrestler who works primarily as a manager. She is best known for her work with WWE, IMPACT and NWA.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1391],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":51,"storytelling":57,"productFit":44,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":59,"psychology":51,"workerManagement":44,"trainingIntensity":58,"technicalCoaching":48,"characterCoaching":74,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":74,"brandBuilding":73,"socialMediaSavvy":71,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":9,"reactionSpeed":58,"consistency":64,"awareness":51,"judgement":48}},{"id":172,"name":"TJP","realName":"TJP","picture":"TJ Perkins.jpg","ability":64,"currentAbility":66,"potentialAbility":66,"charisma":65,"micSkills":78,"popularity":33,"condition":83,"hardcoreAbility":68,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":79,"height":175,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1984-09-03T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"The flashy TJP broke into wrestling as a teenager, traveling throughout California and Mexico to sharpen his skills. He went on to hone his craft further at the Los Angeles dojo of New Japan Pro Wrestling along with Daniel Bryan and Shinsuke Nakamura, among others. After becoming the youngest American to compete for NJPW, TJP continued to travel around the world and establish himself as one of the preeminent grapplers on the planet.\r\n\r\nTJP backed up his swagger in the squared circle with top-notch technical wrestling, which helped him shock the world by defeating tournament favorite Kota Ibushi on his way to winning the inaugural Cruiserweight Classic and becoming the first WWE Cruiserweight Champion.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":5,"teams":[2159,3640,3882,4274,4275],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":75,"storytelling":78,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":79,"psychology":75,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":80,"technicalCoaching":75,"characterCoaching":64,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":64,"brandBuilding":48,"socialMediaSavvy":51,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":80,"consistency":70,"awareness":75,"judgement":85},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-172","wrestlerId":172,"promotionId":5,"startDate":"2026-01-17T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2028-01-17T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2028-01-17T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":173,"name":"Brodie Lee","realName":"Brodie Lee","picture":"Brodie Lee.jpg","ability":68,"currentAbility":65,"potentialAbility":65,"charisma":78,"micSkills":71,"popularity":43,"condition":83,"hardcoreA