4,"charisma":83,"micSkills":73,"popularity":61,"condition":82,"hardcoreAbility":84,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"striker","gender":"M","weight":120,"height":177,"base":"Canada","birthplace":"Canada","dateOfBirth":"1984-05-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Kevin Owens is an outspoken, Quebec-born brawler who bolts around the ring with equal parts grace and bad intentions. \r\n\r\nLauded by The Rock and possessing what WWE Hall of Famer “Stone Cold” Steve Austin described as a “hell of an arsenal,” Owens earned many accolades in North America and abroad.\r\n\r\nKO became a man of the people when he engaged in an epic struggle with Shane McMahon, and Owens prevailed when he defeated Shane-O-Mac in a Ladder Match during the premiere of Friday Night SmackDown to earn the right to fire his rival! Owens kept rolling when he was selected by Raw in the 2019 WWE Draft, immediately engaging in a heated rivalry with Seth Rollins and defeating him at WrestleMania in a match that saw KO come crashing down on Rollins after taking an awe-inspiring leap from the top of the WrestleMania sign!\r\n\r\nNow that he's back on SmackDown as a result of the 2020 WWE Draft, KO will be looking to dole out Stunners and fight his way to the top of the blue brand.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[1040,1114,1256,1330,1360,1744,2761,3450],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":81,"storytelling":82,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":82,"psychology":81,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":79,"technicalCoaching":64,"characterCoaching":83,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":83,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":85,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":79,"consistency":83,"awareness":81,"judgement":89},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-257","wrestlerId":257,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2014-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":258,"name":"Kyle O'Reilly","realName":"Kyle O'Reilly","picture":"Kyle OReilly.jpg","ability":61,"currentAbility":69,"potentialAbility":69,"charisma":84,"micSkills":82,"popularity":37,"condition":75,"hardcoreAbility":86,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":91,"height":177,"base":"Canada","birthplace":"Canada","dateOfBirth":"1987-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2005-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Kyle O’Reilly wants to shock the system of NXT, and with Roderick Strong, Adam Cole and Bobby Fish as his allies, he’s well on his way to reaching that goal. O’Reilly, Strong, Cole and Fish constitute the alliance known as The Undisputed ERA, a lawless outfit that has wreaked havoc in NXT since their emergence in August 2017. Employing a wolf pack mentality, the group has attacked everyone from Drew McIntyre to SAnitY, destabilizing the entire black-and-yellow-brand in the process. Causing carnage, however, isn’t a new trait for O’Reilly. Even prior to joining NXT, he carved out a niche as one of the ring’s most well-versed and dangerous competitors. With a background that spans Brazilian jiu-jitsu, kickboxing and other martial arts, O’Reilly is equally equipped to trade strikes as he is to cinch in submission holds. O’Reilly also formed championship tag team combinations with both Cole and Fish before exposing NXT to The Undisputed ERA.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[1062,1288,1289,1356,1635,1762,3429,4175],"record":{"wins":0,"lo