ronger. With his new change in attitude and in-ring style, he found instant success.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":38,"teams":[1216,1403,2890,3031],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":80,"storytelling":84,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":29,"matchLayout":85,"psychology":80,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":60,"technicalCoaching":66,"characterCoaching":45,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":71,"mediaHandling":45,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":34,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":60,"consistency":58,"awareness":80,"judgement":88},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-317","wrestlerId":317,"promotionId":38,"startDate":"1996-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":318,"name":"Takashi Iizuka","realName":"Takashi Iizuka","picture":"Takashi Iizuka.jpg","ability":83,"currentAbility":88,"potentialAbility":88,"charisma":85,"micSkills":75,"popularity":4,"condition":77,"hardcoreAbility":81,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":107,"height":177,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1966-08-02T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1985-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Takayuki Iizuka, better known by his stage name Takashi Iizuka, is a Japanese professional wrestler,Takayuki Iizuka made his debut for New Japan Pro Wrestling in November 1986, wrestling against Akira Nogami. In June 1989, Iizuka and Hiroshi Hase went to the Soviet Union to be trained in sambo. A month later, he won his first championship, the IWGP Tag Team Championship, with veteran Riki Choshu. In October 1995, he changed his ring name from Takayuki to Takashi. In June 1996, he won his second IWGP Tag Team title, this time with another veteran, Kazuo Yamazaki. Recieved a serious brain concussion in 2001, but returned to wrestling in late 2002. Continued to rise up the ranks upon his return, with no slowing down. Cranky old wrestler turned brawler.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":38,"teams":[952,994,3035,3036,3037,3038],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":75,"storytelling":78,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":30,"matchLayout":79,"psychology":75,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":43,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":69,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":70,"mediaHandling":69,"brandBuilding":56,"socialMediaSavvy":34,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":43,"consistency":71,"awareness":75,"judgement":85},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-318","wrestlerId":318,"promotionId":38,"startDate":"2017-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":319,"name":"Hirooki Goto","realName":"Hirooki Goto","picture":"Hirooki Goto.jpg","ability":62,"currentAbility":70,"potentialAbility":70,"charisma":81,"micSkills":75,"popularity":30,"condition":83,"hardcoreAbility":72,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"submission","gender":"M","weight":103,"height":177,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1979-06-25T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2003-07-06T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Hirooki Goto, who graduated from New Japan Dojo on 06 July 2003, is a Japanese wrestler who works in the USA, Mexico and Japan. He is a 5'11\", 227lb worker who is classed as using a Impactful style. He uses the GTR as his finis