"Toru Yano.jpg","ability":69,"currentAbility":68,"potentialAbility":68,"charisma":62,"micSkills":83,"popularity":23,"condition":76,"hardcoreAbility":58,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"comedy","gender":"M","weight":115,"height":182,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1978-05-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Toru Yano, a 2002 graduate of the New Japan Dojo, is a Japanese wrestler who works in America, Canada, Mexico and Japan. He is a Middleweight who is classed as using a Comedy style. He is best known for his work with NJPW, NOAH and ROH.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":38,"teams":[952,994,3043,3045,3048,3657],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":73,"storytelling":75,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":16,"matchLayout":76,"psychology":73,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":86,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":84,"mediaHandling":86,"brandBuilding":40,"socialMediaSavvy":78,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":82,"awareness":73,"judgement":84},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-336","wrestlerId":336,"promotionId":38,"startDate":"2005-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":337,"name":"Milano Collection A.T.","realName":"Milano Collection A.T.","picture":"Milano Collection AT.jpg","ability":81,"currentAbility":91,"potentialAbility":91,"charisma":81,"micSkills":100,"popularity":14,"condition":56,"hardcoreAbility":100,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":85,"height":180,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1976-08-27T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Akihito Terui, also known as Milano Collection A.T., is a retired Japanese professional wrestler. Now works often as a color commentator. Terui made his debut in 2000 in Toryumon, and gained success. He later adopted the persona of Milano Collection A.T. (A.T. being his initials; compare Magnum T.A. in the United States) to achieve greater success. He worked for New Japan Pro Wrestling as a part of the R.I.S.E. faction. He competed in Total Nonstop Action Wrestling's World X Cup as a part of Team Japan, winning his first and only singles match for TNA against Curry Man, gaining 2 points for his team. On January 18, 2010, Terui announced his retirement from the professional wrestling because of inferior oblique muscle palsy, brought on by an excessively strong thrust kick to the eye by Gedo. A retirement ceremony was held on February 14.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":61,"teams":[2975,3033],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":82,"storytelling":83,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":83,"psychology":82,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":75,"technicalCoaching":83,"characterCoaching":87,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":87,"brandBuilding":56,"socialMediaSavvy":58,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":75,"consistency":69,"awareness":82,"judgement":89},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-337","wrestlerId":337,"promotionId":61,"startDate":"2019-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":338,"name":"Kuniaki Kobayashi","realName":"Kuniaki Kobayashi","picture":"Kuniaki Kobayashi.jpg","ability":100,"currentAbility":96,"potentialAbility":96,"charisma":87,"micSkills":100,"popularity":6,"condition":70,"hardcoreAbility":88,"injuryProne":68,"type":"writer","style":"submission","gender":"M","weight":105,"height":180,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1956-01-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1972-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":true,"story":"Kuniaki Kobayashi was a Japanese Junior Heavyweight professional wrestler. He started wrestling at the age of 16. He wrestled numerous acclaimed matches against the first two Tiger Masks (Satoru Sayama and Mitsuharu Misawa.) He is also regarded as the first \"Tiger Hunter\" because of his dealings with the Tiger Masks. He also served as the first opponent for Jushin Liger under this persona. Upon his retirement in April 2000, Kobayashi has remained involved in puroresu, currently as caretaker of the New Japan Dojo. He occasionally wrestles in legends matches.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":92,"storytelling":94,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":95,"psychology":92,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":45,"technicalCoaching":61,"characterCoaching":42,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":42,"brandBuilding":25,"socialMediaSavvy":40,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":45,"consistency":40,"awareness":92,"judgement":95}},{"id":339,"name":"Kazuo Yamazaki","realName":"Kazuo Yamazaki","picture":"Kazuo Yamazaki.jpg","ability":58,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":55,"charisma":55,"micSkills":60,"popularity":4,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":41,"injuryProne":100,"type":"commentator","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":103,"height":185,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1962-08-15T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1980-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Kazuo Yamazaki is a former Japanese professional wrestler, who is known for his work in New Japan Pro Wrestling and UWF International. Yamazaki's wrestling career began in May 1982 in New Japan Pro Wrestling. In 1984, Yamazaki joined the Japanese UWF. However, differences between his mentor Satoru Sayama and Akira Maeda over direction caused the promotion to fail. He rejoined New Japan in 1985 as a junior heavyweight. Despite this, he found more success in tag teams in 1987, winning the IWGP Tag Team Championship with one of his mentors, Yoshiaki Fujiwara. In 1988, however, the UWF was reconstituted as Newborn UWF and Yamazaki joined it, and stayed there until it folded in December 1990. Kazuo Yamazaki now works as a wrestling instructor at the New Japan Pro Wrestling dojo and sometimes acts as color commentator for the NJPW program on TV Asahi.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":38,"teams":[3037,3039],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":77,"storytelling":80,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":81,"psychology":77,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":65,"technicalCoaching":33,"characterCoaching":56,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":56,"brandBuilding":14,"socialMediaSavvy":42,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":65,"consistency":80,"awareness":77,"judgement":86},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-339","wrestlerId":339,"promotionId":38,"startDate":"2005-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"20