 who is classed as using a Brawler style. He is best known for his work with NORTH, ICW and TNT.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1652],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":40,"storytelling":42,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":45,"matchLayout":42,"psychology":40,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":55,"technicalCoaching":20,"characterCoaching":44,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":55,"mediaHandling":44,"brandBuilding":33,"socialMediaSavvy":40,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":55,"consistency":44,"awareness":40,"judgement":64}},{"id":520,"name":"Dralistico","realName":"Dralistico","picture":"Mistico II.jpg","ability":59,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"charisma":54,"micSkills":67,"popularity":22,"condition":91,"hardcoreAbility":68,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":76,"height":172,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1992-09-15T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"He is one of the characters with a great reputation within Mexican Wrestling, possessor of one of the most representative images of this sport both inside and outside our borders.\r\n\r\nOriginally from Tala Jalisco, his first steps in this sport were led by his uncles, the Pit Bulls in his homeland. Soon he decided to pack suitcases and make the trip to Mexico City to seek an opportunity in the World Wrestling Council. This opportunity led him to become as part of The 2011 Generation, a group of promising young people and thus began his adventure in the In Search of an Idol tournament under the name of Dragon Lee.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[982,3161,3533],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":57,"storytelling":63,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":65,"psychology":57,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":78,"technicalCoaching":67,"characterCoaching":58,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":58,"brandBuilding":72,"socialMediaSavvy":44,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":78,"consistency":65,"awareness":57,"judgement":74},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-520","wrestlerId":520,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2022-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":521,"name":"Metalik","realName":"Metalik","picture":"Mascara Dorada.jpg","ability":56,"currentAbility":59,"potentialAbility":59,"charisma":48,"micSkills":66,"popularity":31,"condition":88,"hardcoreAbility":70,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":86,"height":172,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1988-11-03T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2005-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Metalik is a masked Mexican luchador who works in America, Canada, Mexico and Japan. He is a Small worker who is classed as using a Luchador style. He is best known for his work with WWE, NJPW, CMLL, NJoA and ROH. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[2255,2362],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":68,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":18,"matchLayout":70,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":67,"characterCoaching":57,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":82,"mediaHandling":57,"brandBuilding":52,"socialMediaSavvy":54,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":67,"awareness":62,"judgement":77}},{"id":522,"name":"Titán","realName":"Titán","picture":"Titan.jpg","ability":74,"currentAbility":64,"potentialAbility":64,"charisma":55,"micSkills":56,"popularity":19,"condition":92,"hardcoreAbility":68,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":85,"height":167,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1990-10-15T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"The daring and suicidal style of Titán has made him a great figure in the CMLL and an ambassador of Mexican wrestling outside national borders due to his constant presentations in Japan, the United States and England, mainly.\r\n\r\nArising from the legendary gymnasium of the Arena Coliseo de Occidente, Titan began his career precisely in Guadalajara under the name of Palacio Negro, with which he won the admiration of the public from Guadalajara; but its quality could not be limited, so he took the big step and ventured to try his luck in the Mexican capital.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[1547,1548,2434,4259,4260],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":71,"storytelling":75,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":76,"psychology":71,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":80,"technicalCoaching":69,"characterCoaching":64,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":64,"brandBuilding":73,"socialMediaSavvy":48,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":80,"consistency":56,"awareness":71,"judgement":83},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-522","wrestlerId":522,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2008-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":523,"name":"Marco Corleone","realName":"Marco Corleone","picture":"Mark Jindrak.jpg","ability":65,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"charisma":60,"micSkills":60,"popularity":17,"condition":80,"hardcoreAbility":76,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":118,"height":193,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1977-06-26T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Mark Robert Jindrak  is an American professional wrestler, best known for his appearances with World Championship Wrestling (WCW) and World Wrestling Entertainment (WWE) as Mark Jindrak. He currently wrestles on the independent circuit under his real name and competed for the for Mexican promotion Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) under the ring name Marco Corleone for 3 years until jumping to rival promotion Asistencia Asesoría y Administración (AAA) in March 2009. Mark was also on the Keuka (New York) College Basketball team and at one time boasted the highest vertical leap in WWE. On December 10, 2011, CMLL announced that Corleone would return to the promotion on December 16 at CMLL's Sin Piedad show. Due to his success in Mexican promotions, Jindrak has appeared on several Mexican game shows, soap operas, and TV shows, and been featured on the covers of magazines.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3237],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":58,"storytelling":61,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":62,"psychology":58,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":64,"technicalCoaching":46,"characterCoaching":54,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":54,"brandBuilding":72,"socialMediaSavvy":42,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":64,"consistency":63,"awareness":58,"judgement":75}},{"id":524,"name":"Máximo","realName":"Máximo","picture":"Maximo.jpg","ability":61,"currentAbility":60,"potentialAbility":60,"charisma":74,"micSkills":62,"popularity":5,"condition":61,"hardcoreAbility":68,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":91,"height":167,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1980-04-02T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"José Christian Alvarado Ruiz is a Mexican Luchador best known under the ring name Máximo. Alvarado wrestles as an Exótico character, a character that appears to be homosexual but he is married to wrestler India Sioux and together they have a son. Alvarado made his professional wrestling debut in April, 2000 under the ring name Corazon de Dragón (\"Dragonheart\") and later worked as Pepe Rous. After gaining a bit of experience he took the name \"Brazo, Jr.\" – since his older brother was wrestling as Brazo de Plata, Jr. he played a character that was supposed to be the son of El Brazo. The two sons of Brazo de Plata teamed up with the son of Brazo de Oro who wrestled as Brazo de Oro, Jr. to form the next generation of \"Los Brazos\". José Christian Alvarado was repackaged as Máximo (\"Maximus\"), a character inspired by the Roman era and was supposed to team up with Los Romanos (Caligula and Mesalla) but instead he was turned into an Exótico character.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":69,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":69,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":45,"characterCoaching":73,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":73,"brandBuilding":49,"socialMediaSavvy":64,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":69,"awareness":68,"judgement":81}},{"id":525,"name":"DMT Azul","realName":"DMT Azul","picture":"Diamante Azul.jpg","ability":63,"currentAbility":63,"potentialAbility":63,"charisma":50,"micSkills":65,"popularity":5,"condition":81,"hardcoreAbility":47,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":102,"height":180,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1983-12-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2007-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"DMT Azul is a masked Mexican luchador who works exclusively in Mexico. He is a 6'0\", 224lb worker who is classed as using a Luchador style. He uses the El Escudo and the German Suplex as his finishers. He is best known for his work with CMLL, AAA, IWRG and The Crash. He is currently the IWRG Intercontinental Heavyweight champion.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":30,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":61,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":63,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":43,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":43,"brandBuilding":77,"socialMediaSavvy":37,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":55,"awareness":56,"judgement":74},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-525","wrestlerId":525,"promotionId":30,"startDate":"2021-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":526,"name":"Shocker","realName":"Shocker","picture":"Shocker_alt.jpg","ability":58,"currentAbility":62,"potentialAbility":62,"charisma":77,"micSkills":67,"popularity":8,"condition":54,"hardcoreAbility":73,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":98,"height":177,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1971-09-12T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1992-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"José Luis Jair Soria is a Mexican professional wrestler, who wrestles under the name Shocker. He has in the past branched out into the United States, working for Total Nonstop Action Wrestling. José Jair trained for his professional wrestling career under the very well regarded wrestling trainer Diablo Velasco as well as his father Ruben Soria before making his professional wrestling career on October 15, 1992 using the ring name Shocker. He would later also train under El Satánico. Shocker first made a name for himself in CMLL and got his first push when he won the Gran Alterntiva tournament along with his partner, Silver King, in 1995. Shocker lost his mask to Mr Niebla 1999. While continuing to work in TNA, he jumped from CMLL, who he had been with for ten years, for CMLL's rival AAA with Vampiro and various other wrestlers. Shocker jumped ship from Asistencia Asesoría y Administración back to Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre again in 2007.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":75,"storytelling":77,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":31,"matchLayout":77,"psychology":75,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":62,"technicalCoaching":58,"characterCoaching":74,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":69,"mediaHandling":74,"brandBuilding":55,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":62,"consistency":54,"awareness":75,"judgement":85}},{"id":527,"name":"Valiente","realName":"Valiente","picture":"Valiente.jpg","ability":64,"currentAbility":70,"potentialAbility":70,"charisma":62,"micSkills":76,"popularity":6,"condition":79,"hardcoreAbility":85,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":92,"height":167,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1974-05-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1996-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Valiente is a Mexican luchador enmáscarado whose real name is not a matter of public record, as is often the case with masked wrestlers in Mexico where their private lives are kept a secret from the wrestling fans. Valiente made his debut in 1996, working on the Mexican independent circuit. After not making much headway Valiente actually retired from professional wrestling in the late 1990s. After almost five years away from the ring Valiente returned to wrestling in the early 2000s, hoping to make a name for himself.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":79,"storytelling":81,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":81,"psychology":79,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":72,"characterCoaching":57,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":57,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":44,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":76,"awareness":79,"judgement":87},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-527","wrestlerId":527,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2003-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":528,"name":"Blue Panther","realName":"Blue Panther","picture":"Blue Panther_alt.jpg","ability":72,"currentAbility":73,"potentialAbility":73,"charisma":84,"micSkills":71,"popularity":19,"condition":53,"hardcoreAbility":91,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":98,"height":165,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1960-09-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1978-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Genaro Vazquez Nevarez is a Mexican professional wrestler better known by his ring name Blue Panther. The \"Blue\" part of his ring name is an homage to Aníbal, a wrestler he looked up to growing up who wore a blue mask, Has won many titles in CMLL. Blue Panther began wrestling in northern Mexico in the late 1970s before getting noticed by wrestler and promoter René Guajardo in Monterrey. Guarjardo got Panther booked in Universal Wrestling Association and Panther made his debut in their main building, El Toreo de Cuatro Caminos in Naucalpan, in 1981. In September 19, 2008, Blue Panther was finally unmasked when he lost a Mask vs. Mask match against Villano V. In March, 2013 Blue Panther was forced to team up with the rudo Rey Escorpión to participate in the 2013 Torneo Nacional de Parejas Increibles (\"National Incredible Pairs Tournament\"), a tag team tournament teaming up wrestlers who would never team up otherwise.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":94,"storytelling":95,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":10,"matchLayout":96,"psychology":94,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":58,"technicalCoaching":80,"characterCoaching":67,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":90,"mediaHandling":67,"brandBuilding":68,"socialMediaSavvy":58,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":58,"consistency":67,"awareness":94,"judgement":96},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-528","wrestlerId":528,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"1997-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":529,"name":"Ángel de Oro","realName":"Ángel de Oro","picture":"Angel de Oro.jpg","ability":78,"currentAbility":69,"potentialAbility":69,"charisma":58,"micSkills":72,"popularity":10,"condition":87,"hardcoreAbility":59,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":83,"height":175,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1988-03-21T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2005-07-14T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Ángel de Oro is one of the young figures with a promising future within the ranks of the World Wrestling Council. He arrived together with his brother Ángel de Plata (Niebla Roja) at the Arena México causing a pleasant impression, first in the training sessions with El Satánico, and then in the strings before a demanding and knowledgeable public. \r\n\r\nOriginally from Gómez Palacio, Durango, he is part of a group of fighters who are raising the Lagunera region.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[1175,4286,4287],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":77,"storytelling":80,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":16,"matchLayout":81,"psychology":77,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":82,"technicalCoaching":70,"characterCoaching":72,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":84,"mediaHandling":72,"brandBuilding":76,"socialMediaSavvy":64,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":82,"consistency":80,"awareness":77,"judgement":86},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-529","wrestlerId":529,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2008-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":531,"name":"Brazo de Plata","realName":"Brazo de Plata","picture":"Brazo de Plata.jpg","ability":97,"currentAbility":87,"potentialAbility":87,"charisma":85,"micSkills":88,"popularity":4,"condition":58,"hardcoreAbility":94,"injuryProne":83,"type":"writer","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":135,"height":167,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1963-03-19T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1977-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":true,"story":"José Alvarado Nieves is a Mexican Luchador best known under the ring name Brazo de Plata that he has been using since his debut in 1977 and also for his appearances for WWE as \"Super Porky\". Alvarado is a part of the Alvarado wrestling family which includes his father Shadito Cruz, five brothers who used the \"Brazo\" name at some point and several third generation wrestlers who have appeared over the last couple of years. Alvarado made his debut as \"Brazo De Plata\" (Spanish for \"Silver arm\"), an Enmascarado who worked mainly in Tag team action with his brother who worked as Brazo de Oro (\"Gold arm\") and in trios action with another brother known simply as El Brazo (\"the arm\"). In 2009 after leaving AAA, Plata began working independent dates throughout the country as well as regularly for International Wrestling Revolution Group and Perros del Mal Producciones.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":73,"storytelling":76,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":32,"matchLayout":77,"psychology":73,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":38,"technicalCoaching":25,"characterCoaching":71,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":68,"mediaHandling":71,"brandBuilding":31,"socialMediaSavvy":70,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":38,"consistency":43,"awareness":73,"judgement":84}},{"id":532,"name":"Robin","realName":"Robin","picture":"Robin.jpg","ability":42,"currentAbility":51,"potentialAbility":51,"charisma":41,"micSkills":57,"popularity":3,"condition":95,"hardcoreAbility":66,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":68,"height":162,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1990-11-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Robin is a Mexican luchador enmascarado and is a part of the extensive Alvarado wrestling family, the son of José Alvarado Nieves who wrestles as \"Brazo de Plata\" and grandson of Juan Alvarado Ibarra, better known as Shadito Cruz. The wrestler currently known as \"Robin\" started his wrestling career by using the ring name Robin Hood, Jr., after his deceased uncle José Aarón Alvarado Nieves who wrestled as \"Robin Hood\" for the major part of his wrestling career. He worked primarily on the Mexican Independent circuit, including some shows for the Los Perros del Mal wrestling promotion. He began working for Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL), one of Mexico's largest and the world's oldest wrestling promotion, in 2010 not long after his father José Alvarado Nieves (also known as \"Brazo de Plata\") made his return to the promotion. in CMLL he shortened his name to simply \"Robin\" and it was publicly acknowledged that he was the son of José Alvarado, not José Aarón Alvarado.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":55,"storytelling":60,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":19,"matchLayout":62,"psychology":55,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":76,"technicalCoaching":58,"characterCoaching":63,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":81,"mediaHandling":63,"brandBuilding":38,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":76,"consistency":66,"awareness":55,"judgement":73},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-532","wrestlerId":532,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2010-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":533,"name":"Delta.","realName":"Delta.","picture":"Delta.jpg","ability":61,"currentAbility":51,"potentialAbility":51,"charisma":38,"micSkills":48,"popularity":4,"condition":87,"hardcoreAbility":37,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":90,"height":175,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1985-08-05T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2007-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Delta is a Mexican Luchador enmascarado. The future Delta began training for a professional wrestling career while he was still at college, spending over four years training under his father, while simultaneously keeping up with his school work. He made his debut in May, 2007 under the name \"Hijo del Trueno\", wearing a thunderbolt adorned mask and trunks. He worked for various independent promotions, especially in his home state of Monterrey. In 2009 he achieved one of his childhood dreams as he began working for Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) based in Mexico City, Mexico. In CMLL he received further training from Franco Colombo as well as a new ring name, mask and outfit as he became \"Delta\".","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1204],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":42,"storytelling":53,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":45,"matchLayout":56,"psychology":42,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":80,"technicalCoaching":55,"characterCoaching":27,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":55,"mediaHandling":27,"brandBuilding":39,"socialMediaSavvy":20,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":80,"consistency":80,"awareness":42,"judgement":65}},{"id":534,"name":"Guerrero Maya Jr.","realName":"Guerrero Maya Jr.","picture":"Guerrero Maya.jpg","ability":55,"currentAbility":64,"potentialAbility":64,"charisma":74,"micSkills":52,"popularity":8,"condition":82,"hardcoreAbility":60,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":88,"height":175,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1985-08-08T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Guerrero Maya, Jr. is a Mexican luchador enmascarado. Maya, Jr. is the son of Esteban Mares Castañeda, better known under the ring names Black Terry and Guerrero Maya. Guerrero Maya, Jr. has previously competed as the enmascarado characters Samba and Multifacético (the third person to use that name). The man known under the ring name Guerrero Maya, Jr. earned a degree in Business Administration from a European University before his professional wrestling career, noting that it was important to him to have a well rounded background, to combine intellect with skill. In late 2007 he was given a new ring name and mask and became Multifacético (\"Multi-faceted\"), the third wrestler to actually use the name and mask in IWRG. The Multifacético stopped appearing on IWRG shows in early 2009 with no explanation for the disappearance. A few months later CMLL announced that the son of retired enmascarado Guerrero Maya was joining CMLL, using the ring name Guerrero Maya, Jr.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[1204],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":69,"storytelling":73,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":74,"psychology":69,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":74,"technicalCoaching":73,"characterCoaching":54,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":54,"brandBuilding":71,"socialMediaSavvy":25,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":74,"consistency":73,"awareness":69,"judgement":81},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-534","wrestlerId":534,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2009-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":535,"name":"Rey Cometa","realName":"Rey Cometa","picture":"Rey Cometa.jpg","ability":74,"currentAbility":66,"potentialAbility":66,"charisma":59,"micSkills":77,"popularity":8,"condition":83,"hardcoreAbility":84,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":83,"height":170,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1983-03-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Mario Alberto González is a Mexican Luchador currently working under the ring name Rey Cometa. The man that would later wrestle as Rey Cometa was trained by Dragon de Oriente I, II, Kaoma, Jr. and Atomico de Oro before making his debut on April 30, 1999 at the age of 16. He first gained national exposure when he worked for Asistencia Asesoría y Administración (AAA) from 2005 until 2008. In AAA he was a part of the group Real Fuerza Aérea, consisting of young high flying wrestlers. Pegasso and Rey Cometa initially used the Real Fuerza Aérea name in CMLL as well, but quickly abandoned it when AAA objected to the use of the name.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[2920],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":74,"storytelling":76,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":76,"psychology":74,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":74,"technicalCoaching":64,"characterCoaching":61,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":61,"brandBuilding":55,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":74,"consistency":65,"awareness":74,"judgement":84},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-535","wrestlerId":535,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2008-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":536,"name":"El Hijo del Fantasma","realName":"El Hijo del Fantasma","picture":"Hijo del Fantasma.jpg","ability":57,"currentAbility":64,"potentialAbility":64,"charisma":64,"micSkills":55,"popularity":39,"condition":83,"hardcoreAbility":78,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":90,"height":177,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1984-04-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"With nearly two decades of experience and a rich sports-entertainment heritage coursing through his veins, Santos Escobar arrived in NXT as El Hijo del Fantasma, with potential as high as he’s capable of soaring through the air.\r\n\r\nThe second-generation Superstar is a veteran of the Mexican wrestling scene. Hailing from Mexico City, he is the son of legendary luchador El Fantasma and nephew of the late Arkangel de la Muerte. Though he’s beyond well-versed in the art of lucha libre, what sets Escobar apart from many is his unusual ability to blend highflying with more powerful maneuvers.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":67,"storytelling":71,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":72,"psychology":67,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":64,"characterCoaching":58,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":58,"brandBuilding":64,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":58,"awareness":67,"judgement":80}},{"id":537,"name":"Luis Mante","realName":"Luis Mante","picture":"Diamante.jpg","ability":62,"currentAbility":65,"potentialAbility":65,"charisma":56,"micSkills":68,"popularity":9,"condition":91,"hardcoreAbility":83,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":96,"height":180,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1992-02-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Diamante is a Mexican luchador enmascarado whose name translates as \"Diamond\". The wrestler later known as Diamante made his debut at a very early age, initially working as Chamaco Meza (\"Kid\" Meza) and also worked as Aero Boy early on, working primarily in Nuevo León. Later on he adopted a new ring name and image as Principe Diamante (\"Prince Diamond\"). He worked for Asistencia Asesoría y Administración at the age of just 16, wrestling at the 2008 Rey de Reyes. Principe Diamante signed a contract with Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) in the summer of 2009, but had his ring name changed to \"Diamante\" since CMLL already had a wrestler called Principe working for them. He made his in ring debut for CMLL on August 17, 2009. The first sign of Diamante's potential in CMLL came on June 16, 2010 when he entered in the 2010 torneo Gran Alternativa, where a rookie and a \"veteran\" wrestler teamed up for a tag team tournament.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":14,"teams":[3889],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":65,"storytelling":70,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":71,"psychology":65,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":65,"characterCoaching":68,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":69,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":82,"awareness":65,"judgement":79},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-537","wrestlerId":537,"promotionId":14,"startDate":"2019-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":538,"name":"Stuka Jr.","realName":"Stuka Jr.","picture":"Stuka.jpg","ability":73,"currentAbility":71,"potentialAbility":71,"charisma":75,"micSkills":67,"popularity":8,"condition":75,"hardcoreAbility":60,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":86,"height":172,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1979-07-17T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2005-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Stuka Jr. is a Mexican luchador enmascarado. Stuka, Jr. is not, despite what the name indicates, the son of Luchador Stuka but his much younger brother. Stuka, Jr. made his professional wrestling debut in 2005 after training with his older brother Stuka. He took the name Stuka, Jr. after his brother, adopting a ring outfit adorned with German Iro Crosses and a mask fashioned to look like aviator goggles and a German helmet. Stuka, Jr. made his CMLL debut on April 30, 2006, working mainly in the opening matches while receiving additional training by CMLL's head trainer Satánico.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":82,"storytelling":83,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":16,"matchLayout":83,"psychology":82,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":72,"characterCoaching":45,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":84,"mediaHandling":45,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":55,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":80,"awareness":82,"judgement":89},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-538","wrestlerId":538,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2005-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":539,"name":"Tritón","realName":"Tritón","picture":"Triton.jpg","ability":51,"currentAbility":49,"potentialAbility":49,"charisma":63,"micSkills":61,"popularity":3,"condition":90,"hardcoreAbility":33,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":85,"height":167,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1987-03-23T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2006-11-20T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Tritón is a Mexican luchador enmascarado. Tritón is the son of Luchador Flash, although he is no relation to Fuego, who used to work as \"Flash\" as well. The wrestler later known as Tritón made his debut on November 20, 2006 under the ring name Metal Blanco (\"White Metal\") incorporating white and metallic fabric in both his mask and wrestling trunks. By the end of 2010 Metal Blanco, along with Palacio Negro made their wrestling debut in Mexico City, appearing at CMLL's main arena Arena Mexico. Metal Blanco and Palacio Negro stopped appearing in Mexico City in early November, 2011 in preparation for being repackaged with new masks and ring names. The two were reintroduced as Titán (Palacio Negro) and Tritón (Metal Blanco), presented as new versions of characters used in the early 1990s in CMLL.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1547,1548,1725],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":55,"storytelling":60,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":30,"matchLayout":62,"psychology":55,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":49,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":70,"mediaHandling":49,"brandBuilding":55,"socialMediaSavvy":48,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":73,"awareness":55,"judgement":73}},{"id":540,"name":"El Sagrado","realName":"El Sagrado","picture":"El Sagrado.jpg","ability":55,"currentAbility":65,"potentialAbility":65,"charisma":50,"micSkills":74,"popularity":4,"condition":80,"hardcoreAbility":49,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":90,"height":175,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1975-12-19T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1992-04-30T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Luis Fernando Lopez Ramos is a Mexican professional wrestler better known as El Sagrado (Spanish for \"The Sacred One\"). Besides wrestling Lopez also studied religion, urged by his mother to seek the priesthood when he was old enough. According to Lopez he met Fray Tormenta, the famous Mexican wrestling priest who told Lopez to follow his own desires, which in turn let Lopez to become a wrestler. Whether this is actually true or part of the storyline build up around the \"El Sagrado\" character is not known, but Javier has stated that he met Fray Tormenta in several interviews. On his debut (aged 12) Lopez shared a ring with one of the big names of the early 1990s, Rayo de Jalisco, Jr. The CMLL gave Lopez´s the name \"El Sagrado\", a new outfit including a mask with a silver cross on it and a storyline that claimed that he was the protoge of Fray Tormenta.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":73,"storytelling":76,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":13,"matchLayout":77,"psychology":73,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":68,"technicalCoaching":67,"characterCoaching":63,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":87,"mediaHandling":63,"brandBuilding":52,"socialMediaSavvy":53,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":68,"consistency":62,"awareness":73,"judgement":84},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-540","wrestlerId":540,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"1999-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":541,"name":"Fuego","realName":"Fuego","picture":"Fuego.jpg","ability":51,"currentAbility":54,"potentialAbility":54,"charisma":60,"micSkills":39,"popularity":5,"condition":85,"hardcoreAbility":60,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":78,"height":175,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1981-12-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2003-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Fuego is a Mexican luchador enmascarado. Fuego made his professional wrestling debut in 2003, immediately adopting the ring name flash and an outfit and mask that was patterened after the comic book character the Flash, although he would often change the main color of his outfit to blue or white and not just the red of the original character. By 2008 Flash had begun teaming with Stuka, Jr. on a semi-regular basis, especially on CMLL's \"lower level\" shows away from Arena Mexico. At a CMLL press conference on November 19, 2009 it was announced that Flash had changed his name to \"Fuego\" (\"Fire\") and along with the name changed his outfit to a \"fire\" inspired outfit instead of the outfit that closely resembled the DC superhero.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":59,"storytelling":64,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":17,"matchLayout":66,"psychology":59,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":67,"technicalCoaching":53,"characterCoaching":67,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":83,"mediaHandling":67,"brandBuilding":51,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":67,"consistency":73,"awareness":59,"judgement":75},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-541","wrestlerId":541,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2004-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":542,"name":"Francisco Lutteroth","realName":"Francisco Lutteroth","picture":"Paco Alonso.jpg","ability":0,"currentAbility":0,"potentialAbility":0,"charisma":0,"micSkills":13,"popularity":7,"condition":55,"hardcoreAbility":16,"injuryProne":99,"type":"wrestler","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":71,"height":162,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1952-09-19T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1975-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":true,"story":"Francisco Alonso Lutteroth, commonly referred to as Paco Alonso is the owner of the professional wrestling promotion Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL), the world's oldest wrestling promotion. Alonso is the grandson of CMLL founder Salvador Lutteroth and took control of the company in 1980. Alonso began working for EMLL in 1975 around the same time as Salvador Lutteroth's son, Chavo Lutteroth, took control of the promotion. Over the next five years Alonso worked in a promotional capaticy while Chavo Lutteroth ran the company, Lutteroth did not command the same respect as his father and by 1980 he handed over control and later ownership to Paco Alonso. Who had the ability and intelligence to make the company evolve and succeed. Alonso relatively reclusive from the public eye and has only given a few interviews in his time in charge of the promotion.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":36,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":36,"brandBuilding":25,"socialMediaSavvy":42,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":0,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0}},{"id":543,"name":"Magnus","realName":"Magnus","picture":"Magnus_CMLL.jpg","ability":55,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"charisma":55,"micSkills":60,"popularity":10,"condition":87,"hardcoreAbility":52,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":85,"height":175,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1993-02-17T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2009-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Magnus is a Mexican Reality TV personality and luchador enmascarado. He is the son of Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre trainer and booking team member Tony Salazar and the nephew of Manuel Almanza who worked under the ring name \"Dr. Karontes\". Magnus is the cousin of the original Místico (now Sin Cara in WWE) as well as the cousin on wrestlers Argenis, Argos, Astro Boy, Dr. Karontes, Jr. and an unidentified member of Los Mini Psycho Circus. Magnus briefly wrestled for Toryumon Mexico as \"Astro Boy\" , a ring name also used by three of his older cousins before him. Magnus started his Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) career as a member of the informal Generación 2011 stable, which also included fellow debutants Bobby Zavala, Enrique Vera, Jr., Hombre Bala, Jr., Dragon Lee, Hijo del Signo and Super Halcón, Jr. Magnus returned to CMLL in October, 2012 coinciding with the debut Season 2 of El Luchador.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[4149,4150,4151],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":64,"storytelling":66,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":26,"matchLayout":67,"psychology":64,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":58,"characterCoaching":56,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":74,"mediaHandling":56,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":55,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":65,"awareness":64,"judgement":78},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-543","wrestlerId":543,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2011-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":545,"name":"Starman","realName":"Starman","picture":"Starman.jpg","ability":51,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"charisma":56,"micSkills":45,"popularity":2,"condition":70,"hardcoreAbility":59,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":85,"height":167,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1974-11-16T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1994-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":true,"story":"Starman is a Mexican professional wrestler whose real name is not a matter of public record. He made his debut on April 30, 1994 in Naucalpan as Ultramán Jr. During his time in Naucalpan, he won the mask of Tortuguillo Karateka IV, one of the Ninja Turtles. By 1995 he had his first Japanese tour in July wrestling in Pro Wrestling Fujiwara Gumi. On January 23, 1996 he made his debut in CMLL teaming with Alacran de Durango and Olimpus defeating Fiero, America, and Linx. Later on he was in a tournament of Block B for the CMLL World Welterweight Championship. On the first round, he lost to Karloff Lagarde, Jr. In October 1998 he changed his name to Starman to avoid legal trouble with the original Ultramán (not a relative). By 2005, Starman started to wrestle in Japan again this time in New Japan Pro Wrestling (NJPW).","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":63,"storytelling":70,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":34,"matchLayout":72,"psychology":63,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":71,"technicalCoaching":69,"characterCoaching":34,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":66,"mediaHandling":34,"brandBuilding":27,"socialMediaSavvy":14,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":71,"consistency":81,"awareness":63,"judgement":78}},{"id":546,"name":"MVP","realName":"MVP","picture":"MVP.jpg","ability":72,"currentAbility":65,"potentialAbility":65,"charisma":59,"micSkills":65,"popularity":39,"condition":67,"hardcoreAbility":58,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"submission","gender":"M","weight":117,"height":187,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1973-10-28T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Half-man, half-amazing. That’s the boast former United States Champion Montel Vontavious Porter cribbed from hip-hop mastermind Nas to describe his particular talent in the ring. Indeed, at his best, the hottest free agent in WWE history seemed to posses abilities that were superhuman. But the onetime convict who fought his way out of a turbulent life of crime was as real as it gets.\r\n\r\nMVP was cheered on by WWE fans during his final years with the company as he enjoyed another reign as United States Champion and formed an impressive tag team with the mighty Mark Henry. Parting ways with WWE in 2010, he went on to compete in the smashmouth rings of Japan, further proving that there was serious skill behind MVP’s swagger.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":73,"storytelling":76,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":18,"matchLayout":77,"psychology":73,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":65,"technicalCoaching":54,"characterCoaching":81,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":82,"mediaHandling":81,"brandBuilding":64,"socialMediaSavvy":81,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":65,"consistency":69,"awareness":73,"judgement":84},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-546","wrestlerId":546,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2024-09-25T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":547,"name":"Pegasso","realName":"Pegasso","picture":"Pegasso.jpg","ability":54,"currentAbility":60,"potentialAbility":60,"charisma":66,"micSkills":60,"popularity":4,"condition":79,"hardcoreAbility":51,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":76,"height":167,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1978-02-25T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-04-30T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Pegasso is a Mexican Luchador enmascarado. The wrestler who would later be best known as Pegasso made his professional wrestling debut on April 30, 1999 after training under Sombra Salvaje, Irasu and Califa. Initially he wrestled under the name Hombre sin Nombre (Spanish for \"the man with no name\"), a concept or \"Gimmick\" often used by Luchadors who have yet to establish a ring persona. In 2000 he began working for Asistencia Asesoría y Administración (AAA), one of Mexico's largest promotions, and was given a new ring persona - Pegasso after the mythological horse. Pegasso and Rey Cometa initially used the Real Fuerza Aérea name in CMLL as well, but quickly abandoned it when AAA objected to the use of the name. Pegasso is not the only Luchador to have used the name Pegasso. Two other luchadors have used a similar name in their: Pegaso who now works as Ciclón Ramírez and Pegaso (II) who is a former CMLL employee of little note.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":71,"storytelling":74,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":75,"psychology":71,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":71,"technicalCoaching":63,"characterCoaching":48,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":48,"brandBuilding":53,"socialMediaSavvy":42,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":71,"consistency":73,"awareness":71,"judgement":83},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-547","wrestlerId":547,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2008-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":548,"name":"Soberano Jr.","realName":"Soberano Jr.","picture":"Soberano.jpg","ability":66,"currentAbility":64,"potentialAbility":64,"charisma":65,"micSkills":53,"popularity":15,"condition":89,"hardcoreAbility":65,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":78,"height":180,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1993-08-12T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2007-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"El Soberano is a Mexican luchador enmascarado. He is a third generation wrestler, son of Euforia and grandson of Pablo Moreno Román, known under the ring name El Soberano. Soberano is Spanish for \"Sovereign\". He made his professional wrestling debut at the age of only 13, working on the local independent circuit in Torreón, Coahuila. He began training in Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) wrestling school and even competed in CMLL's 2010 Bodybuilding contest, before he had made his in ring debut for the company, he placed third in the beginners category.  In March, 2012 Soberano, Jr. was one of the participants in the Torneo Sangre Nueva(\"The New Blood Tournament\") that featured 16 wrestlers classified as rookies, or at least rookie characters. Soberano was injured in a CMLL event May 26, 2013 after Raziel botched a powerbomb, planting Soberano on his head. He was forced to leave the match but returned a week later.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":72,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":74,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":81,"technicalCoaching":67,"characterCoaching":79,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":79,"brandBuilding":80,"socialMediaSavvy":63,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":81,"consistency":70,"awareness":68,"judgement":81},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-548","wrestlerId":548,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2011-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":549,"name":"Stigma","realName":"Stigma","picture":"Stigma_CMLL.jpg","ability":53,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":55,"charisma":49,"micSkills":40,"popularity":4,"condition":96,"hardcoreAbility":54,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":81,"height":162,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1988-04-09T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Stigma is a Mexican luchador enmascarado. While his real name is not public knowledge it has been confirmed that he is the brother of CMLL wrestler Skándalo, son of former wrestler Panico and grandson of Manuel Robles, making him a third generation wrestler. Stigma's official debut date was given as July 26, 2010 but in since he is a masked wrestler it is possible that he worked as a different ring character before that and never revealed it. Stigma trained at the Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) wrestling school in Puebla, Puebla and worked primarily in Arena Puebla early on.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":62,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":24,"matchLayout":64,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":60,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":76,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":48,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":63,"awareness":56,"judgement":74},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-549","wrestlerId":549,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2010-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":550,"name":"Euforia","realName":"Euforia","picture":"Euforia.jpg","ability":78,"currentAbility":75,"potentialAbility":75,"charisma":66,"micSkills":80,"popularity":9,"condition":77,"hardcoreAbility":57,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":95,"height":180,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1974-12-05T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1990-05-28T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Euforia is the ring name of a Mexican Luchador Enmascarado. Euforia is a part of a wrestling group called Los Guerreros del Infierno under the leadership of Último Guerrero.  Euforia has a son, also wrestling known as Soberano, Jr. The wrestler currently known as Euforia made his professional wrestling debut on May 28, 1990 under the name \"Soberano, Jr.\" (\"Sovereign, Jr.\"). He is the son of Soberano and the brother of \"El Hijo del Soberano\" (\"The son of Soberano\") and wrestled for many years alongside both his father and his brother on the Mexican independent circuit. In 2007 Soberano, Jr. returned to the CMLL rings, but had been replackaged as \"Euforia\", a darker Rudo character that teamed up with El Satánico and Nosferatu to form Los Nuevo Infernales.\r\n","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[1183],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":82,"storytelling":83,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":84,"psychology":82,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":80,"technicalCoaching":77,"characterCoaching":68,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":67,"socialMediaSavvy":63,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":80,"consistency":80,"awareness":82,"judgement":89},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-550","wrestlerId":550,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2006-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":552,"name":"Metálico","realName":"Metálico","picture":"Metalico.jpg","ability":84,"currentAbility":75,"potentialAbility":75,"charisma":87,"micSkills":76,"popularity":4,"condition":58,"hardcoreAbility":73,"injuryProne":100,"type":"referee","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":90,"height":170,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1969-11-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1992-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Metálico is a Mexican luchador enmascarado. In 2004 Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) created the Guapos University (\"Hansome University\"), or Guapos U, a storyline mimicking realities shows such as the WWE Tough Enough show, searching for a new member to join Shocker, Máscara Mágica and El Terrible as part of Los Guapos. The contestants included, among others, Tigre Metálico who became a regular worker for CMLL at this point. Tigre Metálico had his ring character changed in June, 2007 becoming simply \"Metálico\", removing any reference to the Tiger character, including a redesign of his wrestling mask. The repackaged Metálico participated in the 2007 Reyes del Aire tournament.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":78,"storytelling":80,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":38,"matchLayout":81,"psychology":78,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":68,"technicalCoaching":65,"characterCoaching":68,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":62,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":35,"socialMediaSavvy":27,"ruleKnowledge":75,"positioning":80,"reactionSpeed":68,"consistency":75,"awareness":78,"judgement":87},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-552","wrestlerId":552,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2004-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":553,"name":"Dutch Mantel","realName":"Dutch Mantel","picture":"Zeb Colter.jpg","ability":53,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"charisma":62,"micSkills":55,"popularity":22,"condition":44,"hardcoreAbility":43,"injuryProne":87,"type":"manager","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":100,"height":180,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1949-11-29T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1973-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Wayne Maurice Keown is an American professional wrestler, better known by his ring name, Dutch Mantel. He is currently retired from in ring action. Keown debuted in 1973. While he primarily wrestled on the independent circuit, he made appearances with World Championship Wrestling (WCW) as Dutch Mantel and with the World Wrestling Federation (WWF) as Uncle Zebekiah in the early to mid-1990s. In the late 1990s and 2000s he worked as a booker for the World Wrestling Council, the International Wrestling Association and Total Nonstop Action Wrestling. On February 11, 2013, Mantel returned to WWE under the name of Zeb Colter, as the manager of Jack Swagger. Colter's character was that of a racist and xenophobic heel who strongly advocated anti-immigrant beliefs.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":84,"storytelling":86,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":17,"matchLayout":86,"psychology":84,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":20,"technicalCoaching":7,"characterCoaching":71,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":83,"mediaHandling":71,"brandBuilding":55,"socialMediaSavvy":63,"ruleKnowledge":32,"positioning":46,"reactionSpeed":20,"consistency":28,"awareness":84,"judgement":90}},{"id":554,"name":"Sensei","realName":"Sensei","picture":"Sensei.jpg","ability":61,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":55,"charisma":70,"micSkills":41,"popularity":2,"condition":70,"hardcoreAbility":66,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":84,"height":170,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1978-09-16T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1995-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Sensei is a Mexican Luchador enmascarado. Initially the wrestler who would later work as Sensei used the ring name Kundalini when he made his debut in 1995. He was one of the first wrestlers to work for International Wrestling Revolution Group (IWRG) when it formed in 1996. In IWRG he was given the name Fantasy along with a colorful outfit and mask. The year 2000 became his break-out year as he teamed with Black Dragon to reach the finals of a tournament to crown the first ever IWRG Intercontinental Tag Team Champions but lost to Yasushi Kanda and Susumu Mochizuki on January 2, 2000. In 2005 Fantasy left IWRG and joined Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL), changed his gimmick to Sensei and made his debut on June 15, 2005.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":55,"storytelling":61,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":29,"matchLayout":63,"psychology":55,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":52,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":71,"mediaHandling":52,"brandBuilding":49,"socialMediaSavvy":44,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":63,"awareness":55,"judgement":73}},{"id":555,"name":"Leono","realName":"Leono","picture":"Leono.jpg","ability":51,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":55,"charisma":61,"micSkills":51,"popularity":2,"condition":82,"hardcoreAbility":44,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":80,"height":175,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1982-09-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2003-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Leono is a Mexican luchador, whose ring name is the Spanish translation of Lion-O from the ThunderCats cartoon. He began his wrestling career working under the ring name \"Mustang Negro\" (\"Black Mustang\") but only used the name briefly from his debut in 2003 until early 2004. In 2004 he changed his ring name to Leono, the Spanish name for Lion-O of the ThunderCats, which was also reflected in the fact that Leono often had the ThunderCats logo on his trunks. On March 30, 2007 Leono made his first appearance on one of CMLL's major annual shows, teaming with El Sagrado and Volador, Jr. for the 2007 Homenaje a Dos Leyendas (\"Homage to Two Legends\") show. The trio lost to Black Warrior, Misterioso, Jr. and Tarzan Boy two falls to one.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":49,"storytelling":59,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":19,"matchLayout":63,"psychology":49,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":55,"characterCoaching":58,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":81,"mediaHandling":58,"brandBuilding":37,"socialMediaSavvy":47,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":77,"awareness":49,"judgement":69},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-555","wrestlerId":555,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2004-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":556,"name":"Bengala","realName":"Bengala","picture":"Bengala_CMLL.jpg","ability":44,"currentAbility":49,"potentialAbility":49,"charisma":45,"micSkills":63,"popularity":3,"condition":71,"hardcoreAbility":37,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":81,"height":167,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1982-10-17T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1991-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Bengala is a Mexican luchador enmascarado who previously wrestled for many years under the ring name Sombra de Plata but changed his ring persona in 2009, a move that is not acknowledged in storyline terms. He began his professional wrestling career under the ring name Príncipe Odín, Jr. (\"Prince Odin, Jr.), an enmascarado character based on his father Principe Odin, the same name his younger brother would take over. As Principe Odin, Jr. he worked primarily on the Mexican independent circuit from his debut in 1991 until around 1999. A number of wrestlers have used the ring name Sombra de Plata (\"Silver Shadow\") over the years, which leads to some confusion as to who played the role at what point in time. It has been established that the person under the Sombra de Plata mask that made his Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) debut in 1998 was new to the character at the time and the last person to use the ring name up until now.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":39,"storytelling":52,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":47,"matchLayout":57,"psychology":39,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":51,"characterCoaching":36,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":53,"mediaHandling":36,"brandBuilding":36,"socialMediaSavvy":42,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":60,"awareness":39,"judgement":63}},{"id":557,"name":"Niebla Roja","realName":"Niebla Roja","picture":"Niebla Rojo_alt2.jpg","ability":69,"currentAbility":67,"potentialAbility":67,"charisma":76,"micSkills":52,"popularity":9,"condition":89,"hardcoreAbility":61,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":84,"height":175,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1986-07-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Niebla Roja is the current ring name of a Mexican Luchador Enmascarado formerly known as Ángel de Plata. His brother is also a masked luchador working under the ring name Ángel de Oro. In Durango he feuded with his younger brother, in a feud that was so well received by the crowd that both his brother and he received an invitation to train at Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre's (CMLL) wrestling school in Guadalajara, Jalisco. The duo made their CMLL debut on July 4, 2008 wrestling as a team dubbed Los Angeles Celestiales. On March 30, 2012, Ángel de Plata underwent a complete character overhaul, debuting a new mask and attire and switching his ring name to Niebla Roja (\"Red Mist\"), while also turning rudo in the process. On July 6 2012, Niebla Roja was named the newest member of Último Guerrero's Los Guerreros del Infierno stable.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[1175,4286,4287],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":73,"storytelling":76,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":77,"psychology":73,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":78,"technicalCoaching":68,"characterCoaching":69,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":69,"brandBuilding":75,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":78,"consistency":73,"awareness":73,"judgement":84},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-557","wrestlerId":557,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2008-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":558,"name":"Dragón Rojo Jr.","realName":"Dragón Rojo Jr.","picture":"Dragon Rojo.jpg","ability":52,"currentAbility":61,"potentialAbility":61,"charisma":59,"micSkills":61,"popularity":5,"condition":83,"hardcoreAbility":71,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":85,"height":177,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1982-11-03T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2001-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Dragón Rojo, Jr. is the grandson of Dragón Rojo and has previously worked as \"Zaracatán, Jr.\" and \"Diamante Negro\" but has achieved the majority of his success as Dragón Rojo, Jr. After training for two years under Raúl Díaz and Dandy Garcia he made his debut on June 28, 2001 using the name \"Zaracatán Jr.\", a masked técnico (good guy) ring persona. He was named the Lagunero area \"Rookie of the year\" for his work in the local promotion that put on shows in Torreón and Gómez Palacio in Durango. After his rookie year he suffered an injury that forced him out of wrestling for two years while rehabilitating. He and Último Guerrero were the longest reigning CMLL World Tag Team Champions in history.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[1783],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":73,"storytelling":76,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":24,"matchLayout":77,"psychology":73,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":55,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":76,"mediaHandling":55,"brandBuilding":67,"socialMediaSavvy":48,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":67,"awareness":73,"judgement":84},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-558","wrestlerId":558,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2007-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":559,"name":"Rey Escorpión","realName":"Rey Escorpión","picture":"Rey Escorpion.jpg","ability":66,"currentAbility":64,"potentialAbility":64,"charisma":61,"micSkills":61,"popularity":8,"condition":75,"hardcoreAbility":84,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"striker","gender":"M","weight":95,"height":172,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1979-01-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1996-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Fabian Nuñez Napoles is the ring name of Mexican Luchador currently working under the ring name Rey Escorpión. Escorpión began working on and off for Asistencia Asesoría y Administración (AAA) starting around 2000, working primarily on smaller shows when AAA toured the north of Mexico. After leaving AAA Nuñez began working for Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL), the other major wrestling promotion in Mexico. In CMLL he worked as either Escorpión or Scorpión and primarily appeared in the opening match of shows. On January 29 2013, Escorpión defeated Volador Jr. for his first reign as CMLL World Light Heavyweight Champion. After having won the 2011 Gran Alternativa as a rookie, Rey Escorpión participated in the 2013 Gran Alternativa tournament as the experienced wrestler, teaming with rookie Boby Zavala.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":73,"storytelling":75,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":24,"matchLayout":75,"psychology":73,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":62,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":76,"mediaHandling":62,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":55,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":72,"awareness":73,"judgement":84}},{"id":560,"name":"Pólvora","realName":"Pólvora","picture":"Polvora.jpg","ability":60,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":55,"charisma":53,"micSkills":41,"popularity":4,"condition":81,"hardcoreAbility":64,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":85,"height":170,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1979-07-19T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Pólvora  is the ring name of a Mexican Luchador Enmascarado. Pólvora's brother is also a professional wrestler, under the ring name Inquisidor. Pólvora made his professional wrestling debut in 2000, mainly teaming with his brother Vaquero on the Mexican independent circuit. By 2005 both Pólvora and Vaquero began working for Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL), mainly on the promotions minor shows or in the opening match of their big shows from Arena México. Pólvora left Los Cancerberos in late November, 2012 and began teaming up with Rey Escorpión and Dragón Rojo, Jr. in their feud against Escorpión and Rojo's former Los Guerreros del Infierno team mates Último Guerrero, Niebla Roja and former Cancerbero Euforia.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[1183,1783],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":58,"storytelling":65,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":32,"matchLayout":67,"psychology":58,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":65,"technicalCoaching":59,"characterCoaching":54,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":68,"mediaHandling":54,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":54,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":65,"consistency":75,"awareness":58,"judgement":75},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-560","wrestlerId":560,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2002-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":561,"name":"Rey Bucanero","realName":"Rey Bucanero","picture":"Rey Bucanero.jpg","ability":59,"currentAbility":64,"potentialAbility":64,"charisma":57,"micSkills":49,"popularity":9,"condition":71,"hardcoreAbility":54,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":94,"height":175,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1974-07-19T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1991-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Arturo García Ortiz is a Mexican professional wrestler who works under the ring name Rey Bucanero (Buccaneer King). Outside of lucha libre, he has also worked in Japan for New Japan Pro Wrestling, Frontier Martial Arts Wrestling, Toryumon and Dragondoor. After being trained by his uncles and spending several years working undercards for independents and undercards for Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre, he got his first push in late 1996 after winning the Gran Alternativa tournament with Emilio Charles, Jr. He returned to CMLL in 1999 and feuded extensively with Olímpico and the build up pointed to a mask vs. mask match between the two. On June 4, 2013, Bucanero's near two-year reign as the NWA World Historic Light Heavyweight Champion came to an end, when he lost the title to Diamante Azul.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1068,1186,1187],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":76,"storytelling":78,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":16,"matchLayout":79,"psychology":76,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":63,"technicalCoaching":58,"characterCoaching":75,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":84,"mediaHandling":75,"brandBuilding":52,"socialMediaSavvy":66,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":63,"consistency":47,"awareness":76,"judgement":86}},{"id":562,"name":"Volador Jr.","realName":"Volador Jr.","picture":"Volador Jr.jpg","ability":80,"currentAbility":73,"potentialAbility":73,"charisma":68,"micSkills":65,"popularity":26,"condition":82,"hardcoreAbility":66,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":87,"height":172,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1981-01-26T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Heir to the legendary Remo Banda, this fighter can be considered a young experienced in this sport, as his record is truly impressive and he is considered one of the best exponents of this sport worldwide. \r\n\r\nPossessor of a spectacular and suicidal style, little by little he was seizing the affection of the fans, which has placed him as one of their favorites regardless of the side in which he is. \r\n\r\nOn September 13, 2013 his career took a 180 degree turn after having participated in a homerun of masks with a suicide ending to commemorate the 80th Anniversary of the CMLL in which he and La Sombra defeated Atlantis and Último Guerrero to win the right to face in a duel of Mask against Mask between them, from which, he was forced to reveal the face of Ramón Ibarra Rivera.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[2434],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":83,"storytelling":85,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":16,"matchLayout":85,"psychology":83,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":84,"technicalCoaching":77,"characterCoaching":73,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":84,"mediaHandling":73,"brandBuilding":79,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":84,"consistency":73,"awareness":83,"judgement":90},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-562","wrestlerId":562,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2001-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":564,"name":"Negro Casas","realName":"Negro Casas","picture":"Negro Casas.jpg","ability":70,"currentAbility":73,"potentialAbility":73,"charisma":58,"micSkills":67,"popularity":11,"condition":66,"hardcoreAbility":58,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":79,"height":167,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1960-01-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1979-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"A true living legend, Negro Casas is part of the Casas wrestling family. He entered the family business in 1979 and developed into one of the finest talents in lucha libre history, having great matches into his 60s and showing little sign of slowing down. He has also trained several wrestlers, including Konnan, Heavy Metal, Mephisto and Ricky Marvin. Now in the twilight of his career, he remains a top rudo for CMLL.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":5,"teams":[981,2918,2921],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":92,"storytelling":94,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":12,"matchLayout":95,"psychology":92,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":78,"characterCoaching":58,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":88,"mediaHandling":58,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":44,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":73,"awareness":92,"judgement":95},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-564","wrestlerId":564,"promotionId":5,"startDate":"2023-01-21T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":565,"name":"El Felino","realName":"El Felino","picture":"Felino_alt.jpg","ability":63,"currentAbility":68,"potentialAbility":68,"charisma":80,"micSkills":77,"popularity":9,"condition":57,"hardcoreAbility":57,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":86,"height":167,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1964-03-19T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1984-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"El Felino  is the ring name of Jorge Luis Casas Ruiz, who is a Mexican professional wrestler.He is the son of wrestler and referee Pepe Casas, the brother of Negro Casas and Heavy Metal and the cousin of Black Star. His sons are also both wrestlers under the names of Tiger Kid (Tiger in CMLL) and Puma King (Puma in CMLL) respectively, something El Felino subtly acknowledged in the past by wearing a replica of Kid Tiger's tights on at least one occasion. On September 2, 2008 the last Casas brother, El Felino turned Rudo as well and joined La Peste Negra. After Felino joined the group Heavy Metal was quietly phased out as he was not comfortable working the comedic style. On March 15, 2013 El Felino teamd up with his sons Tiger and Puma to defeat the team of Guerrero Maya, Jr., Delta and Tritón in the opening match of the 2013 Homenaje a Dos Leyendas.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":86,"storytelling":87,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":12,"matchLayout":88,"psychology":86,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":58,"technicalCoaching":70,"characterCoaching":65,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":88,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":49,"socialMediaSavvy":55,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":58,"consistency":65,"awareness":86,"judgement":92},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-565","wrestlerId":565,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"1999-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":566,"name":"Felino Jr.","realName":"Felino Jr.","picture":"Tiger.jpg","ability":68,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"charisma":66,"micSkills":61,"popularity":7,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":43,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":79,"height":175,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1987-02-12T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2006-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Tiger is a Mexican Luchador enmascarado. He was previously known by the ring name Tiger Kid but the name was shortened in June 2011. He frequently teams with his brother, luchador Puma King. He is part of the Casas wrestling family, son of El Felino using a ring character and a mask very similar to his father and has been trained by his uncle, professional wrestler Negro Casas. nitially Tiger Kid worked for International Wrestling Revolution Group (IWRG) but began making appearances in Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) by 2007, also training at their wrestling school in Guadalajara, Jalisco under CMLL trainers El Hijo del Gladiador, Franco Columbo, Satánico, Ringo Mendoza and Virus.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[1534],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":72,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":73,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":79,"technicalCoaching":68,"characterCoaching":44,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":44,"brandBuilding":60,"socialMediaSavvy":32,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":79,"consistency":73,"awareness":68,"judgement":81},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-566","wrestlerId":566,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2007-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":567,"name":"Puma King","realName":"Puma King","picture":"Puma King.jpg","ability":60,"currentAbility":63,"potentialAbility":63,"charisma":49,"micSkills":56,"popularity":10,"condition":88,"hardcoreAbility":75,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":90,"height":172,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1990-07-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2006-11-28T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Puma King is a masked Mexican luchador who works in America, Mexico, the British Isles, Japan and Europe. He is a Lightweight who is classed as using a Luchador style. He is best known for his work with CMLL, AAA, DDT, PWG, MLW and IWRG.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1534],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":67,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":40,"matchLayout":69,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":75,"technicalCoaching":72,"characterCoaching":69,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":60,"mediaHandling":69,"brandBuilding":69,"socialMediaSavvy":53,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":75,"consistency":56,"awareness":62,"judgement":77}},{"id":568,"name":"Mephisto","realName":"Mephisto","picture":"Mephisto.jpg","ability":64,"currentAbility":71,"potentialAbility":71,"charisma":59,"micSkills":84,"popularity":8,"condition":71,"hardcoreAbility":68,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":90,"height":172,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1968-12-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1988-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Mephisto whose birth name is unknown, is a Mexican professional wrestler. Mephisto is the son of Luchador Astro Rey/Kahoz and has previously worked both as Astro Rey Jr. and Kahoz Jr. but has been most successful as Mephisto. Since adopting the Mephisto gimmick he has been associated with the group Los Infernales especially Averno who has been his regular tag team partner for years. Mephisto and Averno are considered one of the top permanent teams in Mexico since 2000. After training under his father, and his uncle the Luchador known as \"El Gallo Giro\" he made his debut as \"Kahoz Jr.\", as a tribute to his dad’s last gimmick. From 1988 until 1993 he wrestled as Kahoz Jr. His father, however, urged him to change gimmicks to the one that got his father the most fame \"Astro Rey Jr.\".","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[1189],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":84,"storytelling":85,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":15,"matchLayout":86,"psychology":84,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":70,"characterCoaching":71,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":85,"mediaHandling":71,"brandBuilding":56,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":78,"awareness":84,"judgement":90},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-568","wrestlerId":568,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"1992-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":569,"name":"Ephesto","realName":"Ephesto","picture":"Ephisto.jpg","ability":64,"currentAbility":66,"potentialAbility":66,"charisma":53,"micSkills":76,"popularity":5,"condition":61,"hardcoreAbility":84,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":95,"height":175,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1965-06-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1982-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Ephesto is a Mexican Luchador Enmascarado. His current ring name \"Ephesto\" is derived from the Spanish name for Hephaestus, the Greek God of fire, Hefesto. Ephesto is a member of the stable Los Hijos de Averno (Spanish for the sons of Hell) with Averno and Mephisto. He made his debut in 1982 at the age of 16 after training with Halco Suriano, Asterión, Satánico and Blue Panther. His first ring persona was Pantera del Ring (Spanish for the Panther of the Ring), a masked luchador with a panther inspired mask and trunks, inspired by his trainer Blue Panther. In late 2005, only months after losing the Trios titles Safair became El Hombre sin Nombre (Spanish for \"The Man without name\"), a ring persona & name that indicates that the wrestler is a \"blank slate\", as he has no name and wrestles in plain black clothes & mask. CMLL started a contest for the fans to come up with a new name and ring persona for this wrestler. He became Ephesto in 2007.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[2854],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":82,"storytelling":82,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":82,"psychology":82,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":60,"technicalCoaching":58,"characterCoaching":64,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":64,"brandBuilding":48,"socialMediaSavvy":53,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":60,"consistency":68,"awareness":82,"judgement":89},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-569","wrestlerId":569,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2000-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":570,"name":"Black Warrior","realName":"Black Warrior","picture":"Black Warrior.jpg","ability":46,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":55,"charisma":45,"micSkills":48,"popularity":4,"condition":66,"hardcoreAbility":38,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":90,"height":177,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1969-01-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1984-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":true,"story":"Jesus Toral López is a luchador who has worked almost exclusively in Mexico. López has achieved most success under the ring name Black Warrior and had worked for Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) since 1995. Before assuming the \"Black Warrior\" ring persona, López worked for almost a decade under various ring personas, generally with little success. His only previous ring persona of note was that of \"Bronce\" (Spanish for Bronze) where he was a part of the \"Los Metalicos\" team, a team that was popular in the early 1990s, teaming with Oro and Plata. López is the nephew of Luchador Blue Panther, the son-in-law of Mana Negro and the brother-in-law of Mano Negro, Jr. On June 20, 2012, Black Warrior turned rudo and formed the Los Depredadores del Aire.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":54,"storytelling":62,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":64,"psychology":54,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":58,"technicalCoaching":61,"characterCoaching":49,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":49,"brandBuilding":42,"socialMediaSavvy":35,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":58,"consistency":75,"awareness":54,"judgement":72}},{"id":571,"name":"Mr. Aguila","realName":"Mr. Aguila","picture":"Mr Aguila.jpg","ability":48,"currentAbility":57,"potentialAbility":57,"charisma":65,"micSkills":63,"popularity":8,"condition":72,"hardcoreAbility":45,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":107,"height":185,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1977-12-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1994-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Jose Seldano is a Mexican professional wrestler. He is best known in the US for his work in the World Wrestling Federation as Essa Ríos and for his work for Total Nonstop Action Wrestling (TNA), CMLL and Asistencia Asesoría y Administración (AAA) as Mr. Águila. Saldaña made his debut in the WWF on the November 3, 1997 episode of Raw is War as part of its newly relaunched Light Heavyweight division at the age of 18, wrestling under the Ring name Águila. He had a high-flying match with Michinoku during ECW's 1999 Cyberslam event before capturing the WWF Light Heavyweight title from Gillberg on his 'debut' as Essa Ríos during February 13, 2000 edition of Sunday Night Heat. On May 16, 2010, Mr. Águila returned to CMLL, interfering in a match between Psicosis II and La Sombra, siding with Psicosis II and a group called Los Invasores.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1271,3197],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":54,"storytelling":62,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":33,"matchLayout":64,"psychology":54,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":65,"technicalCoaching":55,"characterCoaching":62,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":67,"mediaHandling":62,"brandBuilding":57,"socialMediaSavvy":53,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":65,"consistency":55,"awareness":54,"judgement":72}},{"id":572,"name":"Olímpico","realName":"Olímpico","picture":"Olimpico_alt.jpg","ability":67,"currentAbility":70,"potentialAbility":70,"charisma":75,"micSkills":70,"popularity":4,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":84,"injuryProne":100,"type":"referee","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":92,"height":177,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1965-12-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1992-09-13T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Joel Bernal Galicia better known under the ring name Olímpico is a Mexican Luchador. Olímpico is sometimes Anglicised as \"Olympico\", and means \"Olympian\" in Spanish. From his debut in 1992 until late 2008 Olímpico worked for Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL), since then he has worked for Promociones Perros del Mal, International Wrestling Revolution Group (IWRG), World Wrestling Alliance (WWA) and the Mexican independent circuit before returning to CMLL in mid-2010 as part of Los Invasores. For many years Olimpico's real name was not a matter of public record, as is often the case with masked wrestlers in Mexico where their private lives are kept a secret from the wrestling fans. He was unmasked on September 3, 2010 and had to reveal his real name.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":84,"storytelling":85,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":85,"psychology":84,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":52,"technicalCoaching":71,"characterCoaching":47,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":47,"brandBuilding":34,"socialMediaSavvy":36,"ruleKnowledge":70,"positioning":76,"reactionSpeed":52,"consistency":58,"awareness":84,"judgement":90},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-572","wrestlerId":572,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2010-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":573,"name":"Psicosis II","realName":"Psicosis II","picture":"Psicosis II.jpg","ability":68,"currentAbility":59,"potentialAbility":59,"charisma":64,"micSkills":74,"popularity":5,"condition":76,"hardcoreAbility":79,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":85,"height":172,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1967-02-22T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1992-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Juan Ebodio Gonzalez is a Mexican Luchador enmascarado better known under the ring name Psicosis. Gonzalez was the second wrestler to work as Psicosis, given the ring character by Asistencia Asesoría y Administración (AAA) to replace the Original Psicosis, and is often denoted Psicosis II. When Gonzalez left AAA in early 2009 he was briefly replaced by a third Psicosis. He is not referred to as \"Psicosis II\" on promotional material, instead the name is used to distinguish himself from the original Psicosis. Juan Gonzalez was trained by his father, who wrestled under the ring name El Puma. Upon his debut he began working as El Puma, Jr. mainly in the Puebla region and in Tijuana, Baja California. When he began wrestling in Tijuana in 1994 he received additional training by Rey Misterio, Sr. and also adopted the ring persona \"León Negro\".","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":71,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":29,"matchLayout":72,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":68,"technicalCoaching":55,"characterCoaching":65,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":71,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":48,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":68,"consistency":63,"awareness":68,"judgement":81}},{"id":574,"name":"Histeria","realName":"Histeria","picture":"Histeria.jpg","ability":45,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":55,"charisma":45,"micSkills":65,"popularity":5,"condition":80,"hardcoreAbility":73,"injuryProne":99,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":90,"height":167,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1969-06-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1985-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Histeria is a Mexican luchador enmascarado, currently working under the ring name Morphosis. Histeria is best known for the 14 years he worked for Asistencia Asesoría y Administración (AAA), until leaving in 2009. He is the second person to wrestle as \"Histeria\", taking over from the previous wrestler who became known as Super Crazy. Histeria's real name is not a matter of public record, as is often the case with masked wrestlers in Mexico where their private lives are kept a secret from the wrestling fans. On April 12, 2010 a contingent of former AAA wrestlers including Histeria, Psicosis II, Maniaco, El Alebrije and Cuije appeared on a Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) show in Puebla, Puebla. The group drove into the arena in a black SUV and attacked La Sombra, El Hijo del Fantasma and La Máscara after they just finished wrestling.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":49,"storytelling":59,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":47,"matchLayout":62,"psychology":49,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":69,"technicalCoaching":55,"characterCoaching":47,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":53,"mediaHandling":47,"brandBuilding":60,"socialMediaSavvy":40,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":69,"consistency":78,"awareness":49,"judgement":69}},{"id":575,"name":"Vangellys","realName":"Vangellys","picture":"Vangellys.jpg","ability":53,"currentAbility":54,"potentialAbility":54,"charisma":42,"micSkills":52,"popularity":3,"condition":64,"hardcoreAbility":72,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":95,"height":180,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1981-09-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Vangelis, sometimes spelled Vangellys is the ring name of a Mexican luchador. He quickly began working for Asistencia Asesoría y Administración (AAA), training at their school while only occasionally wrestling on their television shows. Vangelis was teamed up with Jimmy Boy and Billy to form a boy band inspired group called Los Spice Boys. In 2001 Vangelis was given a new ring character, that of a Nazi soldier, complete with swastika armband and the Nazi salute. In 2005 Vangelis traveled to Japan to work for an extended period of time in the Japanese Dragon Gate promotion. On December 4, 2007 Vangelis worked his first match for Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL).","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":58,"storytelling":62,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":30,"matchLayout":64,"psychology":58,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":63,"technicalCoaching":47,"characterCoaching":51,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":70,"mediaHandling":51,"brandBuilding":49,"socialMediaSavvy":45,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":63,"consistency":58,"awareness":58,"judgement":75}},{"id":576,"name":"Sangre Azteca","realName":"Sangre Azteca","picture":"Sangre Azteca.jpg","ability":60,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"charisma":52,"micSkills":53,"popularity":3,"condition":82,"hardcoreAbility":52,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":81,"height":167,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1975-11-05T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1996-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Sangre Azteca is a Mexican luchador enmascarado. After getting trained by Scorpio and Raúl Reyes, he made his debut at the age of 21 and had a win during his debut match. In 1999, 2001, 2003, 2004, and 2005, Sangre Azteca participated in the Gran Alternativa, but failed to make it past the qualifying round each year. During a Mexican National Welterweight Championship defense against Dragón Rojo, Jr., the two went to a double count out, which led Sangre Azteca to state that he was impressed by Rojo's ability. The two soon began working together along with Black Warrior to form the group Poder Mexica.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":51,"storytelling":61,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":64,"psychology":51,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":67,"technicalCoaching":66,"characterCoaching":42,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":42,"brandBuilding":29,"socialMediaSavvy":33,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":67,"consistency":71,"awareness":51,"judgement":71}},{"id":577,"name":"Virus","realName":"Virus","picture":"Virus.jpg","ability":69,"currentAbility":76,"potentialAbility":76,"charisma":67,"micSkills":74,"popularity":7,"condition":69,"hardcoreAbility":88,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":79,"height":162,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1968-12-09T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1986-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Ricardo Amezquita Cardeño is a Mexican Luchador best known under the ring name, Virus. As Virus Amezquita has held the CMLL Japan Super Lightweight Championship, CMLL World Super Lightweight Championship and the Mexican National Lightweight Championship and is currently the leader of Los Cancerberos del Infierno. Ricardo Amezquita made his professional wrestling debut on April 20, 1986, under the ring name \"Bird Boy\", an enmascarado with a bird inspired ring persona. Because of his small size he mainly worked on the low end of the card in the Universal Wrestling Association promotion. In early 1998 he made his debut as part of the regular sized division under the name \"Virus\", no mention was made that Virus used to work as Damiancito El Guerrero or the fact that he still held the CMLL World Mini-Estrella Championship.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":89,"storytelling":92,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":7,"matchLayout":93,"psychology":89,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":86,"characterCoaching":65,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":93,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":44,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":77,"awareness":89,"judgement":93},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-577","wrestlerId":577,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"1992-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":578,"name":"Raziel","realName":"Raziel","picture":"Raziel.jpg","ability":45,"currentAbility":54,"potentialAbility":54,"charisma":58,"micSkills":39,"popularity":4,"condition":82,"hardcoreAbility":55,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":85,"height":167,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1973-02-08T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1996-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":true,"story":"Raziel is the ring name of a Mexican Luchador Enmascarado. The name Raziel is taken from the name of an Archangel in Jewish mysticism and is some times also written as \"Raciel\". The wrestler who is currently known as Raziel trained under Skayde and Aaron Alvarado Nieves, better known as Brazo Cibernetico and was considered one of their top pupils at the time. Upon his debut in 1996 he adopted the ring persona \"Neo\", teaming up with a fellow Skayde/Alvarado graduate who wrestled as \"Geo\", both enmascarados (masked wrestlers) who wrestled a high flying style. On November 18, 2009 CMLL presented a new Rudo group that they had formed, Los Cancerberos del Infierno (\"The Infernal Cerberus\") a team led by veteran mid-carder Virus and consisted of rookies Pólvora and Euforia as well as two new characters never used before - Raziel and Cancerberos. It was later revealed that Raziel and Cancerbero were not two new wrestlers CMLL brought in but actually the repackaged Los Romanos.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[196,1182],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":61,"storytelling":68,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":31,"matchLayout":70,"psychology":61,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":64,"characterCoaching":53,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":69,"mediaHandling":53,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":53,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":67,"awareness":61,"judgement":77}},{"id":579,"name":"Cancerbero","realName":"Cancerbero","picture":"Cancerbero.jpg","ability":62,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"charisma":55,"micSkills":57,"popularity":4,"condition":74,"hardcoreAbility":48,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":90,"height":177,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1977-01-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1997-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Daniel Nuñez Hernandez is a Mexican Luchador Enmascarado currently working under the ring name Cancerbero. Hernandez began his wrestling career using the ring name El Potro )(\"The Colt\") and later on wrestled as El Monstruo I, teaming with El Monstruo II. El Monstruo I was unmasked by Gran Cuchillo on December 8, 2002 when he lost a Lucha de Apuesta, bet match. In 2005 he began working for Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) and was teamed up with another recent CMLL signee. CMLL gave Hernandez a new identity as Messala, the ring persona was that of a roman soldier complete with a mask designed to look like a Roman soldier's helmet. On November 18, 2009 CMLL presented a new Rudo group that they had formed, Los Cancerberos del Infierno (\"The Infernal Cerberus\") a team led by veteran mid-carder Virus and consisted of rookies Pólvora and Euforia as well as two new characters never used before - Raziel and Cancerberos.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[196,1182],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":67,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":51,"matchLayout":68,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":64,"technicalCoaching":67,"characterCoaching":51,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":49,"mediaHandling":51,"brandBuilding":30,"socialMediaSavvy":39,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":64,"consistency":62,"awareness":62,"judgement":77},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-579","wrestlerId":579,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2002-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":580,"name":"Nitro","realName":"Nitro","picture":"Nitro.jpg","ability":65,"currentAbility":66,"potentialAbility":66,"charisma":62,"micSkills":61,"popularity":3,"condition":66,"hardcoreAbility":56,"injuryProne":83,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":84,"height":170,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1966-08-15T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1984-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Nitro is a Mexican professional wrestler. In early 1992, Nitro joined CMLL and was gimmicked as Filiso as a tecnico who was in the undercards. By 1996 Filiso tried to participate for the Torneo Gran Alternativa but failed to make it. Later on in 2005, he joined the team call Pandilla Guerrera also including Sangre Azteca and Doctor X. In early 2009, Nitro was injured and was undergoing double knee surgery which let him 8 months out of action. By the late 2009 Nitro was able to return in full conditions. Nitro kept teaming with his teammates Guerreros Tuareg in CMLL on the undercard matches. Nitro suffered a broken knee-cap during a match on August 15, 2012.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":79,"storytelling":81,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":36,"matchLayout":82,"psychology":79,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":55,"technicalCoaching":58,"characterCoaching":65,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":64,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":42,"socialMediaSavvy":53,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":55,"consistency":53,"awareness":79,"judgement":87},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-580","wrestlerId":580,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"1992-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":583,"name":"Disturbio","realName":"Disturbio","picture":"Disturbio.jpg","ability":53,"currentAbility":56,"potentialAbility":56,"charisma":49,"micSkills":70,"popularity":4,"condition":87,"hardcoreAbility":43,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":85,"height":165,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1979-03-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Disturbio is the ring name of Israel Aguilar Alvarez, a Mexican luchador. Aguilar made his professional wrestling debut on December 22, 2004 working on the Mexican Independent circuit, particularly for King Bulls Wrestling (KBW) that promoted shows primarily in Tampico, Tamaulipas. Disturbio began working regularly for CMLL in 2009, making his Arena Mexico debut on CMLL's main show, Super Viernes on April 9, 2009 as he teamed up with Durango Kid to defeat Bengala and Delta. A week later he was teamed up with El Terrible to participate in the 2010 Gran Alternativa.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":52,"storytelling":60,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":47,"matchLayout":62,"psychology":52,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":51,"characterCoaching":47,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":53,"mediaHandling":47,"brandBuilding":49,"socialMediaSavvy":40,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":78,"awareness":52,"judgement":71},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-583","wrestlerId":583,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2007-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":584,"name":"Gran Guerrero","realName":"Gran Guerrero","picture":"Gran Guerrero.jpg","ability":72,"currentAbility":62,"potentialAbility":62,"charisma":66,"micSkills":77,"popularity":8,"condition":93,"hardcoreAbility":52,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":99,"height":172,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1993-07-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Taurus is a Mexican luchador enmascarado. He was originally introduced to the wrestling world under the ring name \"Último Guerrero, Jr.\" in 2008 by his father Último Guerrero, but he made his wrestling debut under the name Taurus, with no official acknowledgment of the family relationship by CMLL. In 2008 Último Guerrero introduced \"Último Guerrero, Jr.\" to the wrestling world and while it is not uncommon for fake relatives to be promoted in Lucha Libre, there was a legitimate blood relationship between the two. He would later adopt the ring name \"Taurus\" in order to gain experience as a wrestler before using the name full time. Shortly after his DragonMania VII appearance Taurus was announced as part of Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre's (CMLL) Generacion 2012, a group of young wrestlers who made their debut in 2012. It recently came to light that Taurus was actually the younger brother of Ultimo Guerrero - whatever the relationship he is related to Ultimo Guerrero one way or another.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":66,"storytelling":69,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":30,"matchLayout":70,"psychology":66,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":76,"technicalCoaching":55,"characterCoaching":58,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":70,"mediaHandling":58,"brandBuilding":76,"socialMediaSavvy":45,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":76,"consistency":64,"awareness":66,"judgement":80},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-584","wrestlerId":584,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2012-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":585,"name":"Inquisidor","realName":"Inquisidor","picture":"Inquisidor.jpg","ability":63,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":53,"charisma":38,"micSkills":54,"popularity":3,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":59,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":75,"height":167,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1977-03-24T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1995-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Inquisidor is the current ring name of Juan Miguel Escalante Grande, a Mexican luchador enmascarado. Escalante started out wrestling in the Mini-Estrella division, which in Mexico is more than just midget professional wrestling exclusively for little people, but also includes a number of wrestlers who just happen to be short compared to the average. In 2000 Escalante's brother made his professional wrestling debut, working under the name Pólvora (\"Gunpowder\"), which lead Vaquerito to leave the Mini-Estrellas division and work as simply \"Vaquero\". He made his in ring debut as Inquisidor on July 8, 2008 unveiling his new look that included a mask that covered his entire face except for his eyes with a design that was mainly black but with a stylized red axe on the front of it.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":60,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":38,"matchLayout":62,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":66,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":49,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":62,"mediaHandling":49,"brandBuilding":62,"socialMediaSavvy":40,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":66,"consistency":56,"awareness":56,"judgement":74},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-585","wrestlerId":585,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"1998-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":587,"name":"El Satánico","realName":"El Satánico","picture":"Satanico.jpg","ability":73,"currentAbility":73,"potentialAbility":73,"charisma":60,"micSkills":85,"popularity":5,"condition":56,"hardcoreAbility":86,"injuryProne":83,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":97,"height":172,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1949-10-26T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1973-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Daniel López López is a Mexican Luchador, or professional wrestler best known under the ring name Satánico. As Satánico he's best known for his decade long relationship with a wrestling group called Los Infernales as he's been the core member of various combinations of the group from the middle of the 1980s until 2007. López made his professional wrestling debut on June 17, 1973 using the name El Satánico Dr. No (\"The Satanic Dr. No\") named after the James Bond movie villain Dr. No. After a few months the name was shortened to just \"El Satánico\". He was originally an enmascarado but lost his mask as a result of a Lucha de Apuesta, or \"bet match\" against El Vengador on January 4, 1974. In 2009 Satánico announced that he was reducing the number of shows he worked to focus on his work at CMLL’s wrestling school.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":100,"storytelling":100,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":15,"matchLayout":100,"psychology":100,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":55,"technicalCoaching":74,"characterCoaching":68,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":85,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":48,"socialMediaSavvy":54,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":55,"consistency":73,"awareness":100,"judgement":100},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-587","wrestlerId":587,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2021-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":588,"name":"Espanto Jr.","realName":"Espanto Jr.","picture":"Espanto Jr.jpg","ability":50,"currentAbility":51,"potentialAbility":51,"charisma":64,"micSkills":51,"popularity":4,"condition":85,"hardcoreAbility":40,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":90,"height":170,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1986-03-29T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2001-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Espanto Jr. is a Mexican luchador enmascarado. He is the son of the original Espanto, Jr. and part of an extensive wrestling family. The wrestler later known as Espanto, Jr. made his debut in October or 2001 under the name El Moro, Jr. a tribute to both his father and grandfather. Initially he worked primarily at the Andrade family owned Arena Olimpico Laguna in Gómez Palacio, Durango, Mexico. In 2010 he adopted the ring identity of El Hijo del Pentagón, or \"The Son of Pentagón\" based on the Pentagón character that his father was the first wrestler to play. In 2012 Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) introduced their Generacion 2012, (\"Generation 2012\"), basically the 2012 \"graduating class\" from CMLL's wrestling school which Espanto Jr was a part of.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[3070],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":52,"storytelling":57,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":38,"matchLayout":58,"psychology":52,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":60,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":55,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":62,"mediaHandling":55,"brandBuilding":55,"socialMediaSavvy":47,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":60,"consistency":74,"awareness":52,"judgement":71},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-588","wrestlerId":588,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2012-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":590,"name":"Dr. Alfonso Morales","realName":"Dr. Alfonso Morales","picture":"Alfonso Morales.jpg","ability":0,"currentAbility":0,"potentialAbility":0,"charisma":13,"micSkills":8,"popularity":6,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":19,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":97,"height":170,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1949-02-04T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1979-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":true,"story":"Dr. Alfonso Morales is a popular Mexican wrestling announcer, he is fan of technical wrestling, and has worked in AAA, CMLL, EMLL and others as a broadcaster for Televisa. He's also hosted the the program \"Las noches del Santo\" (Santo's night). Morales is the current director of the Box Y Lucha Magazine and also works as a commentator for boxing matches. On the week Tinieblas debuted, lucha announcer Dr. Alfonso Morales was absent. Dr. Morales missing a show is a strange event, he's a tall man, and Tinieblas is a tall man, so some believed the announcer was actually under the mask. This is not true. Morales is not Tinieblas, and has done commentary on his matches. Despite the evidence to the contrary, the urban legend of Morales being Tinieblas still surfaces from time to time.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":54,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":54,"brandBuilding":16,"socialMediaSavvy":48,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":0,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0}},{"id":591,"name":"Miguel Linares","realName":"Miguel Linares","picture":"Miguel Linares.jpg","ability":71,"currentAbility":75,"potentialAbility":75,"charisma":60,"micSkills":87,"popularity":3,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":68,"injuryProne":54,"type":"commentator","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":73,"height":162,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1962-03-22T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1980-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Miguel Linares is a Mexican announcer. He is probably best known for calling the action for CMLL alongside Alfonso Morales and Leobardo Magadan on Televisa in Mexico.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":49,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":49,"brandBuilding":22,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":0,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-591","wrestlerId":591,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2020-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":592,"name":"Rafa El Maya","realName":"Rafa El Maya","picture":"Rafael Maya.jpg","ability":70,"currentAbility":78,"potentialAbility":78,"charisma":67,"micSkills":65,"popularity":1,"condition":55,"hardcoreAbility":87,"injuryProne":100,"type":"referee","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":82,"height":162,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1952-11-25T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1973-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":true,"story":"Rafa El Maya was a Mexican luchador who passed away on 03 August 2025.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":33,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":33,"brandBuilding":25,"socialMediaSavvy":20,"ruleKnowledge":78,"positioning":62,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0}},{"id":593,"name":"Bestia Negra I","realName":"Bestia Negra I","picture":"Bestia Negra I.jpg","ability":66,"currentAbility":73,"potentialAbility":73,"charisma":67,"micSkills":71,"popularity":2,"condition":50,"hardcoreAbility":93,"injuryProne":69,"type":"referee","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":94,"height":170,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1963-01-21T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1981-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Bestia I is a Mexican referee. He was a midcard wrestler for all of his career throughout the 70's and 80's. After retiring he stuck around the world of Lucha Libre and eventually became a referee in CMLL.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":73,"storytelling":72,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":63,"matchLayout":71,"psychology":73,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":4,"characterCoaching":50,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":37,"mediaHandling":50,"brandBuilding":5,"socialMediaSavvy":40,"ruleKnowledge":73,"positioning":78,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":22,"awareness":73,"judgement":84},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-593","wrestlerId":593,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2004-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":594,"name":"Sarah Stock","realName":"Sarah Stock","picture":"Sarah Stock.jpg","ability":82,"currentAbility":86,"potentialAbility":86,"charisma":80,"micSkills":94,"popularity":8,"condition":71,"hardcoreAbility":90,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"high flyer","gender":"F","weight":57,"height":165,"base":"Canada","birthplace":"Canada","dateOfBirth":"1979-03-04T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Sarah Stock  is a Canadian professional wrestler. She is most notably known under the ring name Dark Angel and is also known for her time in Total Nonstop Action Wrestling (TNA), where, under the ring name Sarita, she became a two-time TNA Knockouts Tag Team Champion, holding the title once with both Taylor Wilde and Rosita. Stock has wrestled for many independent promotions throughout North America, facing both male and female wrestlers. Stock began training as a professional wrestler in Winnipeg, Manitoba's Top Rope Championship Wrestling. In 2003, in an effort to improve her skills in the wrestling ring, Stock moved to Monterrey, Mexico to face the female wrestlers there. Upon returning to Mexico, Stock signed with Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL), AAA's rival promotion. She began working regularly for CMLL as Dark Angel in the promotion's newly-rebuilt women's division.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[2683,2784],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":72,"storytelling":76,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":77,"psychology":72,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":67,"characterCoaching":66,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":66,"brandBuilding":56,"socialMediaSavvy":50,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":70,"awareness":72,"judgement":83}},{"id":595,"name":"Marcela","realName":"Marcela","picture":"marcela.jpg","ability":58,"currentAbility":67,"potentialAbility":67,"charisma":57,"micSkills":81,"popularity":6,"condition":66,"hardcoreAbility":68,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"F","weight":60,"height":152,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1971-05-31T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1985-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"María Elena Santamaría Gómez is a Mexican professional wrestler, known mainly for her work in the Mexican professional wrestling promotion Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL), where she works under the ring name Marcela. María Santamaría made her professional wrestling debut in 1985, using the ring name \"Marcela\" and initially worked on the Mexican independent circuit. In the early 1990s she began working for Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL). In the mid-1990s and early 2000s CMLL did not focus on their women's division, which meant that Marcela also worked for a variety of other minor Mexican promotions. On December 9, 2012 Marcela defeated Ludark Shaitan to win the Xtreme Mexican Wrestling XMW Women's Championship.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[2450,2451],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":82,"storytelling":84,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":85,"psychology":82,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":65,"characterCoaching":63,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":63,"brandBuilding":55,"socialMediaSavvy":47,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":68,"awareness":82,"judgement":89},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-595","wrestlerId":595,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"1997-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":596,"name":"Koji Kanemoto","realName":"Koji Kanemoto","picture":"Koji Kanemoto.jpg","ability":64,"currentAbility":70,"potentialAbility":70,"charisma":74,"micSkills":60,"popularity":7,"condition":61,"hardcoreAbility":51,"injuryProne":87,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":80,"height":177,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1966-10-31T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1990-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Koji Kanemoto is a Japanese professional wrestler of Zainichi Korean descent. Best known for working with New Japan Pro-Wrestling. Has been one of the greats of the Junior Heavyweight division for decades. Even has strong showings against heavyweights due to his great strikes and submission skills. Kanemoto was the first man to defend the IWGP Junior Heavyweight Championship in the United States, a match against Alex Wright at Starrcade '95: World Cup of Wrestling (although World Championship Wrestling did not announce it as such). On June 14, 2009 Kanemoto forced Prince Devitt to submit to his trademark Ankle Lock, winning the Best of the Super Juniors tournament for the third time, becoming only the second man to do so. Now, with injuries and age catching up with him, he's taken to a relaxed schedule.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1125,1519,2972,2973,2974,3020,3046,3223,3224,3225],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":79,"storytelling":83,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":84,"psychology":79,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":66,"technicalCoaching":73,"characterCoaching":55,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":55,"brandBuilding":55,"socialMediaSavvy":49,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":66,"consistency":54,"awareness":79,"judgement":87}},{"id":597,"name":"Beth Phoenix","realName":"Beth Phoenix","picture":"Beth Phoenix.jpg","ability":64,"currentAbility":63,"potentialAbility":63,"charisma":58,"micSkills":73,"popularity":34,"condition":77,"hardcoreAbility":73,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"F","weight":68,"height":167,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1980-11-24T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"No female competitor ever dominated her division as convincingly as Beth Phoenix.\r\n\r\nWhile watching WWE with her grandmother on weekend mornings as a young girl, Phoenix knew her calling was to crush the competition in pursuit of in-ring glory. By high school, she was already blazing trails, becoming the first female on her school’s varsity wrestling team.\r\n\r\nAfter graduating from college with a degree in criminal justice in hand, Phoenix pursued WWE, hoping to bring her own brand of justice to the women’s division. Early on, she laid down the law in WWE, but following some encouraging early wins, her momentum unexpectedly stalled when her jaw was artfully rearranged during a match against Victoria. A year later, with her mandible fully repaired, Phoenix picked up right where she left off … dominating the field, but now as the self-appointed “Glamazon.”","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[2770],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":72,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":74,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":68,"technicalCoaching":49,"characterCoaching":64,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":64,"brandBuilding":70,"socialMediaSavvy":61,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":68,"consistency":78,"awareness":68,"judgement":81}},{"id":599,"name":"Estrellita","realName":"Estrellita","picture":"Estrellita.jpg","ability":54,"currentAbility":44,"potentialAbility":44,"charisma":34,"micSkills":59,"popularity":4,"condition":77,"hardcoreAbility":39,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"F","weight":58,"height":162,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1977-10-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1993-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"\"La Britney Spears de la Lucha\" Estrellita is the ring name of Viviana Ochoa Barradas a Mexican luchadora. Ochoa is the grand daughter of professional wrestler Rafael Barradas and decided to follow in his footsteps, becoming a professional wrestler herself in 1993 under the ring name Estrellita, Spanish for \"Little Star\". Estrellita began working for Asistencia Asesoría y Administración (AAA) around 1997 as a tecnica. She participated in AAA's second annual Reina de Reina (\"Queen of Queens\") tournament, but did not win it. In September 2010 Estrellita appeared in Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) as part of a group called Los Invasores, former AAA wrestlers playing off a storyline that they were \"invading\" CMLL. This marked the first time that Estrellita worked as ruda.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":53,"storytelling":54,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":54,"psychology":53,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":54,"technicalCoaching":42,"characterCoaching":60,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":55,"socialMediaSavvy":51,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":54,"consistency":65,"awareness":53,"judgement":72}},{"id":600,"name":"La Silueta","realName":"La Silueta","picture":"Silueta.jpg","ability":62,"currentAbility":59,"potentialAbility":59,"charisma":74,"micSkills":56,"popularity":5,"condition":88,"hardcoreAbility":57,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"F","weight":57,"height":157,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1985-12-15T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2006-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Silueta is the ring name of Joana Guadalupe Jiménez Hernández a Mexican luchadora. She originally worked as an enmascarada, or masked wrestler but was forced to unmask after losing a match to Zeuxis. She began her training for a professional wrestling career at the age of only 13, training in the wrestling school of Francisco Gaitan. She made her professional wrestling debut in 2006 and received additional training from Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) trainers Máscara Mágica II, Gran Cochisse and El Satánico. CMLL decided to book Silueta in a storyline with ruda newcomer Zeuxis that developed over the summer of 2010. The storyline started out with the two being on opposite sides of a number of Best two out of three falls six-woman tag team matches where Zeuxis would focus on trying to unmask her opponent, going so far as to rip Silueta's mask apart, causing Siluta to respond in kind. The storyline led to a Luchas de Apuestas.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":65,"storytelling":69,"productFit":84,"riskTaking":24,"matchLayout":71,"psychology":65,"workerManagement":84,"trainingIntensity":72,"technicalCoaching":60,"characterCoaching":64,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":76,"mediaHandling":64,"brandBuilding":59,"socialMediaSavvy":24,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":17,"reactionSpeed":72,"consistency":72,"awareness":65,"judgement":73},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-600","wrestlerId":600,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2008-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":601,"name":"Luna Mágica","realName":"Luna Mágica","picture":"Luna Magica.jpg","ability":43,"currentAbility":49,"potentialAbility":49,"charisma":42,"micSkills":56,"popularity":2,"condition":80,"hardcoreAbility":55,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"F","weight":55,"height":147,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1978-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1996-04-08T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Luna Mágica  is the ring name of Maria De Los Angeles Aranda Ramirez. Maria Aranda and Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) Booking team member Franco Colombo have at least one child together, born in early 2009. Aranda took over 18 months off from wrestling while pregnant, due to complications with her pregnancy. Aranda made her professional wrestling debut in 1996, working under the ring name Luna Mágica, initially competing on the independent circuit including the Monterrey based Lucha Libre Femenil promotion. In 2005 CMLL restarted their women's division, adding a number of female competitors to their roster including Luna Mágica.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":42,"storytelling":54,"productFit":60,"riskTaking":33,"matchLayout":58,"psychology":42,"workerManagement":60,"trainingIntensity":53,"technicalCoaching":49,"characterCoaching":56,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":67,"mediaHandling":56,"brandBuilding":34,"socialMediaSavvy":18,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":12,"reactionSpeed":53,"consistency":45,"awareness":42,"judgement":49}},{"id":602,"name":"Lluvia","realName":"Lluvia","picture":"Lluvia.jpg","ability":59,"currentAbility":57,"potentialAbility":57,"charisma":46,"micSkills":50,"popularity":5,"condition":92,"hardcoreAbility":51,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"F","weight":60,"height":157,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1984-08-09T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Lluvia is the ring name of a Mexican luchadora enmascarado. Lluvia is the daughter of professional wrestler Andrés Durán Reyes, better known under the ring name Sangre Chicana (\"Chicano Blood\") and the sister of Sangre Chicana, Jr. unlike her father or her brother Lluvia decided to work as a tecnico while her father was one of the most famous rulebreakers of the 1980's. Lluvia was originally trained by her father, Sangre Chicana before making her professional wrestling debut on April 30, 2008. She would become a regular for CMLL only a few months later, continuing her wrestling training under CMLL trainers El Satánico and Último Guerrero. On December 6, 2011 during a CMLL show Lluvia and Luna Mágica defeated La Comandante and Zeuix to win the Reina World Tag Team Championship, a title promoted by Japanese wrestling promotion Universal Woman's Pro Wrestling Reina. The victory meant that the two traveled to Japan to defend the titles in early 2012.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[3534,4123],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":65,"storytelling":67,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":68,"psychology":65,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":78,"technicalCoaching":53,"characterCoaching":62,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":62,"brandBuilding":68,"socialMediaSavvy":51,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":78,"consistency":56,"awareness":65,"judgement":79},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-602","wrestlerId":602,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2008-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":604,"name":"La Amapola","realName":"La Amapola","picture":"La Amapola.jpg","ability":69,"currentAbility":61,"potentialAbility":61,"charisma":74,"micSkills":64,"popularity":5,"condition":65,"hardcoreAbility":45,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"F","weight":60,"height":157,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1971-09-09T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Guadalupe Ramona Olvera is a Mexican Luchadora, best known under the ring name La Amapola (Spanish for \"The Poppy\"). At 1,442 days, she is the longest reigning CMLL World Women's Champion. Olvera made her professional wrestling debut in December 1997 after training with Super Muñeco, Satánico and Adonis Salazar, whom she would later marry. She took the ring name \"La Amapola\", an enmascarado, or masked wrestler. Amapola began her career working for CMLL (CMLL), which she has worked for ever since. In the late 1990s and early 2000s CMLL did not focus on their women's division, which cause La Amapola to also work for a variety of other minor Mexican promotions. She was offered a contract with CMLL's main Mexican rival AAA, but declined, opting to stay with CMLL in the hopes that they would focus on women's wrestling like they had in the mid to early 1990s.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":73,"storytelling":75,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":76,"psychology":73,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":56,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":69,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":69,"brandBuilding":63,"socialMediaSavvy":68,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":56,"consistency":60,"awareness":73,"judgement":84},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-604","wrestlerId":604,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"1998-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":606,"name":"Tiffany","realName":"Tiffany","picture":"Tiffany.jpg","ability":59,"currentAbility":52,"potentialAbility":52,"charisma":52,"micSkills":52,"popularity":4,"condition":68,"hardcoreAbility":63,"injuryProne":86,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"F","weight":68,"height":167,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1973-02-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1993-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Xóchitl Leyva Sánchez is a Mexican luchadora. She has won the 2003, 2005 and 2008 Reina de Reinas tournaments and has held the Mexican National Women's Championship two times. After working for Asistencia Asesoría y Administración (AAA) for the majority of her career, she jumped to Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) in September 2010.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":61,"storytelling":66,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":31,"matchLayout":67,"psychology":61,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":58,"technicalCoaching":54,"characterCoaching":51,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":69,"mediaHandling":51,"brandBuilding":46,"socialMediaSavvy":36,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":58,"consistency":56,"awareness":61,"judgement":77}},{"id":607,"name":"Lady Apache","realName":"Lady Apache","picture":"Lady Apache.jpg","ability":43,"currentAbility":52,"potentialAbility":52,"charisma":44,"micSkills":59,"popularity":4,"condition":63,"hardcoreAbility":42,"injuryProne":93,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"F","weight":56,"height":157,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1970-06-26T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1986-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Sandra González Calderón is a Mexican professional wrestler or Luchadora, best known under the ring name Lady Apache. González's ring name comes from the \"family name\" of Mario Balbuena González who wrestles under the name Gran Apache; whom she was married to when she made her wrestling debut in 1986 but later divorced. As Lady Apache, González has mainly worked for Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) and Asistencia Asesoría y Administración (AAA), Mexico's two largest professional wrestling promotions during her career, switching back and forth several times. González is a three time CMLL World Women's Champion, a two time Mexican National Women's Champion and two time AAA Reina de Reinas. On August 20, 2010 it was announced that Lady Apache was pregnant and for that reason had to stop wrestling for at least seven months.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":55,"storytelling":63,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":36,"matchLayout":65,"psychology":55,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":45,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":69,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":64,"mediaHandling":69,"brandBuilding":49,"socialMediaSavvy":70,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":45,"consistency":50,"awareness":55,"judgement":73}},{"id":608,"name":"Zeuxis","realName":"Zeuxis","picture":"Zeuxis.jpg","ability":59,"currentAbility":61,"potentialAbility":61,"charisma":75,"micSkills":70,"popularity":6,"condition":91,"hardcoreAbility":52,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"F","weight":67,"height":160,"base":"USA","birthplace":"Puerto Rico","dateOfBirth":"1988-11-03T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Zeuxis is a Puerto Rican luchadora enmascarada. She also makes regular tours of Japan with the Reina Joshi Puroresu promotion. Zeuxis' real name is not a matter of public record, as is often the case with masked wrestlers in Mexico where their private lives are kept a secret from the wrestling fans. The wrestler known as Zeuxis was born in Puerto Rico, but lived and trained for her professional wrestling debut in Mexico. She was initially trained by Negro Navarro before making her debut, and later by El Satánico when she joined Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL). MLL decided to book Zeuxis in a storyline with tecnica newcomer Silueta that developed over the summer of 2010. The storyline started out with the two being on opposite sides of a number of Best two out of three falls six-woman tag team matches where Zeuxis would focus on trying to unmask her opponent, going so far as to rip Silueta's mask apart. The storyline led to a Luchas de Apuestas.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":66,"storytelling":70,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":72,"psychology":66,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":76,"technicalCoaching":64,"characterCoaching":60,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":64,"socialMediaSavvy":35,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":76,"consistency":68,"awareness":66,"judgement":80},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-608","wrestlerId":608,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2023-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":609,"name":"Kensuke Sasaki","realName":"Kensuke Sasaki","picture":"Kensuke Sasaki.jpg","ability":85,"currentAbility":90,"potentialAbility":90,"charisma":99,"micSkills":89,"popularity":8,"condition":58,"hardcoreAbility":83,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"submission","gender":"M","weight":115,"height":177,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1966-08-04T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1986-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Kensuke Sasaki is a Japanese professional wrestler who currently wrestles for various promotions through his own agency, Diamond Ring. He is the first of two men ever to hold all 3 of puroresu's major heavyweight titles (the IWGP Heavyweight Championship, the AJPW Triple Crown Championship, and the GHC Heavyweight Championship), the other being Yoshihiro Takayama. Kensuke Sasaki debuted in Riki Choshu's Japan Pro Wrestling (a satellite of All Japan Pro Wrestling) in February 1986. Sasaki follow Choshu as he returned to New Japan Pro Wrestling in 1987. During that time, he teamed up with the likes of Osamu Matsuda and Kenichi Oya. Between 2001 and 2003, Sasaki took a couple hiatuses from pro wrestling and focused on Mixed Martial Arts. He has two fights under his belt, winning both by submission in the first round beating Dan Chase in 2001 and future UFC fighter Christian Wellisch in 2003.\r\n","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1135,3039,3215,3216],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":80,"storytelling":85,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":86,"psychology":80,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":67,"technicalCoaching":65,"characterCoaching":60,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":75,"socialMediaSavvy":53,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":67,"consistency":81,"awareness":80,"judgement":88}},{"id":610,"name":"KENTA","realName":"KENTA","picture":"KENTA.jpg","ability":77,"currentAbility":69,"potentialAbility":69,"charisma":69,"micSkills":81,"popularity":34,"condition":66,"hardcoreAbility":65,"injuryProne":93,"type":"wrestler","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":91,"height":172,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1981-03-12T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"KENTA, a 2000 graduate of the AJPW Dojo, is a Japanese wrestler who works in America, Canada and Japan. He is a Middleweight who is classed as using a Technician Striker style. He is best known for his work with WWE, NJPW, IMPACT, NOAH, NXT, NJoA and ROH. He is currently the NJPW STRONG Openweight champion. He is the protege of Kenta Kobashi. He has been half of the Tag Team Of The Year two times.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":45,"teams":[3022,3023,3024,4103,4104],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":75,"storytelling":80,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":33,"matchLayout":81,"psychology":75,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":75,"technicalCoaching":69,"characterCoaching":82,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":67,"mediaHandling":82,"brandBuilding":77,"socialMediaSavvy":67,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":75,"consistency":57,"awareness":75,"judgement":85},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-610","wrestlerId":610,"promotionId":45,"startDate":"2025-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":611,"name":"Rockstar Spud","realName":"Rockstar Spud","picture":"Rockstar Spud.jpg","ability":74,"currentAbility":77,"potentialAbility":77,"charisma":77,"micSkills":76,"popularity":21,"condition":82,"hardcoreAbility":77,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":64,"height":160,"base":"UK","birthplace":"England","dateOfBirth":"1983-01-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2001-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"First introduced in 2018 as the dapper General Manager of 205 Live, Maverick wasted no time reinvigorating the Cruiserweight division, leading it into a renaissance period. He wore his passion on his sleeve, beaming enthusiastically whenever he spoke of his vision for the purple brand, and did everything in his power to ensure 205 Live lived up to its reputation as The Most Exciting Hour on Television.\r\n\r\nMaverick enjoyed similar success once he decided to become a ringside manager for the tag team AOP. In short order, he guided his charges to the Raw Tag Team Title. When that association dissolved, Maverick turned his sights toward active competition and began obsessively pursuing (and eventually defending) the 24/7 Championship, leading to impromptu title bouts in parking lots, the locker room area … and even at his own wedding!","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[2343,2819],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":54,"storytelling":57,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":45,"matchLayout":58,"psychology":54,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":66,"technicalCoaching":44,"characterCoaching":75,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":55,"mediaHandling":75,"brandBuilding":48,"socialMediaSavvy":75,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":66,"consistency":70,"awareness":54,"judgement":72},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-611","wrestlerId":611,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2022-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":612,"name":"Jay Bradley","realName":"Jay Bradley","picture":"Jay Bradley.jpg","ability":52,"currentAbility":57,"potentialAbility":57,"charisma":54,"micSkills":58,"popularity":4,"condition":79,"hardcoreAbility":53,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"striker","gender":"M","weight":118,"height":190,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1980-11-17T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Jay Bradley is an American wrestler who works in America, Canada, the British Isles and Japan. He is a Light Heavyweight who is classed as using a Brawler style. He is one half of The Fixers alongside Wrecking Ball Legursky. He is best known for his work with WWE, IMPACT and NWA.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3380,3723],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":54,"storytelling":57,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":58,"psychology":54,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":62,"technicalCoaching":45,"characterCoaching":54,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":54,"brandBuilding":49,"socialMediaSavvy":44,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":62,"consistency":77,"awareness":54,"judgement":72}},{"id":614,"name":"Chris Masters","realName":"Chris Masters","picture":"Chris Masters.jpg","ability":47,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":53,"charisma":41,"micSkills":58,"popularity":19,"condition":75,"hardcoreAbility":35,"injuryProne":95,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":122,"height":190,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1983-01-08T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"\"The Masterpiece\" Chris Masters never met a mirror he didn't like. Sporting the kind of physique usually only seen in comic books, the 6-foot-4, 265-pound Adonis was cocky beyond compare with the power and ability to back it up in the ring. Debuting on Raw in early 2005, Masters quickly caught the attention of the WWE Universe thanks to his unbelievable build and his devastating finishing maneuver, The Master Lock. A wrenching full nelson, the hold was applied to some of WWE's greatest Superstars, including Shawn Michaels and John Cena. Believing his maneuever to be unbreakable, Masters began offering up thousands of dollars to anyone who was willing to try and escape. These \"Master Lock Challenges\" usually ended with a grinning Masters and a volunteer screaming in agony.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3082,3083],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":57,"storytelling":60,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":26,"matchLayout":61,"psychology":57,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":62,"technicalCoaching":31,"characterCoaching":58,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":74,"mediaHandling":58,"brandBuilding":65,"socialMediaSavvy":45,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":62,"consistency":68,"awareness":57,"judgement":74}},{"id":615,"name":"Raven","realName":"Raven","picture":"Raven.jpg","ability":27,"currentAbility":34,"potentialAbility":34,"charisma":38,"micSkills":24,"popularity":24,"condition":53,"hardcoreAbility":52,"injuryProne":84,"type":"commentator","style":"striker","gender":"M","weight":107,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1964-09-08T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1988-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Raven, a 1988 graduate of the The Monster Factory, is a retired American wrestler who works as a colour commentator, a manager, an on-screen personality and a road agent. He is best known for his work with WWE, WCW, IMPACT, ECW, AJPW, NWA, ROH and MLW.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3267,3268],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":80,"storytelling":79,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":46,"matchLayout":78,"psychology":80,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":41,"technicalCoaching":31,"characterCoaching":85,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":54,"mediaHandling":85,"brandBuilding":48,"socialMediaSavvy":80,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":41,"consistency":41,"awareness":80,"judgement":88}},{"id":616,"name":"Jinsei Shinzaki","realName":"Jinsei Shinzaki","picture":"Jinsei Shinzaki.jpg","ability":83,"currentAbility":85,"potentialAbility":85,"charisma":97,"micSkills":79,"popularity":6,"condition":61,"hardcoreAbility":98,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":108,"height":177,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1966-12-02T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1984-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Kensuke Shinzaki is a Japanese professional wrestler, better known by his stage names Jinsei Shinzaki and Hakushi. Hakushi is the WWF derivation (1995–96) of his Japanese persona, a Buddhist pilgrim. Hakushi's style of wrestling was a precursor to the luchador style which became emphasized in major wrestling promotions from the mid-1990s to the mid-2000s. As the only Light heavyweight wrestler in the promotion, Shinzaki has competed in major promotions such as New Japan, All Japan, and FMW, challenging their talent. In 1995, he entered the World Wrestling Federation (WWF) as a Japanese villain named Hakushi (White Messenger). On April 15, 2011, Shinzaki returned to the United States to wrestle for Chikara in the 2011 King of Trios tournament, where he would represent Michinoku Pro with Dick Togo and the Great Sasuke.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":70,"teams":[3178,3179,3180],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":70,"storytelling":73,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":74,"psychology":70,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":55,"technicalCoaching":50,"characterCoaching":79,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":79,"brandBuilding":67,"socialMediaSavvy":73,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":55,"consistency":65,"awareness":70,"judgement":82},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-616","wrestlerId":616,"promotionId":70,"startDate":"2020-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":618,"name":"Shigeo Okumura","realName":"Shigeo Okumura","picture":"Okumura.jpg","ability":62,"currentAbility":65,"potentialAbility":65,"charisma":53,"micSkills":72,"popularity":8,"condition":76,"hardcoreAbility":51,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":95,"height":180,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1972-05-25T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1993-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Shigeo Okumura is a Japanese professional wrestler. Okumura originally worked for Tokyo Pro Wrestling (TPW) and later on All Japan Pro Wrestling (AJPW) in Japan but moved to Mexico in 2005 to work for CMLL full-time. Okumura usually teams up with wrestlers from Japan who visit CMLL, currently as a group known as La Ola Amarilla (Spanish for \"The Yellow Wave\"). Okumura and Yujiro won the 2009 version of the Gran Alternativa tournament. In mid-2004 Okumura travelled to Mexico on a \"learning trip\", to improve his in ring skills by being exposed to other wrestling styles than the Japanese style. In Mexico he began working for Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) as a Heel \"Anti-Mexico\" character. The \"Anti-Mexico\" character stood in contrast to Okumura's personal views as he liked living and working in Mexico so much that he has remained there since 2004.","alte