, Yuu Yamagata is a veteran who started out on the joshi circuit before moving to K-DOJO. Like fellow female roster member Bambi, she alternates between competing against the women (or at least now against Bambi) and competing against the men, primarily in tag team action. She has won a few tournaments in K-DOJO, most notably a tournament in 2008 to get into a league to determine a challenger to the Champion Of STRONGEST-K. Yamagata left K-DOJO after the promotion’s July 31, 2011 event, leaving Bambi as the promotion’s only female member. She is now a freelancer.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3001],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":59,"storytelling":71,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":34,"matchLayout":75,"psychology":59,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":65,"technicalCoaching":66,"characterCoaching":55,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":66,"mediaHandling":55,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":45,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":65,"consistency":75,"awareness":59,"judgement":75}},{"id":686,"name":"Ruby Soho","realName":"Ruby Soho","picture":"Heidi Lovelace.jpg","ability":59,"currentAbility":56,"potentialAbility":56,"charisma":43,"micSkills":51,"popularity":31,"condition":95,"hardcoreAbility":56,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"F","weight":55,"height":160,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1991-01-09T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Ruby Soho is an American wrestler who works in America, Canada, the British Isles and Japan. She is a Small worker who is classed as using a Regular style. She is best known for her work with WWE, AEW, NXT, SHIMMER, Smash and CHIKARA.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[1363,1811,3346],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":55,"storytelling":58,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":37,"matchLayout":59,"psychology":55,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":53,"characterCoaching":74,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":63,"mediaHandling":74,"brandBuilding":62,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":52,"awareness":55,"judgement":73},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-686","wrestlerId":686,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2021-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":687,"name":"Dave Prazak","realName":"Dave Prazak","picture":"Dave Prazak.jpg","ability":71,"currentAbility":61,"potentialAbility":61,"charisma":62,"micSkills":54,"popularity":4,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":47,"injuryProne":53,"type":"commentator","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":66,"height":167,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1978-11-19T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1996-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Dave Prazak is a professional wrestling manager and commentator. He works for many independent wrestling promotions in America. He is the founder of the all female wrestling promotion Shimmer Women Athletes. Prazak began his career in the professional wrestling industry as a ring announcer in 1996. Prazak worked as a manager from 1996 until 2002, at one point managing Independent Wrestling Association Mid-South (IWA Mid-South) IWA Mid-South Heavyweight Champion CM Punk. In late 2004, he began making appearances for Full Impact Pro (FIP) as a manager, forming the stable (faction), DP Associates. In 2005 Prazak founded Shimmer Women Athletes, along with Allison Danger, because he thought wrestling fans wanted to see female wrestlers do more than strip in the ring.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":77,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":60,"storytelling":42,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":36,"psychology":60,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":70,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":70,"brandBuilding":31,"socialMediaSavvy":72,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":0,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":0,"awareness":60,"judgement":36},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-687","wrestlerId":687,"promotionId":77,"startDate":"2018-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":688,"name":"Allison Danger","realName":"Allison Danger","picture":"Allison Danger.jpg","ability":27,"currentAbility":31,"potentialAbility":31,"charisma":19,"micSkills":29,"popularity":6,"condition":77,"hardcoreAbility":45,"injuryProne":100,"type":"commentator","style":"all rounder","gender":"F","weight":56,"height":167,"base":"Canada","birthplace":"Canada","dateOfBirth":"1977-03-31T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Cathy Allison Corino is a Canadian professional wrestler and professional wrestling manager, better known by her ring name, Allison Danger. Corino's older brother Steve is a professional wrestler as well, and while working for Extreme Championship Wrestling (ECW) he introduced his sister to the ECW locker room. Corino befriended Francine. Corino adopted the persona of Allison Danger, a tattooed punk. Throughout 2003 Danger worked for Jersey All Pro Wrestling and IWA Mid South. Between July and August 2003 she toured Japan, replacing her friend Lucy Furr. Danger joined Ring of Honor (ROH) as the manager of the Christopher Street Connection. Danger is heavily involved with the running of Chicago based female independent circuit independent professional wrestling promotion Shimmer Women Athletes. She co-runs the promotion along with Dave Prazak, as well as being an active wrestler and color commentator for the DVDs.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1290,2823,2824],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":76,"storytelling":81,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":82,"psychology":76,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":75,"technicalCoaching":65,"characterCoaching":69,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":69,"brandBuilding":40,"socialMediaSavvy":65,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":75,"consistency":84,"awareness":76,"judgement":86}},{"id":689,"name":"Bryce Remsburg","realName":"Bryce Remsburg","picture":"Bryce Remsburg.jpg","ability":79,"currentAbility":86,"potentialAbility":86,"charisma":76,"micSkills":76,"popularity":2,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":93,"injuryProne":90,"type":"referee","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":66,"height":165,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1983-01-04T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2001-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Bryce Remsburg is an American man who works primarily as a referee. He is best known for his work with AEW.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":4,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":96,"matchLayout":5,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":4,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":61,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":4,"mediaHandling":61,"brandBuilding":20,"socialMediaSavvy":64,"ruleKnowledge":86,"positioning":69,"reactionSpeed":4,"consistency":44,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-689","wrestlerId":689,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2019-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":690,"name":"Tommy Dreamer","realName":"Tommy Dreamer","picture":"Tommy Dreamer.jpg","ability":54,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"charisma":53,"micSkills":53,"popularity":17,"condition":60,"hardcoreAbility":43,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"hardcore","gender":"M","weight":116,"height":185,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1971-02-13T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1989-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Tommy Dreamer was every bit as tough as all the other barbed wire-scarred wrestlers in the ECW locker room, but what made the kid from Yonkers, N.Y. an icon of the renegade Philadelphia promotion wasn’t his tenacity — it was his loyalty.\r\n\r\nAn integral part of ECW both in the ring and behind the scenes up until the company’s 2001 demise, Dreamer was the only competitor who stayed faithful to Paul Heyman’s sports-entertainment madhouse through its most turbulent years. This distinction earned him the moniker of “The ECW Original” and the admiration of the Philly faithful, but The City of Brotherly Love wasn’t always so kind to Tommy Dreamer.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":65,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":24,"matchLayout":66,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":48,"technicalCoaching":36,"characterCoaching":65,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":76,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":42,"socialMediaSavvy":64,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":48,"consistency":64,"awareness":62,"judgement":77}},{"id":691,"name":"Daffney","realName":"Daffney","picture":"Daffney.jpg","ability":66,"currentAbility":59,"potentialAbility":59,"charisma":50,"micSkills":53,"popularity":7,"condition":60,"hardcoreAbility":70,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"all rounder","gender":"F","weight":59,"height":165,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1975-07-17T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":true,"story":"Shannon Claire Spruill is an American professional wrestler and valet. She is best known for her appearances with World Championship Wrestling between 1999 and 2001 under the ring name Daffney and for working for Total Nonstop Action Wrestling, where she used the ring name \"The Governor\", a caricature of Alaska governor and former United States Vice Presidential candidate Sarah Palin, before returning to her Daffney ring name and gimmick. In November 1999, she responded to a World Championship Wrestling (WCW) contest looking to acquire new talent and was hired. In WCW, Spruill played Daffney, the mentally deranged, besotted girlfriend of David Flair, managing him and Crowbar. On May 15, 2000 Daffney and Crowbar defeated WCW World Cruiserweight Champion Chris Candido and his girlfriend Tammy Lynn Sytch in a mixed tag team match and were declared co-champions.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":66,"storytelling":68,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":17,"matchLayout":69,"psychology":66,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":65,"technicalCoaching":46,"characterCoaching":77,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":83,"mediaHandling":77,"brandBuilding":46,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":65,"consistency":66,"awareness":66,"judgement":80}},{"id":692,"name":"Lance Storm","realName":"Lance Storm","picture":"Lance Storm.jpg","ability":85,"currentAbility":90,"potentialAbility":90,"charisma":79,"micSkills":100,"popularity":13,"condition":81,"hardcoreAbility":91,"injuryProne":86,"type":"writer","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":105,"height":177,"base":"Canada","birthplace":"Canada","dateOfBirth":"1969-04-03T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1990-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Lance Timothy Evers known professionally by his ring name Lance Storm, is a retired Canadian professional wrestler. He is best known for his work in World Wrestling Entertainment, Extreme Championship Wrestling, and World Championship Wrestling. He runs a pro wrestling school, Storm Wrestling Academy, in Calgary, Alberta, Canada. Since leaving WWE, Storm has made several appearances on the independent circuit. At Hardcore Homecoming on November 4, 2005 in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, Storm interfered in a steel cage match between Justin Credible and Jerry Lynn, helping Credible defeat Lynn. At the December 3, 2005 Ring of Honor show Steel Cage Warfare in New York, New York, Storm congratulated ROH World Champion Bryan Danielson following a successful title defense against Rocky Romero. On June 22 2013, Storm worked for the House of Hardcore promotion, losing to its founder Tommy Dreamer in a main event singles match.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":28,"teams":[282,584],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":80,"storytelling":85,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":87,"psychology":80,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":29,"technicalCoaching":66,"characterCoaching":62,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":62,"brandBuilding":51,"socialMediaSavvy":51,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":29,"consistency":64,"awareness":80,"judgement":88},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-692","wrestlerId":692,"promotionId":28,"startDate":"2022-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":693,"name":"Ayumi Kurihara","realName":"Ayumi Kurihara","picture":"Ayumi Kurihara.jpg","ability":45,"currentAbility":48,"potentialAbility":48,"charisma":58,"micSkills":45,"popularity":5,"condition":91,"hardcoreAbility":42,"injuryProne":100,"type":"manager","style":"all rounder","gender":"F","weight":57,"height":162,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1984-07-13T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2005-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Ayumi Kurihara is a joshi puroresu wrestler who grew up around pro wrestling. Ayumi entered training with the women's pro wrestling promotion AtoZ and then transferred to M's Style, where she learned the craft from well-known Japanese female wrestlers Gami, Mariko Yoshida, AKINO, and Michiko Ohmukai. Ayumi debuted in 2005, at the age of 20. She is viewed as one of the future stars of joshi puroresu in Japan as she has a hunger and desire second to none in the younger class.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[2760],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":80,"storytelling":85,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":87,"psychology":80,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":90,"technicalCoaching":71,"characterCoaching":69,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":69,"brandBuilding":60,"socialMediaSavvy":49,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":90,"consistency":96,"awareness":80,"judgement":88}},{"id":694,"name":"Shane Douglas","realName":"Shane Douglas","picture":"Shane Douglas.jpg","ability":63,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":53,"charisma":53,"micSkills":45,"popularity":4,"condition":70,"hardcoreAbility":49,"injuryProne":50,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":111,"height":180,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1964-11-21T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1982-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Troy Shane Martin is an American professional wrestler and promoter, better known by his ring name Shane Douglas. In the course of his career, which has spanned two decades, Douglas has wrestled in Extreme Championship Wrestling and World Championship Wrestling and briefly in the World Wrestling Federation. Martin most recently worked for Total Nonstop Action Wrestling. Martin is recognized as a 5-time world champion, having held the NWA World Heavyweight Championship once and the ECW World Heavyweight Championship 4 times. He is recognized by WWE as the first Extreme Championship Wrestling World Heavyweight Champion.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1038,1329,3292],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":64,"storytelling":69,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":35,"matchLayout":70,"psychology":64,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":31,"technicalCoaching":37,"characterCoaching":80,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":65,"mediaHandling":80,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":75,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":31,"consistency":38,"awareness":64,"judgement":78}},{"id":695,"name":"John Silver","realName":"John Silver","picture":"John Silver.jpg","ability":63,"currentAbility":68,"potentialAbility":68,"charisma":54,"micSkills":57,"popularity":22,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":63,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":81,"height":160,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1990-06-04T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2007-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"John Silver is an American professional wrestler who is also known as The Shard, most notable for his time in CHIKARA. He started out as the evil, mirror-image of Jigsaw, but over the course of seven or so months in 2012, The Shard was able to win over his template. Some may say he corrupted Jig, and it's easy to see why. The duo, dubbed Pieces of Hate, has ruthlessly cut a path across the company like a runaway buzzsaw across a hardwood floor. However, were Shard's motives as part of the Gekido more noble than anyone would let on? Was he really seeing an underlying, tangible evil in the guidance of Mike Quackenbush? There are two sides to every story, you know, and one man's terrorist is another's freedom fighter.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":49,"teams":[628,1275,1385,1386,1954,2402,2723,3768],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":66,"storytelling":70,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":19,"matchLayout":71,"psychology":66,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":82,"technicalCoaching":63,"characterCoaching":77,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":81,"mediaHandling":77,"brandBuilding":48,"socialMediaSavvy":68,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":82,"consistency":84,"awareness":66,"judgement":80},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-695","wrestlerId":695,"promotionId":49,"startDate":"2023-04-20T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"inDevelopment":true},{"id":697,"name":"UltraMantis Black","realName":"UltraMantis Black","picture":"Ultramantis Black.jpg","ability":62,"currentAbility":60,"potentialAbility":60,"charisma":70,"micSkills":60,"popularity":3,"condition":80,"hardcoreAbility":40,"injuryProne":98,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":91,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1975-07-17T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"UltraMantis Black originally had his sights set on a career in the world of Baseball and was at one stage drafted by the Texas Rangers until his career was cut short due to a motorcycle accident. Mantis then began working in various backyard promotions putting his body on the line for virtually peanuts until he joined the CHIKARA Wrestle Factory and trained under Mike Quackenbush and Tom Carter. Now known as a fantastic commentator as well as the leader of the Order of the Neo Solar Temple. As part of his gimmick, he wears a mantis mask. As UltraMantis, his original red and green attire was based on the main protagonist from the Kamen Rider series, while his ring name was derived from another Japanese television program, Ultraman. In May 2004 he renamed himself UltraMantis Black and adopted a new mask and a red and black attire, while also beginning to express communist views.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1017,3314],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":70,"storytelling":75,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":76,"psychology":70,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":60,"technicalCoaching":60,"characterCoaching":80,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":80,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":68,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":60,"consistency":71,"awareness":70,"judgement":82}},{"id":698,"name":"Frightmare","realName":"Frightmare","picture":"Frightmare.jpg","ability":56,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":53,"charisma":55,"micSkills":38,"popularity":3,"condition":85,"hardcoreAbility":68,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":77,"height":170,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1990-07-24T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Frightmare is a professional wrestler, who performs primarily in the Chikara professional wrestling promotion, where he is the current Young Lions Cup Champion. He has also worked for promotions such as Evolve Wrestling, International Wrestling Cartel, IWA East Coast and Jersey All Pro Wrestling. Just like his mentor Hallowicked, Frightmare wears a mask and holds an incoherent speech pattern. Frightmare made his Chikara debut on November 16, 2008, accompanying Hallowicked and Delirious to the ring on a chain leash. On January 16, 2010, Frightmare made his debut for Evolve Wrestling, at the promotion's first ever show, teaming with Hallowicked and Mike Quackenbush in a six man tag team match.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1105],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":61,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":35,"matchLayout":62,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":79,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":60,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":65,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":44,"socialMediaSavvy":60,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":79,"consistency":73,"awareness":56,"judgement":74}},{"id":699,"name":"Hallowicked","realName":"Hallowicked","picture":"Hallowicked.jpg","ability":56,"currentAbility":65,"potentialAbility":65,"charisma":53,"micSkills":65,"popularity":4,"condition":72,"hardcoreAbility":62,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":96,"height":185,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1981-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Hallowicked is an American professional wrestler known as a staple of the Chikara promotion. His accomplishments in the promotion include becoming the inaugural Young Lions Cup Champion, a one-time Campeon de Parejas and the winner of the 2003 Tag World Grand Prix and 2012 King of Trios tournaments. He currently also serves as an assistant trainer at The Wrestle Factory, operated by Chikara founder Mike Quackenbush. Throughout his career he has also worked for promotions such as Combat Zone Wrestling, Dragon Gate USA, Evolve Wrestling, Full Impact Pro, Jersey All Pro Wrestling, Pro Wrestling Guerrilla and Ring of Honor. He is known for his ghoulish looks and incoherent speech pattern.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1017,1105,2637,3314],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":72,"storytelling":76,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":18,"matchLayout":77,"psychology":72,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":72,"technicalCoaching":67,"characterCoaching":65,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":82,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":38,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":72,"consistency":70,"awareness":72,"judgement":83}},{"id":701,"name":"Jigsaw","realName":"Jigsaw","picture":"Jigsaw.jpg","ability":53,"currentAbility":60,"potentialAbility":60,"charisma":54,"micSkills":53,"popularity":4,"condition":77,"hardcoreAbility":47,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":86,"height":185,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1983-12-16T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2003-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Jigsaw is an American professional wrestler. Best known for his work with Chikara Pro. Jigsaw made his Chikara debut in late 2002, forming a rudo tag team named The Conundrum with Rorschach, while also occasionally teaming with Eddie Kingston and BlackJack Marciano as a member of The Toxic Trio. In 2006, he competed in Combat Zone Wrestling's annual Best of the Best tournament, losing to Austin Aries and B-Boy in the opening round.  Jigsaw joined Ring of Honor in 2007, forming The Vulture Squad alliance with Jack Evans, Ruckus, Julius Smokes to combat The Age of the Fall alliance. Jigsaw made a return to Chikara, sans mask, in September 2008, saving his trainer Mike Quackenbush from a violent assault at the hands of the UnStable. On June 28, 2012, working under the ring name Rubix, he made his debut for Total Nonstop Action Wrestling (TNA), losing to Sonjay Dutt in a TNA X Division Championship tournament qualifying match on Impact Wrestling.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1275],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":67,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":33,"matchLayout":69,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":54,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":67,"mediaHandling":54,"brandBuilding":51,"socialMediaSavvy":39,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":65,"awareness":62,"judgement":77}},{"id":703,"name":"Sinn Bodhi","realName":"Sinn Bodhi","picture":"Sinn Bodhi.jpg","ability":58,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":55,"charisma":51,"micSkills":53,"popularity":5,"condition":84,"hardcoreAbility":70,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":106,"height":185,"base":"Canada","birthplace":"Canada","dateOfBirth":"1973-08-29T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Nicholas \"Nick\" Cvjetkovich is a Canadian professional wrestler of British and Serbian descent, better known as The Original Sinn, or simply Sinn (also stylized as SiNN). He also worked for World Wrestling Entertainment on its SmackDown brand as Kizarny. Cvjetkovich was trained as a wrestler by Rob Fuego and Ron Hutchison in Orangeville, Ontario and also trained for (and later earned) his black belt at Alex Atkinson's Black Belt Institute. His debut match was in 2000 against El Fuego during the Apocalypse Wrestling Federation's Iron Man Tournament at the Canadian National Exhibition. Cvjetkovich made his debut in Total Nonstop Action Wrestling on August 13, 2003, under the name \"Sinn\". On the October 10, 2008 edition of SmackDown, vignettes promoting the debut of Cvjetkovich, now under the ring name Kizarny, began to air. He later described his character as being as \"if Jake \"The Snake\" Roberts and Doink produced a lovechild.\"","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":58,"storytelling":62,"productFit":70,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":63,"psychology":58,"workerManagement":70,"trainingIntensity":64,"technicalCoaching":31,"characterCoaching":66,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":66,"brandBuilding":38,"socialMediaSavvy":58,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":14,"reactionSpeed":64,"consistency":38,"awareness":58,"judgement":63}},{"id":704,"name":"Karen Jarrett","realName":"Karen Jarrett","picture":"Karen Jarrett.jpg","ability":48,"currentAbility":47,"potentialAbility":47,"charisma":44,"micSkills":42,"popularity":12,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":40,"injuryProne":38,"type":"manager","style":"all rounder","gender":"F","weight":65,"height":175,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1972-10-12T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Karen Jarrett (née Smedley) is an American former professional wrestling valet and personality. She is most famous for her stint in Total Nonstop Action Wrestling from 2007 - 2008. She is the former wife of professional wrestler and Olympic gold medalist Kurt Angle. She has two children with her former husband Kurt Angle: a daughter named Kyra Angle (born December 2, 2002) and son named Kody Angle (born October 26, 2006). Their daughter, Kyra, has been seen on TNA television several times. Kyra was also seen in the WWE's 2006 Hall of Fame ceremony with her father. In September 2008, it was reported that Karen had legitimately filed for divorce from Kurt. The divorce was finalized on October 26, 2008. As of August 21, 2010, she has been married to TNA founder and wrestler Jeff Jarrett.\r\n","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":44,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":69,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":69,"brandBuilding":66,"socialMediaSavvy":54,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":0,"reactionSpeed":44,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-704","wrestlerId":704,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2023-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":705,"name":"Akira Taue","realName":"Akira Taue","picture":"Akira Taue.jpg","ability":50,"currentAbility":56,"potentialAbility":56,"charisma":54,"micSkills":60,"popularity":6,"condition":22,"hardcoreAbility":71,"injuryProne":38,"type":"wrestler","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":120,"height":190,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1961-05-08T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1988-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Akira Taue is a Japanese retired professional wrestler, and is the current President of Pro Wrestling NOAH. He is also a former AJPW Triple Crown champion, a former GHC Heavyweight Champion and has had fourteen 5 Star Matches as awarded by the Wrestling Observer Newsletter. Before becoming a professional wrestler, Akira Taue competed as a sumo wrestler, debuting in January 1980. He debuted in a tag team match for All Japan Pro Wrestling on January 2, 1988, teaming with the legendary Giant Baba against Buddy Landel and Paul Harris. On June 27, 2009, following the June 13 death of Mitsuharu Misawa, Akira Taue was appointed as the new president of Pro Wrestling Noah. On May 12, 2013, Taue announced that he would be officially retiring.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1097],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":92,"storytelling":93,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":93,"psychology":92,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":23,"technicalCoaching":45,"characterCoaching":60,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":51,"socialMediaSavvy":55,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":23,"consistency":35,"awareness":92,"judgement":95}},{"id":706,"name":"Atsushi Kotoge","realName":"Atsushi Kotoge","picture":"Atsushi Kotoge.jpg","ability":66,"currentAbility":68,"potentialAbility":68,"charisma":71,"micSkills":62,"popularity":5,"condition":79,"hardcoreAbility":70,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":83,"height":175,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1985-10-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2005-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Atsushi Kotoge  is a Japanese professional wrestler, currently signed to Pro Wrestling Noah. He is also known for his time in Osaka Pro Wrestling, where he was part of the tag team Momo no Seishun Tag with Daisuke Harada. Kotoge and Harada are former three-time Osaka Pro Wrestling Tag Team Champions and have also worked together for various other promotions across Japan and for Philadelphia, Pennsylvania–based Chikara in the United States. Kotoge made his debut for Osaka Pro Wrestling on April 29, 2005, at the promotion's sixth anniversary show, facing Kabuto Beetle. In April 2010, Kotoge along with Harada and their former Blood & Guts partner Tadasuke traveled to the United States to represent Osaka Pro in Chikara's 2010 King of Trios tournament. On May 1, 2012, Kotoge appeared at a press conference, where he was officially presented as Pro Wrestling Noah's newest signee.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":45,"teams":[1227],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":73,"storytelling":76,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":24,"matchLayout":77,"psychology":73,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":80,"technicalCoaching":73,"characterCoaching":65,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":76,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":80,"consistency":68,"awareness":73,"judgement":84},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-706","wrestlerId":706,"promotionId":45,"startDate":"2012-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":707,"name":"Mohammed Yone","realName":"Mohammed Yone","picture":"Mohammad Yone.jpg","ability":70,"currentAbility":63,"potentialAbility":63,"charisma":63,"micSkills":53,"popularity":7,"condition":64,"hardcoreAbility":72,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"submission","gender":"M","weight":110,"height":182,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1976-02-23T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1995-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Satoshi Yoneyama, better known by his ring name Mohammed Yone , is a Japanese professional wrestler, currently working for Pro Wrestling NOAH. He is known for his trademark afro hairstyle, which has earned him the nickname \"Mr. Afro\". Recently, he had cut his hair short and changed his pants color to black and red in order to sesemble more like his new formed stable CHANGE partners. Yone has competed all over the world including in the UK for the 1PW promotion at their Know Your Enemy events in 2006, teaming with Takeshi Morishima whilst they held the GHC tag-team titles.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":45,"teams":[1772,1773,2295,2367,3060,3872],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":72,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":73,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":62,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":65,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":66,"socialMediaSavvy":54,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":62,"consistency":57,"awareness":68,"judgement":81},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-707","wrestlerId":707,"promotionId":45,"startDate":"2001-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":708,"name":"Naomichi Marufuji","realName":"Naomichi Marufuji","picture":"Naomichi Marufuji.jpg","ability":70,"currentAbility":69,"potentialAbility":69,"charisma":64,"micSkills":75,"popularity":28,"condition":49,"hardcoreAbility":59,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":90,"height":172,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1979-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Naomichi Marufuji is a Japanese professional wrestler who competes for Pro Wrestling Noah, with occasional appearances in other professional wrestling promotions like Ring of Honor, All Japan Pro Wrestling and New Japan Pro Wrestling, among others. Marufuji is the first of only two Grand Slam Champion in Pro Wrestling Noah history. He is also the only man to win Junior Heavyweight Championships in all three major Japanese promotions. In 2009, he was appointed to the position of Vice President of the promotion. Marufuji pursued amateur wrestling and basketball during his high school days before joining All Japan Pro Wrestling. In early and mid-2005, Marufuji toured through Germany and Austria, competing for world Xtreme wrestling and Rings of Europe.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":45,"teams":[2736,3023,3048,3061],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":76,"storytelling":80,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":18,"matchLayout":81,"psychology":76,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":66,"technicalCoaching":71,"characterCoaching":69,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":82,"mediaHandling":69,"brandBuilding":78,"socialMediaSavvy":60,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":66,"consistency":64,"awareness":76,"judgement":86},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-708","wrestlerId":708,"promotionId":45,"startDate":"2000-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":709,"name":"Tsutomu Hirayanagi","realName":"Tsutomu Hirayanagi","picture":"Tsutomu Hirayanagi.jpg","ability":76,"currentAbility":78,"potentialAbility":78,"charisma":66,"micSkills":74,"popularity":4,"condition":83,"hardcoreAbility":74,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":85,"height":167,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1980-03-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2005-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Tsutomu Hirayanagi better known by his ring name Genba Hirayanagi is a Japanese professional wrestler. Hirayanagi was a competitor in amateur wrestling in high school. In June 2004 he entered the Pro Wrestling Noah dojo where, under the mentorship of Akira Taue, he was trained as a professional wrestler. Hirayanagi was a part of the first dojo class, debuting before his other group members. A solid wrestler so far, gaining experience slowly. The summer of 2007 saw Hirayanagi venture to the United Kingdom to perform in 6 matches on the British independent circuit. His UK debut came in July 20 2007. In 2008, Hirayanagi made his Ring of Honor debut in the opening match of the 14 September ROH: The Tokyo Summit show.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1090,3049],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":64,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":32,"matchLayout":66,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":69,"technicalCoaching":60,"characterCoaching":55,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":68,"mediaHandling":55,"brandBuilding":33,"socialMediaSavvy":29,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":69,"consistency":75,"awareness":56,"judgement":74}},{"id":710,"name":"Hajime Ohara","realName":"Hajime Ohara","picture":"Hajime Ohara.jpg","ability":53,"currentAbility":62,"potentialAbility":62,"charisma":77,"micSkills":70,"popularity":6,"condition":83,"hardcoreAbility":80,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":90,"height":172,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1984-07-24T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Hajime Ohara is a Japanese professional wrestler known for his work in Pro Wrestling Zero1, Kensuke Office, Hustle and Dradition In Japan. Ohara worked for Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre  (CMLL) in Mexico for several years as part of his training mixing the Lucha Libre style of Mexico with the Japanese Puroresu style of wrestling. Hajime Ohara trained for his professional wrestling debut under Último Dragón and Jorge Rivera, better known as Skayde. Through his connections with Dragón and Rivera, Ohara started out his career working in Mexico, first for Toryumon Mexico and soon after for Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL). On May 12, 2013, Ohara began working for Pro Wrestling Noah as a replacement for the injured GHC Junior Heavyweight Tag Team Champion Suwa.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":45,"teams":[1000,1090,1774],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":64,"storytelling":69,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":71,"psychology":64,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":79,"technicalCoaching":72,"characterCoaching":36,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":36,"brandBuilding":41,"socialMediaSavvy":28,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":79,"consistency":84,"awareness":64,"judgement":78},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-710","wrestlerId":710,"promotionId":45,"startDate":"2015-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":712,"name":"Takashi Sugiura","realName":"Takashi Sugiura","picture":"Takashi Sugiura.jpg","ability":76,"currentAbility":75,"potentialAbility":75,"charisma":64,"micSkills":86,"popularity":16,"condition":66,"hardcoreAbility":85,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"submission","gender":"M","weight":93,"height":175,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1970-05-31T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-12-23T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Takashi Sugiura is a Japanese professional wrestler. Sugiura was an accomplished judoka in high school. And narrowly missed the cut representing Japan at the 1996 Summer Olympics. He then became an Self Defense Instructor & was recruited to the All Japan Pro Wrestling Dojo by Tamon Honda, who (along with Yoshihiro Takayama) oversaw all of Sugiura's training. Sugiura made his debut in December 23, 2000 when he partnered Masao Inoue and Takeshi Rikio in a tag team match against Takeshi Morishima, Yoshinobu Kanemaru and Kentaro Shiga. Sugiura wrestled as a junior heavyweight in his earlier pro career and is a former GHC Junior Heavyweight Champion. Sugiura moved up to heavyweight and became the second longest reigning GHC Heavyweight Champion, having held the title for 581 days between December 2009 and July 2011. As of September 2011, Sugiura is the chairman of Noah's Wrestler's Association and holds the concomitant position on the promotion's board of directors.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":45,"teams":[1013,3061,3926],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":81,"storytelling":85,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":19,"matchLayout":86,"psychology":81,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":76,"technicalCoaching":75,"characterCoaching":55,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":81,"mediaHandling":55,"brandBuilding":66,"socialMediaSavvy":40,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":76,"consistency":77,"awareness":81,"judgement":89},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-712","wrestlerId":712,"promotionId":45,"startDate":"2000-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":713,"name":"Yoshihiro Takayama","realName":"Yoshihiro Takayama","picture":"Yoshihiro Takayama.jpg","ability":66,"currentAbility":72,"potentialAbility":72,"charisma":64,"micSkills":68,"popularity":9,"condition":14,"hardcoreAbility":86,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":125,"height":193,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1966-09-19T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1992-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Yoshihiro Takayama is a Japanese professional wrestler and mixed martial artist. Takayama is well known for his ability to endure massive amounts of punishment, especially after his fight at PRIDE 21 against Don Frye. He is the second of two men to hold all 3 of puroresu's major heavyweight titles (the IWGP Heavyweight Championship, the AJPW Triple Crown Championship, and the GHC Heavyweight Championship), the other being Kensuke Sasaki. Takayama started in UWF International, but due to the focus of the promotion on star Nobuhiko Takada, he wasn't able to go past the mid-card level. In 1995-96, with the interpromotional feuds with New Japan Pro Wrestling and WAR, he formed the \"Golden Cups\" stable with Yoji Anjo and Kenichi Yamamoto to compete in tag team and six-man matches. In 2017, Takayama was paralysed after a botched sunset flip.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[2733,2734,2735,2888,2889,2905,3300],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":66,"storytelling":75,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":78,"psychology":66,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":76,"technicalCoaching":72,"characterCoaching":71,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":71,"brandBuilding":69,"socialMediaSavvy":65,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":76,"consistency":62,"awareness":66,"judgement":80}},{"id":714,"name":"Shuhei Taniguchi","realName":"Shuhei Taniguchi","picture":"Maybach Taniguchi.jpg","ability":60,"currentAbility":59,"potentialAbility":59,"charisma":54,"micSkills":68,"popularity":5,"condition":77,"hardcoreAbility":68,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"submission","gender":"M","weight":105,"height":180,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1976-10-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2005-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Shuhei Taniguchi is a Japanese professional wrestler, who currently works for Pro Wrestling Noah under the ring name Maybach Taniguchi. Shuhei Taniguchi first started competitive wrestling when he was in high school. Just as Pro Wrestling Noah wrestlers Takashi Sugiura and Tamon Honda before him, Shuhei represented the armed forces in amaresu. Taniguchi joined the Pro Wrestling Noah dojo on May 5, 2005 and spent many months training. He finally debuted along with Atsushi Aoki, Ippei Ota, and Akihiko Ito on December 24, 2005 as part of Noah's annual Christmas Eve Noahful Gift in Differ show. In early 2012 he turned on his friend and tag partner Go Shiozaki and then joined No Mercy. He then transformed himself into a stronger and more vicious wrestler and changed his name to \"Maybach Taniguchi.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":45,"teams":[3053,3872],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":67,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":68,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":53,"characterCoaching":50,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":50,"brandBuilding":50,"socialMediaSavvy":40,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":78,"awareness":62,"judgement":77},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-714","wrestlerId":714,"promotionId":45,"startDate":"2005-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":715,"name":"Akitoshi Saito","realName":"Akitoshi Saito","picture":"Akitoshi Saito.jpg","ability":23,"currentAbility":32,"potentialAbility":32,"charisma":24,"micSkills":40,"popularity":5,"condition":60,"hardcoreAbility":16,"injuryProne":100,"type":"commentator","style":"submission","gender":"M","weight":123,"height":175,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1965-08-08T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1990-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Akitoshi Saito is a Japanese professional wrestler who is best known for his work in New Japan Pro Wrestling and Pro Wrestling NOAH. Before pro wrestling, Akitoshi Saito was trained in karate by Masashi Aoyagi. Saito seconded Aoyagi in his matches against Atsushi Onita in Frontier Martial-Arts Wrestling in 1989. He was trained for pro wrestling by Aoyagi and Yoshiaki Fujiwara. Saito made his pro wrestling debut in Pioneer Senshi and spent much of his early career in W*ING, a small promotion where he enjoyed moderate success. He joined New Japan Pro Wrestling in December 1991, along with his mentor Masashi Aoyagi, feuding with Shiro Koshinaka and Kuniaki Kobayashi. In 1992, the four formed a faction later named Heisei Ishingun, but left the promotion in 1998. After a lengthy hiatus, Saito made his surprise return to pro wrestling in October 2000 for Pro Wrestling NOAH.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":45,"teams":[1906,2295,2935],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":78,"storytelling":79,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":79,"psychology":78,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":56,"technicalCoaching":51,"characterCoaching":53,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":53,"brandBuilding":38,"socialMediaSavvy":48,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":56,"consistency":66,"awareness":78,"judgement":87},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-715","wrestlerId":715,"promotionId":45,"startDate":"2000-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":716,"name":"Daisuke Harada","realName":"Daisuke Harada","picture":"Daisuke Harada.jpg","ability":63,"currentAbility":64,"potentialAbility":64,"charisma":63,"micSkills":52,"popularity":5,"condition":72,"hardcoreAbility":65,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":80,"height":167,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1986-11-13T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2003-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Daisuke Harada is a Japanese professional wrestler, currently signed to Pro Wrestling Noah. He is also known for his time in Osaka Pro Wrestling, where he was a two-time Osaka Pro Wrestling Champion and a two-time Osaka Pro Wrestling Tag Team Champion as part of the tag team Momo no Seishun Tag with Atsushi Kotoge. Harada and Kotoge have also worked together for various other promotions across Japan and for Philadelphia, Pennsylvania based Chikara in the United States. Harada reportedly first got interested in professional wrestling through the video game Toukon Ratsuden, after which his first in–person professional wrestling experience was attending the January 4, 1998, Final Power Hall in Tokyo Dome show, witnessing the conclusion of Riki Choshu's retirement tour.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1227],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":72,"storytelling":76,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":26,"matchLayout":77,"psychology":72,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":82,"technicalCoaching":72,"characterCoaching":55,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":74,"mediaHandling":55,"brandBuilding":60,"socialMediaSavvy":48,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":82,"consistency":78,"awareness":72,"judgement":83}},{"id":717,"name":"Marshall Von Erich","realName":"Marshall Von Erich","picture":"Marshall Von Erich.jpg","ability":56,"currentAbility":59,"potentialAbility":59,"charisma":68,"micSkills":62,"popularity":7,"condition":95,"hardcoreAbility":76,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":104,"height":190,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1992-11-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2012-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Grappling and learning new techniques on the beaches of Kauai from his father, Kevin Von Erich, this Texas born bad ass is a force to reckon with.\r\n\r\nPreferring to fight barefoot, like his father, Marshall is a 3rdgeneration grappler. Similar to his father, Marshall also possesses one of the best dropkicks in the sport, attaining a vertical leap that would put most athletes to shame.  Shocking fans and devastating opponents with his signature moonsault, Marshall is exceptional in every way.\r\n\r\nA top-level wrestler in both singles and tag team competition with his older brother, Ross, Marshall fights for his family’s name and their future.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":49,"teams":[232,1523,1873,4024,4025],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":51,"storytelling":56,"productFit":22,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":57,"psychology":51,"workerManagement":22,"trainingIntensity":75,"technicalCoaching":55,"characterCoaching":67,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":67,"brandBuilding":73,"socialMediaSavvy":45,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":4,"reactionSpeed":75,"consistency":68,"awareness":51,"judgement":39},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-717","wrestlerId":717,"promotionId":49,"startDate":"2024-07-20T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-07-20T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-07-20T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"inDevelopment":true},{"id":718,"name":"Ross Von Erich","realName":"Ross Von Erich","picture":"Ross Von Erich.jpg","ability":43,"currentAbility":51,"potentialAbility":51,"charisma":54,"micSkills":47,"popularity":7,"condition":95,"hardcoreAbility":71,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":98,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1988-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2012-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"A strategist inside the ring, Ross wastes no movement, systematically focusing on his opponents’ weaknesses until they are too tired to endure his blitzing offense. Featuring fast and furious brawling, cutting-edge grappling and Brazilian Jiu-Jitsui mat work, his arsenal also includes uncanny aerial attacks.\r\n\r\nProud and serious, Ross Von Erich mixes technical wrestling, brawling, MMA and aerial attacks to make for a customized hybrid wrestling style.\r\n\r\nA dangerous competitor both in singles competition as well as a franchise tag team unit with his younger brother, Marshall, Ross Von Erich is a top ranked competitor in both divisions.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":49,"teams":[232,1523,1873,4024,4025],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":44,"storytelling":49,"productFit":22,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":51,"psychology":44,"workerManagement":22,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":46,"characterCoaching":50,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":50,"brandBuilding":68,"socialMediaSavvy":45,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":4,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":61,"awareness":44,"judgement":35},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-718","wrestlerId":718,"promotionId":49,"startDate":"2024-07-20T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-07-20T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-07-20T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"inDevelopment":true},{"id":719,"name":"Masao Inoue","realName":"Masao Inoue","picture":"Masao Inoue.jpg","ability":63,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":55,"charisma":42,"micSkills":65,"popularity":5,"condition":66,"hardcoreAbility":50,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"submission","gender":"M","weight":106,"height":177,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1970-03-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1988-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Started out in All Japan as an underling to Kawada and Taue. Moved to NOAH and stayed close with Taue, and also Akitoshi Saito. A strong wrestler. Was given a big chance, taking on Jun Akiyama in the Budokan, where he impressed greatly, only to be sent back to the midcard of NOAH. Inoue was a founding member of the Dark Agents stable along with Akitoshi Saito and Takashi Sugiura. He would be second-in-command to Saito. Inoue generally spent his time near the bottom card, not receiving very many high profile matches. fter several years of struggling to make it up the card, Inoue and seven other NOAH wrestlers were given a huge opportunity to main event a Tokyo Nippon Budokan event. GHC Heavyweight Champion Jun Akiyama proposed a tournament to determine his next challenger. Masao Inoue shocked many wrestling fans by beating rookie Shuhei Taniguchi, Takuma Sano, and finally stablemate Akitoshi Saito to win the tournament.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1906],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":63,"storytelling":68,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":69,"psychology":63,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":58,"technicalCoaching":45,"characterCoaching":62,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":62,"brandBuilding":47,"socialMediaSavvy":51,"ruleKnowledge":16,"positioning":33,"reactionSpeed":58,"consistency":59,"awareness":63,"judgement":78}},{"id":720,"name":"Ricky Marvin","realName":"Ricky Marvin","picture":"Ricky Marvin.jpg","ability":58,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"charisma":44,"micSkills":46,"popularity":9,"condition":71,"hardcoreAbility":50,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":79,"height":167,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1980-01-08T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1995-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Ricardo Fuentes Romero is a Mexican professional wrestler, known by his ringname Ricky Marvin, who is widely regarded for his work in the Japanese promotion Pro Wrestling Noah. He occasionally wrestles as the masked Mushiking Joker, the arch-enemy of Mushiking Terry, who was played by his then tag team partner Kotaro Suzuki. Suzuki and Ricky Marvin were the first Japanese/foreigner team to win the GHC Junior Heavyweight Tag Team Championship. Ricardo Fuentes was trained for his professional wrestling career by his father Aries and later on by Ringo Mendoza, Negro Casas and Memo Diaz when he began working for Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre. On April 15, 2013, Marvin returned to AAA, joining Los Perros del Mal.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[291,3034],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":58,"storytelling":66,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":33,"matchLayout":68,"psychology":58,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":63,"characterCoaching":62,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":67,"mediaHandling":62,"brandBuilding":48,"socialMediaSavvy":51,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":63,"awareness":58,"judgement":75}},{"id":721,"name":"Super Crazy","realName":"Super Crazy","picture":"Super Crazy.jpg","ability":70,"currentAbility":62,"potentialAbility":62,"charisma":74,"micSkills":61,"popularity":19,"condition":62,"hardcoreAbility":78,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":98,"height":170,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1973-12-03T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1988-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Francisco Pantoja Islas is a Mexican Luchador, best known by his ring name Super Crazy. Francisco Islas made his professional wrestling debut in February 1988, at just 14 years of age, after being trained by his older brother Rey Pantera. Islas took the ring name \"Super Crazy\". He initially worked as an enmascaradoPantoja is most known for his three year run in World Wrestling Entertainment. In Mexico Pantoja has worked for Asistencia Asesoría y Administración. Pantoja first got American exposure by working for Extreme Championship Wrestling. He has also toured Japan on several occasions working for New Japan Pro Wrestling, Pro Wrestling ZERO-ONE and most recently for All Japan Pro Wrestling and Pro Wrestling NOAH.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":45,"teams":[291,1007,1222,2180,3266],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":69,"storytelling":71,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":36,"matchLayout":72,"psychology":69,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":62,"technicalCoaching":63,"characterCoaching":68,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":64,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":48,"socialMediaSavvy":45,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":62,"consistency":52,"awareness":69,"judgement":81},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-721","wrestlerId":721,"promotionId":45,"startDate":"2022-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":722,"name":"Takuma Sano","realName":"Takuma Sano","picture":"Takuma Sano.jpg","ability":77,"currentAbility":85,"potentialAbility":85,"charisma":77,"micSkills":73,"popularity":9,"condition":75,"hardcoreAbility":89,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":110,"height":177,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1965-02-02T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1984-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Naoki Sano is a Japanese professional wrestler. He currently goes by the name Takuma Sano. Sano was a member of the 1984 New Japan Pro Wrestling (NJPW) dojo class, and in his first few years, he was a jobber. In 1989, he won the Young Lions Cup and he had numerous acclaimed matches against Jushin Liger. In July 1990, Sano moved to the Super World of Sports (SWS) after a big money offer from Megane Super, the company backing the promotion. In UWFI, he adopted the name Yuhi Sano. Adopting the shinguards and trunks typical of shoot style wrestlers. In 2001, he joined Pro Wrestling Noah. He became Takuma Sano, for a year wearing tights and wrestling junior heavyweights, but after fully turning heavyweight, he went back to the shinguards and trunks.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3300],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":70,"storytelling":75,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":77,"psychology":70,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":63,"technicalCoaching":67,"characterCoaching":47,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":47,"brandBuilding":44,"socialMediaSavvy":34,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":63,"consistency":62,"awareness":70,"judgement":82}},{"id":723,"name":"Yoshinari Ogawa","realName":"Yoshinari Ogawa","picture":"Yoshinari Ogawa.jpg","ability":95,"currentAbility":94,"potentialAbility":94,"charisma":95,"micSkills":100,"popularity":5,"condition":58,"hardcoreAbility":77,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":82,"height":167,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1966-11-02T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1985-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Yoshinari Ogawa is a Japanese professional wrestler who currently works for Pro Wrestling Noah. He has earned the nickname of \"Rat Boy\" due to his sneaky, clever in-ring tactics and baiting his opponents into quick pins. Yoshinari Ogawa debuted in All Japan Pro Wrestling in 1985, working on the undercard, until joining Genichiro Tenryu's group Revolution, which helped him elevated higher in the card. He remained in the group until it disbanded in 1990, upon Tenryu's abrupt departure from AJPW. After Tenryu left, Ogawa became one of the top stars in AJPW's junior heavyweight division in the 1990s, winning the junior heavyweight championship three times. He also reigned as tag team champion with his mentor, Mitsuharu Misawa. Ogawa left AJPW for Misawa's newly started Pro Wrestling Noah in 2000, where he continued his tag team with Misawa. On April 4, 2002 he scored a huge upset, beating Jun Akiyama very quickly to become the GHC Heavyweight Champion.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":45,"teams":[1865,2374,3052,3064,3065],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":88,"storytelling":89,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":12,"matchLayout":89,"psychology":88,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":63,"technicalCoaching":68,"characterCoaching":65,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":88,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":36,"socialMediaSavvy":63,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":63,"consistency":62,"awareness":88,"judgement":93},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-723","wrestlerId":723,"promotionId":45,"startDate":"2000-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":724,"name":"Mikey Nicholls","realName":"Mikey Nicholls","picture":"Mikey Nicholls.jpg","ability":59,"currentAbility":63,"potentialAbility":63,"charisma":54,"micSkills":71,"popularity":22,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":64,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":104,"height":182,"base":"Australia","birthplace":"Australia","dateOfBirth":"1985-08-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2001-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Mikey Nicholls, a 2011 graduate of the Pro Wrestling NOAH Dojo, is an Australian wrestler who works in America, Canada, the British Isles, Japan and Oceania. He is a Middleweight who is classed as using a Technician style. He is one half of TMDK alongside Shane Haste. He is best known for his work with NJPW, NOAH and NXT. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":49,"teams":[1536,2311,2779,3032,3866],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":70,"storytelling":72,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":73,"psychology":70,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":54,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":54,"brandBuilding":50,"socialMediaSavvy":48,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":77,"awareness":70,"judgement":82},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-724","wrestlerId":724,"promotionId":49,"startDate":"2026-03-11T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2028-03-11T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2028-03-11T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":725,"name":"Shane Haste","realName":"Shane Haste","picture":"Shane Haste.jpg","ability":77,"currentAbility":67,"potentialAbility":67,"charisma":70,"micSkills":69,"populari