A","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1976-10-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2006-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Keith Harris is a referee from the North Eatern US who has mostly worked for Squared Circle Wrestling where has performed as a referee and on screen authority figure.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":1,"storytelling":1,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":99,"matchLayout":1,"psychology":1,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":6,"technicalCoaching":2,"characterCoaching":52,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":1,"mediaHandling":52,"brandBuilding":30,"socialMediaSavvy":52,"ruleKnowledge":70,"positioning":56,"reactionSpeed":6,"consistency":1,"awareness":1,"judgement":1}},{"id":948,"name":"Roddy Piper","realName":"Roddy Piper","picture":"Roddy Piper.jpg","ability":57,"currentAbility":60,"potentialAbility":60,"charisma":55,"micSkills":50,"popularity":35,"condition":48,"hardcoreAbility":50,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":104,"height":185,"base":"Canada","birthplace":"Canada","dateOfBirth":"1954-04-17T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1972-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":true,"story":"Although today he enjoys favored status as a beloved member of the WWE Hall of Fame, \"Rowdy\" Roddy Piper began his WWE career as one of the most-hated villains ever to step between the ropes. After making his bones in the NWA during the late '70s, the Hot Rod came to WWE in 1984, where he quickly rose to astronomical heights. His battles with Hulk Hogan became a WWE mainstay, and the two often engaged in heated banter during interview segments that rank among the most-entertaining interview segments in the company’s history. Rowdy” Roddy Piper has claimed he was born to controversy, and his wild, freewheeling life has proven that statement to be more than hyperbole. Now into his fifth decade as a WWE Superstar, Piper continues to shake things up wherever he goes. As John Cena, who was confronted by Piper on a November 2011 installment of \"Piper’s Pit\" learned, just when you think you know the answers, he changes the questions.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":83,"storytelling":85,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":14,"matchLayout":85,"psychology":83,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":37,"technicalCoaching":36,"characterCoaching":87,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":86,"mediaHandling":87,"brandBuilding":77,"socialMediaSavvy":85,"ruleKnowledge":20,"positioning":36,"reactionSpeed":37,"consistency":65,"awareness":83,"judgement":90}},{"id":949,"name":"Sean Carr","realName":"Sean Carr","picture":"Sean Carr.jpg","ability":37,"currentAbility":45,"potentialAbility":45,"charisma":49,"micSkills":34,"popularity":0,"condition":90,"hardcoreAbility":36,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":95,"height":187,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1988-01-05T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Sean Carr is an American professional wrestler, best known for his work on the New York and New England independent scenes. He has worked for ECPW, WXW and 2CW. Alongside Kage, Carr has formed a formidable tag team known as Team CK. In 2CW they've won the Tag Team Titles.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":31,"storytelling":38,"productFit":40,"riskTaking":36,"matchLayout":40,"psychology":31,"workerManagement":40,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":40,"characterCoaching":55,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":64,"mediaHandling":55,"brandBuilding":42,"socialMediaSavvy":44,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":8,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":69,"awareness":31,"judgement":35}},{"id":953,"name":"Terry Funk","realName":"Terry Funk","picture":"Terry Funk.jpg","ability":49,"currentAbility":57,"potentialAbility":57,"charisma":57,"micSkills":43,"popularity":20,"condition":39,"hardcoreAbility":59,"injuryProne":87,"type":"wrestler","style":"striker","gender":"M","weight":112,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1944-06-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1962-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":true,"story":"Terry Funk is a semi-retired American professional wrestler and former actor known chiefly for the hardcore wrestling style he adopted in the latter part of his career that inspired many younger wrestlers, including Mick Foley. Funk has appeared in the NWA, AWA, WWF/E, WCW, ECW, ROH, and TNA. Funk is a five-time World Champion, having held the NWA World Heavyweight Championship once and ECW World Heavyweight Championship twice (ECW awarded him the honorary lifetime title of ECW Champion due to his contributions to the promotion) and IWA World Heavyweight Championship twice. He is the only man to have been inducted into the WWE, WCW, Professional Wrestling, NWA, Hardcore, Wrestling Observer, and St. Louis Wrestling Halls of Fame. Funk was a primary subject of the documentary film Beyond the Mat, and is often noted for the longevity of his career, which has included multiple \"retirement\" matches.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1060,1427,3245,3304],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":88,"storytelling":92,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":29,"matchLayout":93,"psychology":88,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":38,"technicalCoaching":23,"characterCoaching":69,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":71,"mediaHandling":69,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":64,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":38,"consistency":41,"awareness":88,"judgement":93}},{"id":956,"name":"Jeremy Hardy","realName":"Jeremy Hardy","picture":"Jeremy Hardy.jpg","ability":39,"currentAbility":47,"potentialAbility":47,"charisma":54,"micSkills":38,"popularity":0,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":32,"injuryProne":100,"type":"referee","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":93,"height":170,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1981-08-05T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2003-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Jeremy Hardy is an American professional wrestling referee. He is known for his work with various independant promotions (mainly based in Utah) such as American Championship Wrestling-Utah from 2003-2010, Ultra-Championship Zero Wrestling in Utah, American Xtreme in Utah, Real Mexican Wrestling in Utah and Future Stars Of Wrestling in Las Vegas.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":27,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":27,"brandBuilding":5,"socialMediaSavvy":12,"ruleKnowledge":47,"positioning":38,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0}},{"id":968,"name":"Latin Lover","realName":"Latin Lover","picture":"Latin Lover.jpg","ability":85,"currentAbility":82,"potentialAbility":82,"charisma":79,"micSkills":87,"popularity":6,"condition":71,"hardcoreAbility":72,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":98,"height":182,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1967-10-25T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1992-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Victor Manuel Resendiz Ruiz is a Mexican Luchador  and actor. He is best known under his ring name Latin Lover, which he is also credited as for his acting career. Resendiz is best known for wrestling in the Mexican Asistencia Asesoría y Administración (AAA) promotion, but has also worked for the World Wrestling Federation (WWF) and currently works for the Perros del Mal and Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) promotions under the ring name Latino. Resendiz and his partner Mariana Vallejo Isrrade won the very first Bailando por un Sueño dance competition in 2005.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":5,"teams":[3181],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":64,"storytelling":67,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":68,"psychology":64,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":53,"technicalCoaching":55,"characterCoaching":70,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":70,"brandBuilding":68,"socialMediaSavvy":72,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":53,"consistency":71,"awareness":64,"judgement":78},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-968","wrestlerId":968,"promotionId":5,"startDate":"2024-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":977,"name":"Angel Blue","realName":"Angel Blue","picture":"Angel Blue.jpg","ability":33,"currentAbility":40,"potentialAbility":40,"charisma":49,"micSkills":34,"popularity":0,"condition":93,"hardcoreAbility":47,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"F","weight":49,"height":152,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1990-08-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Angel Blue was trained by both Lance Hoyt and Wally Darkmon before making her debut in PCW on their Uncut shows, originally as Alektra Blue(not to be confused with the adult film star of the same name). She has since been working on the Texas independent circuit as \"The Mega Star\" Angel Blue. Blue has made her biggest splash in ACW in Austin. Her first run in ACW saw her as a member of the Smurf Nation and winning the ACW Joshi Title. Her latest run has seen her align herself with the promotion's owner, Darin Childs, on a mission to reclaim what she believes is her rightful ACW Joshi Title.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":38,"storytelling":44,"productFit":40,"riskTaking":45,"matchLayout":46,"psychology":38,"workerManagement":40,"trainingIntensity":72,"technicalCoaching":43,"characterCoaching":39,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":55,"mediaHandling":39,"brandBuilding":52,"socialMediaSavvy":40,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":8,"reactionSpeed":72,"consistency":53,"awareness":38,"judgement":39}},{"id":983,"name":"JD Griffey","realName":"JD Griffey","picture":"Jerome Daniels.jpg","ability":48,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":53,"charisma":38,"micSkills":68,"popularity":1,"condition":92,"hardcoreAbility":51,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"submission","gender":"M","weight":93,"height":190,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1984-05-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2007-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"\"Flawless\" Jerome Daniels has been flawless LONG before two bimbos claimed to be flawless(even though they were anything but). Jerome began his career in PCW(Texas), and would venture his way over to XCW, where he joined up with manager Lance Romance and his stable, International Playaz Club. He then went on to team with Nobe Bryant to win the NWA Texas Tag Team Titles on two occasions. Lately, he's been teaming with \"Main Event\" Mike Foxx and Byron Wilcott as Team ATM. The trio would utilize the Freebird Rule as they won the NWA TXO Tag Team Titles. In other promotions, Jerome and Byron team up under the tag team name of \"Addictive and Expensive.\"","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":53,"storytelling":57,"productFit":61,"riskTaking":31,"matchLayout":59,"psychology":53,"workerManagement":61,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":63,"characterCoaching":64,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":69,"mediaHandling":64,"brandBuilding":64,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":12,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":66,"awareness":53,"judgement":56}},{"id":997,"name":"Ric Manning","realName":"Ric Manning","picture":"Rick Manning.jpg","ability":72,"currentAbility":73,"potentialAbility":73,"charisma":67,"micSkills":71,"popularity":1,"condition":83,"hardcoreAbility":53,"injuryProne":100,"type":"referee","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":104,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1957-06-12T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1977-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Ric Manning has probably worked for almost every Texas wrestling show under the sun, including NWA Southwest, PCW(Arlington), XCW, NTWA... the list goes on and on. A class act who stays out of backstage squabbles, politics and the like, and manages to get along with everybody. No one seems to have a bad thing to say about the Texas based referee who was trained by David Manning of WCCW fame. While refereeing in XCW, he refereed under the pseudonym of \"George Lucas,\" a nickname he earned for bearing a resemblance to the movie director of the same name. Ric also appeared on \"Walker: Texas Ranger\" with Rowdy Roddy Piper and Rugged Rod Price in an episode filmed at the famed Dallas Sportatorium.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":48,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":41,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":50,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":50,"brandBuilding":16,"socialMediaSavvy":38,"ruleKnowledge":73,"positioning":58,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":83,"awareness":68,"judgement":41}},{"id":998,"name":"Rob Moore","realName":"Rob Moore","picture":"Rob Moore.jpg","ability":46,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":55,"charisma":51,"micSkills":61,"popularity":1,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":72,"injuryProne":100,"type":"commentator","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":128,"height":187,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1961-09-16T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1981-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Despite having never worked for any of the bigger companies, Rob Moore is a very capable announcer, and is very professional, staying out of any backstage politics and strife, managing to get along with everybody. Texas promotions he has called play by play for include NWA Southwest, PCW in Arlington, XCW in Denton, and most recently, IHWE and Killer Tim Brooks' NTWA.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":65,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":50,"socialMediaSavvy":64,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":0,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":70,"awareness":0,"judgement":0}},{"id":1000,"name":"Ryan Davidson","realName":"Ryan Davidson","picture":"Ryan Davidson.jpg","ability":62,"currentAbility":63,"potentialAbility":63,"charisma":67,"micSkills":56,"popularity":1,"condition":90,"hardcoreAbility":74,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":110,"height":187,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1985-04-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2005-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"\"Ruthless\" Ryan Davidson is an Oklahoma based wrestler that works shows mostly in Oklahoma and Texas. He had worked for Total Texas Wrestling in Graham, Texas, as well as for Texas All-Star Wrestling. He received further training and really honed his skills for Booker T's PWA in Houston, Texas, where he is a former Iron Man and Tag Team Champion. Ryan made an appearance on WWE Monday Night Raw in January 2007, portraying a security guard that was confiscating DX signs, and ranked #18 in the 2005 Oklafan Top 50, and shot up to #2 on the Oklafan Top 50 the following year. He also clocked in at #60 on the 2007 Indywarz Texas Top 100.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":65,"storytelling":67,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":28,"matchLayout":67,"psychology":65,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":72,"technicalCoaching":48,"characterCoaching":62,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":72,"mediaHandling":62,"brandBuilding":53,"socialMediaSavvy":59,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":72,"consistency":72,"awareness":65,"judgement":79}},{"id":1002,"name":"Tim Storm","realName":"Tim Storm","picture":"Tim Storm.jpg","ability":55,"currentAbility":60,"potentialAbility":60,"charisma":59,"micSkills":73,"popularity":6,"condition":84,"hardcoreAbility":64,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":118,"height":187,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1965-02-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1995-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Tim Storm is an American wrestler who works exclusively in America. He is a Light Heavyweight who is classed as using a Regular style. He is best known for his work with NWA and CWFH. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":79,"teams":[3019,3964],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":73,"storytelling":73,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":14,"matchLayout":73,"psychology":73,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":68,"technicalCoaching":28,"characterCoaching":65,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":86,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":64,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":68,"consistency":69,"awareness":73,"judgement":84},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1002","wrestlerId":1002,"promotionId":79,"startDate":"2016-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1006,"name":"El Oriental","realName":"El Oriental","picture":"El Oriental_alt.jpg","ability":67,"currentAbility":62,"potentialAbility":62,"charisma":59,"micSkills":72,"popularity":7,"condition":78,"hardcoreAbility":52,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":80,"height":165,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1972-12-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1990-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Noé Astro Moreno León is a Mexican Luchador known under the ring name El Oriental. He is the son of wrestler and promoter Alfonso \"Acorazado\" Moreno and has worked over 70 tours of Japan. The person who would later become known as El Oriental was born on December 6, 1972 son of Mexican luchador and wrestling promoter Alfonso Moreno. Later on Moreno along with Dr. Wagner and Blue Panther trained El Oriental for his professional wrestling career. He made his debut on October 23, 1992 in Arena Azteca Budokan, the arena his father operated at the time. El Oriental adopted the ring name upon making his debut and has competed exclusively under that name since then. Early in his career he worked mainly in or around his home state of Ciudad Nezahualcóyotl, Mexico State, often working with his sisters Cynthia, Rossy and Esther Moreno.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3136,3167],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":64,"storytelling":68,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":34,"matchLayout":69,"psychology":64,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":62,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":60,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":66,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":67,"socialMediaSavvy":51,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":62,"consistency":78,"awareness":64,"judgement":78}},{"id":1007,"name":"Esther Moreno","realName":"Esther Moreno","picture":"Esther Moreno.jpg","ability":65,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":55,"charisma":69,"micSkills":67,"popularity":4,"condition":59,"hardcoreAbility":61,"injuryProne":93,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"F","weight":59,"height":149,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1969-02-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1984-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"María Esther Moreno León is a Mexican luchadora, best known under the ring name Esther Moreno. In AAA she is a former 2 time AAA Reina de Reinas Champion. In the early 1990s Esther and her sister Cynthia Moreno travelled to Japan to wrestle for All Japan Women's Pro-Wrestling. On April 21, 1991 the Moreno sisters defeated Etsuko Mita and Mima Shimoda to win the AJW Tag Team Championship, making them the first Mexican team to hold a championship in Japan.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3137,3138,3139],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":65,"storytelling":69,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":70,"psychology":65,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":47,"technicalCoaching":63,"characterCoaching":58,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":58,"brandBuilding":44,"socialMediaSavvy":42,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":47,"consistency":47,"awareness":65,"judgement":79}},{"id":1008,"name":"Shinjiro Otani","realName":"Shinjiro Otani","picture":"Shinjiro Otani.jpg","ability":76,"currentAbility":70,"potentialAbility":70,"charisma":85,"micSkills":56,"popularity":13,"condition":1,"hardcoreAbility":73,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":97,"height":177,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1972-07-21T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1992-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Shinjiro Otani is a Japanese professional wrestler contracted to Pro Wrestling ZERO1. Otani is also the acting President of the company. Otani was the first WCW World Cruiserweight Champion, defeating Wild Pegasus in a tournament final to be crowned champion on March 20, 1996. This was the start of his push as a legitimate junior heavyweight contender. Over the years, Otani earned the J-Crown and was also part of the first IWGP Junior Heavyweight Tag Team Champions with Tatsuhito Takaiwa. On January 4, 2013, at Wrestle Kingdom 7 in Tokyo Dome, Otani made a special return to New Japan, when he replaced an injured Daichi Hashimoto in a tag team match, where he and Keiji Mutoh were defeated by Hiroyoshi Tenzan and Satoshi Kojima.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":45,"teams":[623,2317,2954,2955,2956,3059,3224,3225],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":79,"storytelling":84,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":18,"matchLayout":85,"psychology":79,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":68,"technicalCoaching":73,"characterCoaching":66,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":82,"mediaHandling":66,"brandBuilding":53,"socialMediaSavvy":51,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":68,"consistency":62,"awareness":79,"judgement":87},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1008","wrestlerId":1008,"promotionId":45,"startDate":"2026-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2028-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2028-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1009,"name":"Johnny Gargano","realName":"Johnny Gargano","picture":"Johnny Gargano.jpg","ability":65,"currentAbility":71,"potentialAbility":71,"charisma":64,"micSkills":58,"popularity":40,"condition":85,"hardcoreAbility":61,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":90,"height":175,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1987-08-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2005-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"mid","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Since starting his path to Superstardom, the man known as Johnny Wrestling has heard “no” more times than he can count. When he first broke in, he was told he was too small to be a serious contender, and he still has the rejection email he received after attending a WWE tryout in 2015, keeping it as a reminder of how far he’s come. Because make no mistake, the self-described “chubby kid from Cleveland” — who used to play-wrestle on mattresses and aspire to become the next Shawn Michaels — has come a long, long way. Starting out as an unsigned free agent, Gargano first made his mark in NXT in a tag team with Tommaso Ciampa. The duo known as #DIY lifted NXT’s tandem division to new heights, producing classic rivalries against the likes of The Revival and AOP, as well as an impressive NXT Tag Team Title reign. After the team’s implosion in 2017, a fate brought on by Ciampa’s ruthless betrayal of Gargano, the two Superstars experienced more ups and downs than a rollercoaster ride.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[906,1352,2454,2809,3856],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":76,"storytelling":78,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":79,"psychology":76,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":84,"technicalCoaching":75,"characterCoaching":68,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":55,"socialMediaSavvy":63,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":84,"consistency":81,"awareness":76,"judgement":86},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1009","wrestlerId":1009,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2022-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":1010,"name":"CIMA","realName":"CIMA","picture":"CIMA.jpg","ability":76,"currentAbility":68,"potentialAbility":68,"charisma":66,"micSkills":72,"popularity":17,"condition":71,"hardcoreAbility":76,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":82,"height":172,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1977-11-15T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1997-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"CIMA is a Japanese wrestler who works in America, the British Isles and Japan. He is a Lightweight who is classed as using a Technician Flyer style. He is best known for his work with WCW, NJPW, CMLL, AEW, AJPW, Dragongate, PWG, wXw, DDT, ROH, MLW, BJW, ZERO1, GLEAT, The Crash, WRESTLE-1, DEFY, IWRG, FCP, DTU and SWE. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1266,1327,1555,2006,2297],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":70,"storytelling":75,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":76,"psychology":70,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":76,"characterCoaching":83,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":83,"brandBuilding":72,"socialMediaSavvy":65,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":64,"awareness":70,"judgement":82}},{"id":1011,"name":"Stalker Ichikawa","realName":"Stalker Ichikawa","picture":"Stalker Ichikawa.jpg","ability":58,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":55,"charisma":59,"micSkills":59,"popularity":4,"condition":66,"hardcoreAbility":70,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"comedy","gender":"M","weight":65,"height":162,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1974-10-12T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Kanji Ichikawa better known by his stage name \"Hollywood\" Stalker Ichikawa is a Japanese professional wrestler. Stalker Ichikawa is one of the most popular superstars from Dragon Gate. A member of Último Dragón's Toryumon Dojo second class gifted with an extensive amateur wrestling background, Ichikawa is one of the many comedy characters whose purpose is more based on entertaining the fans than it is to actually win matches. Stalker's matches do not last very long, often within five to ten minutes tops. His offenses would have little to no effect on his opponents and they would simply side-step whenever he attempts any sort of high flying move. In some cases, just as Stalker is about to be hit by his opponent's finisher some one, usually his wife Namiko, would throw in the towel to stop the match. The opponent would still hit him with his finisher shortly after.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":66,"storytelling":70,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":71,"psychology":66,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":64,"technicalCoaching":51,"characterCoaching":82,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":82,"brandBuilding":20,"socialMediaSavvy":78,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":64,"consistency":65,"awareness":66,"judgement":80}},{"id":1012,"name":"Shingo Takagi","realName":"Shingo Takagi","picture":"Shingo Takagi.jpg","ability":75,"currentAbility":74,"potentialAbility":74,"charisma":79,"micSkills":84,"popularity":35,"condition":74,"hardcoreAbility":85,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"submission","gender":"M","weight":100,"height":175,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1982-11-21T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Shingo Takagi, a 2004 graduate of the Dragon Gate Dojo, is a Japanese wrestler who works in America, Canada, Mexico, the British Isles and Japan. He is a Middleweight who is classed as using a Impactful style. He is best known for his work with NJPW, Dragongate, wXw and ROH. He is currently the NJPW King Of Pro Wrestling champion. He was voted Young Wrestler Of The Year in 2005.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":38,"teams":[1229,1351,1785,2944,2949,4293],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":83,"storytelling":84,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":85,"psychology":83,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":86,"technicalCoaching":73,"characterCoaching":60,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":73,"socialMediaSavvy":46,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":86,"consistency":84,"awareness":83,"judgement":90},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1012","wrestlerId":1012,"promotionId":38,"startDate":"2018-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":1017,"name":"Nobuhiko Takada","realName":"Nobuhiko Takada","picture":"Nobuhiko Takada.jpg","ability":50,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"charisma":67,"micSkills":61,"popularity":7,"condition":85,"hardcoreAbility":42,"injuryProne":90,"type":"manager","style":"submission","gender":"M","weight":100,"height":180,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1962-04-12T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1981-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Nobuhiko Takada is a Japanese mixed martial arts fighter and professional wrestler. He is best known for helping to popularize shoot-style professional wrestling, as one of the biggest stars of the UWF in the '80s and '90s. Despite his irregular fight record and kayfabe politics, Takada is credited with the existence of PRIDE and the Japanese MMA boom, and is widely considered to be one of the main promotors of mixed martial arts both nationally and internationally. Nobuhiko Takada made his professional wrestling debut in 1981 against Norio Honaga, for New Japan Pro Wrestling, where he started his career as a Junior Heavyweight.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":78,"storytelling":82,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":84,"psychology":78,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":51,"technicalCoaching":64,"characterCoaching":69,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":69,"brandBuilding":71,"socialMediaSavvy":69,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":51,"consistency":49,"awareness":78,"judgement":87}},{"id":1018,"name":"Animal Hamaguchi","realName":"Animal Hamaguchi","picture":"Animal Hamaguchi.jpg","ability":86,"currentAbility":93,"potentialAbility":93,"charisma":85,"micSkills":84,"popularity":5,"condition":44,"hardcoreAbility":98,"injuryProne":71,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":103,"height":167,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1947-08-31T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1965-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Heigo Hamaguchi is a Japanese retired professional wrestler, better known by the ring name Animal Hamaguchi.  During his career he was recognized as a talented tag team wrestler despite his small size for a heavyweight, and today he is recognized as a trainer in both professional and amateur wrestling. Hamaguchi debuted in 1969 in the old International Wrestling Enterprise. He was a regular mid-carder although his teams with Mighty Inoue and Rusher Kimura were main event. Hamaguchi retired in 1995, after his team lost the title, to dedicate full-time to his dojo, today recognized as one of the premier independent wrestling schools in Japan.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":86,"storytelling":90,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":15,"matchLayout":92,"psychology":86,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":38,"technicalCoaching":39,"characterCoaching":51,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":85,"mediaHandling":51,"brandBuilding":38,"socialMediaSavvy":47,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":38,"consistency":49,"awareness":86,"judgement":92}},{"id":1019,"name":"Akira Hokuto","realName":"Akira Hokuto","picture":"Akira Hokuto.jpg","ability":96,"currentAbility":95,"potentialAbility":95,"charisma":95,"micSkills":83,"popularity":18,"condition":56,"hardcoreAbility":84,"injuryProne":30,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"F","weight":63,"height":165,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1967-07-13T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1985-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Hisako Sasaki is a former professional wrestler better known as Akira Hokuto. She is married to wrestler Kensuke Sasaki. Akira was one of the most talented women wrestlers in the world, while active. She along with Kensuke, have taken in Katsuhiko Nakajima in as their almost adopted son. She also helps with the running of Diamond Ring (ex-Kensuke Office)","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":90,"storytelling":91,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":29,"matchLayout":91,"psychology":90,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":44,"technicalCoaching":68,"characterCoaching":69,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":71,"mediaHandling":69,"brandBuilding":78,"socialMediaSavvy":63,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":44,"consistency":53,"awareness":90,"judgement":94}},{"id":1020,"name":"Obariyon","realName":"Obariyon","picture":"Obariyon.jpg","ability":51,"currentAbility":59,"potentialAbility":59,"charisma":64,"micSkills":65,"popularity":2,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":75,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":87,"height":167,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1987-11-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"The Batiri is a professional wrestling alliance in the Chikara promotion. The team currently includes Kobald, Kodama and Obariyon; the first performs under a goblin mask, while the latter two wear face paint with the wrestling characters of demons. Both Kodama's and Obariyon's ring names come from Japanese folklore from the characters of Kodama and Obariyon, while Kobald is named after the German word for goblin. All three men were trained at Chikara's Wrestle Factory by then head trainers Claudio Castagnoli and Mike Quackenbush. On August 28, 2010, Obariyon made his professional wrestling debut for the Chikara promotion, defeating Dustin Rayz in the first round of the Young Lions Cup VIII tournament.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[308,3221,3222],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":61,"productFit":48,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":62,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":48,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":56,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":56,"brandBuilding":32,"socialMediaSavvy":58,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":10,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":75,"awareness":56,"judgement":53}},{"id":1021,"name":"Kodama","realName":"Kodama","picture":"Kodama.jpg","ability":51,"currentAbility":51,"potentialAbility":51,"charisma":62,"micSkills":46,"popularity":2,"condition":96,"hardcoreAbility":57,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":84,"height":167,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1982-07-26T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"The Batiri is a professional wrestling alliance in the Chikara promotion. The team currently includes Kobald, Kodama and Obariyon; the first performs under a goblin mask, while the latter two wear face paint with the wrestling characters of demons. Both Kodama's and Obariyon's ring names come from Japanese folklore from the characters of Kodama and Obariyon, while Kobald is named after the German word for goblin. All three men were trained at Chikara's Wrestle Factory by then head trainers Claudio Castagnoli and Mike Quackenbush. On September 18, Obariyon entered a four-way tag team match, teaming with the debuting Kodama, with the two wearing identical attire and face paint. The two were the second team eliminated from the match by The Osirian Portal.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[308,3221,3222],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":53,"storytelling":56,"productFit":46,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":57,"psychology":53,"workerManagement":46,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":51,"characterCoaching":45,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":45,"brandBuilding":30,"socialMediaSavvy":47,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":9,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":77,"awareness":53,"judgement":50}},{"id":1024,"name":"Onryo","realName":"Onryo","picture":"Onryo.jpg","ability":68,"currentAbility":64,"potentialAbility":64,"charisma":64,"micSkills":60,"popularity":3,"condition":72,"hardcoreAbility":72,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":96,"height":170,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1975-07-09T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1995-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"An amateur wrestler at university, Onryo debuted as \"Wolf Ozawa\" in Wrestle Dream Factory, a ring name he would revive several years later. Onryo wrestled in FMW until his closure, then joined WMF. In 2003 he created with the Crazy SKB, \"666 Triplefiesta\", a bizarre indy promotion, which soon gathered fan interest. Onryo took part in the Super J Cup 2000 and was eliminated in the semifinals by CIMA. Despite never being a top wrestler in any promotion, Onryo was able to win some individual and tag team titles during his career. Onryo's character is inspired to a supernatural creature of the japanese folklore; an Onryo is a ghost who can return to the physical world seeking for vengeance.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":71,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":72,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":74,"technicalCoaching":68,"characterCoaching":72,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":72,"brandBuilding":52,"socialMediaSavvy":74,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":74,"consistency":69,"awareness":68,"judgement":81}},{"id":1025,"name":"Hagane Shinnou","realName":"Hagane Shinnou","picture":"MADOKA.jpg","ability":53,"currentAbility":59,"potentialAbility":59,"charisma":46,"micSkills":60,"popularity":5,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":70,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":80,"height":175,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1983-12-12T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2003-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Hagane Shinnou is a Japanese wrestler who works exclusively in Japan. He is a Lightweight who is classed as using a Technician Flyer style. He is best known for his work with AEW, GanPro and Gatoh Move. He is currently the Super Asia champion.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":103,"teams":[2953,3175],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":69,"storytelling":73,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":75,"psychology":69,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":78,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":59,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":59,"brandBuilding":42,"socialMediaSavvy":49,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":78,"consistency":73,"awareness":69,"judgement":81},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1025","wrestlerId":1025,"promotionId":103,"startDate":"2012-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1026,"name":"Ricochet","realName":"Ricochet","picture":"Ricochet.jpg","ability":53,"currentAbility":63,"potentialAbility":63,"charisma":67,"micSkills":56,"popularity":46,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":51,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":85,"height":172,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1988-10-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2003-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"mid","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Ricochet is an American wrestler who works in the USA, Canada, Mexico, the British Isles, Japan, Europe and Oceania. He is a 5'9\", 188lb worker who is classed as using a High Flyer style. He uses the 630° Splash as his finisher. He is best known for his work with WWE, AEW, NJPW, NXT, Dragon Gate, PWG, wXw, RevPro, Lucha Ungrnd, Beyond, EVOLVE, AAW, IWA-MS, Defiant, DTU, CHIKARA and CZW. He is engaged to someone outside the wrestling business. He was voted Male Independent Wrestler Of The Year in 2014.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[1106,1219,1327,1647,2075,2704,3712],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":68,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":70,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":83,"technicalCoaching":63,"characterCoaching":55,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":55,"brandBuilding":70,"socialMediaSavvy":42,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":83,"consistency":80,"awareness":62,"judgement":77},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1026","wrestlerId":1026,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2024-08-25T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-08-25T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-08-25T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1028,"name":"Cody Hall","realName":"Cody Hall","picture":"Cody Hall.jpg","ability":40,"currentAbility":43,"potentialAbility":43,"charisma":30,"micSkills":52,"popularity":6,"condition":94,"hardcoreAbility":44,"injuryProne":89,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":122,"height":205,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1991-05-31T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2012-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Cody Hall is an American wrestler who works in America, Canada, the British Isles, Japan and Europe. He is a Light Heavyweight who is classed as using a Powerhouse style. He is best known for his work with NJPW, AAA, NOAH, DDT, GWF, RevPro and TNT.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1001],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":40,"storytelling":45,"productFit":86,"riskTaking":52,"matchLayout":46,"psychology":40,"workerManagement":86,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":21,"characterCoaching":53,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":48,"mediaHandling":53,"brandBuilding":64,"socialMediaSavvy":47,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":17,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":52,"awareness":40,"judgement":58}},{"id":1029,"name":"Arik Cannon","realName":"Arik Cannon","picture":"Arik Cannon.jpg","ability":57,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":55,"charisma":65,"micSkills":59,"popularity":5,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":72,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":92,"height":172,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1981-12-23T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2001-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Arik Cannon is a professional wrestler known for competing in companies such as Chikara, IWA Mid-South, All American Wrestling and Wrestling Society X. Arik Cannon was trained at Midwest Pro Wrestling and is known for wrestling in IWA Mid-South. There, he became the IWA Mid-South Heavyweight Champion by defeating Petey Williams in the Ted Petty Invitational Tournament. He defended it against Roderick Strong and Austin Aries, but was forced to give it up due to injury in 2004. He returned to wrestling in 2005 and entered Chikara's Tag World Grand Prix 2005 with partner Claudio Castagnoli and made it to the finals to face Superfriends, Chris Hero and Mike Quackenbush. On September 6, 2009, Cannon made his debut for Dragon Gate USA at the tapings of the promotion's second pay-per-view titled Untouchable.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[2680],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":47,"storytelling":54,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":56,"psychology":47,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":67,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":67,"brandBuilding":32,"socialMediaSavvy":60,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":78,"awareness":47,"judgement":68}},{"id":1030,"name":"Lince Dorado","realName":"Lince Dorado","picture":"Lince Dorado.jpg","ability":56,"currentAbility":52,"potentialAbility":52,"charisma":64,"micSkills":60,"popularity":20,"condition":85,"hardcoreAbility":47,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":82,"height":167,"base":"USA","birthplace":"Puerto Rico","dateOfBirth":"1987-05-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2007-02-17T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Lince Dorado, a 2006 graduate of the CHIKARA Wrestlefactory, is a masked Puerto Rican wrestler who works in America, Canada, Mexico and Japan. He is a Small worker who is classed as using a Luchador style. He is one half of Good Lucha Things alongside Samuray del Sol. He is best known for his work with WWE, CMLL, MLW, REVOLVER and CHIKARA.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":65,"teams":[2255,2362,2762,3946,3961],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":54,"storytelling":60,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":39,"matchLayout":62,"psychology":54,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":78,"technicalCoaching":44,"characterCoaching":45,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":61,"mediaHandling":45,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":33,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":78,"consistency":65,"awareness":54,"judgement":72},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1030","wrestlerId":1030,"promotionId":65,"startDate":"2025-01-17T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2027-01-17T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2027-01-17T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"inDevelopment":true},{"id":1035,"name":"Heddi Karaoui","realName":"Heddi Karaoui","picture":"Heddi Karaoui.jpg","ability":67,"currentAbility":57,"potentialAbility":57,"charisma":55,"micSkills":59,"popularity":7,"condition":93,"hardcoreAbility":45,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"submission","gender":"M","weight":100,"height":175,"base":"Europe","birthplace":"France","dateOfBirth":"1983-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Heddi Karaoui is a French wrestler who works all over the world. He is a 5'10\", 220lb worker who is classed as using a MMA Crossover style. He uses the Chickenwing and the Knockout Punch as his finishers. He is best known for his work with CMLL, DDT, wXw, IWRG, BJW, GCW, BZW and NLL. Outside of wrestling he is a former MMA fighter.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":43,"storytelling":51,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":54,"psychology":43,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":82,"technicalCoaching":73,"characterCoaching":51,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":51,"brandBuilding":56,"socialMediaSavvy":36,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":82,"consistency":61,"awareness":43,"judgement":66}},{"id":1036,"name":"Mark Andrews","realName":"Mark Andrews","picture":"Mark Andrews.jpg","ability":63,"currentAbility":56,"potentialAbility":56,"charisma":49,"micSkills":45,"popularity":18,"condition":90,"hardcoreAbility":63,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":73,"height":170,"base":"UK","birthplace":"Wales","dateOfBirth":"1992-01-25T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2006-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"When Mark Andrews hits the ring, one thing is clear: It’s time to fly.\r\n\r\nInspired by the likes of Rey Mysterio and Shawn Michaels, Andrews is a high-flyer of the finest caliber. With a picture-perfect Shooting Star Press and Standing Moonsault among the many dazzling aerial attacks in his arsenal, Andrews possesses a unique skillset that makes him stand out from others in the NXT UK scene.\r\n\r\nAndrews is a bit of a renaissance man, too, counting videography, video editing, graphic design and clothing design among his many skills. Plus, he’s the bassist and vocalist in the Welsh pop-punk outfit Junior. More than anything, he’s a top-tier competitor.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[728,944,1058,1849,2197,2357,3734,3930,3931],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":54,"storytelling":61,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":24,"matchLayout":63,"psychology":54,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":79,"technicalCoaching":53,"characterCoaching":56,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":76,"mediaHandling":56,"brandBuilding":48,"socialMediaSavvy":44,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":79,"consistency":67,"awareness":54,"judgement":72}},{"id":1037,"name":"Zumbi","realName":"Zumbi","picture":"Zumbi.jpg","ability":57,"currentAbility":47,"potentialAbility":47,"charisma":39,"micSkills":45,"popularity":1,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":62,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":76,"height":170,"base":"Other","birthplace":"Brazil","dateOfBirth":"1984-12-24T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2007-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Zumbi is a masked Brazilian wrestler who was trained by El Mexicano. He performs in his home country for the Brazilian Wrestling Federation as well as appearing in Puerto Rico and Mexico for various promotions. He is a master in Capoeira and uses this in his wrestling style, pulling off some very unique moves.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":42,"storytelling":48,"productFit":40,"riskTaking":47,"matchLayout":50,"psychology":42,"workerManagement":40,"trainingIntensity":84,"technicalCoaching":54,"characterCoaching":34,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":53,"mediaHandling":34,"brandBuilding":23,"socialMediaSavvy":20,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":8,"reactionSpeed":84,"consistency":62,"awareness":42,"judgement":41}},{"id":1039,"name":"Super Nova","realName":"Super Nova","picture":"Super Nova.jpg","ability":50,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":55,"charisma":44,"micSkills":69,"popularity":6,"condition":82,"hardcoreAbility":39,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":77,"height":162,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1986-06-29T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Super Nova is the current ring name of a Mexican Luchador enmascarado, Super Nova is the son of Luchador El Texano and the brother of El Texano, Jr. in addition to being the cousin of another Luchador called Mictlán. Súper Nova's real name is not a matter of public record, as is often the case with masked wrestlers in Mexico where their private lives are kept a secret from the wrestling fans. Only his paternal surname is a matter of public record, Aguilar Leos, as his brother's real name, Juan Aguilar Leos, is publicly known.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3356,3648,4243],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":57,"storytelling":62,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":64,"psychology":57,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":76,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":53,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":53,"brandBuilding":49,"socialMediaSavvy":44,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":76,"consistency":74,"awareness":57,"judgement":74}},{"id":1040,"name":"Buggy Nova","realName":"Buggy Nova","picture":"Buggy Nova.jpg","ability":32,"currentAbility":38,"potentialAbility":38,"charisma":41,"micSkills":27,"popularity":0,"condition":98,"hardcoreAbility":58,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"F","weight":64,"height":170,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1989-11-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2009-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Natalie Laura Osman is an American professional wrestler and valet. She is known both for working for WWE in their developmental territory NXT Wrestling, under the ring name Skyler Moon, and for working for Southern California independent promotions including National Wrestling Alliance, Pro Wrestling Bushido, Mach One Wrestling, Empire Wrestling Federation, as well as Shimmer Women Athletes under the names Buggy Nova, or simply Buggy. After her non--compete clause ended, Osman returned to the independent circuit under the 'Buggy Nova name. Her first appearance came at Full Impact Pro Establish Dominance in which she accompanied The Scene and was used to persuade Kenneth Cameron into joining them, which she failed to do.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":37,"storytelling":42,"productFit":19,"riskTaking":29,"matchLayout":43,"psychology":37,"workerManagement":19,"trainingIntensity":74,"technicalCoaching":35,"characterCoaching":56,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":71,"mediaHandling":56,"brandBuilding":43,"socialMediaSavvy":51,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":4,"reactionSpeed":74,"consistency":62,"awareness":37,"judgement":30}},{"id":1041,"name":"Aeroboy","realName":"Aeroboy","picture":"Aeroboy.jpg","ability":49,"currentAbility":50,"potentialAbility":50,"charisma":55,"micSkills":51,"popularity":2,"condition":89,"hardcoreAbility":44,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":80,"height":172,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1990-08-03T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2003-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"One of the many young wrestlers to fall in love with the extreme wrestling style. Along with schoolmate Violento Jack began working backyard shows in his early teens and has since caught on with some of the hardcore groups to start up in recent years such as NGX and DTU. Has since become a core member of DTU, including representing them in IWRG. Is known for using a stapler during his matches.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":108,"teams":[1184],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":47,"storytelling":52,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":38,"matchLayout":54,"psychology":47,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":68,"technicalCoaching":55,"characterCoaching":48,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":62,"mediaHandling":48,"brandBuilding":38,"socialMediaSavvy":32,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":68,"consistency":61,"awareness":47,"judgement":68},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1041","wrestlerId":1041,"promotionId":108,"startDate":"2018-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1042,"name":"Relámpago","realName":"Relámpago","picture":"Relampago.jpg","ability":47,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":53,"charisma":47,"micSkills":65,"popularity":3,"condition":88,"hardcoreAbility":69,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":74,"height":165,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1981-02-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2003-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Relámpago is a masked Mexican luchador who works exclusively in Mexico. He is a Lightweight who is classed as using a Luchador style. He is best known for his work with AAA, IWRG and DTU.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":58,"storytelling":60,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":29,"matchLayout":61,"psychology":58,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":69,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":34,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":71,"mediaHandling":34,"brandBuilding":43,"socialMediaSavvy":33,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":69,"consistency":67,"awareness":58,"judgement":75}},{"id":1044,"name":"Pirata Morgan Jr.","realName":"Pirata Morgan Jr.","picture":"Pirata Morgan Jr.jpg","ability":61,"currentAbility":62,"potentialAbility":62,"charisma":69,"micSkills":47,"popularity":3,"condition":88,"hardcoreAbility":76,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":96,"height":170,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1981-01-23T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Pirata Morgan Jr. is a Mexican luchador enmascarado. Pirata Morgan, Jr.'s real name is not a matter of public record, as is often the case with masked wrestlers in Mexico where their private lives are kept a secret from the wrestling fans. He is the son of professional wrestler Pedro Ortiz Villanueva, better known as Pirata Morgan, and not a fictional family relationship as it sometimes the case in Lucha Libre.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1203],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":64,"storytelling":67,"productFit":61,"riskTaking":22,"matchLayout":68,"psychology":64,"workerManagement":61,"trainingIntensity":62,"technicalCoaching":47,"characterCoaching":62,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":78,"mediaHandling":62,"brandBuilding":46,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":12,"reactionSpeed":62,"consistency":69,"awareness":64,"judgement":63}},{"id":1045,"name":"Hijo de Pirata Morgan","realName":"Hijo de Pirata Morgan","picture":"Hijo Pirata Morgan.jpg","ability":48,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"charisma":60,"micSkills":56,"popularity":2,"condition":90,"hardcoreAbility":51,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":80,"height":167,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1992-02-28T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2005-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Antheus Ortiz Chávez, better known under the ring name Hijo de Pirata Morgan is a Mexican luchador. Hijo de Pirata Morgan's real name was not a matter of public record until March 16, 2013 where he lost his wrestling mask and had to reveal his real name. This is often the case with masked wrestlers in Mexico where their private lives are kept a secret from the wrestling fans while they are masked. He is legitimately the son of professional wrestler Pedro Ortiz Villanueva, better known as Pirata Morgan, and not a storyline family relationship as it sometimes the case in Lucha Libre.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1203],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":60,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":61,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":71,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":64,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":64,"brandBuilding":43,"socialMediaSavvy":58,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":71,"consistency":66,"awareness":56,"judgement":74}},{"id":1047,"name":"QT Marshall","realName":"QT Marshall","picture":"QT Marshall.jpg","ability":87,"currentAbility":82,"potentialAbility":82,"charisma":89,"micSkills":77,"popularity":24,"condition":88,"hardcoreAbility":86,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":106,"height":180,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1985-07-16T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"QT Marshall is an American wrestler who works exclusively in North America. He is a Lightweight who is classed as using a Regular style. He is best known for his work with AEW, AAA, ROH, NJoA, PROGRESS and AAW.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[1218,1989,2741,4363,4364],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":63,"storytelling":69,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":14,"matchLayout":71,"psychology":63,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":74,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":58,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":86,"mediaHandling":58,"brandBuilding":44,"socialMediaSavvy":60,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":74,"consistency":73,"awareness":63,"judgement":78},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1047","wrestlerId":1047,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2024-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1048,"name":"Silas Young","realName":"Silas Young","picture":"Silas Young.jpg","ability":61,"currentAbility":61,"potentialAbility":61,"charisma":74,"micSkills":69,"popularity":8,"condition":87,"hardcoreAbility":76,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":100,"height":177,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1979-08-09T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"According to Silas Young, he’s the “Last Real Man in Professional Wrestling.” There are plenty of competitors in Ring of Honor who would take issue with that claim, but there’s no denying that Young is one of the toughest and most talented wrestlers in the sport.\r\n\r\nYoung, who competed in the 2013 Top Prospect Tournament, won the 2016 Honor Rumble and scored the biggest victory of his career to that point by defeating former ROH World Champion Jay Lethal in a Last Man Standing Match at Supercard of Honor XI in 2017. Young captured his first title in ROH when he defeated Kenny King, Punishment Martinez and Shane Taylor in a Four Corner Survival Match for the ROH World Television Title at Final Battle 2017.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[970,1953],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":67,"storytelling":71,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":29,"matchLayout":72,"psychology":67,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":74,"technicalCoaching":47,"characterCoaching":63,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":71,"mediaHandling":63,"brandBuilding":65,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":74,"consistency":73,"awareness":67,"judgement":80}},{"id":1049,"name":"Eva Marie","realName":"Eva Marie","picture":"Eva Marie.jpg","ability":26,"currentAbility":33,"potentialAbility":33,"charisma":26,"micSkills":43,"popularity":32,"condition":94,"hardcoreAbility":46,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"F","weight":57,"height":170,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1984-09-19T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2013-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"A former model that traded in the runway for the wrestling ring, Eva Marie’s journey through the ranks of WWE’s Divas division was first chronicled on the hit E! reality series, Total Divas. There, she navigated personal and professional obstacles in an attempt to become the face of the division. When she finally got to the big time, Eva Marie made an immediate impact, slapping Jerry “The King” Lawler across the face in her first appearance on Raw. This red-headed wonder hasn’t stopped for a single second since that day, and she hasn’t cared who she polarizes in the process. Stirring up controversy on Total Divas didn’t even stop her from training independently with former WWE Tag Team Champion “The” Brian Kendrick for a career-altering run down in WWE NXT that is just beginning to bear fruit. Career-altering, that is, both for her and anyone who thinks this red-headed runway vet is anything resembling a pushover.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":38,"storytelling":41,"productFit":25,"riskTaking":36,"matchLayout":42,"psychology":38,"workerManagement":25,"trainingIntensity":59,"technicalCoaching":27,"characterCoaching":73,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":64,"mediaHandling":73,"brandBuilding":80,"socialMediaSavvy":69,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":5,"reactionSpeed":59,"consistency":52,"awareness":38,"judgement":33}},{"id":1051,"name":"Harlem Bravado","realName":"Harlem Bravado","picture":"Harlem Bravado.jpg","ability":58,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"charisma":59,"micSkills":57,"popularity":21,"condition":91,"hardcoreAbility":55,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":101,"height":185,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1989-04-22T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Welcome to Andre Chase University! Take notes. The up-and coming Andre Chase has looked to impose painful education on both NXT and 205 Live, as well as competed in the 2021 NXT Breakout Tournament. Overall, Chase is a quick-thinking Superstar with a strong intellect that gives him the ability to use his environment to his advantage against any opponent and unleash a calculating offense that includes maneuvers like the excruciating STF.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[4027],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":64,"storytelling":68,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":69,"psychology":64,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":55,"characterCoaching":68,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":36,"socialMediaSavvy":73,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":83,"awareness":64,"judgement":78}},{"id":1053,"name":"Thom Latimer","realName":"Thom Latimer","picture":"Bram.jpg","ability":66,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"charisma":66,"micSkills":43,"popularity":18,"condition":82,"hardcoreAbility":59,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"striker","gender":"M","weight":108,"height":187,"base":"UK","birthplace":"England","dateOfBirth":"1986-08-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Thom Latimer is an English wrestler who works in the USA, Canada, Mexico, the British Isles and Japan. He is a 6'3\", 238lb worker who is classed as using a Brawler style. He uses the Curb Stomp and the Velvet Noise as his finishers. He is best known for his work with TNA, NWA and MLP. He is currently the NWA World's Heavyweight champion. He is married to Kamille.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":79,"teams":[1378,1416,1927],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":57,"storytelling":62,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":30,"matchLayout":64,"psychology":57,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":42,"characterCoaching":68,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":5