0Z","debut":"2000-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"The wrestler formerly known as Super Shenlong until spring 2012, he was a masked wrestler who is supposed to be a Chinese wrestler in Dragon Gate. He is a NEX talent and lower-card wrestler who usually works opening matches and garnered a cult fan following because he’s the perennial underdog as well as be a hero to Chinese fans for trying to break through in Japan. During the major faction shifting of early 2012 Shenlong turned heel and changed his name to Mondai Ryu (the kanji loosely translates as “Problem Dragon”), aligning himself with Akira Tozawa’s MAD BLANKEY faction and antagonizing the faces and opposition, usually by throwing white powder in a bucket he carries around.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":14,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":58,"storytelling":61,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":26,"matchLayout":62,"psychology":58,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":51,"characterCoaching":66,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":74,"mediaHandling":66,"brandBuilding":43,"socialMediaSavvy":47,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":62,"awareness":58,"judgement":75},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1106","wrestlerId":1106,"promotionId":14,"startDate":"2006-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1107,"name":"Eddie Roberts","realName":"Eddie Roberts","picture":"Eddie Roberts.jpg","ability":56,"currentAbility":49,"potentialAbility":49,"charisma":50,"micSkills":45,"popularity":0,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":48,"injuryProne":100,"type":"referee","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":74,"height":162,"base":"UK","birthplace":"Scotland","dateOfBirth":"1993-02-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Eddie Roberts is a Scottish professional wrestling referee who works across Scotland.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":38,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":38,"brandBuilding":8,"socialMediaSavvy":25,"ruleKnowledge":49,"positioning":39,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0}},{"id":1108,"name":"Jackie Polo","realName":"Jackie Polo","picture":"Jackie Polo.jpg","ability":56,"currentAbility":56,"potentialAbility":56,"charisma":48,"micSkills":68,"popularity":1,"condition":91,"hardcoreAbility":37,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":99,"height":185,"base":"UK","birthplace":"Scotland","dateOfBirth":"1987-10-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2007-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"A dominating physical presence, Polo likes to focus on technical wrestling to wear down his opponents in addition to his ability to throw people around like rag dolls with his size and strength. His skills are shadowed only by his ego as Jackie Polo believes himself to be ‘Scotlands BEEEST wrestler’ and will tell that to anyone who crosses his path! Having tagged with Joe Coffey as Legitimate Threat, Polo found success in tag competition teaming with both Mark and Joe Coffey over the years but his quest to prove he is better than all others has led him to go solo in recent years, using his intensity and aggression to show can take on the best of the best and survive.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[861,1279],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":60,"productFit":50,"riskTaking":31,"matchLayout":62,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":50,"trainingIntensity":76,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":67,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":69,"mediaHandling":67,"brandBuilding":52,"socialMediaSavvy":64,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":10,"reactionSpeed":76,"consistency":62,"awareness":56,"judgement":54}},{"id":1109,"name":"Tamina","realName":"Tamina","picture":"Tamina Snuka.jpg","ability":54,"currentAbility":47,"potentialAbility":47,"charisma":41,"micSkills":34,"popularity":27,"condition":68,"hardcoreAbility":65,"injuryProne":99,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"F","weight":77,"height":172,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1978-01-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2009-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Sarona Reiher is an American professional wrestler and is the first female wrestler to come out of the Samoan Wrestling Family. She is the daughter of WWE Hall of Famer Jimmy \"Superfly\" Snuka and the younger sister of former WWE wrestler Deuce. Sarona first began in wrestling after she received the first Lia Maivia Scholarship to train in professional wrestling career at the Wild Samoan Training Center. On December 26, 2009 it was reported through WXW's official twitter account that WWE signed Reiher to a developmental contract and would report to their developmental territory Florida Championship Wrestling for further training.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1243,2443,2771],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":58,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":40,"matchLayout":59,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":58,"technicalCoaching":27,"characterCoaching":53,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":60,"mediaHandling":53,"brandBuilding":52,"socialMediaSavvy":51,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":58,"consistency":50,"awareness":56,"judgement":74}},{"id":1110,"name":"Bayley","realName":"Bayley","picture":"Bayley.jpg","ability":77,"currentAbility":68,"potentialAbility":68,"charisma":73,"micSkills":80,"popularity":56,"condition":85,"hardcoreAbility":78,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"F","weight":54,"height":165,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1989-06-15T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Long before she was a SmackDown LIVE Superstar, Bayley was a 10-year-old superfan in San Jose, Calif., watching her favorites like Lita and Eddie Guerrero on TV. She decided then that she wanted to inspire fans the same way the Superstars of the ’90s and early ’00s did for her.\r\n\r\nNot all that long ago, Bayley still aspired to do all those things, but late 2019 saw the former hugger undergo a jaw-dropping transformation from one of WWE’s most pure personalities into a win-at-all-costs, rule-breaking brawler.\r\n\r\nWhen she turned 18, Bayley started to train for the squared circle, and after learning the ropes on the indies, she joined NXT’s burgeoning Women’s division in 2012. Unlike her contemporaries, she didn’t mirror Charlotte’s confidence, Sasha Banks’ swagger or Becky Lynch’s toughness. Instead, Bayley had an ever-present smile and an overwhelming enthusiasm that made it impossible to root against her.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[1771,4285],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":77,"storytelling":78,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":14,"matchLayout":78,"psychology":77,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":85,"technicalCoaching":65,"characterCoaching":83,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":86,"mediaHandling":83,"brandBuilding":75,"socialMediaSavvy":72,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":85,"consistency":82,"awareness":77,"judgement":86},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1110","wrestlerId":1110,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2016-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":1111,"name":"Joe Cabray","realName":"Joe Cabray","picture":"Luther Ward.jpg","ability":90,"currentAbility":80,"potentialAbility":80,"charisma":77,"micSkills":87,"popularity":5,"condition":87,"hardcoreAbility":69,"injuryProne":90,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":110,"height":182,"base":"UK","birthplace":"Ireland","dateOfBirth":"1982-10-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Luther Ward is no stranger to physicality. Building upon a proud lineage of Irish fighters, Ward views his place on NXT as a birthright. Need further evidence? One need not look further than the last name bestowed upon him by his father; “Ward” is defined as “Soldier of the People.” Since enduring the harshest of wrestling rings throughout Europe, Ward prides himself on being one of the toughest, most hardened and ruthless men to ever come to NXT. This highly disciplined Irish battler takes huge gratification in dismantling his opponents mentally and physically, piece by piece. Now that Ward has finally landed in NXT, his focus is to show the world that he is the toughest Irish man to ever live.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":60,"storytelling":64,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":42,"matchLayout":65,"psychology":60,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":64,"technicalCoaching":51,"characterCoaching":67,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":58,"mediaHandling":67,"brandBuilding":34,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":64,"consistency":62,"awareness":60,"judgement":76}},{"id":1112,"name":"Genki Horiguchi","realName":"Genki Horiguchi","picture":"Genki Horiguchi.jpg","ability":62,"currentAbility":60,"potentialAbility":60,"charisma":63,"micSkills":75,"popularity":6,"condition":71,"hardcoreAbility":62,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":75,"height":170,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1978-09-15T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Genki Horiguchi, is a Japanese professional wrestler. He is currently a full time wrestler and booker for Dragon Gate. He has also competed in Wrestling Society X and Ring of Honor. When Horiguchi's hairline began receding, the fans began to chant H-A-G-E (Japanese for 'bald') at him. He managed to use this to gain a sort of cult popularity, and his catchphrase, \"Who has called me hage?\", is one of the best known in Japan. Horiguchi debuted in Toryumon as a face wrestler with a surfer gimmick. In 2001, he began to lose his hair, and in November he turned heel, cast away his surfer gimmick, and he joined the original M2K as a replacement for Chocoflake K-ICHI. He was the last wrestler to be added to the group.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":14,"teams":[1217],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":74,"storytelling":77,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":78,"psychology":74,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":75,"technicalCoaching":60,"characterCoaching":76,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":76,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":60,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":75,"consistency":71,"awareness":74,"judgement":84},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1112","wrestlerId":1112,"promotionId":14,"startDate":"2004-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1113,"name":"Dan Engler","realName":"Dan Engler","picture":"Rudy Charles.jpg","ability":75,"currentAbility":79,"potentialAbility":79,"charisma":68,"micSkills":81,"popularity":2,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":79,"injuryProne":51,"type":"referee","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":75,"height":167,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1977-11-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1995-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Dan Engler is an American man who works primarily as a referee. He is best known for his work with WWE and TNA. He was voted Referee Of The Year in 2018.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":51,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":51,"brandBuilding":1,"socialMediaSavvy":40,"ruleKnowledge":79,"positioning":63,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1113","wrestlerId":1113,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2020-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":1114,"name":"Mike Posey","realName":"Mike Posey","picture":"Mike Posey.jpg","ability":77,"currentAbility":70,"potentialAbility":70,"charisma":59,"micSkills":63,"popularity":1,"condition":94,"hardcoreAbility":72,"injuryProne":100,"type":"referee","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":66,"height":172,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1977-08-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"The Birmingham, AL native performed as a wrestler and referee initially in Alabama & Georgia, most notably for NWA Wildside. He joined TNA as a referee, and also wrestled in a feud with David Young as \"Dropkick\" Posey. He resigned from TNA to try-out for WWE and after several dark matches was the 1st referee to join WWE's development promotion Deep South Wrestling, initially without a WWE contract. Soon he was signed. When the ECW brand was launched he joined the WWE roster as one of its refs, eventually becoming the brand's Sr. official. In his time in WWE he was a ref in matches on all three WWE brands and appeared at two WrestleManias. Returning to wrestling in 2009, Mike Posey teamed with former WWE Referee, Wes Adams, as the Official Express and Corey Hollis as Alabama Attitude in ROH. Posey won numerous singles titles.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[327],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":34,"storytelling":42,"productFit":70,"riskTaking":31,"matchLayout":44,"psychology":34,"workerManagement":70,"trainingIntensity":67,"technicalCoaching":38,"characterCoaching":53,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":69,"mediaHandling":53,"brandBuilding":38,"socialMediaSavvy":45,"ruleKnowledge":70,"positioning":70,"reactionSpeed":67,"consistency":73,"awareness":34,"judgement":48},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1114","wrestlerId":1114,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2020-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1115,"name":"Petey Williams","realName":"Petey Williams","picture":"Petey Williams.jpg","ability":79,"currentAbility":85,"potentialAbility":85,"charisma":99,"micSkills":89,"popularity":12,"condition":75,"hardcoreAbility":97,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":81,"height":167,"base":"Canada","birthplace":"Canada","dateOfBirth":"1981-08-26T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Petey Williams, a 2002 graduate of the Can-Am Wrestling School, is a retired Canadian wrestler who works primarily as a road agent. He is best known for his work with WWE, IMPACT, PWG, AJPW, ROH, HOH, Smash, IWA-MS, C4 and CZW. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business. He is the protege of Scott D'Amore. He was voted Young Wrestler Of The Year in 2004.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":69,"storytelling":71,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":72,"psychology":69,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":75,"technicalCoaching":65,"characterCoaching":63,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":63,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":55,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":75,"consistency":73,"awareness":69,"judgement":81},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1115","wrestlerId":1115,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2022-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":1117,"name":"William Grange","realName":"William Grange","picture":"William Grange.jpg","ability":15,"currentAbility":17,"potentialAbility":17,"charisma":23,"micSkills":4,"popularity":1,"condition":91,"hardcoreAbility":21,"injuryProne":100,"type":"commentator","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":89,"height":177,"base":"UK","birthplace":"Scotland","dateOfBirth":"1987-11-28T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"William Grange is a Scottish professional wrestler. Grange has always viewed himself as being better than anyone else. He believes he is the most inteligent man in ICW and it is his God given right to have ICW gold around his waist. With his tag partner Dickie Divers, he is a member of STI, one of the top teams in ICW. Currently embroiled in a fued with the Bucky Boys, Grange deplores the Bucky Boys, the Wee Man in particlaur as he sees them as everything that is wrong with today's society. Voted ICW Best Talker 2011, Grange is never short of words and has said the most controversial things ever uttered in a wrestling ring.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":53,"storytelling":54,"productFit":50,"riskTaking":36,"matchLayout":55,"psychology":53,"workerManagement":50,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":73,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":64,"mediaHandling":73,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":66,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":10,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":67,"awareness":53,"judgement":52}},{"id":1118,"name":"John Myers","realName":"John Myers","picture":"John Myers.jpg","ability":57,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":53,"charisma":64,"micSkills":46,"popularity":0,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":48,"injuryProne":0,"type":"referee","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":93,"height":170,"base":"UK","birthplace":"England","dateOfBirth":"1983-06-03T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2001-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"John Myers is a retired English wrestler who works primarily as a referee. He is best known for his work with NORTH. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":31,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":31,"brandBuilding":16,"socialMediaSavvy":20,"ruleKnowledge":53,"positioning":42,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0}},{"id":1120,"name":"Bill Goldberg","realName":"Bill Goldberg","picture":"Goldberg.jpg","ability":42,"currentAbility":47,"potentialAbility":47,"charisma":49,"micSkills":47,"popularity":68,"condition":63,"hardcoreAbility":41,"injuryProne":90,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":129,"height":190,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1966-12-27T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1997-06-23T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"great","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Bill Goldberg is a retired American wrestler who tends to stay behind the scenes in the wrestling world. He is best known for his work with WWE, WCW and AJPW. He is married to someone outside the wrestling business. He was voted Male Young Wrestler Of The Year in 1998. He is part of the WWE Hall Of Fame.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":57,"storytelling":59,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":56,"matchLayout":60,"psychology":57,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":40,"technicalCoaching":14,"characterCoaching":77,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":44,"mediaHandling":77,"brandBuilding":85,"socialMediaSavvy":61,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":40,"consistency":54,"awareness":57,"judgement":74}},{"id":1121,"name":"Renee Paquette","realName":"Renee Paquette","picture":"Renee Young.jpg","ability":52,"currentAbility":59,"potentialAbility":59,"charisma":46,"micSkills":57,"popularity":37,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":68,"injuryProne":100,"type":"manager","style":"all rounder","gender":"F","weight":68,"height":162,"base":"Canada","birthplace":"Canada","dateOfBirth":"1984-08-19T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2012-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Since making her SmackDown debut on the March 29 edition of the blue brand, Renee Young has quickly proved herself to be a true professional — able to approach WWE Superstars and Divas with the hard questions week in and week out without backing down an inch. A lifelong WWE fan, the lovely broadcast personality came to the squared circle after working with “The Score” in Canada for several years, building her reputation by interviewing high-caliber talent such as The Rolling Stones.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":30,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":85,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":85,"brandBuilding":68,"socialMediaSavvy":67,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":0,"reactionSpeed":30,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1121","wrestlerId":1121,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2022-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":1124,"name":"Michael Hayes","realName":"Michael Hayes","picture":"Michael Hayes.jpg","ability":83,"currentAbility":93,"potentialAbility":93,"charisma":99,"micSkills":91,"popularity":11,"condition":76,"hardcoreAbility":78,"injuryProne":71,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":116,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1959-03-29T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1977-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Michael Seitz  is an American retired professional wrestler and former musician. Seitz is best known for leading The Fabulous Freebirds under the ring name Michael \"P.S.\" (\"Pure Sexy\") Hayes and for his role as an announcer under the name Dok Hendrix in the World Wrestling Federation (WWF). He currently works with WWE as the head of the road agents/producers.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":85,"storytelling":87,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":87,"psychology":85,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":11,"technicalCoaching":3,"characterCoaching":77,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":77,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":68,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":11,"consistency":42,"awareness":85,"judgement":91},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1124","wrestlerId":1124,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2004-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":1128,"name":"Buff Bagwell","realName":"Buff Bagwell","picture":"Buff Bagwell.jpg","ability":45,"currentAbility":52,"potentialAbility":52,"charisma":56,"micSkills":54,"popularity":11,"condition":40,"hardcoreAbility":45,"injuryProne":81,"type":"wrestler","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":111,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1970-01-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1990-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Marcus Alexander Bagwell is an American professional wrestler and actor, better known by his ring name, Buff Bagwell. He is best known for his tenure with World Championship Wrestling between 1991 and 2001, where he was a five time World Tag Team Champion. On April 23, 2012, Bagwell was seriously injured in a car accident. He was subsequently taken to WellStar Kennestone Hospital in his hometown of Marietta, Georgia, where he was placed in the hospital's intensive care unit after suffering broken bones in his neck, face and jaw. After recovering from his injuries, Bagwell resumed his wrestling career and, in early March 2013, he won American Premier Wrestling's Heavyweight Championship after defeating \"Cowboy\" Jeremy Young at APW's Brawl VI event.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[2960,3123],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":53,"storytelling":60,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":33,"matchLayout":63,"psychology":53,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":44,"technicalCoaching":32,"characterCoaching":72,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":67,"mediaHandling":72,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":44,"consistency":45,"awareness":53,"judgement":72}},{"id":1129,"name":"Jake Roberts","realName":"Jake Roberts","picture":"Jake Roberts.jpg","ability":70,"currentAbility":69,"potentialAbility":69,"charisma":65,"micSkills":69,"popularity":31,"condition":49,"hardcoreAbility":51,"injuryProne":66,"type":"manager","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":113,"height":195,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1955-05-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1973-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"upper","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Jake Roberts is a retired American wrestler who works primarily as a manager. He is best known for his work with WWE and AEW. He is part of the WWE Hall Of Fame.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":96,"storytelling":85,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":82,"psychology":96,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":31,"technicalCoaching":33,"characterCoaching":78,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":78,"brandBuilding":49,"socialMediaSavvy":79,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":31,"consistency":31,"awareness":96,"judgement":98},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1129","wrestlerId":1129,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2020-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1132,"name":"Tatanka","realName":"Tatanka","picture":"Tatanka.jpg","ability":52,"currentAbility":52,"potentialAbility":52,"charisma":44,"micSkills":67,"popularity":4,"condition":61,"hardcoreAbility":56,"injuryProne":92,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":120,"height":177,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1965-06-08T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1989-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Christopher \"Chris\" Chavis is a Native American professional wrestler best known for his work with World Wrestling Entertainment as Tatanka, His ring name is a Lakota word that literally means \"bull buffalo.\" He is descended from the Lumbee Native American tribe. In 1989, Chavis left Bally's to pursue an accounting career. He met \"Nature Boy\" Buddy Rogers in Florida at a video store while looking for wrestling tapes. Rogers had Chavis call Larry Sharpe, who ran a wrestling school in southern New Jersey called \"The Monster Factory.\" He had his first match, as Tatanka, against Joe Thunderstorm in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania on January 13, 1990.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":61,"storytelling":65,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":66,"psychology":61,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":38,"technicalCoaching":30,"characterCoaching":58,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":58,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":51,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":38,"consistency":58,"awareness":61,"judgement":77}},{"id":1133,"name":"Nick Dinsmore","realName":"Nick Dinsmore","picture":"Nick Dinsmore.jpg","ability":56,"currentAbility":64,"potentialAbility":64,"charisma":51,"micSkills":50,"popularity":6,"condition":61,"hardcoreAbility":48,"injuryProne":99,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":107,"height":180,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1975-12-17T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1996-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Nicholas David Dinsmore is an American professional wrestler. He is perhaps best known for his time working World Wrestling Entertainment. Over the course of his career, Dinsmore has held the OVW Heavyweight Championship a record nine times, the OVW Southern Tag Team Championship eleven times, a record shared with former tag team partner Rob Conway, and the World Tag Team Championship one time. Dinsmore debuted in 1997, and soon began wrestling in the United States Wrestling Association. In Ohio Valley Wrestling, he formed a successful tag team with Rob Conway, called The Lords of The Ring.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[330,2833],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":73,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":75,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":63,"technicalCoaching":63,"characterCoaching":72,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":72,"brandBuilding":44,"socialMediaSavvy":67,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":63,"consistency":65,"awareness":68,"judgement":81}},{"id":1135,"name":"Necro Butcher","realName":"Necro Butcher","picture":"Necro Butcher.jpg","ability":47,"currentAbility":40,"potentialAbility":40,"charisma":49,"micSkills":55,"popularity":6,"condition":51,"hardcoreAbility":57,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"hardcore","gender":"M","weight":104,"height":185,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1973-07-13T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Dylan Keith Summers is an American professional wrestler best known by his ring name (The) Necro Butcher. Throughout the years he has worked for various promotions, including Beyond Wrestling, Firestormpro, Ring of Honor, Full Impact Pro, IWA-Mid South, Pro Wrestling Guerrilla, Big Japan Pro Wrestling, and Combat Zone Wrestling. Summers is well known for his willingness to participate in a creative and dangerous mix of hardcore wrestling, deathmatches, and brawls, as well as his appearance in the 2008 film The Wrestler.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":38,"storytelling":41,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":65,"matchLayout":42,"psychology":38,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":48,"technicalCoaching":10,"characterCoaching":68,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":35,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":5,"socialMediaSavvy":38,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":48,"consistency":50,"awareness":38,"judgement":63}},{"id":1137,"name":"Ricky Reyes","realName":"Ricky Reyes","picture":"Ricky Reyes.jpg","ability":60,"currentAbility":61,"potentialAbility":61,"charisma":55,"micSkills":56,"popularity":4,"condition":70,"hardcoreAbility":77,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"submission","gender":"M","weight":87,"height":172,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1978-08-21T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Ricky Reyes is a Cuban-American professional wrestler known for his appearances in Ring of Honor, Pro Wrestling Guerrilla, and various other independent promotions, he is currently primarily working for the World Wrestling Council. On September 9, 2006, Reyes debuted in Combat Zone Wrestling (CZW) and joined The Blackout. Reyes left CZW on October 21, 2006 to join Pro Wrestling Unplugged. On the May 25, 2012 episode of WWE SmackDown, Reyes competed in a handicapped match on the losing end of a two-man team versus Ryback. Reyes competed under the name Brian Edwards.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1413,2657,3025,3026,3278,3279],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":61,"storytelling":65,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":29,"matchLayout":66,"psychology":61,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":72,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":51,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":71,"mediaHandling":51,"brandBuilding":38,"socialMediaSavvy":43,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":72,"consistency":67,"awareness":61,"judgement":77}},{"id":1140,"name":"Diamond Dallas Page","realName":"Diamond Dallas Page","picture":"Diamond Dallas Page.jpg","ability":59,"currentAbility":66,"potentialAbility":66,"charisma":74,"micSkills":69,"popularity":41,"condition":61,"hardcoreAbility":52,"injuryProne":57,"type":"manager","style":"striker","gender":"M","weight":112,"height":193,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1956-04-05T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1988-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Starting his career as a manager in the American Wrestling Association in the late '80s, Diamond Dallas Page made his first WWE appearance in 1990 when he drove The Honky Tonk Man and Greg Valentine to the ring in his pink Cadillac at WrestleMania VI.\r\n\r\nAs a result of using yoga to rehabilitate what he thought was a career-ending 1998 back injury in WCW, Page started developing DDP YOGA in 2005. On February 21, 2014, Page appeared on the ABC television series Shark Tank where he declined to sell a 5% share in DDP YOGA for $200,000. He had hoped to use the money to develop a mobile app. The investors believed the company's 2013 profits of $800,000 would decline in future years. Page later said he sold more than $1 million worth of product in the first six days after his appearance and used the revenues to build the DDP YOGA Performance Center in Smyrna, Georgia and develop the DDP NOW mobile app.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3152],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":82,"storytelling":84,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":17,"matchLayout":84,"psychology":82,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":43,"technicalCoaching":27,"characterCoaching":79,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":83,"mediaHandling":79,"brandBuilding":55,"socialMediaSavvy":68,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":43,"consistency":37,"awareness":82,"judgement":89}},{"id":1141,"name":"Hamuko Hoshi","realName":"Hamuko Hoshi","picture":"Hamuko Hoshi.jpg","ability":61,"currentAbility":51,