ively in the promotion, but began expanding her reach in early 2010 and appearing in other promotions-most notably DDT. She currently appears in Ice Ribbon on an occasional basis, usually only doing major events. When not competing she’s a “weathergirl” for Nikkan Sports and she’s also a popular gravure/bikini idol and was the only “survivor” of an apparent gravure idol wrestling promotion. In September 2009 she did a promo video where she did appear in a bikini. She also makes regular appearances on TV Tokyo and is now even a singer!","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":36,"storytelling":44,"productFit":32,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":47,"psychology":36,"workerManagement":32,"trainingIntensity":66,"technicalCoaching":49,"characterCoaching":67,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":67,"brandBuilding":53,"socialMediaSavvy":60,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":6,"reactionSpeed":66,"consistency":55,"awareness":36,"judgement":34}},{"id":1144,"name":"Mio Shirai","realName":"Mio Shirai","picture":"Mio Shirai.jpg","ability":75,"currentAbility":65,"potentialAbility":65,"charisma":68,"micSkills":70,"popularity":3,"condition":70,"hardcoreAbility":60,"injuryProne":83,"type":"wrestler","style":"all rounder","gender":"F","weight":54,"height":162,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1988-02-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2007-03-04T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Mio Shirai is a Japanese professional wrestler, currently working as a freelancer on the Japanese independent circuit for promotions such as Ice Ribbon, Oz Academy, Pro Wrestling Wave, and Union Pro. She is also a member of the tag team Triple Tails.S with Kana, which was originally a stable also including Mio's younger sister Io, who left the group in September 2011. Together Mio and Io are former TLW World Young Women's Tag Team Champions.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":73,"teams":[397,2924],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":80,"storytelling":81,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":82,"psychology":80,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":68,"characterCoaching":73,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":73,"brandBuilding":75,"socialMediaSavvy":68,"ruleKnowledge":69,"positioning":75,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":67,"awareness":80,"judgement":88},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1144","wrestlerId":1144,"promotionId":73,"startDate":"2025-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2027-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2027-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1145,"name":"Dax Harwood","realName":"Dax Harwood","picture":"Scott Dawson.jpg","ability":77,"currentAbility":75,"potentialAbility":75,"charisma":72,"micSkills":61,"popularity":48,"condition":75,"hardcoreAbility":92,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":96,"height":175,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1984-06-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2004-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"mid","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"David Michael Harwood is an American worker from North Carolina best known for his time in WWE under the name Scott Dawson, where he teamed with Dash Wilder as The Revival. Their old school 80s style of tag team wrestling led to them being compared favourably with The Brain Busters (Arn Anderson & Tully Blanchard) and they gained a reputation for having consistently great matches while in NXT. Despite becoming 3-time tag team champions after being called up to the main roster in 2017, they were plagued by poor booking and had multiple requests for their release turned down before finally being let go in April 2020. The former Dawson now goes by the name Dax Harwood and continues to team with Dash, now named Cash Wheeler, under the name \"FTR\" - a reference to their online feud with The Young Bucks through their web series Being The Elite.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[1494,1495,2048,2077,3502,3590,3641],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":84,"storytelling":85,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":17,"matchLayout":85,"psychology":84,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":83,"technicalCoaching":68,"characterCoaching":62,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":83,"mediaHandling":62,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":53,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":83,"consistency":90,"awareness":84,"judgement":90},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1145","wrestlerId":1145,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2020-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1146,"name":"Tom LaRuffa","realName":"Tom LaRuffa","picture":"Tom La Ruffa.jpg","ability":53,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":55,"charisma":45,"micSkills":41,"popularity":5,"condition":88,"hardcoreAbility":52,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":91,"height":177,"base":"Europe","birthplace":"France","dateOfBirth":"1984-05-04T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2007-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Straight from the nightclubs and the casinos of the Jet Set of the French Riviera, this over-the-top Frenchman comes from strong Italian and Greek Origins. His Mediterrean hot temper makes him an unpredictable character – as well as a dangerous one. He prides himself on being a main attraction everywhere he competes and even though small in stature, his intensity and aggressive nature makes him a threat to any giant in NXT. Lefort lives by the motto: “I am not a big guy – but I will do some big things”","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":48,"storytelling":54,"productFit":58,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":56,"psychology":48,"workerManagement":58,"trainingIntensity":62,"technicalCoaching":44,"characterCoaching":64,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":64,"brandBuilding":62,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":12,"reactionSpeed":62,"consistency":84,"awareness":48,"judgement":52}},{"id":1147,"name":"Manami Toyota","realName":"Manami Toyota","picture":"Manami Toyota.jpg","ability":92,"currentAbility":98,"potentialAbility":98,"charisma":100,"micSkills":100,"popularity":9,"condition":75,"hardcoreAbility":99,"injuryProne":90,"type":"writer","style":"high flyer","gender":"F","weight":68,"height":165,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1971-03-02T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1988-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Manami Toyota is a professional wrestler best known for her work with the All Japan Women's Pro-Wrestling (AJW) wrestling promotion. Following AJW's closure she has continued to work in other joshi promotions such as Gaea and NEO. Toyota is a member of the Wrestling Observer Newsletter Hall of Fame. Manami Toyota made her professional wrestling debut on August 5, 1987, at the age of 16, in a singles match against Sachiko Nakamura. Toyota produced her 25th anniversary event on September 22 2012, during which she wrestled in all five matches.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":82,"teams":[2989],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":95,"storytelling":97,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":97,"psychology":95,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":61,"technicalCoaching":69,"characterCoaching":67,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":67,"brandBuilding":63,"socialMediaSavvy":60,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":61,"consistency":73,"awareness":95,"judgement":97},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1147","wrestlerId":1147,"promotionId":82,"startDate":"2018-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1149,"name":"El Pantera","realName":"El Pantera","picture":"El Pantera.jpg","ability":73,"currentAbility":63,"potentialAbility":63,"charisma":71,"micSkills":77,"popularity":4,"condition":47,"hardcoreAbility":73,"injuryProne":98,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":85,"height":167,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1964-02-03T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1985-11-03T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Francisco Javier Pozas is a Mexican professional wrestler, or luchador, who is best known under the ring name El Pantera, but has also worked as Pantera II, El Manaya, América, Tritón and TANAKA over the years. Pozas made his wrestling debut in 1985, working as an enmascarado (masked wrestler) with a panther-inspired mask to go with his ring character of \"El Pantera\". Over the years Pozas has worked in Mexico, Japan and the United States; In Mexico he has worked for Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL), Asistencia Asesoría y Administración (AAA), International Wrestling Revolution Group (IWRG), in Japan he's worked for Universal Lucha Libre (ULL) and All-Japan Pro Wrestling (AJPW) and in the United States he's most known for his work in the World Wrestling Federation (WWF) from 1997 to 1999 and Chikara where he has worked shows since 2007. In 2006 Pantera lost his mask as a result of a match. He, however, continued wearing the mask when working for Chikara.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1202,2762],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":85,"storytelling":86,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":18,"matchLayout":86,"psychology":85,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":49,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":40,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":82,"mediaHandling":40,"brandBuilding":49,"socialMediaSavvy":35,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":49,"consistency":57,"awareness":85,"judgement":91}},{"id":1150,"name":"El Hijo del Pantera","realName":"El Hijo del Pantera","picture":"Hijo del Pantera.jpg","ability":60,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":55,"charisma":52,"micSkills":41,"popularity":4,"condition":93,"hardcoreAbility":59,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":80,"height":170,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1991-12-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Hijo del Pantera is a Mexican enmascarado. He is most active around Queretaro and Arena Naucalpan, almost always working the same shows as his father early on. In 2012, he moved to Japan for an extended stay/training session with Wrestling New Classic, often facing Hajime Ohara. Came back to Mexico for a few months in late 2012 and early 2013, but returned again to Japan","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[1202],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":62,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":34,"matchLayout":64,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":58,"characterCoaching":54,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":66,"mediaHandling":54,"brandBuilding":42,"socialMediaSavvy":36,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":67,"awareness":56,"judgement":74},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1150","wrestlerId":1150,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2024-07-05T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-07-05T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-07-05T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1151,"name":"Tinieblas Jr.","realName":"Tinieblas Jr.","picture":"Tinieblas Jr.jpg","ability":69,"currentAbility":62,"potentialAbility":62,"charisma":68,"micSkills":74,"popularity":7,"condition":79,"hardcoreAbility":46,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":108,"height":190,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1966-05-26T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1990-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Tinieblas, Jr. is the ring name of a Mexican Luchador enmascarado. Tinieblas, Jr.'s full name is not a matter of public record, as is often the case with masked wrestlers in Mexico where their private lives are kept a secret from the wrestling fans. He is the son of Manuel Leal, who has wrestled for many years under the ring name Tinieblas. Tinieblas is Spanish for \"Darkness\". During the summer of 2010, Tinieblas, Jr. began working for a newly created wrestling promotion, backed by MTV2 called Lucha Libre USA, wrestling on their first television taping on June 19, 2010.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3167],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":64,"storytelling":69,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":70,"psychology":64,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":55,"technicalCoaching":67,"characterCoaching":39,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":39,"brandBuilding":67,"socialMediaSavvy":25,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":55,"consistency":64,"awareness":64,"judgement":78}},{"id":1153,"name":"Lexie Fyfe","realName":"Lexie Fyfe","picture":"Lexie Fyfe.jpg","ability":90,"currentAbility":81,"potentialAbility":81,"charisma":79,"micSkills":85,"popularity":3,"condition":85,"hardcoreAbility":85,"injuryProne":93,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"F","weight":61,"height":160,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1968-05-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1995-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Mary Beth Bentley, is an American professional wrestler. She has wrestled in various independent wrestling promotions, most notably for Shimmer Women Athletes and has had tryouts for both WWE and WCW. When Shine Wrestling was established on July 20, 2012, Lexie began her stint as a babyface authority figure for the promotion.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3235],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":70,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":72,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":55,"technicalCoaching":42,"characterCoaching":66,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":66,"brandBuilding":38,"socialMediaSavvy":51,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":55,"consistency":55,"awareness":62,"judgement":77}},{"id":1154,"name":"Rain","realName":"Rain","picture":"Rain.jpg","ability":50,"currentAbility":59,"potentialAbility":59,"charisma":65,"micSkills":58,"popularity":2,"condition":87,"hardcoreAbility":65,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"F","weight":58,"height":165,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1981-09-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Bonnie Maxon is an American professional wrestler best known by her ring name Rain or as Payton Banks in Total Nonstop Action Wrestling. She formerly tag teamed with partner Lacey to form The Minnesota Home-Wrecking Crew (a play on the name of the Minnesota Wrecking Crew), but following Lacey's retirement, she teamed with British wrestler Jetta to form The International Home Wrecking Crew. Rain made her debut for new women's wrestling promotion Shine Wrestling, stylized as SHINE, on July 20 in Ybor City, Florida where she defeated Nikki Roxx.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[2950],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":48,"storytelling":55,"productFit":70,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":58,"psychology":48,"workerManagement":70,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":53,"characterCoaching":67,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":67,"brandBuilding":49,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":14,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":80,"awareness":48,"judgement":57}},{"id":1156,"name":"April Hunter","realName":"April Hunter","picture":"April Hunter.jpg","ability":42,"currentAbility":43,"potentialAbility":43,"charisma":47,"micSkills":46,"popularity":3,"condition":70,"hardcoreAbility":53,"injuryProne":78,"type":"wrestler","style":"all rounder","gender":"F","weight":68,"height":172,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1974-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"April Hunter is an American professional wrestler, professional wrestling valet and fitness and glamour model. She has appeared in many publications, from MuscleMag International to Playboy Magazine and even has her own comic book series, Code Red by Pickle Press. In 1999 after Hunter appeared in Playboy, she was hired by World Championship Wrestling (WCW) as a member of the NWo Girls. Hunter trained to become a professional wrestler with Killer Kowalski in Boston. he was the only female in the class and soon began working on the independent circuit and overseas. Hunter formed a tag team with fellow Kowalski graduate Nikki Roxx in World Xtreme Wrestling known as The Killer Babes.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3297,3335],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":42,"storytelling":46,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":34,"matchLayout":47,"psychology":42,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":42,"technicalCoaching":32,"characterCoaching":61,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":66,"mediaHandling":61,"brandBuilding":44,"socialMediaSavvy":54,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":42,"consistency":49,"awareness":42,"judgement":65}},{"id":1159,"name":"Jessie Belle","realName":"Jessie Belle","picture":"Je