lse,"story":"Makoto Saito, better known by his stage name K-ness is a Japanese professional wrestler for Dragon Gate. He debuted in Michinoku Pro around the same time as Gamma, and then went on to wrestle on the Japanese indy circuit. He joined Toryumon in 1999 as MAKOTO, with a vampire style gimmick. As MAKOTO he was a member of the legendary Crazy Max stable. However, he did not get along with TARU, and eventually was kicked out of the stable after losing to TARU in a loser leaves match. In November 2003 he suffered a major shoulder injury which caused him to miss out on the majority of 2004, and the switch from Toryumon to Dragon Gate. By the time K-ness returned, Ultimo Dragon had left the promotion and taken the Toryumon trademark with him.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1031,1145],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":55,"storytelling":64,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":38,"matchLayout":67,"psychology":55,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":71,"technicalCoaching":65,"characterCoaching":59,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":62,"mediaHandling":59,"brandBuilding":65,"socialMediaSavvy":32,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":71,"consistency":72,"awareness":55,"judgement":73}},{"id":1245,"name":"Magnitude Kishiwada","realName":"Magnitude Kishiwada","picture":"Magnitude Kishiwada.jpg","ability":61,"currentAbility":57,"potentialAbility":57,"charisma":51,"micSkills":60,"popularity":3,"condition":66,"hardcoreAbility":71,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"striker","gender":"M","weight":90,"height":172,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1971-05-09T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1993-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Toyonari Fujita better known as Magnitude Kishiwada, is a Japanese wrestler. He wrestles for the Dragon Gate promotion. During his highschool life, Fujita trained in artistic gymnastics and powerlifting, and years later, he showed interest in professional wrestling. For many years Fujita trained in worked in preliminary matches in Japan's hardcore wrestling promotions, including FMW, W*ING, and Big Japan Pro Wrestling, competing under his real name, and as Toryu. He eventually landed in Osaka Pro, where he became a kaiju character named Monster Zeta Mandora. However, he gained fame in early 2002 by turning heel and renaming himself, Big Boss MA-G-MA.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":58,"storytelling":64,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":45,"matchLayout":66,"psychology":58,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":63,"technicalCoaching":42,"characterCoaching":47,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":55,"mediaHandling":47,"brandBuilding":44,"socialMediaSavvy":22,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":63,"consistency":49,"awareness":58,"judgement":75}},{"id":1246,"name":"Masaaki Mochizuki","realName":"Masaaki Mochizuki","picture":"Masaaki Mochizuki.jpg","ability":76,"currentAbility":71,"potentialAbility":71,"charisma":79,"micSkills":71,"popularity":6,"condition":73,"hardcoreAbility":59,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":85,"height":172,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1970-01-17T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1994-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Masaaki Mochizuki is a Japanese professional wrestler, currently performing for Dragon Gate and its international expansion Dragon Gate USA. He hosted his self-produced show, Buyuden. A graduate of Koji Kitao's Buko Dojo, Masaaki spent the early part of his career wrestling for various promotions across Japan, namely WAR and BattlARTS. Most notable was his appearance in the 1995 Super J Cup, where he took on Shinjiro Otani of New Japan Pro Wrestling in the first round. Despite losing, Masaaki looked very competitive, using his sharp kicks and quick submission holds to pose a serious threat to the more experienced Otani. In December, he celebrated 10 years in wrestling by defeating CIMA for Dragon Gate's top prize, the Open the Dream Gate Championship. He held the title for 11 months before losing it to Magnitude Kishiwada on November 4, 2005. When 2006 rolled around, he began to distance himself from Final M2K a bit.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":14,"teams":[1555,1582,2453,3999,4000],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":80,"storytelling":83,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":84,"psychology":80,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":80,"technicalCoaching":76,"characterCoaching":58,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":58,"brandBuilding":61,"socialMediaSavvy":55,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":80,"consistency":71,"awareness":80,"judgement":88},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1246","wrestlerId":1246,"promotionId":14,"startDate":"2004-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1247,"name":"Akira Tozawa","realName":"Akira Tozawa","picture":"Akira Tozawa.jpg","ability":79,"currentAbility":70,"potentialAbility":70,"charisma":59,"micSkills":83,"popularity":30,"condition":84,"hardcoreAbility":50,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":71,"height":167,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1985-07-22T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2005-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Inside the ring and out, Akira Tozawa is an audacious Superstar. As the third-ever graduate of Japan’s world-respected Dragon Gate dojo, Tozawa helped blaze a trail as an early staple of the Dragon Gate organization. Yet, Tozawa’s vicious strikes have been felt worldwide, courtesy of several tours around the globe. Along the way, the trash-talking, fearless fighter has crossed paths with the likes of Kevin Owens, Dean Ambrose and Sami Zayn. Tozawa has unleashed his unique brand of brutality, including a big boot that leaves its imprint via countless kick varieties and enough German suplexes to make Brock Lesnar proud. With agility and athleticism to spare, no opponent is safe from his far-reaching bicycle kick.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[921,1229,1256,4071],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":70,"storytelling":75,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":76,"psychology":70,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":87,"technicalCoaching":75,"characterCoaching":76,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":76,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":68,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":87,"consistency":73,"awareness":70,"judgement":82},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1247","wrestlerId":1247,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2016-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":1248,"name":"Taku Iwasa","realName":"Taku Iwasa","picture":"Taku Iwasa.jpg","ability":47,"currentAbility":50,"potentialAbility":50,"charisma":58,"micSkills":45,"popularity":3,"condition":83,"hardcoreAbility":47,"injuryProne":99,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":90,"height":177,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1978-04-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Taku Iwasa is a Japanese professional wrestler who currently wrestles for Dragon Gate. Iwasa graduated as part of the Toryumon T2P class. He initially portrayed Takamichi Iwasa, a Satanic character. Injuries derailed his career, and he soon ended up as a jobber to the stars. He was briefly scouted by the famous Crazy MAX stable, and they gave him a ten match trial series. CMAX was never truly interested in Iwasa, though, and he lost all 10 matches. Following this, he joined forces with Raimu Mishima, who had been exiled from M2K for losing too many matches and general weakness. They petitioned to form their own unit, but were unable to do so. They then left for America to undergo Warrior Training. In mid-2009, Iwasa abruptly announced his retirement. On March 1, 2011, Iwasa announced that he would be making a return from his 18 month hiatus. Iwasa never returned to a full time wrestling schedule. He has not wrestled since 2012, although he maintains his spot on the Dragon Gate roster.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[935],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":70,"storytelling":72,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":49,"matchLayout":73,"psychology":70,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":60,"technicalCoaching":38,"characterCoaching":49,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":51,"mediaHandling":49,"brandBuilding":33,"socialMediaSavvy":42,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":60,"consistency":22,"awareness":70,"judgement":82}},{"id":1249,"name":"Takashi Okamura","realName":"Takashi Okamura","picture":"Takashi Okamura.jpg","ability":47,"currentAbility":46,"potentialAbility":46,"charisma":53,"micSkills":49,"popularity":2,"condition":92,"hardcoreAbility":47,"injuryProne":50,"type":"wrestler","style":"submission","gender":"M","weight":75,"height":167,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1964-09-04T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1994-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":true,"story":"Takashi Okamura was a Japanese wrestler who passed away on 25 April 2025. He is best known for his work with Dragon Gate.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":70,"storytelling":72,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":66,"matchLayout":72,"psychology":70,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":39,"technicalCoaching":44,"characterCoaching":45,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":34,"mediaHandling":45,"brandBuilding":31,"socialMediaSavvy":55,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":39,"consistency":33,"awareness":70,"judgement":82}},{"id":1250,"name":"Takayuki Yagi","realName":"Takayuki Yagi","picture":"Takayuki Yagi.jpg","ability":76,"currentAbility":68,"potentialAbility":68,"charisma":66,"micSkills":56,"popularity":2,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":49,"injuryProne":57,"type":"referee","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":80,"height":167,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1975-05-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1993-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Takayuki Yagi is a referee and former wrestler for Dragon Gate. Yagi joined the Toryumon system as a part of the T2P class. He started his career under his real name, and his initial gimmick was that of a fisherman who carried a large flag with a sea-oriented design to the ring. Following the formation of the Italian Connection on March 3, 2002, he was accepted into the unit and renamed Pescatore Yagi, \"pescatore\" being the Italian word for fisherman, and he began carrying a large Italian flag to the ring instead. Yagi's in-ring career would end as part of the unnamed ItaCon breakaway faction. Yagi returned to Dragon Gate, but as a referee rather than a wrestler. It is presumed that he stepped down because of injury.\r\nHis first role as a referee was that of a face referee who was continually bothered by the antics of the Florida Brothers.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":14,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":20,"storytelling":29,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":77,"matchLayout":32,"psychology":20,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":41,"technicalCoaching":53,"characterCoaching":56,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":23,"mediaHandling":56,"brandBuilding":40,"socialMediaSavvy":42,"ruleKnowledge":68,"positioning":74,"reactionSpeed":41,"consistency":44,"awareness":20,"judgement":52},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1250","wrestlerId":1250,"promotionId":14,"startDate":"2004-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1251,"name":"Eita","realName":"Eita","picture":"Eita.jpg","ability":67,"currentAbility":66,"potentialAbility":66,"charisma":79,"micSkills":72,"popularity":7,"condition":91,"hardcoreAbility":80,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":75,"height":167,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1991-10-27T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2011-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Eita, a 2011 graduate of the Dragon Gate Dojo, is a Japanese wrestler who works in Mexico and Japan. He is a Lightweight who is classed as using a Technician Flyer style. He is best known for his work with NJPW, NOAH, Dragon Gate, IWRG, EVOLVE, FCP and DTU.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":45,"teams":[1224],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":65,"storytelling":70,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":72,"psychology":65,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":72,"characterCoaching":78,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":78,"brandBuilding":68,"socialMediaSavvy":69,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":56,"awareness":65,"judgement":79},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1251","wrestlerId":1251,"promotionId":45,"startDate":"2022-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":1252,"name":"T-Hawk","realName":"T-Hawk","picture":"T-Hawk.jpg","ability":64,"currentAbility":67,"potentialAbility":67,"charisma":56,"micSkills":72,"popularity":8,"condition":92,"hardcoreAbility":60,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"submission","gender":"M","weight":88,"height":172,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1990-04-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"T-Hawk, a 2010 graduate of the Dragon Gate Dojo, is a Japanese wrestler who works in America, Mexico, the British Isles, Japan and Europe. He is a Lightweight who is classed as using a Impactful style. He is best known for his work with NJPW, AEW, DDT, Dragongate, BJW, AJPW, wXw, GLEAT, IWRG, WRESTLE-1, EVOLVE and DTU.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":96,"teams":[1224,3542,3977],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":72,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":73,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":86,"technicalCoaching":71,"characterCoaching":60,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":71,"socialMediaSavvy":45,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":86,"consistency":77,"awareness":68,"judgement":81},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1252","wrestlerId":1252,"promotionId":96,"startDate":"2021-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1253,"name":"Syachihoko BOY","realName":"Syachihoko BOY","picture":"Shachi Boi.jpg","ability":41,"currentAbility":48,"potentialAbility":48,"charisma":41,"micSkills":34,"popularity":3,"condition":81,"hardcoreAbility":67,"injuryProne":99,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":90,"height":170,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1980-11-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"BOY entered the system around the same time as Masato Yoshino. The two are contemporaries and remain close friends to this day. After debuting with Dragon Gate as Shachihoko Machine, he also began competing as Shisa BOY. He continued to do both characters for several years, although it eventually became obvious it was him under both masks. During a November 2011 Triangle Gate match, his Shachihoko mask was removed and he was sent to the backstage area. He returned with the Shisa BOY mask. From that time forward, he would occasionally appear with the characters mixed up. He formally fused them in the summer of 2012, becoming Shachihoko BOY. Shisa BOY & Shachihoko Machine appear to be sealed for the time being. His hard work improving his physical conditioning paid off in late 2012 when he was promoted from his Window spot to WORLD-1 International. He followed best friend Masato Yoshino to Monster Express.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":14,"teams":[932,2948],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":63,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":44,"matchLayout":65,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":71,"technicalCoaching":46,"characterCoaching":49,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":56,"mediaHandling":49,"brandBuilding":38,"socialMediaSavvy":45,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":71,"consistency":47,"awareness":56,"judgement":74},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1253","wrestlerId":1253,"promotionId":14,"startDate":"2004-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1254,"name":"U-T","realName":"U-T","picture":"U-T.jpg","ability":46,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":53,"charisma":47,"micSkills":68,"popularity":4,"condition":82,"hardcoreAbility":65,"injuryProne":77,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":70,"height":160,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1993-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2013-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"U-T was scheduled to debut under his real name on 12tth April 2013 in his hometown of Nagoya. Less than 24 hours before the match, Eita sent a message to the DG office and the fans stating that Tanaka had accepted his solicitation to come train in Mexico. In doing so he became the first member of the roster to debut in Mexico since the Toryumon X class. His new identity was revealed during the first Millenials video. He was now U-T.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":14,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":55,"storytelling":61,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":24,"matchLayout":63,"psychology":55,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":75,"technicalCoaching":60,"characterCoaching":63,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":76,"mediaHandling":63,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":55,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":75,"consistency":56,"awareness":55,"judgement":73},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1254","wrestlerId":1254,"promotionId":14,"startDate":"2013-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1255,"name":"Yosuke<3Santa Maria","realName":"Yosuke<3Santa Maria","picture":"YosukeSanta Maria.jpg","ability":52,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":55,"charisma":64,"micSkills":60,"popularity":4,"condition":94,"hardcoreAbility":46,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":73,"height":170,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1991-12-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2011-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Part of the 2011 debut class, Yosuke became the 3rd generation incarnation of the Super Shenlong character in 2012. After losing his mask in 2013, he briefly competed under his real name. No longer wanting to hide his feelings, he asked to join the Millenial so he could be with the man he loved, Eita. He underwent a shocking transformation, letting his true self shine through.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":14,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":61,"storytelling":66,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":24,"matchLayout":68,"psychology":61,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":76,"technicalCoaching":58,"characterCoaching":79,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":76,"mediaHandling":79,"brandBuilding":53,"socialMediaSavvy":75,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":76,"consistency":68,"awareness":61,"judgement":77},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1255","wrestlerId":1255,"promotionId":14,"startDate":"2011-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1256,"name":"Ken'ichiro Arai","realName":"Ken'ichiro Arai","picture":"Kenichiro Arai.jpg","ability":53,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":53,"charisma":41,"micSkills":48,"popularity":4,"condition":79,"hardcoreAbility":50,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":80,"height":172,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1972-07-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Keni'chiro Arai is a Japanese wrestler for Dragon Gate. Keni'chiro Arai, also known as AraKen, is a second term graduate of Último Dragón's Toryumon Japan group, and has been a mainstay on the roster ever since. He participated in FMW before joining Toryumon. He debuted as a heel, but turned face within the year and remained so for over a decade. On October 13, 2010, the Deep Drunkers lost a six man tag team match to World-1 and were as a result forced to split up. However, following the match World-1 member Naruki Doi turned on his stablemates and joined the former Deep Drunkers and Takuya Sugawara to form a new heel group. They however decided that Arai was not needed in the new group and kicked him out.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":14,"teams":[935,2937],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":57,"storytelling":65,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":36,"matchLayout":67,"psychology":57,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":59,"characterCoaching":64,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":64,"mediaHandling":64,"brandBuilding":33,"socialMediaSavvy":58,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":75,"awareness":57,"judgement":74},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1256","wrestlerId":1256,"promotionId":14,"startDate":"2019-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1257,"name":"Kotoka","realName":"Kotoka","picture":"Kotoka.jpg","ability":52,"currentAbility":44,"potentialAbility":44,"charisma":30,"micSkills":34,"popularity":6,"condition":82,"hardcoreAbility":58,"injuryProne":98,"type":"manager","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":66,"height":162,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1990-01-08T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2009-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"CIBA is lone survivor of the 2009 NEX class. After debuting under his real name, he was granted entry to WORLD-1. In a bit of irony, he was asked by his stablemates to shorten his ringname to simply Kotoka. The reason being that his last name Shiiba was too similar to CIMA. He felt insulted by being left out of the match that forced the end of W1, so he remained independent during the BW vs. JIII war. Rejected by the units that formed in the aftermath, he allied with the Windows group. He felt he fit in with them, since he was already being passed over for less experienced members by the other units. He formed a bond with CIMA during an excursion to Russia. This lead to him being bestowed the costume and offense of the DG ace. He began competing as CIBA. He also works as a regular reporter for the ABC Television morning news show Ohayou Asahi Desu.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":48,"storytelling":57,"productFit":60,"riskTaking":36,"matchLayout":60,"psychology":48,"workerManagement":60,"trainingIntensity":72,"technicalCoaching":69,"characterCoaching":61,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":64,"mediaHandling":61,"brandBuilding":47,"socialMediaSavvy":45,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":12,"reactionSpeed":72,"consistency":53,"awareness":48,"judgement":53}},{"id":1258,"name":"Takayuki Mori","realName":"Takayuki Mori","picture":"Anthony W Mori.jpg","ability":92,"currentAbility":87,"potentialAbility":87,"charisma":76,"micSkills":83,"popularity":3,"condition":80,"hardcoreAbility":87,"injuryProne":71,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":70,"height":167,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1976-09-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Takayuki Mori  is a retired Japanese professional wrestler, better known by the ring name Anthony W. Mori. He is best known for working for Dragon Gate. Mori debuted with the Toryumon T2P class in 2000 under his real name. The following year, he became KENtaro Mori, \"Barbie's boyfriend\", and the year after that, he switched over to his current gimmick of Anthony W. Mori, a royal prince. Mori wrestled his retirement match on December 2, 2010. He remains with Dragon Gate in a backstage role.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":14,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":74,"storytelling":77,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":78,"psychology":74,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":53,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":60,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":47,"socialMediaSavvy":64,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":53,"consistency":47,"awareness":74,"judgement":84},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1258","wrestlerId":1258,"promotionId":14,"startDate":"2004-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1259,"name":"Mikey Whipwreck","realName":"Mikey Whipwreck","picture":"Mikey Whipwreck.jpg","ability":72,"currentAbility":75,"potentialAbility":75,"charisma":60,"micSkills":67,"popularity":4,"condition":71,"hardcoreAbility":90,"injuryProne":71,"type":"writer","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":82,"height":167,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1973-06-04T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1994-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"John Watson  is an American professional wrestler, better known by his ring name Mikey Whipwreck. He is best known for his career with Extreme Championship Wrestling, where he became the third ECW Triple Crown Champion. Before becoming a professional wrestler, Whipwreck joined Extreme Championship Wrestling and was part of their ring crew, who would usually work for free as long as they could have fun in the ring themselves before and after shows had finished.  Booker Paul Heyman asked Mikey to wrestle competitively in ECW after he watched Whipwreck practice a variety of aerial maneuvers before a live show began. In early 2001, Whipwreck announced his intention to retire in May 2002 if he was not hired by the World Wrestling Federation, expressing an interest in pursuing a career in pyrotechnics. By June 11 he had decided to retire by September of that year, as his wrestling style had begun resulting in a number of nagging injuries.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[2887,3246],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":50,"storytelling":60,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":37,"matchLayout":64,"psychology":50,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":60,"technicalCoaching":43,"characterCoaching":51,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":63,"mediaHandling":51,"brandBuilding":34,"socialMediaSavvy":44,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":60,"consistency":38,"awareness":50,"judgement":70}},{"id":1260,"name":"Brandon Tolle","realName":"Brandon Tolle","picture":"Brandon Tolle.jpg","ability":70,"currentAbility":64,"potentialAbility":64,"charisma":50,"micSkills":62,"popularity":1,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":45,"injuryProne":33,"type":"referee","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":71,"height":162,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1985-07-05T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2003-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Brandon Tolle began his journey into the wrestling industry on his 18th birthday in 2003, after meeting his trainer Russell Jones in 2003 in Cincinnati. He began by training to be a wrestler, but after refereeing for a promotion in southern Kentucky when a referee was needed, he found out that refereeing was a better fit for him. He then began the task of mastering the craft that is being a Professional Wrestling Referee. Since that time Brandon has worked for over 25 different companies throughout the United States and Canada. Brandon is continually working to be the best that there is in the wrestling business when it comes to referees and will not stop until he is living his dream of working for WWE or TNA. Brandon has worked for companies such as Dragon Gate USA, Ring of Honor, The National Wrestling Alliance based out of Charlotte, NC, NWA Championship Wrestling from Hollywood, Insanity Pro Wrestling, Prime Time Wrestling, Maximum Pro Wrestling, Border City Wrestling and more.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":28,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":58,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":23,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":23,"brandBuilding":22,"socialMediaSavvy":12,"ruleKnowledge":64,"positioning":51,"reactionSpeed":58,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1260","wrestlerId":1260,"promotionId":28,"startDate":"2019-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1261,"name":"Shane McMahon","realName":"Shane McMahon","picture":"Shane McMahon.jpg","ability":42,"currentAbility":49,"potentialAbility":49,"charisma":37,"micSkills":56,"popularity":51,"condition":67,"hardcoreAbility":29,"injuryProne":95,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":104,"height":185,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1970-01-15T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1989-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Born with sports-entertainment in his blood, Shane McMahon has thrilled the WWE Universe with his daredevil decisions both in and out of the ring.\r\n\r\nThe only son of WWE Chairman Mr. McMahon, Shane grew up in sports-entertainment, learning the ins and outs of the business while holding various positions, including referee and announcer. In fact, Shane was the play-by-play man on the debut edition of Sunday Night Heat in 1999.\r\n\r\nIt wasn’t until the younger McMahon stepped out from behind the microphone that the WWE Universe saw how like his father he was, yet different in many ways. There’s no doubt that Shane McMahon inherited his father’s entrepreneurial spirit. However, he put a modern twist on it. He eschewed a suit and tie for a more casual look, not unlike contemporary moguls like Mark Cuban. His flamboyant, cocky attitude could be both endearing and irritating.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":55,"storytelling":55,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":57,"matchLayout":55,"psychology":55,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":42,"technicalCoaching":26,"characterCoaching":72,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":43,"mediaHandling":72,"brandBuilding":52,"socialMediaSavvy":65,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":42,"consistency":55,"awareness":55,"judgement":73}},{"id":1262,"name":"Kazushi Miyamoto","realName":"Kazushi Miyamoto","picture":"Kazushi Miyamoto.jpg","ability":50,"currentAbility":54,"potentialAbility":54,"charisma":62,"micSkills":45,"popularity":5,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":41,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"submission","gender":"M","weight":118,"height":180,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1979-02-22T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2001-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Kazushi Miyamoto  will forever have the distinction of being the first post-split graduate of the All Japan Pro Wrestling dojo. While in the Dojo Miyamoto was trained by Hiroshi Hase, Johnny Smith, and his mentor Toshiaki Kawada. Miyamoto was so serious about wrestling for All Japan, he originally asked Giant Baba in 1996, but was denied due to his young age. After completing training in the Dojo, Miyamoto debuted on August 19, 2001 against Hiroshi Hase. A Jr. Heavyweight when he debuted, for the remainder of the year he opened cards and wrestled different veterans to help him hone his craft. He started 2002 off by pickingup his first pinfall victory in a tag team match, and a couple days later he had his first singles victory over Yasu Urano. For the rest of 2002 he continued wrestling towards the beginning of the card, waiting for his chance to elevate to a more meaningful role.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3044],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":53,"storytelling":60,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":36,"matchLayout":63,"psychology":53,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":38,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":64,"mediaHandling":38,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":33,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":55,"awareness":53,"judgement":72}},{"id":1263,"name":"HUB","realName":"HUB","picture":"HUB.jpg","ability":50,"currentAbility":51,"potentialAbility":51,"charisma":53,"micSkills":66,"popularity":3,"condition":78,"hardcoreAbility":45,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":80,"height":167,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1978-08-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"HUB is a Japanese wrestler who has worked for Osaka Pro, Dragon Gate and AJPW among others. He was trained by Super Delfin and has gone by many names over his many years in the business, such as GOA, Super Dolphin and Zero among others.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[2891],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":51,"storytelling":60,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":31,"matchLayout":63,"psychology":51,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":55,"characterCoaching":58,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":69,"mediaHandling":58,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":42,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":62,"awareness":51,"judgement":71}},{"id":1264,"name":"Kento Miyahara","realName":"Kento Miyahara","picture":"Kento Miyahara.jpg","ability":85,"currentAbility":76,"potentialAbility":76,"charisma":82,"micSkills":85,"popularity":8,"condition":80,"hardcoreAbility":86,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"submission","gender":"M","weight":102,"height":182,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1989-02-27T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Kento Miyahara is a Japanese wrestler who works in Mexico, the British Isles and Japan. He is a Middleweight who is classed as using a Impactful style. He is best known for his work with NOAH, Dragongate, DDT, BJW, AJPW, FREEDOMS and IWRG. He is currently the Triple Crown Heavyweight champion. He is the protege of Kensuke Sasaki.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":3,"teams":[1696,2143,2301,3055,3665],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":84,"storytelling":86,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":87,"psychology":84,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":91,"technicalCoaching":75,"characterCoaching":88,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":88,"brandBuilding":88,"socialMediaSavvy":71,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":91,"consistency":86,"awareness":84,"judgement":90},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1264","wrestlerId":1264,"promotionId":3,"startDate":"2014-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":1265,"name":"Hibiscus Mii","realName":"Hibiscus Mii","picture":"Apple Miyuki_alt2.jpg","ability":50,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":55,"charisma":42,"micSkills":65,"popularity":2,"condition":89,"hardcoreAbility":35,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"comedy","gender":"F","weight":52,"height":149,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1985-06-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Hibiscus Mii is a female professional wrestler, who currently works for Ryukyu Dragon Pro Wrestling. She is better known under her previous ring name Apple Miyuki under which she worked mainly for the Kaientai Dojo and Osaka Pro Wrestling promotions. She debuted on January 14, 2002, in Puerto Rico against another Kaientai Dojo wrestler, Ofune. 2007 saw a change for Apple, as with GET and RAVE being combined together. She had a small feud with Yu Yamagata to see who was the top women's wrestler in K-Dojo. They had two matches against each other, splitting them both, before throwing away their differences, and they have yet to have had a third singles match. In March 2013, Miyuki announced that she was joining the new Ryukyu Dragon Pro Wrestling promotion, adopting the new ring name Hibiscus Mii in the process.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3427],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":67,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":69,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":72,"technicalCoaching":60,"characterCoaching":73,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":73,"brandBuilding":52,"socialMediaSavvy":64,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":72,"consistency":75,"awareness":62,"judgement":77}},{"id":1266,"name":"Yuzuki Aikawa","realName":"Yuzuki Aikawa","picture":"Yuzuki Aikawa.jpg","ability":40,"currentAbility":48,"potentialAbility":48,"charisma":44,"micSkills":57,"popularity":5,"condition":79,"hardcoreAbility":43,"injuryProne":100,"type":"referee","style":"all rounder","gender":"F","weight":46,"height":154,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1983-05-16T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Yuzuki Aikawa is a Japanese gravure idol and retired professional wrestler. Starting her modeling career in 2003, Aikawa went on to become one of Japan's top gravure idols, earning the nickname \"The Gravure Queen of the Next Generation\" by appearing in various men's magazines, advertising campaigns, films, television programs and video games. In 2010, Aikawa transitioned into professional wrestling, joining the newly founded World Wonder Ring Stardom promotion, becoming its public face and the inaugural holder of the Wonder of Stardom and Goddesses of Stardom Championships. Aikawa's first year in professional wrestling ended with the Tokyo Sports magazine naming her the 2011 female wrestler of the year. A year later, having successfully defended the Wonder of Stardom Championship throughout the year, while also winning the inaugural 5Star GP, Aikawa became the first wrestler to win the award two times in a row.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3317],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":58,"storytelling":62,"productFit":23,"riskTaking":34,"matchLayout":64,"psychology":58,"workerManagement":23,"trainingIntensity":67,"technicalCoaching":58,"characterCoaching":68,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":66,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":77,"socialMediaSavvy":65,"ruleKnowledge":48,"positioning":43,"reactionSpeed":67,"consistency":56,"awareness":58,"judgement":44}},{"id":1267,"name":"Peter Avalon","realName":"Peter Avalon","picture":"Peter Avalon.jpg","ability":63,"currentAbility":56,"potentialAbility":56,"charisma":55,"micSkills":60,"popularity":10,"condition":93,"hardcoreAbility":36,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":75,"height":175,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1989-06-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Peter Avalon is an American wrestler who works exclusively in America. He is a Small worker who is classed as using a Entertainer style. He is one half of PPRay alongside Ray Rosas. He is best known for his work with AEW and NJoA.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":49,"teams":[631,1280,2155,2384],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":61,"productFit":88,"riskTaking":19,"matchLayout":62,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":88,"trainingIntensity":68,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":58,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":81,"mediaHandling":58,"brandBuilding":25,"socialMediaSavvy":32,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":18,"reactionSpeed":68,"consistency":67,"awareness":56,"judgement":69},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1267","wrestlerId":1267,"promotionId":49,"startDate":"2023-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"inDevelopment":true},{"id":1269,"name":"Kenoh","realName":"Kenoh","picture":"Kenou.jpg","ability":72,"currentAbility":71,"potentialAbility":71,"charisma":73,"micSkills":68,"popularity":7,"condition":85,"hardcoreAbility":83,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":95,"height":172,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1985-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2008-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Daisuke Nakae is a Japanese professional wrestler, better known for his ring name Kenou. Nakae, a decorated nippon kempo practitioner, started his career in professional wrestling in the Michinoku Pro Wrestling Dojo, where he was introduced by Jinsei Shinzaki. He debuted in 2007 under the name of Kenou (?? Keno?, Fist King) and wrestled a number of exhibition and low-profile matches against fellow trainees Rui Hiugaji and Takayuki Aizawa. In late 2008, he was sent to Okinawa Pro Wrestling to hone his skills, adopting the name Kanmuriwashi Yoko and the gimmick of an afro kickboxer. In Septiember 2009, Kenou made his return to Michinoku Pro, shockingly beating Tohoku Junior Heavyweight Champion Fujita \"Jr.\" Hayato and capturing the title. He feuded with Hayato and his heel stable, Kowloon, and made alliances with the Michinoku Seikigun, slowly becoming the next ace of the promotion after Yoshitsune's departure.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":45,"teams":[1000,4103,4104],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":76,"storytelling":79,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":33,"matchLayout":80,"psychology":76,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":84,"technicalCoaching":73,"characterCoaching":82,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":67,"mediaHandling":82,"brandBuilding":66,"socialMediaSavvy":73,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":84,"consistency":75,"awareness":76,"judgement":86},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1269","wrestlerId":1269,"promotionId":45,"startDate":"2015-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1270,"name":"Robert King","realName":"Robert King","picture":"Robert King.jpg","ability":62,"currentAbility":69,"potentialAbility":69,"charisma":54,"micSkills":84,"popularity":3,"condition":92,"hardcoreAbility":88,"injuryProne":60,"type":"referee","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":96,"height":170,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1983-03-19T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2001-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Robert King is an American man who works primarily as a referee. He is best known for his work with NWA.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":0,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":0,"brandBuilding":0,"socialMediaSavvy":0,"ruleKnowledge":69,"positioning":55,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":45,"awareness":0,"judgement":0}},{"id":1271,"name":"Mike Chioda","realName":"Mike Chioda","picture":"Mike Chioda.jpg","ability":80,"currentAbility":85,"potentialAbility":85,"charisma":98,"micSkills":89,"popularity":12,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":99,"injuryProne":53,"type":"referee","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":80,"height":180,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1966-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1989-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Michael Joseph \"Mike\" Chioda is a senior referee who is currently signed to WWE. As a young man, Chioda lived close to the Marellas (Gorilla Monsoon and his son Joey), who helped him break into the wrestling business. Being trained as a referee, Chioda first began to appear in WWE in 1989, when it was known as the World Wrestling Federation (WWF), most notably at Survivor Series 1989. After taking a hiatus from refereeing following WrestleMania VII, he began to reappear on camera around 1993. Chioda has also competed in an actual wrestling match, teaming with Chris Jericho and The Rock to take on the team of The Dudley Boyz and referee Nick Patrick on an episode of SmackDown! in 2001.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":35,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":28,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":28,"brandBuilding":7,"socialMediaSavvy":23,"ruleKnowledge":85,"positioning":68,"reactionSpeed":35,"consistency":55,"awareness":0,"judgement":0}},{"id":1272,"name":"Rod Zapata","realName":"Rod Zapata","picture":"Rod Zapata.jpg","ability":67,"currentAbility":76,"potentialAbility":76,"charisma":67,"micSkills":61,"popularity":1,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":65,"injuryProne":60,"type":"referee","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":71,"height":165,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1978-03-27T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1996-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Rod Zapata is an American man who works primarily as a referee. He is best known for his work with WWE.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":51,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":21,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":21,"brandBuilding":0,"socialMediaSavvy":9,"ruleKnowledge":76,"positioning":61,"reactionSpeed":51,"consistency":55,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1272","wrestlerId":1272,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2014-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":1273,"name":"Madman Fulton","realName":"Madman Fulton","picture":"Sawyer Fulton.jpg","ability":39,"currentAbility":49,"potentialAbility":49,"charisma":39,"micSkills":52,"popularity":12,"condition":95,"hardcoreAbility":48,"injuryProne":98,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":145,"height":200,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1990-04-02T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Jacob Southwick is an American professional wrestler. Raised on a small farm in Northern Ohio, Sawyer Fulton worked hard and fought all his life for respect. The simple life led to Sawyer putting on a tremendous amount of size and strength. As he grew, Fulton turned to sports as an outlet of aggression, focusing mainly on wrestling – eventually earning two Ohio State placings and an All-American honors in high school, as well as a Greco Roman All-American and a two-time NCAA All-American in college. Fresh out of college and new to the real world – Sawyer Fulton is here to show that even though he is one of the youngest superstars on the NXT roster, he is also one of the biggest and he will not stop until NXT gold is resting on his shoulder.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[2332,2333,2512,2675],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":45,"storytelling":51,"productFit":92,"riskTaking":38,"matchLayout":53,"psychology":45,"workerManagement":92,"trainingIntensity":63,"technicalCoaching":29,"characterCoaching":51,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":62,"mediaHandling":51,"brandBuilding":68,"socialMediaSavvy":48,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":18,"reactionSpeed":63,"consistency":61,"awareness":45,"judgement":64}},{"id":1274,"name":"Dak Draper","realName":"Dak Draper","picture":"Dak Draper.jpg","ability":66,"currentAbility":56,"potentialAbility":56,"charisma":50,"micSkills":52,"popularity":5,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":56,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":112,"height":193,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1988-03-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2012-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"From a young age, “The Mile High Magnum” Dak Draper knew he was different. He always stood taller, ran faster, and jumped higher than his peers in his beloved home state, Colorado. Dak’s natural abilities made him a stand out wrestler and football player throughout high school and college. After the national wrestling tournament, his senior year of college, he began his professional wrestling training at the WWE Performance Center. Although his athletic pursuits have changed over time, his thirst for competition and more importantly, winning, have stayed the same. He has made it his goal to show that no man can stand toe to toe with the “Mile High Magnum“ and as his hand is raised in victory, he will be the first to tell his opponent “SHAME ON YOU!”","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3714],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":52,"storytelling":56,"productFit":48,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":58,"psychology":52,"workerManagement":48,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":46,"characterCoaching":58,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":58,"brandBuilding":72,"socialMediaSavvy":48,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":10,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":68,"awareness":52,"judgement":50}},{"id":1277,"name":"Buddy Matthews","realName":"Buddy Matthews","picture":"Murphy.jpg","ability":67,"currentAbility":70,"potentialAbility":70,"charisma":81,"micSkills":65,"popularity":37,"condition":90,"hardcoreAbility":61,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":102,"height":175,"base":"Australia","birthplace":"Australia","dateOfBirth":"1988-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2007-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Buddy Matthews is an Australian wrestler who works in the USA, Canada, Japan and Oceania. He is a 5'10\", 224lb worker who is classed as using a Technician Striker style. He uses the Murphy's Law as his finisher. He is best known for his work with WWE, AEW, NXT and MCW. He is married to Rhea Ripley.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[950,2073],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":72,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":73,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":84,"technicalCoaching":72,"characterCoaching":52,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":52,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":38,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":84,"consistency":85,"awareness":68,"judgement":81},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1277","wrestlerId":1277,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2022-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"injury":{"type":"Torn Meniscus","daysToRecover":6},"returnDate":"2026-04-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":1283,"name":"Jakob Hammermeier","realName":"Jakob Hammermeier","picture":"Jakob Hammermeier.jpg","ability":45,"currentAbility":39,"potentialAbility":39,"charisma":43,"micSkills":31,"popularity":1,"condition":93,"hardcoreAbility":23,"injuryProne":100,"type":"commentator","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":90,"height":177,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1986-06-03T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2009-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Troy Brolin, better known by his ring name Jakob Hammermeier is an American professional wrestler who is most notable for his appearances with CHIKARA as a member of Die Bruderschaft des Kreuzes stable. The Pennsylvania native is billed from Zurich, Switzerland.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3183],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":31,"storytelling":38,"productFit":40,"riskTaking":41,"matchLayout":41,"psychology":31,"workerManagement":40,"trainingIntensity":62,"technicalCoaching":54,"characterCoaching":49,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":59,"mediaHandling":49,"brandBuilding":24,"socialMediaSavvy":48,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":8,"reactionSpeed":62,"consistency":54,"awareness":31,"judgement":35}},{"id":1287,"name":"Bob Backlund","realName":"Bob Backlund","picture":"Bob Backlund.jpg","ability":55,"currentAbility":50,"potentialAbility":50,"charisma":56,"micSkills":41,"popularity":21,"condition":59,"hardcoreAbility":64,"injuryProne":63,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":106,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1949-08-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1967-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Bob Backlund experienced success as both an adored hero and a loathed villain in a WWE career that spanned across three decades. The kid from Princeton, Minn., quickly became a fan favorite and the seventh WWE Champion in the company’s history at Madison Square Garden in 1978. But when Backlund left WWE for good in the mid-1990s, he was a deranged madman despised by the fans for his outlandish behavior. It was a stunning transformation for the once beloved man who reigned atop sports-entertainment in the pre-Hogan era. \r\nBacklund’s impressive run at the top and subsequent descent into absurd lunacy makes for one of the most unique careers in WWE history. That’s why it was no surprise when the former WWE Champion was announced as an inductee into the WWE Hall of Fame’s Class of 2013.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3121],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":72,"storytelling":80,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":53,"matchLayout":82,"psychology":72,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":39,"technicalCoaching":37,"characterCoaching":44,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":47,"mediaHandling":44,"brandBuilding":28,"socialMediaSavvy":54,"ruleKnowledge":10,"positioning":28,"reactionSpeed":39,"consistency":28,"awareness":72,"judgement":83}},{"id":1290,"name":"Solar","realName":"Solar","picture":"Solar.jpg","ability":77,"currentAbility":70,"potentialAbility":70,"charisma":65,"micSkills":72,"popularity":7,"condition":58,"hardcoreAbility":60,"injuryProne":98,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":89,"height":170,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1956-05-25T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1975-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Solar is often known as “El Maestro”(“teacher” or “master”). He is the master of a classic wrestling technique that is rooted in holds and clinches but he also has a mastery of a more acrobatic style of wrestling. Solar was born in the state of Jalisco in the town of Zacoalco de Torres into a boyhood of rural poverty. After his family moved to Guadalajara, Solar went with a cousin to see lucha libre for the first time. He has said that, “with lucha libre, it was love at first sight.” He trained under the best lucha libre teachers of the era including El Diablo Velasco and Rene Guajardo. He has wrestled with, and against, the greatest wrestlers that have ever stepped into the ring including El Santo, Lou Thesz, El Solitario and Angel Blanco.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":88,"storytelling":88,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":13,"matchLayout":88,"psychology":88,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":48,"technicalCoaching":92,"characterCoaching":35,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":87,"mediaHandling":35,"brandBuilding":40,"socialMediaSavvy":30,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":48,"consistency":68,"awareness":88,"judgement":93}},{"id":1292,"name":"Alex Reynolds","realName":"Alex Reynolds","picture":"Alex Reynolds.jpg","ability":67,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"charisma":49,"micSkills":52,"popularity":20,"condition":85,"hardcoreAbility":60,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":89,"height":175,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1987-03-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2006-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Alex Reynolds is an American wrestler who works in America and Canada. He is a Lightweight who is classed as using a Regular style. He is one half of The Beaver Boys alongside John Silver. He is best known for his work with AEW, PWG, HOH, DEFY, Beyond, EVOLVE, AIW, A1, CHIKARA and CZW.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":49,"teams":[628,1385,1386,1954,2145,2402,3768],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":57,"storytelling":63,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":28,"matchLayout":65,"psychology":57,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":61,"characterCoaching":65,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":72,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":50,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":74,"awareness":57,"judgement":74},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1292","wrestlerId":1292,"promotionId":49,"startDate":"2023-04-20T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"inDevelopment":true},{"id":1293,"name":"Shinpei Nogami","realName":"Shinpei Nogami","picture":"Shinpei Nogami.jpg","ability":81,"currentAbility":73,"potentialAbility":73,"charisma":58,"micSkills":79,"popularity":5,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":56,"injuryProne":81,"type":"commentator","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":67,"height":175,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1976-07-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Shinpei Nogami is a Japanese announcer who is currently the lead play-by-play for NJPW.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":38,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":8,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":10,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":62,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":62,"brandBuilding":15,"socialMediaSavvy":58,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":0,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1293","wrestlerId":1293,"promotionId":38,"startDate":"2007-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":1294,"name":"Tiger Hattori","realName":"Tiger Hattori","picture":"Tiger Hattori.jpg","ability":7,"currentAbility":0,"potentialAbility":0,"charisma":0,"micSkills":6,"popularity":4,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":0,"injuryProne":39,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":68,"height":162,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1945-07-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1977-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Tiger Hattori is a referee in New Japan who has been involved in wrestling in some form for over 35 years. An amateur wrestler in college, Hattori competed in the All-Japan wrestling championships. Soon afterwards he began working with Hiro Matsuda and Masa Saito before making his referee debut in 1977 in the US. He joined All-Japan in 1980 as an NWA-recognized referee, then moved to New Japan in 1982 before leaving in 1984 to work for Riki Choshu’s Fighting World Of Japan. After the pro wrestling collapse in Japan, Hattori returned to New Japan and was appointed to a referee management position in 2001. He left New Japan again in 2002 but returned in 2004. Today he continues to referee and also does some PR work for the promotion.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":38,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":38,"brandBuilding":38,"socialMediaSavvy":28,"ruleKnowledge":78,"positioning":62,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0}},{"id":1295,"name":"Rey Misterio Sr.","realName":"Rey Misterio Sr.","picture":"Rey Mysterio Sr.jpg","ability":82,"currentAbility":84,"potentialAbility":84,"charisma":84,"micSkills":71,"popularity":4,"condition":77,"hardcoreAbility":73,"injuryProne":81,"type":"writer","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":98,"height":172,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1958-01-08T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1976-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":true,"story":"Rey Misterio Sr. is a retired Mexican luchador who works primarily as a road agent. He is best known for his work with WCW and AAA.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":77,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":30,"matchLayout":80,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":46,"technicalCoaching":53,"characterCoaching":53,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":70,"mediaHandling":53,"brandBuilding":63,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":46,"consistency":51,"awareness":68,"judgement":81}},{"id":1297,"name":"Taya Valkyrie","realName":"Taya Valkyrie","picture":"Taya Valkyrie.jpg","ability":47,"currentAbility":57,"potentialAbility":57,"charisma":44,"micSkills":58,"popularity":28,"condition":82,"hardcoreAbility":54,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"F","weight":66,"height":170,"base":"Canada","birthplace":"Canada","dateOfBirth":"1983-10-22T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Taya Valkyrie, a 2010 graduate of the Storm Wrestling Academy, is a Canadian wrestler who works in America, Canada, Mexico and the British Isles. She is a Small worker who is classed as using a Technician Flyer style. She is best known for her work with AAA, IMPACT, NXT, NWA, MLW and Lucha Ungrnd. She is currently the MLW Women's World Featherweight champion, an IMPACT Knockouts Tag Team champion and the AAA Reina de Reinas champion. She is married to John Hennigan. She is the protege of Lance Storm.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":49,"teams":[4073],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":62,"productFit":88,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":64,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":88,"trainingIntensity":61,"technicalCoaching":51,"characterCoaching":64,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":64,"brandBuilding":70,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":18,"reactionSpeed":61,"consistency":73,"awareness":56,"judgement":69},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1297","wrestlerId":1297,"promotionId":49,"startDate":"2023-12-14T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"inDevelopment":true},{"id":1354,"name":"Domare Stavros","realName":"Domare Stavros","picture":"Domare Stavros.jpg","ability":84,"currentAbility":77,"potentialAbility":77,"charisma":71,"micSkills":86,"popularity":0,"condition":96,"hardcoreAbility":73,"injuryProne":0,"type":"referee","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":97,"height":170,"base":"Europe","birthplace":"Unknown","dateOfBirth":"1970-12-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2006-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"An experianced referee with roots in Greece who has judged main events all over Europe","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":20,"storytelling":19,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":19,"psychology":20,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":3,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":27,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":27,"brandBuilding":17,"socialMediaSavvy":22,"ruleKnowledge":77,"positioning":62,"reactionSpeed":3,"consistency":0,"awareness":20,"judgement":12}},{"id":1366,"name":"Starbuck","realName":"Starbuck","picture":"starbuck.jpg","ability":58,"currentAbility":64,"potentialAbility":64,"charisma":74,"micSkills":64,"popularity":2,"condition":67,"hardcoreAbility":57,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":102,"height":177,"base":"Canada","birthplace":"Canada","dateOfBirth":"1973-04-24T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1994-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"\"The Canadian Rebel\" Starbuck has wrestled all over the world, most notably for the SMASH Promotion in Japan against Tajiri. He started out by getting trained by Lance Storm in Calgary and had his first match in 1994. He has Finnish roots and moved there in the 2000´s and had ambititions of starting a wrestling organisation. After trying a few different concepts he opened up Fight Club Finland in 2006 and the promotion has been growing ever since.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":75,"storytelling":77,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":78,"psychology":75,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":68,"technicalCoaching":55,"characterCoaching":61,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":61,"brandBuilding":46,"socialMediaSavvy":58,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":68,"consistency":70,"awareness":75,"judgement":85}},{"id":1393,"name":"Arisa Nakajima","realName":"Arisa Nakajima","picture":"Arisa Nakajima.jpg","ability":75,"currentAbility":70,"potentialAbility":70,"charisma":82,"micSkills":84,"popularity":10,"condition":77,"hardcoreAbility":86,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"all rounder","gender":"F","weight":60,"height":157,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1989-04-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2006-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Arisa Nakajima  is a Japanese professional wrestler. Trained by the Major Girl's Fighting AtoZ promotion, Nakajima made her debut in January 2006, but when the promotion folded the following May, she transferred over to JWP Joshi Puroresu, where she has worked ever since, becoming a two-time JWP Openweight Champion, a two-time JWP Junior and Princess of Pro-Wrestling Champion and a one-time JWP Tag Team and Daily Sports Women's Tag Team Champion in the process. Nakajima retired from professional wrestling in June 2009, but made her return to JWP in April 2012. The following December, Nakajima won JWP's top title, the JWP Openweight Championship, for the first time.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":73,"teams":[1697,2477,3374,3375,3975],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":83,"storytelling":84,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":84,"psychology":83,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":85,"technicalCoaching":83,"characterCoaching":68,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":69,"socialMediaSavvy":55,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":85,"consistency":88,"awareness":83,"judgement":90},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1393","wrestlerId":1393,"promotionId":73,"startDate":"2017-01-26T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1395,"name":"Alisha Edwards","realName":"Alisha Edwards","picture":"Alexis Neveah.jpg","ability":49,"currentAbility":39,"potentialAbility":39,"charisma":29,"micSkills":41,"popularity":13,"condition":87,"hardcoreAbility":54,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"F","weight":54,"height":149,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1987-01-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2006-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Alisha Edwards is an American wrestler who works in the USA and Canada. She is a 5'0\", 119lb worker who is classed as using a Regular style. She uses the Guillotine Drop and the One-handed Bulldog as her finishers. She is best known for her work with TNA. She is married to Eddie Edwards.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":28,"teams":[4005],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":45,"storytelling":47,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":37,"matchLayout":47,"psychology":45,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity"