g over the name, and the one who started making AAA appearances in 2013. Everyone expects this Carta to eventually receive a new identity in AAA, which might finally end the argument.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":30,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":70,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":71,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":75,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":58,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":58,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":55,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":75,"consistency":73,"awareness":68,"judgement":81},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1400","wrestlerId":1400,"promotionId":30,"startDate":"2025-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2027-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2027-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1401,"name":"Cerebro Negro","realName":"Cerebro Negro","picture":"Cerebro Negro.jpg","ability":70,"currentAbility":67,"potentialAbility":67,"charisma":64,"micSkills":61,"popularity":2,"condition":70,"hardcoreAbility":47,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":82,"height":167,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1973-09-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1991-05-30T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Long time IWRG luchador, now one of the core regulars in the promotion. Notable feuds with Mike Segura, Black Terry and Dr. Cerebro. Most recently teamed up with the last two as part of the techinical-rudo trio Los Terribles Cerebros. Periodically disappears from IWRG over conflicts of where else he's working (and allowed to work); disappeared from IWRG in May of 2011 for this sort of reason. Touring small arenas around the exterior of Mexico city, like Arena Aficion and Arena Queretaro, while also working for IWL.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":30,"teams":[3757,3758],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":76,"storytelling":78,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":79,"psychology":76,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":68,"technicalCoaching":62,"characterCoaching":68,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":48,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":68,"consistency":71,"awareness":76,"judgement":86},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1401","wrestlerId":1401,"promotionId":30,"startDate":"1999-07-18T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1402,"name":"CJ Perry","realName":"CJ Perry","picture":"Lana.jpg","ability":61,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":53,"charisma":57,"micSkills":61,"popularity":40,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":65,"injuryProne":100,"type":"manager","style":"powerhouse","gender":"F","weight":52,"height":167,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1985-03-24T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2013-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Born into a wealthy Russian family, Lana’s neighbors were ex-presidents, diplomats and other powerful political figures. Fulfilling her desire to pursue a stateside education, Lana attended Florida State University, where she not only learned English, but also majored in Foreign Affairs, Business and Social Media Marketing.\r\n\r\nEncouraged by her parents to discover an investment hobby, Lana invested her knowledge and business acumen into Rusev. Living by the philosophy that no mountain is too high to climb, Lana has used her cunning to conquer WWE.\r\n\r\nFollowing Rusev’s impressive debut in the 2014 Royal Rumble Match, Lana put The Bulgarian Brute on full display. Helping deliver their message of superiority to the WWE Universe, Lana also pledged her heart along with her service, accepting Rusev’s marriage proposal in 2015. While she’s occasionally mixed it up as an in-ring competitor on SmackDown LIVE, Lana has also been instrumental in leading Rusev to three United States Championships.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[2442],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":37,"storytelling":39,"productFit":45,"riskTaking":36,"matchLayout":40,"psychology":37,"workerManagement":45,"trainingIntensity":64,"technicalCoaching":29,"characterCoaching":74,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":64,"mediaHandling":74,"brandBuilding":65,"socialMediaSavvy":78,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":9,"reactionSpeed":64,"consistency":60,"awareness":37,"judgement":40}},{"id":1404,"name":"Yutaka Yoshie","realName":"Yutaka Yoshie","picture":"Yutaka Yoshie.jpg","ability":57,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":55,"charisma":42,"micSkills":56,"popularity":5,"condition":74,"hardcoreAbility":69,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"striker","gender":"M","weight":150,"height":177,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1974-01-05T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1994-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":true,"story":"Yutaka Yoshie is a Japanese professional wrestler, currently working as a freelancer in Japan, performing for promotions such as All Japan Pro Wrestling, New Japan Pro Wrestling, Pro Wrestling Noah and Pro Wrestling Zero1. In New Japan he is a former IWGP Tag Team Champion and in Zero1 a former NWA Intercontinental Tag Team Champion. On January 26, 2014, Yoshie formed a super heavyweight tag team with AJPW Triple Crown Heavyweight Champion Akebono.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1216,3021,3299],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":64,"storytelling":65,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":34,"matchLayout":66,"psychology":64,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":58,"technicalCoaching":39,"characterCoaching":51,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":66,"mediaHandling":51,"brandBuilding":44,"socialMediaSavvy":42,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":58,"consistency":64,"awareness":64,"judgement":78}},{"id":1406,"name":"Abismo Negro Jr.","realName":"Abismo Negro Jr.","picture":"Abismo Negro Jr.jpg","ability":58,"currentAbility":56,"potentialAbility":56,"charisma":53,"micSkills":45,"popularity":7,"condition":85,"hardcoreAbility":56,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":87,"height":172,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1990-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2006-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Abismo Negro Jr. is a masked Mexican luchador who works in the USA and Mexico. He is a 5'9\", 191lb worker who is classed as using a Luchador style. He uses the Styles Clash as his finisher. He is best known for his work with AAA, IWRG, The Crash and DTU.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":5,"teams":[743,2871],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":64,"storytelling":67,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":26,"matchLayout":68,"psychology":64,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":74,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":63,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":74,"mediaHandling":63,"brandBuilding":66,"socialMediaSavvy":48,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":74,"consistency":74,"awareness":64,"judgement":78},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1406","wrestlerId":1406,"promotionId":5,"startDate":"2019-05-02T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1409,"name":"Io Shirai","realName":"Io Shirai","picture":"Io Shirai.jpg","ability":76,"currentAbility":71,"potentialAbility":71,"charisma":68,"micSkills":69,"popularity":65,"condition":83,"hardcoreAbility":71,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"F","weight":55,"height":152,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1990-05-08T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2007-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"great","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"There are plenty of high-flying Superstars, but there’s only one Genius of the Sky. An aerial artist without peer, Io Shirai touched down in NXT in the summer of 2018, after she was announced to great fanfare as a new signee at a WWE Live Event in Tokyo. For Shirai, who was thrice named the top women's wrestler of the year by national Japanese newspaper Tokyo Sports before joining NXT, her mission is clear: Having ascended the mountaintop in her native country, Shirai wants to conquer new frontiers and prove that she’s not only the best wrestler in her homeland, but in the entire world. Moonsaults, hurricanranas and springboard dropkicks are Shirai’s stock-in-trade, and you’d expect nothing less from a Superstar who cites Rey Mysterio as her greatest inspiration. The WWE Universe saw Shirai’s gravity-defying antics up-close for the first time in the 2018 Mae Young Classic, where The Genius of the Sky soared all the way to the tournament final at WWE Evolution.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[397,1533,2807,4309],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":80,"storytelling":82,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":24,"matchLayout":83,"psychology":80,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":83,"technicalCoaching":78,"characterCoaching":79,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":76,"mediaHandling":79,"brandBuilding":81,"socialMediaSavvy":68,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":83,"consistency":74,"awareness":80,"judgement":88},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1409","wrestlerId":1409,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2022-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":1410,"name":"Jaki Numazawa","realName":"Jaki Numazawa","picture":"Jaki Numazawa.jpg","ability":52,"currentAbility":51,"potentialAbility":51,"charisma":42,"micSkills":44,"popularity":4,"condition":55,"hardcoreAbility":69,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"hardcore","gender":"M","weight":100,"height":172,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1977-06-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2000-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Jaki Numazawa  is a Japanese professional wrestler best known by his stage name \"Kokutenshi\" Jaki Numazawa. He currently wrestles for Big Japan Pro Wrestling where he has held the BJW Deathmatch Heavyweight Championship on one occasion. He also appeared in the Dirty Sanchez movie with other wrestlers from Big Japan Pro Wrestling when they were wrestling the Dirty Sanchez team.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[908,1735],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":53,"storytelling":57,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":44,"matchLayout":58,"psychology":53,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":66,"technicalCoaching":51,"characterCoaching":37,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":56,"mediaHandling":37,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":15,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":66,"consistency":69,"awareness":53,"judgement":72}},{"id":1411,"name":"Rasse","realName":"Rasse","picture":"Rasse.jpg","ability":54,"currentAbility":51,"potentialAbility":51,"charisma":47,"micSkills":38,"popularity":4,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":71,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":75,"height":162,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1982-05-21T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2002-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Masaki Okimoto  is a Japanese professional wrestler from Neyagawa, Japan; he's a current member of the Michinoku Pro Wrestling roster as Rasse. He mainly uses a high-flying style. He has worked for many Japanese federations: after graduating in the 9th Toryumon school class term, he debuted in 2002 in Toryumon Mexico with the gimmick of Small Dandy Fuji, a little version of the Japanese wrestler Sumo Dandy Fujii, teaming up with SUWAcito and Mini CIMA, forming the Mini CMAX stable; he continued using this gimmick during 2003. He joined Michinoku Pro Wrestling, originally as Michinoku Ranger Silver with Michinoku Ranger Gold as his partner. He later changed his name and gimmick to Rasse, a masked character representing the Aomori Nebuta Matsuri, which he currently uses. Rasse gained a title shot for the Tohoku Tag Titles, teaming up with Shanao, and losing to Great Sasuke & Dick Togo, and lost the final match for the Tohoku Jr. Heavyweight Title to Takeshi Minamino.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3066,3101],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":63,"storytelling":65,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":31,"matchLayout":66,"psychology":63,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":85,"technicalCoaching":58,"characterCoaching":60,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":69,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":49,"socialMediaSavvy":54,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":85,"consistency":74,"awareness":63,"judgement":78}},{"id":1413,"name":"Savio Vega","realName":"Savio Vega","picture":"Savio Vega.jpg","ability":91,"currentAbility":84,"potentialAbility":84,"charisma":70,"micSkills":85,"popularity":10,"condition":61,"hardcoreAbility":93,"injuryProne":87,"type":"writer","style":"striker","gender":"M","weight":118,"height":177,"base":"USA","birthplace":"Puerto Rico","dateOfBirth":"1964-08-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1984-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"A perennial main eventer in Puerto Rico, Vega is one of the island’s greatest brawlers known for his explosive spinning heel kick, jumping high kick and fighting spirit.\r\n\r\nVega lit up New York City in the mid 1990s teaming with Razor Ramon to form one of the most beloved tag teams of the era. However, many may know of Vega’s ultraviolet alter ego “TNT” who has caused havoc throughout the sport dating back decades.\r\n\r\nOne of the most decorated Caribbean grapplers in the history of the sport, Savio Vega has won countless championships in the Caribbean and has served as a general manager for Puerto Rico’s top organizations over the past few years.\r\n\r\nVega, who splits his time bet