, Phillips grew up watching “Stone Cold” Steve Austin, in addition to his hometown-based ECW. Since making his NXT debut in September 2012, Phillips can be heard broadcasting alongside WWE Superstars William Regal, Brad Maddox and Alex Riley. Taking his love of WWE to the forefront, Phillips now gets to call the action of the NXT Superstars and Divas who will pave the wave of the future for years to come. He is also an announcer on \"WWE Superstars\" and conducts backstage interviews for the WWE App.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":28,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":63,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":63,"brandBuilding":45,"socialMediaSavvy":55,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":0,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1631","wrestlerId":1631,"promotionId":28,"startDate":"2022-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1632,"name":"Tsukushi","realName":"Tsukushi","picture":"Tsukushi.jpg","ability":62,"currentAbility":57,"potentialAbility":57,"charisma":57,"micSkills":53,"popularity":4,"condition":84,"hardcoreAbility":59,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"F","weight":44,"height":142,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1997-09-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Tsukushi  is a Japanese professional wrestler. Trained by Emi Sakura, Tsukushi made her debut for her Ice Ribbon promotion in January 2010 as part of a trial series with Kurumi. After winning the fan voting, Tsukushi was made an official part of Ice Ribbon's roster the following March and she has since wrestled regularly for the promotion.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[2067,2475,2924],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":67,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":30,"matchLayout":68,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":81,"technicalCoaching":68,"characterCoaching":68,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":70,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":55,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":81,"consistency":73,"awareness":62,"judgement":77}},{"id":1634,"name":"Tzuki","realName":"Tzuki","picture":"Tzuki.jpg","ability":30,"currentAbility":32,"potentialAbility":32,"charisma":45,"micSkills":47,"popularity":2,"condition":64,"hardcoreAbility":47,"injuryProne":89,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":40,"height":106,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1973-12-31T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1987-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Tzuki is a Mexican Luchador enmascarado, or masked professional wrestler, who works as a Mini-Estrella or \"Mini\" division in Mexico. Throughout his career Tzuki has worked under various ring names, most notably Máscarita Sagrada, Jr., Mini Rey Misterio Jr. and Max Mini. Tzuki has worked for (AAA), the World Wrestling Federation (WWF) and a variety of special appearances for independent promotions all over Mexico, the United States, Europe and Japan and currently works for Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL). Tsuky's real name is not a matter of 