debut":"2005-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"The man that NXT announcer Wade Barrett has described as a “human torture device” sharpened his skills by competing around the world before coming to the black-and-gold brand in 2020. His impact was immediate, and within months of his debut, Thatcher dispatched of the double-tough Riddle, putting him to sleep in NXT’s first Fight Pit, an unforgiving caged fighting arena. Thatcher didn’t slow down from there, going on to pick fights with members of NXT’s master class, from Kushida to Tommaso Ciampa.\r\n\r\nTo observe Thatcher in practice is like watching an anaconda overwhelm its prey. He patiently devours his opponents, their cries of agony playing like a beautiful symphony in his head. His rear-naked choke is suffocating, his cravat just an excuse to twist necks like crankshafts. Most devastating of all is his Fujiwara Armbar, which has forced innumerable competitors into submission.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":65,"teams":[1296,1799,2331,2830,2831],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":74,"storytelling":77,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":15,"matchLayout":78,"psychology":74,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":85,"technicalCoaching":82,"characterCoaching":57,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":85,"mediaHandling":57,"brandBuilding":51,"socialMediaSavvy":50,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":85,"consistency":87,"awareness":74,"judgement":84},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1655","wrestlerId":1655,"promotionId":65,"startDate":"2024-11-09T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1668,"name":"Malia Hosaka","realName":"Malia Hosaka","picture":"Malia Hosaka.jpg","ability":57,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"charisma":60,"micSkills":67,"popularity":4,"condition":76,"hardcoreAbility":53,"injuryProne":81,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"F","weight":59,"height":160,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1969-10-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1987-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Malia Hosaka was trained by Killer Kowalski at the wrestling training camp run by Misty Blue Simmes. In her debut match, Hosaka (wearing a Mary Lou Retton-inspired gymnastics outfit and billed as \"Malia Ho\") teamed with Simmes against Mad Dog Debbie Irons and Linda Dallas. Hosaka joined World Championship Wrestling in 1996 and competed in their newly formed women's division. She wrestled in the tournament to crown the first WCW Women's Champion, but was eliminated by Zero (Chigusa Nagayo). In 1999, Hosaka signed a developmental contract with World Wrestling Federation. WWF kept her under contract for a year, and shortly before her contract expired they considered bringing her to the main roster under the name \"Aphrodisia\" and pairing her with soon-to-be debuting talent Essa Rios. Instead, the role was given to Amy Dumas and the character was renamed \"Lita\". Hosaka was then released due to an internal lack of character idea development.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3235],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":73,"storytelling":75,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":75,"psychology":73,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":54,"technicalCoaching":54,"characterCoaching":54,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":54,"brandBuilding":46,"socialMediaSavvy":43,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":54,"consistency":54,"awareness":73,"judgement":84}},{"id":1670,"name":"Demus","realName":"Demus","picture":"Demus 666.jpg","ability":68,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"charisma":52,"micSkills":47,"popularity":5,"condition":84,"hardcoreAbility":60,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":80,"height":157,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1980-08-28T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1997-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Pequeño Damián 666  is a Mexican professional wrestler. Pequeño Damián 666 is a part of Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre's (CMLL) Mini-Estrella, or \"Mini\" division. Pequeño Damián 666 ring character is a Mini-version of wrestler Damián 666. In early June, 2010 he changed his ring name to Demus 3:16 as Damián 666 held the trademark to the name and would no longer allow him to use it.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":108,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":63,"storytelling":66,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":40,"matchLayout":67,"psychology":63,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":53,"characterCoaching":67,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":60,"mediaHandling":67,"brandBuilding":33,"socialMediaSavvy":73,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":54,"awareness":63,"judgement":78},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1670","wrestlerId":1670,"promotionId":108,"startDate":"2018-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1671,"name":"Aéreo","realName":"Aéreo","picture":"Aereo.jpg","ability":44,"currentAbility":48,"potentialAbility":48,"charisma":46,"micSkills":60,"popularity":2,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":42,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":59,"height":157,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1990-09-05T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2005-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Víctor Gonzalo Barragán Hernández is a Mexican luchador, or professional wrestler currently working for the Mexican professional wrestling promotion Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) in their Mini-Estrella division. Working in the Mini-Estrellas division does not necessarily mean that Aéreo is a dwarf as several wrestlers who are just shorter in stature work in the \"Mini\" division. Barragán works under the ring name Aéreo, Spanish for \"Air\".","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":52,"storytelling":58,"productFit":59,"riskTaking":33,"matchLayout":60,"psychology":52,"workerManagement":59,"trainingIntensity":65,"technicalCoaching":53,"characterCoaching":46,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":67,"mediaHandling":46,"brandBuilding":23,"socialMediaSavvy":30,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":12,"reactionSpeed":65,"consistency":72,"awareness":52,"judgement":55},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1671","wrestlerId":1671,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2010-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1672,"name":"Marti Belle","realName":"Marti Belle","picture":"Marti Belle.jpg","ability":38,"currentAbility":47,"potentialAbility":47,"