-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1975-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Rayo de Jalisco Jr. is the ring name of a Mexican Luchador Enmascarado (masked professional wrestler) whose real name has not been revealed, per Lucha Libre traditions. Rayo de Jalisco, Jr. is the son of Rayo de Jalisco a famous wrestler from the early days of Lucha Libre; he also has a son who wrestles under the name Rayman. Rayo, Jr. is a former two time CMLL World Heavyweight Champion and the reigning WWA World Heavyweight Champion, a title he has held since March 21, 2003. Rayo de Jalisco, Jr.'s real name is not a matter of public record, as is often the case with masked wrestlers in Mexico where their private lives are kept a secret from the wrestling fans.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":64,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":53,"matchLayout":64,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":36,"technicalCoaching":41,"characterCoaching":46,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":47,"mediaHandling":46,"brandBuilding":46,"socialMediaSavvy":33,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":36,"consistency":42,"awareness":62,"judgement":77}},{"id":1675,"name":"Rayman","realName":"Rayman","picture":"RayMan.jpg","ability":38,"currentAbility":48,"potentialAbility":48,"charisma":55,"micSkills":43,"popularity":2,"condition":93,"hardcoreAbility":58,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":86,"height":167,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1978-10-25T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1999-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"First came to peoples attention in Mexico City as an undercard wrestler named Rayman. Was revealed to be the son of Rayo de Jalisco Jr. and given the El Hijo del Rayo de Jalisco Jr. character in 2001, pushed as a new young star and teaming with the likes of El Hijo del Santo and Negro Casas. Allegedly, his father soon grew jealous when promoters started to book his son instead of him, and the two had some falling out. El Hijo del Rayo de Jalisco Jr. switched to the identity Hombre Sin Nombre character for a time, then switched back to being called Rayman, but lost the moment he had as Rayo de Jalisco and was never a top star again.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":44,"storytelling":54,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":33,"matchLayout":57,"psychology":44,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":54,"characterCoaching":44,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":67,"mediaHandling":44,"brandBuilding":53,"socialMediaSavvy":38,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":60,"awareness":44,"judgement":66}},{"id":1676,"name":"James Maritato","realName":"James Maritato","picture":"Little Guido.jpg","ability":70,"currentAbility":60,"potentialAbility":60,"charisma":50,"micSkills":65,"popularity":8,"condition":74,"hardcoreAbility":66,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":77,"height":165,"base":"Europe","birthplace":"Italy","dateOfBirth":"1972-03-12T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1991-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"James Maritato is an American professional wrestler, of Italian origin, currently working on the independent circuit. He is best known for his work in World Wrestling Entertainment (WWE) and Extreme Championship Wrestling (ECW) under the ring names Little Guido Maritato and Nunzio. In 1992 he joined Extreme Championship Wrestling (ECW) under the name Damian Stone. He was later given the gimmick of Little Guido and put in the comedy stable the Full Blooded Italians (F.B.I.), alongside an African American named \"The Italian Stallion\" J.T. Smith, Tracy Smothers, and \"The Big Don\" Tommy Rich. None of whom, with the exception of Maritato, were really of Italian descent. He is also known to have played the role of female wrestler Raisha Saeed on at least 2 ocassions, both times the woman who normally donned the gimmick was in the match as his opponent (Cheerleader Melissa)","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[496,3184,3185,3709],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":73,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":16,"matchLayout":75,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":55,"technicalCoaching":55,"characterCoaching":70,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":84,"mediaHandling":70,"brandBuilding":35,"socialMediaSavvy":58,"ruleKnowledge":61,"positioning":69,"reactionSpeed":55,"consistency":58,"awareness":68,"judgement":81}},{"id":1677,"name":"Moose","realName":"Moose","picture":"Moose.jpg","ability":70,"currentAbility":60,"potentialAbility":60,"charisma":56,"micSkills":48,"popularity":29,"condition":84,"hardcoreAbility":46,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":136,"height":193,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1984-04-23T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2014-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Moose’s six years as an offensive lineman playing for the NFL prepared him to become a stand-out in the world of professional wrestling. A two-time IMPACT Grand Champion, Moose is easily one of IMPACT’s most hard hitting competitors. With a passion for athletics and knowledge in the industry, Moose is able to set himself apart from the rest.\r\n\r\nMoose continues to re-invent himself and is a fixture in the main event picture. What does the future hold for Mr. IMPACT Wrestling?","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":28,"teams":[3811],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":60,"storytelling":62,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":63,"psychology":60,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":71,"technicalCoaching":42,"characterCoaching":60,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":60,"brandBuilding":78,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":71,"consistency":70,"awareness":60,"judgement":76},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1677","wrestlerId":1677,"promotionId":28,"startDate":"2016-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1678,"name":"Chase Owens","realName":"Chase Owens","picture":"Chase Owens.jpg","ability":41,"currentAbility":51,"potentialAbility":51,"charisma":64,"micSkills":54,"popularity":13,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":67,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":93,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1990-03-07T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2007-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Chase Owens is an American wrestler who works in America, Canada and Japan. He is a Middleweight who is classed as using a Regular style. He is best known for his work with NJPW.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":38,"teams":[3642],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":58,"storytelling":62,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":26,"matchLayout":63,"psychology":58,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":70,"technicalCoaching":47,"characterCoaching":49,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":74,"mediaHandling":49,"brandBuilding":46,"socialMediaSavvy":41,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":70,"consistency":72,"awareness":58,"judgement":75},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1678","wrestlerId":1678,"promotionId":38,"startDate":"2015-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1682,"name":"Máscara Sagrada","realName":"Máscara Sagrada","picture":"Mascara Sagrada.jpg","ability":59,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":53,"charisma":50,"micSkills":48,"popularity":7,"condition":56,"hardcoreAbility":70,"injuryProne":84,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":115,"height":177,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1959-11-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1978-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Máscara Sagrada made his debut in 1978 as Hecatombe, and spent the next 9 years under the mask before using a number of names, including Mágico before becoming Máscara Sagrada in 1989. He split from CMLL to join AAA in 1992, before returning to CMLL after a dispute with Antonio Pena in 1997. He went back and forth between the two companies and is currently working in AAA on a temporary basis.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"l