15, the Brahmans began working for the Freedoms promotion under masks and the ring names El Hijo del Winger Uno and El Hijo del Winger Dos, winning the King of Freedom World Tag Team Championship on January 29, 2015.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":94,"teams":[1394,1395,2462,2463],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":67,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":18,"matchLayout":69,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":71,"technicalCoaching":48,"characterCoaching":70,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":82,"mediaHandling":70,"brandBuilding":16,"socialMediaSavvy":73,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":71,"consistency":72,"awareness":62,"judgement":77},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1740","wrestlerId":1740,"promotionId":94,"startDate":"2009-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1741,"name":"Tessa Blanchard","realName":"Tessa Blanchard","picture":"Tessa Blanchard.jpg","ability":74,"currentAbility":68,"potentialAbility":68,"charisma":57,"micSkills":79,"popularity":29,"condition":98,"hardcoreAbility":57,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"F","weight":57,"height":162,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1995-07-26T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2014-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Tessa Blanchard is a supremely talented American wrestler and the daughter of Four Horsemen legend Tully Blanchard. She made history in 2019 when she became the first woman to hold a men's World Championship in a nationally televised promotion when she won the Impact World Championship from Sami Callihan. Despite her obvious skill and star potential, her career has been derailed by allegations of bullying and racism, compounded by attitude problems which saw her stripped of the Impact World Championship.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[1236,2828,2829],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":66,"storytelling":71,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":18,"matchLayout":72,"psychology":66,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":83,"technicalCoaching":69,"characterCoaching":69,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":82,"mediaHandling":69,"brandBuilding":85,"socialMediaSavvy":56,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":83,"consistency":73,"awareness":66,"judgement":80},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1741","wrestlerId":1741,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2025-10-10T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2027-10-10T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2027-10-10T00:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":1742,"name":"The Blue Meanie","realName":"The Blue Meanie","picture":"The Blue Meanie.jpg","ability":43,"currentAbility":45,"potentialAbility":45,"charisma":30,"micSkills":52,"popularity":5,"condition":73,"hardcoreAbility":27,"injuryProne":80,"type":"wrestler","style":"striker","gender":"M","weight":134,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1973-05-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1994-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Brian Daniel Heffron etter known by the ring name The Blue Meanie, is an American professional wrestler and actor. He is best known for his appearances with ECW from 1995 to 2000 and WWE from 1998 to 2005. Heffron started wrestling in the Midwest out of Al Snow's Bodyslammers Pro Wrestling Gym in Lima, Ohio in March 1994. He continued to wrestle in various independent wrestling promotions throughout the Mid-Atlantic and Midwest regions until 1996. Heffron was noticed by Raven and Stevie Richards at a Steel City Wrestling show in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, and was asked by Raven to become Richards' sidekick in ECW. He went on to become The Blue Meanie, taking his name and persona from the villain of the 1968 animated film Yellow Submarine. Heffron, under his Blue Meanie name, currently wrestles and is a trainer at The Monster Factory.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[515,3305,3306,3307],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":59,"storytelling":64,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":62,"matchLayout":65,"psychology":59,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":47,"technicalCoaching":26,"characterCoaching":74,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":38,"mediaHandling":74,"brandBuilding":28,"socialMediaSavvy":67,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":47,"consistency":33,"awareness":59,"judgement":75}},{"id":1744,"name":"Will Ferrara","realName":"Will Ferrara","picture":"Will Ferrara.jpg","ability":45,"currentAbility":52,"potentialAbility":52,"charisma":62,"micSkills":56,"popularity":2,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":52,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":81,"height":172,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1992-06-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2011-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Will Ferrara  is an American professional wrestler currently signed to Ring of Honor. Ferrara joined the Ring of Honor training school in August of 2012, after establishing a connection through their facebook page. He describes his experience in the training seminars as having completely changed his outlook on wrestling. From that point on, he knew he found the best training outlet for his developing career. During the following year, he made his ROH debut on September 6 during Night #1 of ROH Road to Greatness.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1683],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":54,"storytelling":59,"productFit":71,"riskTaking":21,"matchLayout":60,"psychology":54,"workerManagement":71,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":54,"characterCoaching":35,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":79,"mediaHandling":35,"brandBuilding":35,"socialMediaSavvy":35,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":14,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":76,"awareness":54,"judgement":61}},{"id":1745,"name":"Mahabali Shera","realName":"Mahabali Shera","picture":"Mahabali Shera.jpg","ability":48,"currentAbility":43,"potentialAbility":43,"charisma":49,"micSkills":50,"popularity":8,"condition":93,"hardcoreAbility":60,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"striker","gender":"M","weight":110,"height":190,"base":"Other","birthplace":"India","dateOfBirth":"1990-05-02T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2011-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Mahabali Shera is an Indian wrestler who works in the USA, Canada and India. He is a 6'4\", 242lb worker who is classed as using a Brawler style. He uses the Sky High and the Veera Bomb as his finishers. He is best known for his work with TNA and NXT.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1083,2515],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":38,"storytelling":42,"productFit":64,"riskTaking":28,"matchLayout":43,"psychology":38,"workerManagement":64,"trainingIntensity":61,"technicalCoaching":23,"characterCoaching":48,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":72,"mediaHandling":48,"brandBuilding":69,"socialMediaSavvy":38,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":13,"reactionSpeed":61,"consistency":47,"awareness":38,"judgement":48}},{"id":1746,"name":"Eli Drake","realName":"Eli Drake","picture":"Eli Drake.jpg","ability":61,"currentAbility":63,"potentialAbility":63,"charisma":51,"micSkills":72,"popularity":61,"condition":89,"hardcoreAbility":49,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":104,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1982-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2003-03-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Let LA Knight talk to ya: He has come to NXT to change the game on the black-and-gold brand.\r\n\r\nOne of NXT’s biggest free agent signings in recent history, Knight made a big splash immediately. Making a surprise appearance at NXT TakeOver: Vengeance Day, Knight had a confident message for the NXT Universe signed on the dotted line to officially join the NXT roster.\r\n\r\nKnight has already promised big things on the black-and-gold brand, and why not? He’s tasted success in a variety of independent promotions, capturing championships in both singles and tag team competition.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[883,1497,2001],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":68,"storytelling":70,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":16,"matchLayout":71,"psychology":68,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":71,"technicalCoaching":55,"characterCoaching":86,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":84,"mediaHandling":86,"brandBuilding":83,"socialMediaSavvy":79,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":71,"consistency":78,"awareness":68,"judgement":81},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1746","wrestlerId":1746,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2022-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":1747,"name":"Robert Rodriguez","realName":"Robert Rodriguez","picture":"Robert Rodriguez.jpg","ability":0,"currentAbility":0,"potentialAbility":0,"charisma":9,"micSkills":0,"popularity":1,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":6,"injuryProne":0,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":79,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1968-06-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2014-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Robert Anthony Rodríguez s an American film director, screenwriter, producer, cinematographer, editor cartoonist and musician. He shoots and produces many of his films in Mexico and his native Texas. He has directed successful and groundbreaking film sagas such as the Mexico Trilogy, From Dusk till Dawn and the 2014 TV series,[3] and the Spy Kids films, as well as The Faculty, The Adventures of Sharkboy and Lavagirl in 3-D, Sin City, Planet Terror, and Machete. He is a friend and frequent collaborator of filmmaker Quentin Tarantino. In December 2013, Rodriguez launched his own cable TV channel, El Rey.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":42,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":42,"brandBuilding":0,"socialMediaSavvy":49,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":0,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0}},{"id":1748,"name":"John Gaburick","realName":"John Gaburick","picture":"John Gaburick.jpg","ability":90,"currentAbility":81,"potentialAbility":81,"charisma":74,"micSkills":90,"popularity":1,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":75,"injuryProne":0,"type":"writer","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":96,"height":170,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1966-04-22T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1998-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Prior to joining TNA Entertainment, Gaburick spent the past 13 years in production at WWE. While there, he was awarded the PROMAX/BDA Brandbuilder of the Year Award and guided all image and brand-building media campaigns, as well as network documentary programming. Additionally, he spent 10 years as Operations Manager for National Business Archives in Jessup, Maryland. He earned a Bachelor of Arts from Towson University in Towson, Maryland and is a proud member of The Towson University Athletic Hall of Fame.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":61,"storytelling":43,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":37,"psychology":61,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":12,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":12,"brandBuilding":18,"socialMediaSavvy":15,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":0,"awareness":61,"judgement":77},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-1748","wrestlerId":1748,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2020-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":1749,"name":"Aliyah","realName":"Aliyah","picture":"Jasmin Areebi.jpg","ability":48,"currentAbility":40,"potentialAbility":40,"charisma":35,"micSkills":34,"popularity":14,"condition":97,"hardcoreAbility":59,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"F","weight":51,"height":157,"base":"Canada","birthplace":"Canada","dateOfBirth":"1994-11-23T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2013-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Young, bold and boundlessly athletic, Aliyah welcomes the spotlight, perhaps because she’s no stranger to it. The WWE Universe has tracked her journey to Superstardom, beginning with appearances on the WWE Network original series Breaking Ground (where cameras documented Aliyah’s days training in the Performance Center) and extending to her first steps inside the NXT ring as a competitor.\r\n\r\nAliyah knew her future was in sports-entertainment the moment she saw Beth Phoenix and Mickie James battle on Raw in her hometown of Toronto. But Aliyah’s path to the squared circle was an indirect one that started with circus training as a teenager, which allowed her to increase her flexibility and master her body movement — qualities that pay dividends inside the ring and spell trouble for her opponents.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[2757,3499],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":39,"storytelling":44,"productFit":73,"riskTaking":34,"matchLayout":46,"psychology":39,"workerManagement":73,"trainingIntensity":57,"technicalCoaching":37,"characterCoaching":52,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":66,"mediaHandling":52,"brandBuilding":52,"socialMediaSavvy":31,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":15,"reactionSpeed":57,"consistency":63,"awareness":39,"judgement":53}},{"id":1750,"name":"Antonio Inoki","realName":"Antonio Inoki","picture":"Antonio Inoki.jpg","ability":53,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"charisma":67,"micSkills":48,"popularity":48,"condition":36,"hardcoreAbility":75,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":102,"height":187,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1943-02-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1960-09-30T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":true,"story":"Muhammad Hussain Inoki is a Japanese professional wrestling promoter, politician, retired professional wrestler and mixed martial artist best known by the ring name Antonio Inoki. He fashioned this name as a homage to wrestler Antonino Rocca. He was also the founder and former owner of New Japan Pro Wrestling, before selling his controlling share in the promotion to Yuke's. Inoki's current Muslim name was revealed in 2012 along with the announcement that he had converted to Islam in 1990.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":93,"storytelling":95,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":42,"matchLayout":96,"psychology":93,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":34,"technicalCoaching":44,"characterCoaching":58,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":58,"mediaHandling":58,"brandBuilding":73,"socialMediaSavvy":45,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":34,"consistency":45,"awareness":93,"judgement":96}},{"id":1751,"name":"Andre the Giant","realName":"Andre the Giant","picture":"Andre the Giant.jpg","ability":24,"currentAbility":23,"potentialAbility":23,"charisma":37,"micSkills":23,"popularity":72,"condition":0,"hardcoreAbility":22,"injuryProne":0,"type":"wrestler","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":239,"height":210,"base":"Europe","birthplace":"France","dateOfBirth":"1946-05-19T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1966-01-25T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"great","prestige":"high","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":true,"story":"André René Roussimoff best known as André the Giant, was a French professional wrestler and actor. His best-remembered acting role was that of Fezzik, the giant in the film The Princess Bride. His size was a result of gigantism caused by excess growth hormone, which later resulted in acromegaly. This led to him being called \"The Eighth Wonder of the World\". In the World Wrestling Federation (now known as WWE), André was a one-time WWF Champion and a one-time WWF World Tag Team Champion. In 1993, André was the inaugural inductee into the WWF Hall of Fame.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3110],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":30,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":40,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":15,"characterCoaching":35,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":35,"brandBuilding":98,"socialMediaSavvy":40,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":0,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0}},{"id":1753,"name":"Super Mega","realName":"Super Mega","picture":"Super Mega.jpg","ability":42,"currentAbility":47,"potentialAbility":47,"charisma":52,"micSkills":39,"popularity":2,"condition":83,"hardcoreAbility":60,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":98,"height":175,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1977-01-08T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1992-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"In 2001 Segura was given a new ring character, he became known as \"Super Mega\" and joined up with Mega and Ultra Mega to form the Los Megas Trio. The Último Vampiro character was given to a fourth and then a fifth person later on, but when Segura began working for Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) he assumed the ring character once more. In CMLL he worked mainly low and mid-card matches but never won any championships while working under the ring character","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[3259],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":60,"storytelling":64,"productFit":80,"riskTaking":34,"matchLayout":65,"psychology":60,"workerManagement":80,"trainingIntensity":54,"technicalCoaching":29,"characterCoaching":33,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":66,"mediaHandling":33,"brandBuilding":34,"socialMediaSavvy":47,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":16,"reactionSpeed":54,"consistency":56,"awareness":60,"judgement":68}},{"id":1759,"name":"BLANK","realName":"BLANK","picture":"Blank.jpg","ability":46,"currentAbility":49,"potentialAbility":49,"charisma":50,"micSkills":52,"popularity":2,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":43,"injuryProne":99,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"M","weight":93,"height":177,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1990-08-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2014-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"BLANK is a masked American wrestler who works in America and Canada. He is a Lightweight who is classed as using a Regular style. He is best known for his work with Beyond, AIW and CHIKARA.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1722,2186,2383],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"