rontier Martial-Arts Wrestling. He is credited with importing to Japan, as well as innovating, the deathmatch style of professional wrestling.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":true,"promotionId":null,"teams":[2883,2884],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":77,"storytelling":78,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":38,"matchLayout":78,"psychology":77,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":46,"technicalCoaching":37,"characterCoaching":84,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":62,"mediaHandling":84,"brandBuilding":55,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":46,"consistency":56,"awareness":77,"judgement":86}},{"id":1966,"name":"Flying Kid Ichihara","realName":"Flying Kid Ichihara","picture":"Akihito Ichihara.jpg","ability":79,"currentAbility":80,"potentialAbility":80,"charisma":84,"micSkills":81,"popularity":3,"condition":79,"hardcoreAbility":94,"injuryProne":100,"type":"writer","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":80,"height":165,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1969-01-24T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1990-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"Ichihara debuted in FMW in 1990 using his real name, Akihito Itahara. He spent 1992 in Mexico and returned in Japan with the masked gimmick of Ray Pandita. He later adopted the ring name of Flying Kid Ichihara and continued working for FMW until its closure. He later worked for several other indy promotions, most notably in Osaka Pro as Ebessan (2nd generation), without reaching the same success of the original one. He now is mostly inactive on the wrestling scene.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"