rone":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":100,"height":170,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1965-09-27T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1988-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Masanori Morimura is a Japanese professional wrestler, better known under his ring name Ricky Fuji. Masanori Morimura started training in the New Japan Pro Wrestling Dojo in 1984, but left the dojo because he was \"young and dumb\". While at the NJPW Dojo, he wanted to be a UWF fighter instead. When he failed to join UWF, he realized he ruined his chances at beginning his career in Japan. He then left Japan in January 1987 for a training expedition in Canada, where he was trained in the Dungeon by Stu Hart and his right-hand man, Mr. Hito. During his time training in Calgary, he suffered a couple major injuries, including a brain hemorrhage, which he fully recovered from. During his training, he would befriend other Japanese stars like Hiroshi Hase and his former NJPW Dojo mates Keiichi Yamada and Shinya Hashimoto.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":63,"storytelling":68,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":28,"matchLayout":70,"psychology":63,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":48,"technicalCoaching":51,"characterCoaching":63,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":72,"mediaHandling":63,"brandBuilding":58,"socialMediaSavvy":54,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":48,"consistency":45,"awareness":63,"judgement":78}},{"id":1981,"name":"Mandy Sacs","realName":"Mandy Sacs","picture":"Amanda Saccomanno.jpg","ability":48,"currentAbility":48,"potentialAbility":48,"charisma":60,"micSkills":44,"popularity":40,"condition":98,"hardcoreAbility":64,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"F","weight":54,"height":160,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1990-07-18T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2015-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":true,"dead":false,"story":"When you’re 5-foot-4 and can lift 225 pounds, you’re bound to turn some heads. That goes double when you look like Mandy Rose. An athletic powerhouse who wouldn't look out of place on a Hollywood red carpet, Rose has the physical prowess and brash attitude required to be a true Superstar. After debuting on Raw as part of Absolution along with Paige and Sonya Deville, The Golden Goddess found herself competing in such landmark moments as the first-ever Women’s Royal Rumble, first-ever Women’s Elimination Chamber Match and the groundbreaking WWE Mixed Match Challenge before moving to SmackDown Live as a part of the 2018 Superstar Shake-up alongside Deville.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1926,2339],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":44,"storytelling":50,"productFit":74,"riskTaking":34,"matchLayout":52,"psychology":44,"workerManagement":74,"trainingIntensity":74,"technicalCoaching":38,"characterCoaching":63,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":66,"mediaHandling":63,"brandBuilding":82,"socialMediaSavvy":54,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":15,"reactionSpeed":74,"consistency":63,"awareness":44,"judgement":56}},{"id":1985,"name":"Nixon Newell","realName":"Nixon Newell","picture":"Nixon Newell.jpg","ability":65,"currentAbility":56,"potentialAbility":56,"charisma":66,"micSkills":63,"popularity":23,"condition":74,"hardcoreAbility":76,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"all rounder","gender":"F","weight":64,"height":165,"base":"UK","birthplace":"Wales","dateOfBirth":"1994-11-15T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2014-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Tegan Nox is determined to make her star shine brighter than ever in NXT. It looks as though nothing can stop her, as The Girl with the Shiniest Wizard has worked too hard to get here. Originally slated to compete in the inaugural Mae Young Classic in 2017, Nox was forced out of the tournament with a torn right ACL. After 10 months on the shelf, the Welsh Superstar made it back in time for the 2018 edition of the 32-woman tournament, where she was considered a favorite to win the whole thing. Nox made it to the quarterfinals, where catastrophe reared its ugly head. A dive to the arena floor resulted in a devastating injury to Nox’s left leg – torn menisci MCL, LCL and ACL. That injury took Tegan out of action for close to a year. After returning to the ring for NXT UK in her home country of Wales, Nox has her sights set on NXT and becoming the NXT Women’s Champion. If her determination is anything to go by, Tegan Nox may prove to be faster, stronger and shinier than anyone.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[795,944,1942,2562,2729],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":57,"storytelling":62,"productFit":70,"riskTaking":30,"matchLayout":63,"psychology":57,"workerManagement":70,"trainingIntensity":77,"technicalCoaching":59,"characterCoaching":65,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":70,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":59,"socialMediaSavvy":51,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":14,"reactionSpeed":77,"consistency":68,"awareness":57,"judgement":62}},{"id":1986,"name":"Mike Sydal","realName":"Mike Sydal","picture":"Mike Sydal.jpg","ability":63,"currentAbility":54,"potentialAbility":54,"charisma":69,"micSkills":68,"popularity":4,"condition":83,"hardcoreAbility":66,"in