ey Race, Rip Rogers & Danny Davis.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":95,"teams":[635,953,954,3390],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":54,"storytelling":61,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":30,"matchLayout":64,"psychology":54,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":79,"technicalCoaching":56,"characterCoaching":69,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":70,"mediaHandling":69,"brandBuilding":37,"socialMediaSavvy":44,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":79,"consistency":58,"awareness":54,"judgement":72},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-2000","wrestlerId":2000,"promotionId":95,"startDate":"2021-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":2001,"name":"Gurv Sihra","realName":"Gurv Sihra","picture":"Gurv Sihra.jpg","ability":54,"currentAbility":60,"potentialAbility":60,"charisma":74,"micSkills":50,"popularity":16,"condition":88,"hardcoreAbility":53,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":72,"height":175,"base":"Canada","birthplace":"Canada","dateOfBirth":"1984-11-13T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2005-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"The Bollywood Boyz, Gurv and Harv Sihra, have used unwavering passion and old fashioned work ethic to climb their way to their current position. lthough they are of Indian descent, their humble beginnings in pro wrestling took place in Canada, where they endured agonizingly long drives and dangerously cold temperatures on what came to be known as “Northern Hell Death Tours” in chase of their dream. That journey also brought them before some of the most knowledgeable wrestling minds in the world today, as the two have sought out training with the likes of The Hart Family, Harley Race, Rip Rogers & Danny Davis.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":95,"teams":[635,953,954,3390],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":55,"storytelling":61,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":63,"psychology":55,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":81,"technicalCoaching":58,"characterCoaching":69,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":69,"brandBuilding":33,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":81,"consistency":70,"awareness":55,"judgement":73},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-2001","wrestlerId":2001,"promotionId":95,"startDate":"2021-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":2003,"name":"Jay White","realName":"Jay White","picture":"Jay White.jpg","ability":80,"currentAbility":71,"potentialAbility":71,"charisma":81,"micSkills":60,"popularity":47,"condition":86,"hardcoreAbility":62,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":100,"height":182,"base":"Australia","birthplace":"New Zealand","dateOfBirth":"1992-10-09T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2013-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Very few stars have burst onto the Ring of Honor scene like Jay White did. Introduced to ROH fans during the Best in the World 2016 pay-per-view, White made his ROH in-ring debut one night later, impressively defeating Kamaitachi and then winning a six-man tag team bout teaming with Motor City Machine Guns.\r\n\r\nThe New Zealand native and graduate of the New Japan Dojo spent nearly a year and a half in ROH on excursion and showed why he is one of the fastest-rising young stars in the sport. White scored victories over the likes of Punishment Martinez, Christopher Daniels, Kenny King, Donovan Dijak and Lio Rush, and he also formed an alliance with Motor City Machine Guns and Jonathan Gresham known as Search and Destroy. White returned to NJPW in 2018 as Switchblade and scored the biggest victory of his career when he defeated Kenny Omega to win the NJPW U.S. Title.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":80,"storytelling":81,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":20,"matchLayout":81,"psychology":80,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":86,"technicalCoaching":67,"characterCoaching":78,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":80,"mediaHandling":78,"brandBuilding":83,"socialMediaSavvy":76,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":86,"consistency":84,"awareness":80,"judgement":88},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-2003","wrestlerId":2003,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2023-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":2005,"name":"Liv Morgan","realName":"Liv Morgan","picture":"Liv Morgan.jpg","ability":53,"currentAbility":53,"potentialAbility":53,"charisma":55,"micSkills":61,"popularity":66,"condition":89,"hardcoreAbility":66,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"F","weight":53,"height":160,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1994-06-08T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2015-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"great","prestige":"mid","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Liv Morgan is an American wrestler who works in the USA and Canada. She is a 5'4\", 117lb worker who is classed as using a Entertainer style. She uses the ObLIVion as her finisher. She is best known for her work with WWE and NXT.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[1811,3487,4112],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":59,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":25,"matchLayout":60,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":48,"characterCoaching":80,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":75,"mediaHandling":80,"brandBuilding":78,"socialMediaSavvy":76,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":72,"awareness":56,"judgement":74},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-2005","wrestlerId":2005,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2017-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":2006,"name":"Masashi Takeda","realName":"Masashi Takeda","picture":"Masashi Takeda.jpg","ability":62,"currentAbility":65,"potentialAbility":65,"charisma":80,"micSkills":72,"popularity":8,"condition":79,"hardcoreAbility":54,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"striker","gender":"M","weight":93,"height":170,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1985-08-13T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2007-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"A shootfighter, Takeda trained in pro-wrestling in E-Style, where he debuted in 2007. After only a few months Takeda started working quite often with bigger promotions, such as DDT and Big Japan and is one of the most popular young shoot-style wrestlers in Japan.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":94,"teams":[1828,2404,2466,2467],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":70,"storytelling":73,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":33,"matchLayout":74,"psychology":70,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":80,"technicalCoaching":65,"characterCoaching":55,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":67,"mediaHandling":55,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":36,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":80,"consistency":79,"awareness":70,"judgement":82},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-2006","wrestlerId":2006,"promotionId":94,"startDate":"2009-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":2007,"name":"Takumi Tsukamoto","realName":"Takumi Tsukamoto","picture":"Takumi Tsukamoto.jpg","ability":59,"currentAbility":54,"potentialAbility":54,"charisma":41,"micSkills":55,"popularity":4,"condition":89,"hardcoreAbility":56,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"hardcore","gender":"M","weight":97,"height":170,"base":"Japan","birthplace":"Japan","dateOfBirth":"1991-01-06T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2009-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"heel","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Tsukamoto began spent 6 years of his youth studying Judo and Karate. In March 2009 he joined BJW right out high school. He would train in the promotion for the next and within 6 months he made his debut that September against Kazuki Hashimoto. Whom both of them trained together in the dojo. On February 2, 2012 Tsukamoto would make his debut in a deathmatch in a 6 man tag match with Jun Kasai and Jaki Numazawa. He would toy around with the idea of jumping into the deathmatch scene, but on September 10th he announced that he would be joining the deathmatch ranks of the promotion.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"ac