lower! Previously known as “Ramon” with R.D. Evans, Moose and Veda Scott in #TheNewStreak Family, the ROH Dojo graduate revealed his true alliance at “Glory by Honor XIII.” On that highly anticipated night, Evans was undefeated at 173 – 0 and competing for the World Television Championship against Jay Lethal. After a back and forth battle, Moose shocked the San Antonio crowd by spearing R.D. and allowing Lethal to retain his TV title. Hathaway appeared and unapologetically revealed that he was the mastermind behind the fall of #TheNewStreak. His actions earned him the reputation as one of the most despised and vengeful personalities within the ROH locker room.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":76,"teams":[2705],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":58,"storytelling":60,"productFit":33,"riskTaking":24,"matchLayout":60,"psychology":58,"workerManagement":33,"trainingIntensity":66,"technicalCoaching":44,"characterCoaching":85,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":76,"mediaHandling":85,"brandBuilding":44,"socialMediaSavvy":79,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":7,"reactionSpeed":66,"consistency":55,"awareness":58,"judgement":48},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-2091","wrestlerId":2091,"promotionId":76,"startDate":"2022-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":2092,"name":"Jeff Cobb","realName":"Jeff Cobb","picture":"Jeff Cobb.jpg","ability":74,"currentAbility":72,"potentialAbility":72,"charisma":60,"micSkills":75,"popularity":30,"condition":75,"hardcoreAbility":85,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":119,"height":175,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1982-07-11T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2009-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Before he even competed in his first match or uttered a single word, Jeff Cobb made a huge impact in Ring of Honor. The powerhouse from Hawaii stormed onto the scene by interrupting a 2018 Top Prospect Tournament match and destroying both competitors. He repeated the scene during two subsequent TPT matches before grabbing a microphone and declaring that the tournament is over because he is the top prospect. Cobb wasted no time making good on his bold assertion. In his official ROH in-ring debut, he steamrolled Punishment Martinez in under 90 seconds to win the ROH World Television Title.\r\n\r\nBefore turning pro in 2009, Cobb represented Guam in the 2004 Summer Olympics. He went on to have major success on the independent wrestling circuit, most notably with Pro Wrestling Guerrilla in California. In September 2018, Cobb won PWG’s prestigious Battle of Los Angeles tournament.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[2315,2765,2766,2767,3881],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":66,"storytelling":67,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":68,"psychology":66,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":77,"characterCoaching":65,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":65,"brandBuilding":65,"socialMediaSavvy":44,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":84,"awareness":66,"judgement":80}},{"id":2093,"name":"Rey Horus","realName":"Rey Horus","picture":"Rey Horus.jpg","ability":53,"currentAbility":59,"potentialAbility":59,"charisma":70,"micSkills":50,"popularity":11,"condition":91,"hardcoreAbility":71,"injuryProne":93,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":75,"height":167,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1984-06-24T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2007-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"In just his second Ring of Honor match, Rey Horus captured the ROH World Six-Man Tag Team Championships with Mexiblood, Bandido and Flamita. For those that have followed Horus’ high-flying career, the instant success should come as no surprise.\r\n\r\nLong-time fans may know Horus from his competing on Lucha Underground under the identity of Dragon Azteca Jr. and for his matches teaming with and against Prince Puma. Horus was trained by Rey Mysterio Jr.’s uncle Rey Misterio Sr. and the Mexican native has an impressive record competing in The Crash, holding their Heavyweight Championship and defending it against Marty Scurll and Jeff Cobb before losing it to Bandido in November.\r\n\r\nNow, Horus, Bandido, and Flamita find themselves aligned under the Mexiblood moniker and their instant success should serve a warning to Ring of Honor that the best is yet to come from this international star!","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":119,"teams":[1976,2313],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":60,"storytelling":67,"productFit":94,"riskTaking":29,"matchLayout":69,"psychology":60,"workerManagement":94,"trainingIntensity":86,"technicalCoaching":68,"characterCoaching":52,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":71,"mediaHandling":52,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":38,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":19,"reactionSpeed":86,"consistency":69,"awareness":60,"judgement":74},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-2093","wrestlerId":2093,"promotionId":119,"startDate":"2024-01-19T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:0