ent":27}},{"id":2659,"name":"Bianca Belair","realName":"Bianca Belair","picture":"Bianca Blair.jpg","ability":57,"currentAbility":64,"potentialAbility":64,"charisma":65,"micSkills":78,"popularity":61,"condition":96,"hardcoreAbility":73,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"F","weight":75,"height":167,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1989-04-09T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2016-09-29T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"good","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Bianca Belair is such a superlative competitor that she considers herself the “EST of WWE.” Proclaiming to be the strongest, fastest, toughest and all-around best Superstar going, Belair has been an exceptional athlete her entire life.\r\n\r\nBefore joining WWE, Belair earned All-SEC and All-American honors in track-and-field at the University of Tennessee. Since her arrival, she has backed up her EST moniker with big numbers in the WWE Performance Center weight room: Belair led the field in the 2016 and 2017 NXT Combines, thanks to feats like deadlifting 415-pounds.\r\n\r\nUnsurprisingly, Belair’s competitive nature has carried over into the ring. Though she relies on rugged power, Belair can be creatively merciless, too, using her long hair braid to whip opponents to shreds. She isn’t afraid to take big risks either, as she showed in the second round of the Mae Young Classic by launching a picture-perfect 450 splash against Kairi Sane.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[3994],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":63,"storytelling":65,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":27,"matchLayout":66,"psychology":63,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":85,"technicalCoaching":52,"characterCoaching":79,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":73,"mediaHandling":79,"brandBuilding":86,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":85,"consistency":76,"awareness":63,"judgement":78},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-2659","wrestlerId":2659,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2016-09-29T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":2663,"name":"Danielle Kamela","realName":"Danielle Kamela","picture":"Danielle Kamela.jpg","ability":37,"currentAbility":42,"potentialAbility":42,"charisma":29,"micSkills":36,"popularity":2,"condition":99,"hardcoreAbility":44,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"F","weight":75,"height":172,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1993-05-20T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2015-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"No stranger to the spotlight, Vanessa Borne was previously a broadcaster for Fox Sports Arizona, as well as a dancer for the Phoenix Suns and a cheerleader for the Arizona Cardinals. During her tenure with the Cardinals, she was featured on one of the world’s biggest stages — the Super Bowl — proving that she has the focus and experience to perform under pressure.\r\n\r\nWith aspirations of becoming a WWE Superstar, Borne trained under Attitude Era Superstar Gangrel and WWE Hall of Famer Rikishi before competing in the inaugural Mae Young Classic. This up-and-coming Superstar also made her NXT debut in 2017, catching the attention of her opponents and fans alike with her impressive agility and rugged determination.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[2757],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":38,"storytelling":42,"productFit":35,"riskTaking":36,"matchLayout":43,"psychology":38,"workerManagement":35,"trainingIntensity":74,"technicalCoaching":34,"characterCoaching":58,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":64,"mediaHandling":58,"brandBuilding":65,"socialMediaSavvy":42,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":7,"reactionSpeed":74,"consistency":56,"awareness":38,"judgement":37}},{"id":2664,"name":"El Cuatrero","realName":"El Cuatrero","picture":"El Cuatrero.jpg","ability":47,"currentAbility":55,"potentialAbility":55,"charisma":59,"micSkills":70,"popularity":6,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":62,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":94,"height":182,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1996-02-02T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2010-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Cuatrero is the youngest of the New Dynamite Generation, but he has shown to have the guts to stand up to any CMLL fighter. Accustomed to a quiet life that only the countryside can give him, he enjoys every stage he is in to the fullest. He has great discipline to get on the CMLL cards and emulate the triumphs of his father Cien Caras.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1610],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":61,"storytelling":66,"productFit":54,"riskTaking":23,"matchLayout":67,"psychology":61,"workerManagement":54,"trainingIntensity":76,"technicalCoaching":61,"characterCoaching":61,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":77,"mediaHandling":61,"brandBuilding":65,"socialMediaSavvy":59,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":11,"reactionSpeed":76,"consistency":71,"awareness":61,"judgement":58}},{"id":2665,"name":"El Santo Jr.","realName":"El Santo Jr.","picture":"El Santo Jr.jpg","ability":61,"currentAbility":52,"potentialAbility":52,"charisma":65,"micSkills":46,"popularity":1,"condition":70,"hardcoreAbility":58,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":95,"height":175,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1997-09-19T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2012-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"El Santo Jr. is a masked Mexican luchador who works in Mexico and Japan. He is a Lightweight who is classed as using a Luchador style. Started his training with Solar & his father at a young age, in 2014 he spent some time training with Pro Wrestling NOAH in Japan. Made his first known wrestling appearance wrestling in London at the York Hall lucha shows put on by his father.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":48,"storytelling":54,"productFit":28,"riskTaking":29,"matchLayout":56,"psychology":48,"workerManagement":28,"trainingIntensity":58,"technicalCoaching":55,"characterCoaching":68,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":71,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":94,"socialMediaSavvy":62,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":6,"reactionSpeed":58,"consistency":66,"awareness":48,"judgement":40}},{"id":2666,"name":"Faye Jackson","realName":"Faye Jackson","picture":"Faye Jackson.jpg","ability":60,"currentAbility":51,"potentialAbility":51,"charisma":56,"micSkills":50,"popularity":1,"condition":82,"hardcoreAbility":44,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"technical","gender":"F","weight":62,"height":160,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1987-06-30T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2016-02-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Faye Jackson burst onto the scene in 2016, making her professional wrestling debut on the very-first Women of Honor television special against international wrestling star ODB. Jumping straight into the deep end, Jackson gave ODB all she had and displayed a fire that showed she would be a force in future Women of Honor bouts. Under the tutelage of veteran star Sumie Sakai, Jackson has become a force to be reckoned with her moves the Triple Spun Milkshake and Chocolate Thunder!","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[2338,3116],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":47,"storytelling":53,"productFit":24,"riskTaking":31,"matchLayout":55,"psychology":47,"workerManagement":24,"trainingIntensity":74,"technicalCoaching":45,"characterCoaching":63,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":69,"mediaHandling":63,"brandBuilding":54,"socialMediaSavvy":47,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":5,"reactionSpeed":74,"consistency":72,"awareness":47,"judgement":38}},{"id":2667,"name":"Flip Gordon","realName":"Flip Gordon","picture":"Flip Gordon.jpg","ability":50,"currentAbility":58,"potentialAbility":58,"charisma":49,"micSkills":73,"popularity":21,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":47,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":94,"height":175,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1991-12-12T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2015-04-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"There’s a famous quote that says to “keep your feet on the ground and keep reaching for the stars.” Flip Gordon has applied his own spin to the sentiment. When the fearless and freakishly agile Gordon is in the ring, his feet quite often are off the ground, but the frequent flyer has seen his career soar to new heights since signing with Ring of Honor in 2017 just two and a half years after his pro wrestling debut.\r\n\r\nUsing his innovative, acrobatic offense to go toe to toe with the best wrestlers on the planet, Gordon’s confidence has grown by leaps and bounds, and it appears the sky’s the limit for the rising star. Gordon, a native of Kalispell, Montana whose background includes amateur wrestling, mixed martial arts and gymnastics, is also an active member of the Army National Guard.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":11,"teams":[2264,2650,3551],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":62,"storytelling":66,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":24,"matchLayout":68,"psychology":62,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":80,"technicalCoaching":54,"characterCoaching":62,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":76,"mediaHandling":62,"brandBuilding":64,"socialMediaSavvy":58,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":80,"consistency":78,"awareness":62,"judgement":77},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-2667","wrestlerId":2667,"promotionId":11,"startDate":"2023-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000,"bookingsPerMonth":4,"type":"non-exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":1000},{"id":2668,"name":"Hahastary","realName":"Hahastary","picture":"Hahastary.jpg","ability":35,"currentAbility":44,"potentialAbility":44,"charisma":51,"micSkills":59,"popularity":3,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":34,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"F","weight":54,"height":160,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1993-10-10T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2011-11-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Hahastary is a masked Mexican luchadora who works exclusively in Mexico. She is a Very Small worker who is classed as using a Luchador style. She is best known for her work with AAA, IWRG and DTU.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":42,"storytelling":48,"productFit":33,"riskTaking":36,"matchLayout":50,"psychology":42,"workerManagement":33,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":53,"characterCoaching":53,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":64,"mediaHandling":53,"brandBuilding":50,"socialMediaSavvy":47,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":7,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":61,"awareness":42,"judgement":38}},{"id":2670,"name":"Montez Ford","realName":"Montez Ford","picture":"Kenneth Crawford.jpg","ability":55,"currentAbility":61,"potentialAbility":61,"charisma":49,"micSkills":46,"popularity":46,"condition":90,"hardcoreAbility":66,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"M","weight":105,"height":182,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1990-05-31T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2015-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"fair","prestige":"mid","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"When you bring the swag like Montez Ford can, you might be forgiven for bragging a bit.\r\n\r\nRecruited into the WWE Performance Center in 2015, Ford was destined for big things from day one. Even though he had no prior experience in sports-entertainment, Ford’s athleticism demanded such high expectations. A track star in his youth, Ford shattered high school records in events like the 200- and 400-meter dash before enlisting in the U.S. Marine Corps, where he accumulated a perfect 300 score on the physical fitness test. King Tez has been no less impressive since joining NXT, either. A 62-inch box jump and 10-foot, 10-inch broad jump are the kind of feats that most men can only dream of. For Ford, “issa light day” at the WWE Performance Center.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":64,"teams":[1603,2361],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":56,"storytelling":60,"productFit":100,"riskTaking":26,"matchLayout":62,"psychology":56,"workerManagement":100,"trainingIntensity":75,"technicalCoaching":58,"characterCoaching":81,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":74,"mediaHandling":81,"brandBuilding":80,"socialMediaSavvy":65,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":20,"reactionSpeed":75,"consistency":84,"awareness":56,"judgement":74},"contract":{"id":"tew-contract-2670","wrestlerId":2670,"promotionId":64,"startDate":"2018-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333,"type":"exclusive","status":"active","autoRenew":false},"contractExpiryDate":"2026-03-31T23:00:00.000Z","wage":4333},{"id":2671,"name":"Lance Lude","realName":"Lance Lude","picture":"Lance Lude.jpg","ability":44,"currentAbility":54,"potentialAbility":54,"charisma":67,"micSkills":40,"popularity":0,"condition":80,"hardcoreAbility":70,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":88,"height":167,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1983-01-28T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2005-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Lance Lude is an American wrestler who works exclusively in America. He is a Lightweight who is classed as using a High Flyer style. He is one half of The Ugly Ducklings alongside Rob Killjoy.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[1602,1839,2968],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":48,"storytelling":55,"productFit":30,"riskTaking":29,"matchLayout":58,"psychology":48,"workerManagement":30,"trainingIntensity":73,"technicalCoaching":52,"characterCoaching":47,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":71,"mediaHandling":47,"brandBuilding":41,"socialMediaSavvy":39,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":6,"reactionSpeed":73,"consistency":68,"awareness":48,"judgement":41}},{"id":2672,"name":"Macey Estrella","realName":"Macey Estrella","picture":"Macey Estrella.jpg","ability":53,"currentAbility":43,"potentialAbility":43,"charisma":53,"micSkills":48,"popularity":34,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":42,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"powerhouse","gender":"F","weight":59,"height":170,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1990-03-24T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2014-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"poor","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"“The Lady of WWE” Lacey Evans mixes the glamour of a pin-up model with the discipline of a warrior.\r\n\r\nAfter growing up in a broken home where everything she owned was shared with her seven siblings, Evans joined the U.S. Marines, graduating with honors from Fort Leonard Hood and serving as military police and on the Special Reaction Team. While still in the service, she opened a construction company, housed and employed three of her siblings, and along with her husband, began the journey of raising a daughter.\r\n\r\nInspired to pursue sports-entertainment after watching a staff sergeant compete at a local event, Evans cut her teeth in southeastern U.S. independents before signing with the WWE Performance Center in April 2016. She steadily worked her way up NXT’s ladder, wrestled in the inaugural Mae Young Classic as well as the 2019 Royal Rumble Match, and ruthlessly punished her peers on the black-and-gold brand.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":43,"storytelling":46,"produc