},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":34,"storytelling":39,"productFit":29,"riskTaking":46,"matchLayout":40,"psychology":34,"workerManagement":29,"trainingIntensity":51,"technicalCoaching":17,"characterCoaching":44,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":54,"mediaHandling":44,"brandBuilding":74,"socialMediaSavvy":26,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":6,"reactionSpeed":51,"consistency":61,"awareness":34,"judgement":32}},{"id":2847,"name":"Warrior Jr.","realName":"Warrior Jr.","picture":"Black Warrior Jr.jpg","ability":53,"currentAbility":56,"potentialAbility":56,"charisma":60,"micSkills":66,"popularity":2,"condition":78,"hardcoreAbility":57,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":97,"height":170,"base":"Mexico","birthplace":"Mexico","dateOfBirth":"1997-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2016-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":true,"retired":false,"dead":true,"story":"Jesus Toral López is a luchador who has worked almost exclusively in Mexico. López has achieved most success under the ring name Black Warrior and had worked for Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL) since 1995. Before assuming the \"Black Warrior\" ring persona, López worked for almost a decade under various ring personas, generally with little success. His only previous ring persona of note was that of \"Bronce\" (Spanish for Bronze) where he was a part of the \"Los Metalicos\" team, a team that was popular in the early 1990s, teaming with Oro and Plata. López is the nephew of Luchador Blue Panther, the son-in-law of Mana Negro and the brother-in-law of Mano Negro, Jr. On June 20, 2012, Black Warrior turned rudo and formed the Los Depredadores del Aire.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":54,"storytelling":59,"productFit