n","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Reggie is an American wrestler who works exclusively in America. He is a Small worker who is classed as using a High Flyer style. He is best known for his work with WWE and NXT. He is dating someone outside the wrestling business.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":35,"storytelling":41,"productFit":17,"riskTaking":33,"matchLayout":43,"psychology":35,"workerManagement":17,"trainingIntensity":71,"technicalCoaching":27,"characterCoaching":68,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":67,"mediaHandling":68,"brandBuilding":55,"socialMediaSavvy":64,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":3,"reactionSpeed":71,"consistency":56,"awareness":35,"judgement":28}},{"id":3862,"name":"Joey Styles","realName":"Joey Styles","picture":"Joey Styles.jpg","ability":47,"currentAbility":57,"potentialAbility":57,"charisma":65,"micSkills":48,"popularity":3,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":68,"injuryProne":0,"type":"commentator","style":"all rounder","gender":"M","weight":71,"height":167,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"1971-07-14T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"1992-08-01T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"At first glance, Joey Styles may not have looked like the perfect candidate to be the voice of Extreme Championship Wrestling. The renegade Philadelphia promotion was wild, carnal and barely suitable for television. Styles, on the other hand, was well-groomed, eloquent and looked more like an ad exec trapped in the middle of a barroom brawl.\r\n\r\nBut the disparity between the competitors throwing chair shots in the ring and the man calling the shots in the announce booth was exactly why it worked so well. While Terry Funk and Sabu tore each other apart in a brutal Barbwire Match, Styles brought a humanity to the ensuing carnage. Think of it this way — Styles was the calm in the middle of a storm. That was until there was a truly unbelievable moment in the match, in which case The Extreme Announcer would unleash the three simple words that became his signature phrase: “Oh my God!\"","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"record":{"wins":0,"losses":0,"draws":0},"history":{"matches":[],"jobs":[],"titles":[]},"staffAttributes":{"bookingLogic":0,"storytelling":0,"productFit":0,"riskTaking":100,"matchLayout":0,"psychology":0,"workerManagement":0,"trainingIntensity":0,"technicalCoaching":0,"characterCoaching":53,"diagnosis":50,"rehabilitation":50,"prevention":0,"mediaHandling":53,"brandBuilding":10,"socialMediaSavvy":43,"ruleKnowledge":0,"positioning":0,"reactionSpeed":0,"consistency":0,"awareness":0,"judgement":0}},{"id":3863,"name":"Brodie Lee Jr.","realName":"Brodie Lee Jr.","picture":"Brodie Lee Jr.jpg","ability":29,"currentAbility":38,"potentialAbility":38,"charisma":34,"micSkills":28,"popularity":8,"condition":100,"hardcoreAbility":23,"injuryProne":100,"type":"wrestler","style":"high flyer","gender":"M","weight":54,"height":167,"base":"USA","birthplace":"United States","dateOfBirth":"2012-01-17T00:00:00.000Z","debut":"2026-04-10T00:00:00.000Z","morale":"broken","prestige":"low","presentation":"face","cardPosition":"lower","masked":false,"retired":false,"dead":false,"story":"Brodie Lee Jr. is the son of deceased wrestler Jon Huber, famously known as Brodie Lee or Luke Harper. During his father's illness, he was signed to an official contract at AEW, the company Huber was working for at the time of his passing, and has since become an on-screen character including doing color commentary on AEW Dark.","alterEgos":[],"managerId":0,"acceptsIndieBookings":false,"promotionId":null,"teams":[],"r